i.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:18:22-07:00","id":1519460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519456#post1519456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a sec... Wasn't &quot;Animal Magnetism&quot; literally one of those bad aspects of past WtA that an update like this was supposed to move past...?!</div> </div> </div> </div>*pulls out pdf* Animal Attraction, which used to be an in-bult 'power' rather than a Gift, could backfire horrifically if you botched, and which I don't think I ever saw actually used (so in practice was a waste of word count). W20 also has an Animal Magnetism merit which makes you especially attractive, but if we assume Appearance was intended as 'ability to make an impression' rather than a 'hotness stat' It's basically a run of the mill Good Looks merit.<br /> <br /> This is actually worse than either version in W20, even though it doesn't directly mention sex and those do. At the same time there's nothing inherently wrong with including mind-whammy powers, but you kind of have to admit you're playing with consent (which I'm not sure is territory Paradox really wants to be in) whether or not it's about getting sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:22:16-07:00","id":1519461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519460#post1519460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *pulls out pdf* Animal Attraction, which used to be an in-bult 'power' rather than a Gift, could backfire horrifically if you botched, and which I don't think I ever saw actually used (so in practice was a waste of word count). W20 also has an Animal Magnetism merit which makes you especially attractive, but if we assume Appearance was intended as 'ability to make an impression' rather than a 'hotness stat' It's basically a run of the mill Good Looks merit.<br /> <br /> This is actually worse than either version in W20, even though it doesn't directly mention sex and those do. At the same time there's nothing inherently wrong with including mind-whammy powers, but you kind of have to admit you're playing with consent (which I'm not sure is territory Paradox really wants to be in) whether or not it's about getting sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description should've been used to avoid the areas where &quot;mind-manipulation&quot; gets into icky territory. Words like &quot;attractive&quot; and mentioning a &quot;Peacock&quot; certainly don't help with that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:41:57-07:00","id":1519466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519454#post1519454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that system for Rites they have in W5 seems very punitive. Also, as we discussed during the previews, it doesn't support the communal aspect of Garou very well.<br /> <br /> This is how Rites work:<br /> <br /> So you have the Ritemaster with a dice-pool like &quot;Honor + Occult&quot; and the Difficulty is usually &quot;Diff = number of participants (minimum is 3, though)&quot;. But mind you having a 1 or 2 on at least two Rage-Dice causes a Brutal Outcome and the Rites each have an additional effect when you have a Brutal Outcome (usually it's a bad one like WP-damage).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the bit that confuses me. Rites are an excellent social and spiritual exercise, but using them like this feels like a really nasty way for things to go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:44:30-07:00","id":1519469,"title":"","content":"so uh, anyone with the book, check p.117 onwards.<br /> <br /> They copied the epic Alby vs Mari fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:51:21-07:00","id":1519471,"title":"","content":"So, are there still three Breeds in the game? Homid, Lupus, and something in between? I could see them renaming and redefining Metis to no longer be \u201cyour parents committed a crime, and you suffer for it\u201d; but I'd be a bit annoyed if they ditch the \u201craised in a sept among other werewolves, you know Garou culture better than most homids or lupus\u201d option that they represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:55:37-07:00","id":1519474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519471#post1519471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are there still three Breeds in the game? Homid, Lupus, and something in between? I could see them renaming and redefining Metis to no longer be \u201cyour parents committed a crime, and you suffer for it\u201d; but I'd be a bit annoyed if they ditch the \u201craised in a sept among other werewolves, you know Garou culture better than most homids or lupus\u201d option that they represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crinos-born aren't a thing in W5 and there are no special systems for wolf-born Garou (it just occasionally comes up in a sidebar as a player-option you could theoretically take). But the game mainly acts like everybody's a Homid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:56:09-07:00","id":1519475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519471#post1519471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are there still three Breeds in the game? Homid, Lupus, and something in between? I could see them renaming and redefining Metis to no longer be \u201cyour parents committed a crime, and you suffer for it\u201d; but I'd be a bit annoyed if they ditch the \u201craised in a sept among other werewolves, you know Garou culture better than most homids or lupus\u201d option that they represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're out. Only Lupus and Homid, and there are no significant differences to them outside the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T10:57:05-07:00","id":1519476,"title":"","content":"So they went full-Forsaken in that regard. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:07:47-07:00","id":1519478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519476#post1519476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they went full-Forsaken in that regard. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like pretend Forsaken, lupus are still a thing. Probably because they're relatively popular, we can bring up issues if we want but many people like the idea of playing a wolf who turns into a human.<br /> <br /> Forsaken is at least honest about wanting everybody to be human-born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:13:00-07:00","id":1519479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519475#post1519475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're out. Only Lupus and Homid, and there are no significant differences to them outside the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lame.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519433#post1519433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do W5's writers have such a hateboner for the Get of Fenris? I mean, fucking Black Spiral Dancers can be saved but not the Fenrir?</div> </div> </div> </div>Others have followed the claims more closely, so you might want to wait for someone else to clarify, but as much as I gather, it's seems like Paradox decided it was both harder to navigate the line between the aspects of the Get that were appealing to Nazis and the aspects that are appealing to people who want to play viking Werewolves, reclaim Nordic iconography, and otherwise just want to be the Not Nazi part of the Get, and at the same time wanted to hard cut themselves away from any claims of Nazi-sympathizing by hard condemning it.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I can understand the logic-resurging Nazi-ism is a hot topic button, and they have historically been <i>really bad</i> at not seeming like they were friendly to such, so a knee jerk is to be expected. On the other hand, this is what happens when you have a &quot;mature&quot; game that has been slowly trying to become a more mature game get handed off to &quot;mature&quot; game developers who want to make a mature game but only understand it in &quot;mature&quot; terms.<br /> <br /> A kinder person would leave it at the product being the result of a person new to these issues trying their best to address them-plenty of vim and verve, but not enough depth of understanding to actually make it work. A meaner person might level something like &quot;the idiot's idea of what it means to handle sensitive issues and past mistakes&quot; at it. For myself, I am content to leave it at &quot;lessons to learn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:20:18-07:00","id":1519482,"title":"","content":"Well, much like there's now an Imbued supplement on STV that retools H5 to actually feature the Imbued, I expect that as soon as STV opens up for W5 material, we'll get a \u201chow to remake the Fenrir as a playable Tribe\u201d book. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Not as good as having it addressed properly in the core book; but better than nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:28:15-07:00","id":1519483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519479#post1519479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lame.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Others have followed the claims more closely, so you might want to wait for someone else to clarify, but as much as I gather, it's seems like Paradox decided it was both harder to navigate the line between the aspects of the Get that were appealing to Nazis and the aspects that are appealing to people who want to play viking Werewolves, reclaim Nordic iconography, and otherwise just want to be the Not Nazi part of the Get, and at the same time wanted to hard cut themselves away from any claims of Nazi-sympathizing by hard condemning it.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I can understand the logic-resurging Nazi-ism is a hot topic button, and they have historically been <i>really bad</i> at not seeming like they were friendly to such, so a knee jerk is to be expected. On the other hand, this is what happens when you have a &quot;mature&quot; game that has been slowly trying to become a more mature game get handed off to &quot;mature&quot; game developers who want to make a mature game but only understand it in &quot;mature&quot; terms.<br /> <br /> A kinder person would leave it at the product being the result of a person new to these issues trying their best to address them-plenty of vim and verve, but not enough depth of understanding to actually make it work. A meaner person might level something like &quot;the idiot's idea of what it means to handle sensitive issues and past mistakes&quot; at it. For myself, I am content to leave it at &quot;lessons to learn.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, frankly this &quot;mature&quot; is more about not addressing certain topics to avoid problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T11:34:49-07:00","id":1519484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519483#post1519483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, frankly this &quot;mature&quot; is more about not addressing certain topics to avoid problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, why some matures are matures and some matures are &quot;matures.&quot; They don't want to support Nazi-ism, sure, great, always a good thing, but the stance they've taken on the Get is a refusal to acknowledge any of the nuance there or own up to the line's problems-heaven forbid they use it as a way to examine how and why people get sucked into ethnonationalism and fascism in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's an immature understanding of what should have been done with the mature content they had to deal wit, is what I was getting at. It's &quot;mature&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:00:23-07:00","id":1519487,"title":"","content":"So: comparing this to Forsaken. Please let me know if I'm getting anything wrong; I'm not posting this as a complaint or critique, just seeking clarity. <br /> <br /> No more Breeds, kind of like Forsaken (with the only difference being that W5 says that if you want to roleplay a Lupus, you can; there just aren't any game systems attached to it).<br /> <br /> Garou <i>tend to have</i> other Garou in their ancestry, but don't have to, kind of like how an Uratha was wolf-kin before the First Change but \u201cwolf-kin\u201d was redefined so that it's not necessarily hereditary. <br /> <br /> Tribes aren't something that you're born into; they're something you join. And they've been reworked to no longer be tied to specific real-world cultures. Again, much like how Forsaken's Tribes are something you join rather than something that you're born into, and aren't tied to specific real-world cultures. The main difference here is that W5 has a dozen Tribes while WtF only has five. <br /> <br /> Can anyone confirm a rumor I heard a while back, that in W5 Stepping Sideways has been restricted to something you can only do in spiritually significant places? If so, that's another Forsaken-ism that W5 has adopted. <br /> <br /> Are there any others? And conversely, what distinguishes W5 from WtF? There's still a Triat, right? And the game is still ultimately about fighting a losing (but not necessarily lost) battle against the end of the world? That would be a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:09:25-07:00","id":1519490,"title":"","content":"There's a Triat, but apparently extremes of any given manifestation can't be detected mystically for whatever reason. Presumably because someone got the wrong idea of what was going on there and put the cart before the horse so that there wouldn't be an &quot;easy excuse&quot; for just killing vampires.<br /> <br /> Joke's on them - if the vampires act the same, that's really all the reason you need to turn them into a Wraith character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-02-2023, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:52:17-07:00","id":1519495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519454#post1519454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that system for Rites they have in W5 seems very punitive. Also, as we discussed during the previews, it doesn't support the communal aspect of Garou very well.<br /> <br /> This is how Rites work:<br /> <br /> So you have the Ritemaster with a dice-pool like &quot;Honor + Occult&quot; and the Difficulty is usually &quot;Diff = number of participants (minimum is 3, though)&quot;. But mind you having a 1 or 2 on at least two Rage-Dice causes a Brutal Outcome and the Rites each have an additional effect when you have a Brutal Outcome (usually it's a bad one like WP-damage).<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a recipe for disaster......this is kind of like V5 in that if the SPCs used the same mechanics as the PCs their society would never have gotten off the ground let alone remained functional for more than a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:55:55-07:00","id":1519497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519487#post1519487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: comparing this to Forsaken. Please let me know if I'm getting anything wrong; I'm not posting this as a complaint or critique, just seeking clarity.<br /> <br /> No more Breeds, kind of like Forsaken (with the only difference being that W5 says that if you want to roleplay a Lupus, you can; there just aren't any game systems attached to it). <b>Correct</b><br /> <br /> Garou <i>tend to have</i> other Garou in their ancestry, but don't have to, kind of like how an Uratha was wolf-kin before the First Change but \u201cwolf-kin\u201d was redefined so that it's not necessarily hereditary. <b>Correct</b><br /> <br /> Tribes aren't something that you're born into; they're something you join. And they've been reworked to no longer be tied to specific real-world cultures. Again, much like how Forsaken's Tribes are something you join rather than something that you're born into, and aren't tied to specific real-world cultures. The main difference here is that W5 has a dozen Tribes while WtF only has five. <b>Correct</b><br /> <br /> Can anyone confirm a rumor I heard a while back, that in W5 Stepping Sideways has been restricted to something you can only do in spiritually significant places? If so, that's another Forsaken-ism that W5 has adopted.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't gotten up to the section on Stepping Sideways as yet but the Loresheet that they dropped a few weeks ago seemed to indicate that it was very, very difficult anywhere other than a Caern.....but there were scant details there so I'll need to read on.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:59:12-07:00","id":1519499,"title":"","content":"Checked. Very different game from what I expected. Different and not that bad. <br /> Quick thoughts:<br /> 1. Sadly there's a lot less number of gifts and rites and fetishes (talismans) and they are truly changed<br /> 2. Garou ability to run through almost everything stayed.<br /> 3. BSD and Cult of Fenrir are somehow rebuilt.<br /> 4. Stargazers again did what they did.<br /> 5. Loreshets are very unexpected.<br /> 6. There's fuel for willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:12:58-07:00","id":1519500,"title":"","content":"No joke, I find the loresheets detailing redeeming a BSD and then the Cult of Fenris one basically just -surviving- being one really REALLY...unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Because the Cult of Fenris still fights to protect Gaia and is seen as bad guys because that is ALL they do and without care about who gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the BSD description pretty much states that the BSDs are still the deranged monsters we know.<br /> <br /> Why is it that you can redeem a horrid cultist who mutilates and tortures at BEST while the side that STILL fights the Wyrm is unable to change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:20:39-07:00","id":1519501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519500#post1519500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No joke, I find the loresheets detailing redeeming a BSD and then the Cult of Fenris one basically just -surviving- being one really REALLY...unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Because the Cult of Fenris still fights to protect Gaia and is seen as bad guys because that is ALL they do and without care about who gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the BSD description pretty much states that the BSDs are still the deranged monsters we know.<br /> <br /> Why is it that you can redeem a horrid cultist who mutilates and tortures at BEST while the side that STILL fights the Wyrm is unable to change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Horrid monster &quot;can be saved&quot;, says someone.<br /> <br /> In other news, imperfect actors attempting to continue struggling against the end continue to be<i> the worst</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:25:05-07:00","id":1519503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519500#post1519500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No joke, I find the loresheets detailing redeeming a BSD and then the Cult of Fenris one basically just -surviving- being one really REALLY...unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Because the Cult of Fenris still fights to protect Gaia and is seen as bad guys because that is ALL they do and without care about who gets hurt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the BSD description pretty much states that the BSDs are still the deranged monsters we know.<br /> <br /> Why is it that you can redeem a horrid cultist who mutilates and tortures at BEST while the side that STILL fights the Wyrm is unable to change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than the information you gave, we can come to the conclusion that the BSD are that way due to the corruption of the Wyrm, the Fenris are that way by choice, so does it kind of explain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:28:15-07:00","id":1519504,"title":"","content":"No; because people can change their choices. Something that was imposed on a person needs to be removed, or else they'll continue to be influenced by it no matter what they choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:36:25-07:00","id":1519505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519503#post1519503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worse than the information you gave, we can come to the conclusion that the BSD are that way due to the corruption of the Wyrm, the Fenris are that way by choice, so does it kind of explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, until we get a description of the Black Spiral in W5, we must assume it works like before. Even if we go by Revised where you CAN force someone to become a BSD, there is still a choice in one's actions during the Dance that could result in them just dying. That and choices AFTER the Dance are still their own.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Fenrir are said to all be under a garou mental illness of a sort and yet they STILL focus on fighting the Wyrm as their main foe.<br /> <br /> Fenrir culture is about the destruction of things and people in pursuit of the Wyrm. BSD culture is enjoying the spoiled world in order to make it be reborn in its image, which includes things the Fenrir do not do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T13:40:54-07:00","id":1519507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519504#post1519504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No; because people can change their choices. Something that was imposed on a person needs to be removed, or else they'll continue to be influenced by it no matter what they choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man... I'm not even going to get into the discussion if a person is capable of changing, which is already very debatable depending on the case, but in this particular case not many are willing to debate or give it a chance because the Get, you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T14:01:44-07:00","id":1519510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519505#post1519505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, until we get a description of the Black Spiral in W5, we must assume it works like before. Even if we go by Revised where you CAN force someone to become a BSD, there is still a choice in one's actions during the Dance that could result in them just dying. That and choices AFTER the Dance are still their own.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Fenrir are said to all be under a garou mental illness of a sort and yet they STILL focus on fighting the Wyrm as their main foe.<br /> <br /> Fenrir culture is about the destruction of things and people in pursuit of the Wyrm. BSD culture is enjoying the spoiled world in order to make it be reborn in its image, which includes things the Fenrir do not do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but that's in the old versions, they already changed elements in W5, it wouldn't be strange for them to change to accommodate that narrative. Even if this is not the case, your reasoning is just a way of interpreting the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T15:40:31-07:00","id":1519516,"title":"","content":"So it sounds like W5 is shaping up about what appearing to be, Knock-off WtF 2E at best, an incoherent mess at worst. Also it sounds like few pages than V5 but like twenty dollars more. Or in other words, Renegade and ParaWolf continue to over price and under deliver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519505#post1519505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, until we get a description of the Black Spiral in W5, we must assume it works like before. Even if we go by Revised where you CAN force someone to become a BSD, there is still a choice in one's actions during the Dance that could result in them just dying. That and choices AFTER the Dance are still their own.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Fenrir are said to all be under a garou mental illness of a sort and yet they STILL focus on fighting the Wyrm as their main foe.<br /> <br /> Fenrir culture is about the destruction of things and people in pursuit of the Wyrm. BSD culture is enjoying the spoiled world in order to make it be reborn in its image, which includes things the Fenrir do not do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay that just feels so stupid to me on several levels. Like back and W20 had played with the idea of a purified BSD might be possible but the one case of that being a BSD that has spent years in a silver sea in Erebus and no one actually knows if he will actually be purified or just die in the process. Yet apparently I guess being corrupted by the Wyrm isn't nearly as big a deal as becoming a fanatical warrior for Gaia...<br /> <br /> It also apparently ignores that plenty of BSD are insane, often of the more violent kind.<br /> <br /> Yet they can be redeemed...<br /> <br /> Like it would be one thing if they were a Garou descended of BSD but were found by others before the BSD could claim them. In fact I think there's a short story revolving around such a character. But we're talking about Garou that have Danced the Spiral and driven into the corrupting embrace of the Wyrm. That should not be something that can be easily overcome. See the W20 example.<br /> <br /> It should be far easier to convince a Fenrir that they are going too far in their actions than it is to convince a BSD.<br /> <br /> While I don't have the W5 and don't know how it describes the Fenrir but the idea that they are all mentally ill and that's why they are what they are leaves me concerned because it almost sounds like they're saying they're irredeemable because they're mentally ill which is a <b><i>really</i></b> bad take to have.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T15:47:41-07:00","id":1519518,"title":"","content":"Well. This is what and who the new Get are. <br /> <br /> <img width=\"347\" height=\"580\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img width=\"343\" height=\"790\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" clas