s=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519518#post1519518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. This is what and who the new Get are.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"347\" height=\"580\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nECNyOI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img width=\"343\" height=\"790\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dm3VD7n.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay it's not as totally bad as I thought. Though it reminds me of the Transition Guide's brief write-up of the Pure Tribes to Apocalypse, especially the Predator Kings which they made an extremist Red Talon Camp that blames humanity for everything and wants to tear everything human down. So yeah, the Fenrir have serious Pure Tribe vibes from that write-up. Which honestly could be another thing on the Knock-off WtF pile.<br /> <br /> There's also really nothing but the name in that screams Fenrir to me. Frankly it sounds more like what I and others had said in the past, that this Cult should have been either Red Talons who already had a strong animosity towards Humans or a cross-tribal group of fanatics that broke away and severe as the dark mirror to the Garou. Personally I lean towards the latter myself as it would still keep the Tribes as playable while giving an antagonist that fills a role that none previously did.<br /> <br /> As for the BSD... why did they change their Totem? What reason was there for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:32:02-07:00","id":1519523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519522#post1519522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the BSD... why did they change their Totem? What reason was there for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing ever changed from the old setting. It was always like this in the world of W5. The story goes that Bat was the one that offered the fallen Spirals a way out of the Spiral.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:36:14-07:00","id":1519524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519455#post1519455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal magnetism is a icky rape power, we're not having anything like that in our Werewolf!<br /> <br /> <img width=\"341\" height=\"328\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/drbLuq8.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/drbLuq8.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/drbLuq8.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's nothing there specifically about sex. It just attracts attention to them. So you walk into a crowded room and pop the gift and everyone will turn to look at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:36:27-07:00","id":1519525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519523#post1519523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing ever changed from the old setting. It was always like this in the world of W5. The story goes that Bat was the one that offered the fallen Spirals a way out of the Spiral.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No I meant out of universe why did they change the BSD's Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:38:40-07:00","id":1519526,"title":"","content":"... wow they did Bat dirty... the whole Shadow Lords trying to repent for Bat thing is kinda wasted if Bat's been with the Wyrm since the BSDs happened.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about having a single Patron for Pentex... and have it be Fly.<br /> <br /> While I get the animist setup of WtA pushes spirits into human perceptions of things on some level, this is something that most serious environmentalists abhor: demonizing crucial animals the keep ecosystems healthy. Bats are spooky, and flies are &quot;dirty&quot; but they're essential for a healthy environment. The diversity and population of fly larvae is one of the best indicators of the health of riparian ecosystems despite decades of attempts to come up with something a bit easier than wading into streams, physically collecting a bunch of samples, setting them back, and getting bit by a lot of bugs in the process. And of course, carnivorous bats eat hugs numbers of pests, while pollinator bats are key to plant health that way.<br /> <br /> It's easy to get people to care about big cute/awesome/etc. mammals. That's why those are the focus of animal conservation advertising. But the actual work of trying to save ecosystems involves a lot of saving creepy crawly things that make most people's skin itch just looking at them. That was a great thing about having both Rat and Cockroach (though I guess Spider isn't so bad in this regard): animals that you don't want to cuddle (no offense to people that keep any as pets, they're fun pets even if most people aren't into it) are just as important to saving Gaia as the majestic ones.<br /> <br /> Whippoorwill didn't make a lick of sense for the BSDs (they're a North American only group within the nightjars), and the whole &quot;goatsucker&quot; myth doesn't have much resonance these days (but at least nightjars had some association with something negative). But surely they could have picked something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:39:36-07:00","id":1519527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519525#post1519525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I meant out of universe why did they change the BSD's Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Totems got flattened and simplified in general. All the tribes are defined by a singular patron now. They needed one totem for them, so they settled on Bat. Just like they rather heavy handedly settled the GW on Spider.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:45:55-07:00","id":1519528,"title":"","content":"And, since screw the edit demons:<br /> <br /> Is anyone else a bit off put that the CoF used to have Wolf as their Totem? That one Tribe got the animal they're all directly associated with?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519524#post1519524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, there's nothing there specifically about sex. It just attracts attention to them. So you walk into a crowded room and pop the gift and everyone will turn to look at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they had plenty of people working on this to know that it would be controversial, and the Gift works just fine as a mechanical replacement for Persuasion; which lets you avoid all the subtext about sex present in calling it Animal Magnetism.<br /> <br /> The phrase &quot;animal magnetism,&quot; was specifically coined to describe the force driving living creatures to pair up and mate, and then how that force could be manipulate to mind-control people into doing stuff against their will by tapping into such primal stuff. It was never a non-sex thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:00:53-07:00","id":1519529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519527#post1519527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Totems got flattened and simplified in general. All the tribes are defined by a singular patron now. They needed one totem for them, so they settled on Bat. Just like they rather heavy handedly settled the GW on Spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be another WtF-ism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:03:34-07:00","id":1519530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519528#post1519528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, since screw the edit demons:<br /> Is anyone else a bit off put that the CoF used to have Wolf as their Totem? That one Tribe got the animal they're all directly associated with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me. I always liked the fact that Wolf was a mysterious totem that was avoiding the Garou for some reason. Having the Patron of all Werewolves favour the Cult seems like a very problematic message.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:05:33-07:00","id":1519531,"title":"","content":"To be fair though, it avoids another WtF-ism, the idea of a Father Wolf. Still\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:14:50-07:00","id":1519533,"title":"","content":"Still reeling that, with the powers of complete retcon and a change of glyph... you still make the Fenrir the antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:26:57-07:00","id":1519534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519529#post1519529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be another WtF-ism.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it a WtF-ism?<br /> <br /> In WtF, the 8 Tribal Totems (5 PC, 3 NPC) are all different wolf-spirits. They're not &quot;flattened&quot; or &quot;simplified&quot; as each of them is their own unique spirit with their own associations, agendas, and so on... there's a reason the 9th seems to be destroyed, and there's 5 vs 3 of them on different sides of a major issue.<br /> <br /> What WtF did, was reinforce the idea that animist werewolves are primarily tied to wolf spirits. Connections to other spirits comes after Wolf, because Wolf is what's in their spiritual nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T17:30:33-07:00","id":1519535,"title":"","content":"It's the \u201ceach Tribe has a single Totem\u201d angle that's a WtF-ism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:01:47-07:00","id":1519543,"title":"","content":"Gee that first paragraph of the Cult of Wolf ( Fenris makes zero sense here....about as much as keeping Fianna did) is doing a lot of work. The Camp was loud and then they took over the Tribe cos they did, then they were stronger as strong as all the other Tribes put together cos they were. Then they did stuff, the stuff they did is basically the stuff Garou are supposed to do but we're gonna add the words pure and impurity in as often as possible even though it doesn't actually have any real bearing on them except as an artifact of earlier development phases when the CoF were the SoH.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:08:26-07:00","id":1519544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BSD v Fenrir redemption angle sounds absolutely bonkers. I'm okay with the idea of trying to and being able to redeem some BSD but the contrast in possibilities there feels forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing it most puts me in mind of, weirdly but I can explain, are those times when fans over in Chronicles-land* start instituting fan material to block off one splat's ability to interact with another splat in some particular way-things like where everyone was rushing to make a archmage-alike with no real ideas beyond denying archmages the ability to change anything about them, or when people started coming up with reasons why a Beast couldn't establish Kinship with a character type, are particular examples that come to mind.<br /> <br /> The reason it comes to mind is that both feel similarly rooted in the idea that permitting the thing in question violates the player's safe sense of ownership and participation with a splat and the game associated with it-which, okay, fair enough, people are allowed to play a game to the extent they are comfortable playing in it-but take the sense of oncoming injury too far and basically try to systemically stall anyone from having the gameplay be possible at all, relying on a sort of word of god and mechanical inherency to forbid it rather than rely on their social network to cater the game in a way that is appreciable for the players. These efforts tend to ultimately just harm the setting and it's cohesion on the whole.<br /> <br /> Of course, the major difference is that this <i>is</i> a actual RAW instituted insecurity, that I kind of honestly find insulting of the player base and would be more upset by if I had any investment in W5 (or World 5E in general). Like, yes, Paradox, I get why you're gunshy about this, but this is not maturity in game development. A sidebar exhorting maturity and sensitivity on the subject would have been. I've got the big girl panties to handle the danger and allure of ethnonationalism and fascism as themes, and I have the responsibility to tailor my game for myself and other players as people want to. I'm not sure why you don't.**<br /> <br /> That said, I think I have to echo the sentiment that I do find most bothersome about this that I had a few months, which comes down to this sentiment:<br /> <br /> Why does a professional product feel like a fanmade product? Why are the most short-sighted works of fans the thing that comes to mind when I stretch to find something like this?<br /> <br /> That is not something I should feel like reading a corebook for a very prominent gameline, even in the context of just the moment.<br /> <br /> *because this is where I have the most experience with these things, not because of anything about Chronicles intrinsically/extrinsically.<br /> **If I wanted to be really negative, I could easily point out that they <i>did</i> spend a lot of time courting edgelords who would be appealed to this sort of shit, and there is a way that just hardlocking these facets of the Get behind the &quot;darkest element of the morality of this game&quot; can <i>actually</i> work as a way of appealing to that fanbase while pretending they aren't, but I would have to be five times more cynical than I am to seriously suggest it. I mostly bring it up to assert now that of the myriad of possible reasons for doing it this way, I actually <i>don't</i> think that this is the mistake they're making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:15:46-07:00","id":1519547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519526#post1519526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whippoorwill didn't make a lick of sense for the BSDs (they're a North American only group within the nightjars), and the whole &quot;goatsucker&quot; myth doesn't have much resonance these days (but at least nightjars had some association with something negative). But surely they could have picked something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shrike is still my go-to replacement for WPW, actually found in Scotland, actually does something horrific that fits the BSDs and keeps the bird-song theme.<br /> <br /> Bat just being outright evil with Fly is short-sighted. If pentex NEEDED a totem, there were options that didn't put poor Fly in a bad light. Liger or any sort of purely man-made chemical would have served better.<br /> <br /> Reading through Cult of Fenris info in addition to Haglust, the condition doesn't have the nuance of Harano. Harano is a depression about feeling powerless in the face of such immense odds. Haglust is &quot;I will take action NOW and I KNOW I'm right&quot;, which doesn't read as a mental disorder. It reads as a really out of place snipe against previous edition garou for wanting to take action and that they often felt they were justified. Given the way frenzy and Rage Dice work, with Red Talons and Silver Fangs nearly unchanged, it reads more as a justification why you cannot play Fenrir than anything that might affect other garou.<br /> <br /> On the positive side, Skin Dancers are now called Stolen Moons and aren't JUST created through skinning garou but with deals to dark spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:27:42-07:00","id":1519552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519547#post1519547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the positive side, Skin Dancers are now called Stolen Moons and aren't JUST created through skinning garou but with deals to dark spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolen Moons seem to be more like really focused Sorcerers or in other cases Mockeries rather than actual Skin Dancers.....they're not exactly heavy hitters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T19:31:42-07:00","id":1519553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519552#post1519552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stolen Moons seem to be more like really focused Sorcerers or in other cases Mockeries rather than actual Skin Dancers.....they're not exactly heavy hitters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that fits, since the more sorcerous werewolves wouldn't be heavy hitters like the garou. From Cyber Record's site, Stolen Moons seems to have been a JS suggestion,too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T21:20:26-07:00","id":1519559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519544#post1519544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I think I have to echo the sentiment that I do find most bothersome about this that I had a few months, which comes down to this sentiment:<br /> <br /> Why does a professional product feel like a fanmade product? Why are the most short-sighted works of fans the thing that comes to mind when I stretch to find something like this?<br /> <br /> That is not something I should feel like reading a corebook for a very prominent gameline, even in the context of just the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not read W5 but the previews I've seen along with everything I've heard about the SI book, V5 Sabbat and H5, have likewise indicated the same to me about the recent 5E products. Frankly with the STV it's made that even worse because there's plenty of STV books I've read or heard about that are very well done and some that are professionally done as any official product and are far better value than recent official products. Which is frankly a bad look for Paradox and Renegade. I should not be thinking that I can't wait to see what fixes the STV comes out with before I actually consider buying the official book. This should not be the TTRPG version of a Bethesda game where I need fan patches to fix lingering bugs that the devs couldn't bothered to fix after years of these issues being known. Especially since unlike Bethesda games, Renegade does not seem to believe in having the occasional sale on their products. At least they don't on DriveThruRPG and frankly if they want me to buy their products on their website, maybe they should start working on improving their products first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T22:49:10-07:00","id":1519560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519535#post1519535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the \u201ceach Tribe has a single Totem\u201d angle that's a WtF-ism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? Every Garou Trbie in WtA has always just had a single Totem. Some Garou might join Camps or similar organizations like Silver Fang Houses that have their own Totems... but that's just like Lodges in WtF. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519547#post1519547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shrike is still my go-to replacement for WPW, actually found in Scotland, actually does something horrific that fits the BSDs and keeps the bird-song theme.<br /> ...<br /> On the positive side, Skin Dancers are now called Stolen Moons and aren't JUST created through skinning garou but with deals to dark spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly do we get rebooted Skin Dancers if kinfolk aren't really a &quot;thing&quot; like they used to be? Are the Stolen Moons more like a particularly nasty group of hunters? Could Minotaur be moved over to be the new BSD Patron if the Stolen Moons changed enough that a spirit of their own isn't really on the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T23:02:55-07:00","id":1519561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519547#post1519547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> with Red Talons and Silver Fangs nearly unchanged, it reads more as a justification why you cannot play Fenrir than anything that might affect other garou.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair red talons are either radically differant or just plain weird depending what you di with them in w5 since lupus may as well not exist and touchstones mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-03-2023, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T23:09:31-07:00","id":1519562,"title":"","content":"Hmm they balanced the triat in strange way in my opinion. BSD may be some legend, and their arrival is something shocking and unexpectted - like Corelli brothers in one of stories from 2ed. They are strange, but I see it as advantage.<br /> Cult of Fenris - the story behind it is typical for the tribe - we are the strongest, but this time they was a stalemante in duel - what I mii is the names. Official characters that Werewolf was full of. And who is elder Jonas? Albrecht? Or just a teasing name. Now I wish that they will quickly release some more things making the game more specific - for example Rage across New York, or Tribebooks? Book of ....? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T00:06:39-07:00","id":1519566,"title":"","content":"My initial W5 thoughts are: &quot;We really really really really hate biological determinism&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12752-mist-walker","name":"Mist-Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T00:36:30-07:00","id":1519567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mist-Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519566#post1519566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial W5 thoughts are: &quot;We really really really really hate biological determinism&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe having them design werewolf wasn't a good move since you're not human and never were so that concept is completely redundant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T00:39:43-07:00","id":1519568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519560#post1519560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly do we get rebooted Skin Dancers if kinfolk aren't really a &quot;thing&quot; like they used to be? Are the Stolen Moons more like a particularly nasty group of hunters? Could Minotaur be moved over to be the new BSD Patron if the Stolen Moons changed enough that a spirit of their own isn't really on the table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much just humans seeking to become werewolves by wearing their skins or making deals with dark spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519561#post1519561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair red talons are either radically differant or just plain weird depending what you di with them in w5 since lupus may as well not exist and touchstones mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the sad part is that the difference is that they now openly eat humans and spread disease among them OR they are preppers and bounty hunters. But the tribal text is basically a more edgy version of your usual Talon spiel, except they now see the Weaver as the biggest threat and the Wyrm as the victim and so its tools could be used.<br /> <br /> So they are doing stuff WORSE than the Fenrir and yet Talons are playable still.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb