iv> </div> </div> </div>Waffling around and pressing brakes on any true fighting the apocalypse. See the side bar Changing Ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:20:16-07:00","id":1519581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519575#post1519575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"434\" height=\"555\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Well holy macaroni, p.38 of W5 has some INTERESTING takes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> soooooo historical trauma is &quot;passed foward through DNA&quot; but all exemples given are about culture and language lost due to social conditioning.<br /> <br /> I have many way to describe that kind of stupidity, but the least of them would probably push the mods to ban me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:20:25-07:00","id":1519582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519579#post1519579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, they really could save quite a bit of word-count in this book if they toned down the constant &quot;Who knows what's actually going on? Some say this, others say this... but eventually, something happened - which nobody's sure about why or how it happened..&quot;. The approach to &quot;lore&quot; in this book feels way too invested in waffling around...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual dura- tion is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the histo- ry. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossi- ble, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I hate this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:26:43-07:00","id":1519583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519580#post1519580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Waffling around and pressing brakes on any true fighting the apocalypse. See the side bar Changing Ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the flip-flopping between &quot;This is the age of Apocalypse, the world is doomed.&quot; and &quot;Garou have to fight against the dying light to <i>avert </i>the Apocalypse!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Way too often the answer to defining elements in the setting and its history ends up having the undertone of &quot;Maybe, maybe not... who knows...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:28:24-07:00","id":1519584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519579#post1519579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, they really could save quite a bit of word-count in this book if they toned down the constant &quot;Who knows what's actually going on? Some say this, others say this... but eventually, something happened - which nobody's sure about why or how it happened..&quot;. The approach to &quot;lore&quot; in this book feels way too invested in waffling around...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They seems to be using the same old &quot;I have little thing to actually say, but I have a required number of world, so I will write empty texts to fill it&quot; as student making a redaction for school.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I didn't know otherwise, all this would make me seriously think that becoming a ttrpg writer is a job requiring no skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T02:31:15-07:00","id":1519585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519583#post1519583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the flip-flopping between &quot;This is the age of Apocalypse, the world is doomed.&quot; and &quot;Garou have to fight against the dying light to <i>avert </i>the Apocalypse!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Way too often the answer to defining elements in the setting and its history ends up having the undertone of &quot;Maybe, maybe not... who knows...&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can almost feel the inner conflict with the two contradictory desired themes of W5<br /> -the game is about activism against climate change!<br /> -but..but...but, we need to have it be about street level and local issues!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:26:21-07:00","id":1519588,"title":"","content":"The beginning of the Silent Strider section is also a good example of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Among wolves, Garou follow where prey leads the pack, and among humans, Garou have historically been found in cultures that are either migratory or diasporic. Deep in their own history, the Silent Striders were themselves\u2026 cursed? by a powerful spirit, malignant and not wholly understood, and as a result they often find sympathetic peoples and familiar practices among ever-moving or dispersed cultures.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This and other such sections... They read less like you're getting stories from a mythical age and more like there's a person who skim-read the W20 corebook a week ago and is now trying to explain the lore to another person from what he can vaguely recall.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought a bit on pg 41 perfectly summarized this book's take on its lore: &quot;No one knows. Everyone has an idea.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:26:43-07:00","id":1519589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519584#post1519584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> They seems to be using the same old &quot;I have little thing to actually say, but I have a required number of world, so I will write empty texts to fill it&quot; as student making a redaction for school.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I didn't know otherwise, all this would make me seriously think that becoming a ttrpg writer is a job requiring no skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious solution would have been to do more stuff, flesh out tribes, go into certain subjects deeper. For example write a time line of garou history with lots if historical events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:28:55-07:00","id":1519590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519588#post1519588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beginning of the Silent Strider section is also a good example of this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This and other such sections... They read less like you're getting stories from a mythical age and more like there's a person who skim-read the W20 corebook a week ago and is now trying to explain the lore to another person from what he can vaguely recall.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought a bit on pg 41 perfectly summarized this book's take on its lore: &quot;No one knows. Everyone has an idea.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>the big problem with this mindset is it makes hard to build setting coherence. I can jump in a w20 game and immediately know why silent striders hate vampires for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T03:34:34-07:00","id":1519592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519590#post1519590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the big problem with this mindset is it makes hard to build setting coherence. I can jump in a w20 game and immediately know why silent striders hate vampires for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even with less specific settings like CofD-games... I never had that sensation reading about the Nameless Empire in MtC 2E edition or Pangaea (and the whole deal with Father Wolf) in WtF 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:25:25-07:00","id":1519599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519588#post1519588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beginning of the Silent Strider section is also a good example of this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This and other such sections... They read less like you're getting stories from a mythical age and more like there's a person who skim-read the W20 corebook a week ago and is now trying to explain the lore to another person from what he can vaguely recall.<br /> <br /> Also, I thought a bit on pg 41 perfectly summarized this book's take on its lore: &quot;No one knows. Everyone has an idea.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> also, it's extremely ill worded. The way the paragraph is written, it can be understood the curse of Set is to be sympathetic with culture on the move and dispersed.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Something that any competent editor would have noticed, and added something like &quot;cursed to ever wander, the silent striders have logically found kinship with ever moving or dispersed cultures&quot;.<br /> <br /> This book is wonderful, in a schadenfreude sort of way. So much amateurism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:30:59-07:00","id":1519600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519575#post1519575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"434\" height=\"555\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Well holy macaroni, p.38 of W5 has some INTERESTING takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This even make sense? Trauma that you take by DNA? If it were the Mokole I would understand, but as far as I know most people tend to have more contact with the culture they grew up in than their ancestors. Or this is some rule from the WOD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:52:38-07:00","id":1519605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519575#post1519575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"434\" height=\"555\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/zGFdV0R.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Well holy macaroni, p.38 of W5 has some INTERESTING takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've looked a bit into this... It's a complex topic, like here's an abstract from an article in an academic journal called <a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/epdf/10.1080/02791072.2003.10399988?needAccess=true\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The Historical Trauma Response Among Natives and Its Relationship with Substance Abuse: A Lakota Illustration&quot;</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historical trauma (HT) is cumulative emotional and psychological wounding over the lifespan and across generations, emanating from massive group trauma experiences; the historical trauma response (HTR) is the constellation of features in reaction to this trauma. The HTR often includes depression, self-destructive behavior, suicidal thoughts and gestures, anxiety, low self-esteem, anger, and difficulty recognizing and expressing emotions. It may include substance abuse, often an attempt to avoid painful feelings through self-medication. Historical unresolved grief is the associated affect that accompanies HTR; this grief may be considered fixated, impaired, delayed, and/or disenfranchised. This article will explain HT theory and the HTR, delineate the features of the HTR and its grounding in the literature, offer specific Native examples of HT and HTR, and will suggest ways to incorporate HT theory in treatment, research and evaluation. The article will conclude with implications for all massively traumatized populations. </div> </div> </div>So &quot;historical trauma&quot; is a thing but I haven't seen anybody tying it to DNA. I guess you could use it as an excuse that it's an in-character-perspective (and from a Silver Fang no less). But this is a real and serious subject, so just dedicating one page seems ill-advised - and on top of that trying to make a case of linking that to Garou... I can see with some of the theories in this book of how Kin are created that you could link those things. But yeah... This thing almost reads like it is making the case that the reason for why Native American Garou exist is &quot;historical trauma&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:52:47-07:00","id":1519606,"title":"","content":"I think its speaking figuratively. The way disenfranchised groups tend to have it worse even if the mechanism of oppression have been removed (ish).<br /> <br /> I do however note it doesn't actually draw a link with garou. Especially as garou tacictly arnt a cohesive identity in w5 and are only debatably disenfranchised.<br /> <br /> more 2.2 hons writting than doctorate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-03-2023, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:00:44-07:00","id":1519607,"title":"","content":"There are studies that show transgenerational effects of trauma via epigenetics. I heard a talk about this from a (now retired) psychology professor who did research in war regions, including research about child soldiers. I'm on my phone right now, but I'm sure you can find his studies on Google Scholar; his name is Thomas Elbert, he taught in Konstanz (Germany).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:09:33-07:00","id":1519610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519606#post1519606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its speaking figuratively. The way disenfranchised groups tend to have it worse even if the mechanism of oppression have been removed (ish).<br /> <br /> I do however note it doesn't actually draw a link with garou. Especially as garou tacictly arnt a cohesive identity in w5 and are only debatably disenfranchised.<br /> <br /> more 2.2 hons writting than doctorate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but there has to be a link... I know it's weird. The title says &quot;Historical Trauma and the connection of the Garou&quot; but aside from &quot;Similar to the Garou&quot; at the beginning that link is never explained. But then why bring it up then? What has the historical trauma of Native Americans got to do with the concept of Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:12:47-07:00","id":1519611,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the more I'm put off by the 'Litany is wrong and easily abused!' talk after the Litany is listed. Because it legit reads like only few tenets were thought about as bad and the rest just don't matter.<br /> <br /> Like, Don't eat humans, Respect those beneath ye, Don't kill each other during a spar, challenge leader outside wartime and such are not even mentioned. Instead the whole set of laws is treated as oppressive from the get-go.<br /> <br /> That and the sheer nihilism and finger pointing found in sections like The Real Problem With the Garou. This game is still named Apocalypse, but now it seems hellbent on guilt-tripping the PCs over it and giving little tools to actually fight back. Because if you DO want to fight back, you are as bad as the Cult of Fenris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:19:19-07:00","id":1519612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519607#post1519607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are studies that show transgenerational effects of trauma via epigenetics. I heard a talk about this from a (now retired) psychology professor who did research in war regions, including research about child soldiers. I'm on my phone right now, but I'm sure you can find his studies on Google Scholar; his name is Thomas Elbert, he taught in Konstanz (Germany).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> these effects though are bad health. Not a trauma you gain by being born, the way it is described is more an assassin's creed genetic memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:30:06-07:00","id":1519614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519611#post1519611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about it, the more I'm put off by the 'Litany is wrong and easily abused!' talk after the Litany is listed. Because it legit reads like only few tenets were thought about as bad and the rest just don't matter.<br /> <br /> Like, Don't eat humans, Respect those beneath ye, Don't kill each other during a spar, challenge leader outside wartime and such are not even mentioned. Instead the whole set of laws is treated as oppressive from the get-go.<br /> <br /> That and the sheer nihilism and finger pointing found in sections like The Real Problem With the Garou. This game is still named Apocalypse, but now it seems hellbent on guilt-tripping the PCs over it and giving little tools to actually fight back. Because if you DO want to fight back, you are as bad as the Cult of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the writer in that section acts like there's a secret clause in the Litany that says &quot;If you have power, abuse the Litany and use it against other Garou&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you actually played it like that, what would even be the point of having Philodox, Galliard and Ragabash in the game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:31:18-07:00","id":1519615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519612#post1519612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> these effects though are bad health. Not a trauma you gain by being born, the way it is described is more an assassin's creed genetic memory</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn't addressing the text itself, more the idea of genetics and trauma. Still, it's potentially not only bad health; on the symposium I participated, Elbert talked about transgenerational trauma fostering appetitive violence (basically, engaging in violence because it feels good).<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not my field of research, so I don't know the current state of research. Still, there are indicators that traumatic experiences can be transferred from one generation to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:45:11-07:00","id":1519617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519614#post1519614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the writer in that section acts like there's a secret clause in the Litany that says &quot;If you have power, abuse the Litany and use it against other Garou&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you actually played it like that, what would even be the point of having Philodox, Galliard and Ragabash in the game...</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that there is an auspice -dedicated- to handling Litany matters seems to be ignored. The philodox section even says they think through their actions, yet the Litany section doesn't consider that the Litany has its fair intrepenters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:47:13-07:00","id":1519618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519615#post1519615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I wasn't addressing the text itself, more the idea of genetics and trauma. Still, it's potentially not only bad health; on the symposium I participated, Elbert talked about transgenerational trauma fostering appetitive violence (basically, engaging in violence because it feels good).<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not my field of research, so I don't know the current state of research. Still, there are indicators that traumatic experiences can be transferred from one generation to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought most theories went with the fact that trauma is carried over generationally from the prior generation into formative experiences for the next generation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T06:05:40-07:00","id":1519622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519617#post1519617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that there is an auspice -dedicated- to handling Litany matters seems to be ignored. The philodox section even says they think through their actions, yet the Litany section doesn't consider that the Litany has its fair intrepenters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the line at one point: &quot;Living by an inflexible code that\u2019s actually flexible when someone powerful decides it should be has a dark side.\u200b&quot; Okay, so if the powerful older Garou are flexible because they want to abuse the Litany and the young Garou are flexible because they don't even like the Litany... who is the party living inflexibly by its code...? What group of Garou is that supposed to be? The way it's written it doesn't seem like there's anybody who's inflexible when it comes to the Litany (you either abuse it or you hate it). And how can you even call the Litany an &quot;inflexible code&quot; when only a couple lines later this writer adds: &quot;Those rules mean different things at different times to different werewolves\u200b...&quot; (and of course, the sentence finishes that this obviously means the Litany is getting abused).<br /> <br /> It's like the idea here is to say that the Litany is bad but the writer has no idea how to express that in terms of worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T06:39:03-07:00","id":1519625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519581#post1519581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> soooooo historical trauma is &quot;passed foward through DNA&quot; but all exemples given are about culture and language lost due to social conditioning.<br /> <br /> I have many way to describe that kind of stupidity, but the least of them would probably push the mods to ban me.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, inherited trauma is thought to be something that occurs through epigenetics at the DNA level, although social and psychological factors may also play a role. The BBC has a decent overview here: <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20190326-what-is-epigenetics\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.bbc.com/future/article/2...is-epigenetics</a><br /> <br /> Think of your genes like a bunch of switches. Real-life events can flip switches on and off to help you better adjust to your environment now, rather than requiring generations of adaptation. (This is overly simplistic, but it's just an analogy.)<br /> <br /> The basic theory is that major stressors and environmental harms can flip these switches and then when we have kids, they're born with some of the same switches already pre-flipped.<br /> <br /> HTR (historical trauma response) is an older, closely related theory, that assumes the effect is entirely psychosocial, rather than biological. Other theories include that it might be biological changes occurring as a result of stress in the womb. The counterargument is that things like a consistent increase in risk of brain haemorrhages or cancer can't be explained by behaviour alone.<br /> <br /> The problem with the writing here is that it doesn't explain or make clear the connection between the things it details and the DNA shifts. It also assumes a general fluency in these issues. Even just an extra line to explain how inherited trauma works would have helped. The problem may also be that it's written IC.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Personally, I would have added an OOC text box to add a bit more context than you'd get from a character writing to one of their peers. But then again, Netchurch never did that, so maybe the problem is bringing in complex IRL science and mixing it meekly with the urban fantasy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T06:46:32-07:00","id":1519626,"title":"","content":"On writing issues, it's full of things like this:<br /> <br /> 'Many Garou believe the Black Spiral to be hidden somewhere in the depths of the Umbra \u2014 probably a portion of it foully proximate to the Wyrm, or somehow in what amounts to its attention, if such a statement can be accurate. Other Garou believe the \u201cBlack Labyrinth\u201d to be a location in the physical world, or even a metaphorical location that moves throughout the physical world, to places where human defilement proves most satisfactory to the Wyrm\u2026 again, if it can be said that the Wyrm \u201cprefers\u201d things.'<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> All of which could be cut down to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Many Garou believe the Black Spiral is hidden deep in the Umbra, where the Wyrm's influence is strongest. Others believe the &quot;Black Labyrinth&quot; to be a place that touches upon the physical world in places of human defilement.'<br /> <br /> Or even just:<br /> <br /> 'The Black Spiral is hidden in the deepest Wyrm-tainted regions of the Umbra, but it spills up into the physical world in places of human defilement.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T06:48:44-07:00","id":1519627,"title":"","content":"Wanted to go back and add something, but rather than edit my post, I thought I'd just put it here:<br /> <br /> There is an argument for not cutting things to bone, but they're not adding texture. Their version doesn't fill me with strong images and colour. It just waffles on. At least with my last version, which is more concise, you get the info you need and you have more space to add in juicy tidbits.<br /> <br /> A good RPG writer can pack tonnes of plot ideas into just a couple of lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Fixed typo 08-03-2023, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T07:18:22-07:00","id":1519629,"title":"","content":"Lol Its like reading an essay from someone trying to ramp up the word counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"htt