hts?p=1519579#post1519579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, they really could save quite a bit of word-count in this book if they toned down the constant &quot;Who knows what's actually going on? Some say this, others say this... but eventually, something happened - which nobody's sure about why or how it happened..&quot;. The approach to &quot;lore&quot; in this book feels way too invested in waffling around...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, it's pulling a Genius: the Transgression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:08:42-07:00","id":1519655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519652#post1519652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which seems odd since Justin mentioned on Twitter he was attempting to get the book down to a certain page count.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure once the writers were told to keep everything mysterious they started adding versions of 'or is it' to the end of every sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519654#post1519654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh god, it's pulling a Genius: the Transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought there everything was true? Particularly the lizards, but everything else as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:26:34-07:00","id":1519657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519655#post1519655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there everything was true? Particularly the lizards, but everything else as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't excuse waffling on your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:56:35-07:00","id":1519661,"title":"","content":"Yep, just as I thought, Werewolf 5 is horrible. <br /> <br /> Now we just wait for the disaster that's going to be M5 (which I hope doesn't come out and Paradox sells off the rights of the franchise by then..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:19:05-07:00","id":1519662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519661#post1519661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, just as I thought, Werewolf 5 is horrible.<br /> <br /> Now we just wait for the disaster that's going to be M5 (which I hope doesn't come out and Paradox sells off the rights of the franchise by then..)</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote from tonights technocracy game-<br /> <br /> &quot;no way in hell are they gonna let us play these guys&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;plus were definitely not going to the moon or power armour&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:31:22-07:00","id":1519666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519662#post1519662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quote from tonights technocracy game-<br /> <br /> &quot;no way in hell are they gonna let us play these guys&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;plus were definitely not going to the moon or power armour&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, if Etherites can't build giant rocketships to go to mars and abduct some alien livestock there's something wrong with the writers of Etherite: the Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:55:33-07:00","id":1519668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519657#post1519657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't excuse waffling on your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when the setting is for W:tA, aka the game that didn't have anywhere near the &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; factor that any of the other games did, because everything about it was supposed to be 100% earnest and up-front. You can't really feel a terrible weight clutching you for your ancestral line having fucked up since the Impergium if you're not really sure that anything actually happened or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T15:19:48-07:00","id":1519670,"title":"","content":"The writing does really feel like my early rpg project writing before my editors tore me a new one. I'm laying this solidly at the editors feet, the writers are writing what they think they are being told to write. Not their fault the instructions are vague and borked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T17:51:26-07:00","id":1519684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519661#post1519661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now we just wait for the disaster that's going to be M5 (which I hope doesn't come out and Paradox sells off the rights of the franchise by then..)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that would be a true... Paradox backlash <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> or in other terms the game is too much full of inaccurate references to a gajillion of real world stuff and beliefs that it won't be allowed to exist. It's too paradoxical to exist<br /> <br /> They should do Wraith next, it's probably the less problematic from a real world perspective.<br /> It has very few direct cultural references and just of long dead civilization mostly.<br /> Plus in the idea of playing the monsters, the ghosts should have always been third<br /> <br /> MtAs is not going to happen unless it will just be another hard reboot, one more edtions war, and no one happy.<br /> And I don't see the point really.<br /> I mean the theme is more relevant today than ever, but probably no one cares","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T18:16:45-07:00","id":1519687,"title":"","content":"I agree. Paradox's goal is to bring the splats back down to street level, making nightly survival the focus, as well as make things darker and more oppressive. That's been Wraith's bag since the beginning. I honestly think Wraith would be pretty perfect for the direction Paradox wants to take things. Conversely I can't imagine them making a new edition of Mage that would be fun to play at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:21:59-07:00","id":1519695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519661#post1519661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, just as I thought, Werewolf 5 is horrible.<br /> <br /> Now we just wait for the disaster that's going to be M5 (which I hope doesn't come out and Paradox sells off the rights of the franchise by then..)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically (since mage is my favorite wod game), I want to see that disaster. I lost all attachment to the idea ov 5th edition after V5, now I'm just interested to see how unimaginative, incomptent and dishonest the writers will be with M5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 08-03-2023, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:25:54-07:00","id":1519696,"title":"","content":"Now for the important question: where are the Ratkin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23696-incisors-of-doom","name":"Incisors-of-Doom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:41:15-07:00","id":1519700,"title":"","content":"This is not at all a serious question, just one that I mull over while wondering if I made the right decision in preordering W5 before reading J.F. Sambrano's posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23696-incisors-of-doom","name":"Incisors-of-Doom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T22:48:00-07:00","id":1519707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incisors-of-Doom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519696#post1519696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for the important question: where are the Ratkin?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as anyone has heard, they were last seen being hinted to be like Beshilu from WtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T22:52:04-07:00","id":1519708,"title":"","content":"I think I realised one of the really depressing parts of the game; The packs have to choose their totems from those of the tribes and even then they have to placate the spirits not chosen lest they refuse to help. Any spirit outside the tribal ones requires a quest.<br /> <br /> I'm not certain if I'm correct, but does this imply that some packs just don't have an unifying totem and everyone follows their tribal ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T02:07:12-07:00","id":1519716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519708#post1519708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I realised one of the really depressing parts of the game; The packs have to choose their totems from those of the tribes and even then they have to placate the spirits not chosen lest they refuse to help. Any spirit outside the tribal ones requires a quest.<br /> <br /> I'm not certain if I'm correct, but does this imply that some packs just don't have an unifying totem and everyone follows their tribal ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the main-reason is that they couldn't figure out how to handle Favors/Bans for non-Tribe-Patron-Spirits. Of course, it's easy to see why: The Tribe-Favors/Bans are completely inconsistent. Honestly, if they had figured out that part first, introducing non-Tribe-Patron-Spirits for Packs wouldn't have been an issue. But with the way things are in this book, where would you even start in deciding what a non-Tribe-Patron-Spirit Favor/Ban-pairing looks like...? And when giving a Pack-non-Tribe-Patron-Spirit a Favor/Ban-pairing you would have to consider how the Ban would work in relationship with the Tribe-Ban. That could lead to problems as well.<br /> <br /> The best solution here would've been to go back to the drawing-board for how Favor/Ban-pairings work in order to accommodate this element in the setting but well... here we are...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T02:28:19-07:00","id":1519718,"title":"","content":"So friends pointed this sidebar out and I think it REALLY showcases what direction W5 is going;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"340\" height=\"372\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> This section reads like one of those &quot;I want the lore to be more vague/like lore in vampire!&quot; posts. I'm not against things being unclear, but a massive part of WtA is that the struggle IS real and IS a massive part of the horror. WtA doesn't work with its core truths vague.<br /> <br /> Now, the horror is clearly no longer pollution or systematic issues. It is other werewolves and the garou nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T02:35:50-07:00","id":1519719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519687#post1519687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Paradox's goal is to bring the splats back down to street level, making nightly survival the focus, as well as make things darker and more oppressive. That's been Wraith's bag since the beginning. I honestly think Wraith would be pretty perfect for the direction Paradox wants to take things. Conversely I can't imagine them making a new edition of Mage that would be fun to play at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll just flatten out the cultural stuff and go back to the early Revised feeling of broken world, street magic and small wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:03:57-07:00","id":1519722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519718#post1519718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So friends pointed this sidebar out and I think it REALLY showcases what direction W5 is going;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"340\" height=\"372\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> This section reads like one of those &quot;I want the lore to be more vague/like lore in vampire!&quot; posts. I'm not against things being unclear, but a massive part of WtA is that the struggle IS real and IS a massive part of the horror. WtA doesn't work with its core truths vague.<br /> <br /> Now, the horror is clearly no longer pollution or systematic issues. It is other werewolves and the garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Werewolves are charged with an unreliable greater purpose by Gaia, a spiritual entity who is herself inherently unknowable&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Heavy sight*<br /> <br /> Do they even think about the words they use?<br /> <br /> How can a purpose be &quot;unreliable&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's not a model, it's not a person or a system. Hence it cannot be either reliable or unreliable. It's.Just.A.Goal!<br /> <br /> And Gaia is now &quot;inherently&quot; unkowable? So nothing can ever be know about her? Who's to say she's not the wyrm then? How can you know destroying the world isn't something she wants? You can't for now she's unknowable by nature.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:17:17-07:00","id":1519724,"title":"","content":"As much as I'm a fan of <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> and its \u201cthe ultimate truth of the setting is unknowable\u201d angle (read: <i>extremely</i> hard to pin down), this is <b>Werewolf</b>, not <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:42:26-07:00","id":1519726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519718#post1519718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So friends pointed this sidebar out and I think it REALLY showcases what direction W5 is going;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"340\" height=\"372\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qOYRz0t.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> This section reads like one of those &quot;I want the lore to be more vague/like lore in vampire!&quot; posts. I'm not against things being unclear, but a massive part of WtA is that the struggle IS real and IS a massive part of the horror. WtA doesn't work with its core truths vague.<br /> <br /> Now, the horror is clearly no longer pollution or systematic issues. It is other werewolves and the garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It ties for the worst piece in the book with the &quot;History of the Garou nation&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:55:59-07:00","id":1519727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519625#post1519625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, inherited trauma is thought to be something that occurs through epigenetics at the DNA level, although social and psychological factors may also play a role. The BBC has a decent overview here: <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20190326-what-is-epigenetics\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.bbc.com/future/article/2...is-epigenetics</a><br /> <br /> Think of your genes like a bunch of switches. Real-life events can flip switches on and off to help you better adjust to your environment now, rather than requiring generations of adaptation. (This is overly simplistic, but it's just an analogy.)<br /> <br /> The basic theory is that major stressors and environmental harms can flip these switches and then when we have kids, they're born with some of the same switches already pre-flipped.<br /> <br /> HTR (historical trauma response) is an older, closely related theory, that assumes the effect is entirely psychosocial, rather than biological. Other theories include that it might be biological changes occurring as a result of stress in the womb. The counterargument is that things like a consistent increase in risk of brain haemorrhages or cancer can't be explained by behaviour alone.<br /> <br /> The problem with the writing here is that it doesn't explain or make clear the connection between the things it details and the DNA shifts. It also assumes a general fluency in these issues. Even just an extra line to explain how inherited trauma works would have helped. The problem may also be that it's written IC.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would have added an OOC text box to add a bit more context than you'd get from a character writing to one of their peers. But then again, Netchurch never did that, so maybe the problem is bringing in complex IRL science and mixing it meekly with the urban fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Thank you for mentioning that. Wouldn\u2019t have expected science to have already come this far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519687#post1519687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Paradox's goal is to bring the splats back down to street level, making nightly survival the focus, as well as make things darker and more oppressive. That's been Wraith's bag since the beginning. I honestly think Wraith would be pretty perfect for the direction Paradox wants to take things. Conversely I can't imagine them making a new edition of Mage that would be fun to play at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Justin Achilli was concerned, for him Mage is about self-determination (Traditions) versus authoritarianism (Technocracy).<br /> <br /> But JA left, so who knows\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incisors-of-Doom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519696#post1519696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for the important question: where are the Ratkin?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're around but the section on what used to be the Fera is another hallmark of this book\u2019s aversion to lore:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou suppose the existence of others similar to themselves \u2014 if not in outlook, then in the ability to assume the mantle of beast and human. Are they allies? Enemies? Reluctant siblings in Gaia? None can say, exactly, and conjecture almost certainly varies day to day. [\u2026]<br /> What Do They Want: The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend. Indeed, many of these other shifters seem to resent the Garou, for the werewolves find themselves anyplace where humans exist, and they may often find themselves at odds with these other shapeshifters over territory, spiritual purpose, or the fates of the humans or beasts around them. </div> </div> </div>I find it a bit funny that this suggests that the War of Rage happened in this setting and actually <i>everybody except the Garou remembers that history</i>. This book funnily ends up portraying Garou as a bunch of amnesiacs.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519718#post1519718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So friends pointed this sidebar out and I think it REALLY showcases what direction W5 is going;<br /> <br /> This section reads like one of those &quot;I want the lore to be more vague/like lore in vampire!&quot; posts. I'm not against things being unclear, but a massive part of WtA is that the struggle IS real and IS a massive part of the horror. WtA doesn't work with its core truths vague.<br /> <br /> Now, the horror is clearly no longer pollution or systematic issues. It is other werewolves and the garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vagueness doesn\u2019t quite work as the writing often ends up just waffling around instead of making the world/lore more mysterious. And then there\u2019s of course this current of nihilistic dismissiveness that runs through the book where the purpose of the Garou is constantly questioned and sometimes there are rhetorical questions about whether the Garou are even capable of making things better (like in the \u201cChanging Ways\u201d sidebar).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T04:28:29-07:00","id":1519728,"title":"","content":"Werewolves being feared and mistrusted by each of the worlds they belong to is a very Forsaken approach. In WTA spirits accept the Garou for the role they have been appointed to and adhere to ancient pacts made between them and the Fera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T04:34:26-07:00","id":1519729,"title":"","content":"Judging it on its own merits rather than in terms of its predesors.....<br /> <br /> It isn't actually very newbie friendly in terms of both presentation, mechanics and lore. Mechanics are quite deep and punitive, the setting is way too vaguely written and their were chunks which I found very hard to read and I was falling back on familiarity with the older product and academic reading.<br /> <br /> Its ultimately way too simular a gaming experience to v5, if youve bought v5 w5 is a waste of money unless you're really invested in v5 but with werewolves.<br /> <br /> Their still using the clunky 5th ed combat system. This I very bad in a game with a strong emphasis on combat. This should have been the first thing to go.<br /> <br /> The tribes are bland and vaguely written. Their should be around 5-7 tops this would allow you to better define them while avoiding building a culture.<br /> <br /> Urban horror games are dime a dozen these days and so has nothing to offer. Either play forsaken or apocalypse revised if you're determined to wod werewolf play just stick to v5 if you like this style of play or go shopping for urban horror/fantasy games otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T04:50:58-07:00","id":1519730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519729#post1519729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judging it on its own merits rather than in terms of its predesors.....<br /> <br /> It isn't actually very newbie friendly in terms of both presentation, mechanics and lore. Mechanics are quite deep and punitive, the setting is way too vaguely written and their were chunks which I found very hard to read and I was falling back on familiarity with the older product and academic reading.<br /> <br /> Its ultimately way too simular a gaming experience to v5, if youve bought v5 w5 is a waste of money unless you're really invested in v5 but with werewolves.<br /> <br /> Their still using the clunky 5th ed combat system. This I very bad in a game with a strong emphasis on combat. This should have been the first thing to go.<br /> <br /> The tribes are bland and vaguely written. Their should be around 5-7 tops this would allow you to better define them while avoiding building a culture.<br /> <br /> Urban horror games are dime a dozen these days and so has nothing to offer. Either play forsaken or apocalypse revised if you're determined to wod werewolf play just stick to v5 if you like this style of play or go shopping for urban horror/fantasy games otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The punitive nature of the mechanics is really an issue. I was thinking like, for example, you as ST create a scenario where a PC confronts some Formori bad guy and said bad guy reveals that he has kidnapped a Touchstone of that PC... The amount of tests and negative mechanics an ST can throw at the PC through the pure existence of that scenario is staggering: Harano, Frenzy, Chagrin, possible Tribe-Ban-trigger, Hauglosk (depending on the Chronicle-Tenets), WP-damage through a social contest, Rage-increase (and if it gets beyond 5 even more WP-damage)... There's just <i>so much</i> an ST could throw at a PC by simply setting up a scene in a certain way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T05:01:17-07:00","id":1519732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519727#post1519727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As far as Justin Achilli was concerned, for him Mage is about self-determination (Traditions) versus authoritarianism (Technocracy).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm genuinely shocked, could it be tht I agree with Achilli for the first time in decades?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519727#post1519727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s of course this current of nihilistic dismissiveness that runs through the book where the purpose of the Garou is constantly questioned and sometimes there are rhetorical questions about whether the Garou are even capable of making things better (like in the \u201cChanging Ways\u201d sidebar).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which put to the lie every attempt to market it as a game about climate activism. &quot;The world is bad, but we won't ever be able to change it for the better&quot; is not the best rallying call.<br /> <br /> It's also incredibly stupid of them to do that. When your game is about supernatural creatures living amongs well known humanity, you can present their weaknesses, but you don't present them as weak.<br /> <br /> At this stage, if we were to resume the creatures of the wod as presented in 5th edition:<br /> <br /> -V5: vampires are all boulimic(nearly always at least 1 hunger)with little to no impulse control(messy criticals) and suffering from heavy emotional disorders (clan compulsion)<br /> <br /> -H5: hunters are people with a schrodinger conviction that magically disappear once they join a group that cannot be contained in a cave<br /> <br /> And now W5: werewolves are now amnesiac with chronic depression.<br /> <br /> I Mean, not remembering basic history, constantly wondering what they are doing and why, never being sure about anything. Are we talking about garou or people suffering from alzheimer?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T05:05:05-07:00","id":1519733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519730#post1519730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The punitive nature of the mechanics is really an issue. I was thinking like, for example, you as ST create a scenario where a PC confronts some Formori bad guy and said bad guy reveals that he has kidnapped a Touchstone of that PC... The amount of tests and negative mechanics an ST can throw at the PC through the pure existence of that scenario is staggering: Harano, Frenzy, Chagrin, possible Tribe-Ban-trigger, Hauglosk (depending on the Chronicle-Tenets), WP-damage through a social contest, Rage-increase (and if it gets beyond 5 even more WP-damage)... There's just <i>so much</i> an ST could throw at a PC by simply setting up a scene in a certain way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if your ideal to play werewolf is to replicate movie werewolves, getting hit with all of those and then closing your shit WOULD fit... Buuut is it fun to play? Someone run this scenario through a dice roller, stat!<br /> <br /> Also, the more I read about Hauglosk, the more it just reads as the ST snapping the offending player's fingers at Doing it Rong. This, given one of the hallmarks of WtA was that there was no right way to garou, is really ironic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T05:15:59-07:00","id":1519734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519733#post1519733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if your ideal to play werewolf is to replicate movie werewolves, getting hit with all of those and then closing your shit WOULD fit... Buuut is it fun to play? Someone run this scenario through a dice roller, stat!<br /> <br /> Also, the more I read about Hauglosk, the more it just reads as the ST snapping the offending player's fingers at Doing it Rong. This, given one of the hallmarks of WtA was that there was no right way to garou, is really ironic.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very serious problem that I haven't seen addressed anywhere in the book is these situational triggers apparently don't make an exception for actions you take under the influence of a Brutal Outcome on a non-violent roll or Frenzy. And of course, there's the line in the Frenzy mechanics about how the ST should take over playing your character if you don't roleplay Frenzy &quot;the right way&quot;...<br /> <br /> Yeah, like the real doom-scenario is the bad guy has kidnapped the PC's Touchstone but the Touchstone is also in the room with the bad guy and the PC. Because then if the Frenzy is triggered and you fail the second Frenzy check as well then you will attack your Touchstone which is another wave of bad mechanics you can throw at the player and if the PC kills their Touchstone you get an automatic raise on either Harano or Hauglosk out of that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T05:54:58-07:00","id":1519736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519727#post1519727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Thank you for mentioning that. Wouldn\u2019t have expected science to have already come this far.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I think it's still largely theoretical, and only partially proven, but then, so is a lot of stuff we take for granted as being &quot;true&quot; (because it's often the best explanation we have so far).<br /> <br /> I think inherited trauma could absolutely be relevant for a game like WTA, given many of its themes. But the problem is that they've kinda shoehorned in an academic essay without context or a precis. Which means it's ripe for misunderstandings and, unfortunately, ridicule, which then undermines the point you want to make.<br /> <br /> It reads to me like this is a statement someone wanted to make on inherited trauma, but rather than include it in the ST chapter, where it would need introducing and some expectation-setting, they thought they could get away with sticking it in as IC flavour text and then not having to deal with it beyond that.<br /> <br /> Which is sorta like the Paradox approach in a nutshell. Try to do something progressive but half-arse it, or not really understand what you're trying to do or why, and so it ends up coming across as cynical, tone-deaf or out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T06:03:15-07:00","id":1519737,"title":"","content":"Not to take away from the serious conversation, but does anyone still have ANY idea wtf the Shadow Lord glyph is meant to be??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T06:27:21-07:00","id":1519739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519737#post1519737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to take away from the serious conversation, but does anyone still have ANY idea wtf the Shadow Lord glyph is meant to be??</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that it's a dagger/klaive piercing skin, implying a stab in the back. But in general the new glyphs lose me. I love the visual language of the old Glyphs and how you can easily turn them into somethign of your own through the vocabulary we have been informed about. I think it was even designed originally by Rich?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:08:28-07:00","id":1519750,"title":"","content":"Aaaand, once you think KM has dropped the matter;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"599\" height=\"201\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> P.322.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:29:29-07:00","id":1519752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519750#post1519750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaand, once you think KM has dropped the matter;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"599\" height=\"201\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> P.322.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even what follows after that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These situations create opportunities to grapple with fascism with more nuance than as simple enemies. How do you bring back a friend who has gone over to a hateful ideology? How do you avoid succumbing to bitterness and desperation, and the simple answers provided by a charismatic demagogue?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what does happen with characters who hit Hauglosk 5...? Let me refresh my memory... oh right, they're turned into NPCs. And let me look up the Rite to bring people back from Hauglosk... oh right, there isn't one.<br /> <br /> This game doesn't cover the topic and idea of bringing Garou back from succumbing to Hauglosk.<br /> <br /> The only way to avert succumbing to Hauglosk is the Touchstone-healing-ability and that's limited to both Harano and Hauglosk as an once-per-story-ability. It would be interesting if the Harano and Hauglosk trackers had more ways to be reduced but they don't. This idea of playing an eco-fascist who flirts with Hauglosk is more a recipe for disaster. Especially since Hauglosk is tested when Chronicle Tenets are broken and assuming that the Chronicle Tenets aren't eco-fascist-friendly this means that said character will succumb to Hauglosk pretty quickly and become an NPC. The mechanics don't support what's suggested here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:39:28-07:00","id":1519753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519752#post1519752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way to avert succumbing to Hauglosk is the Touchstone-healing-ability and that's limited to both Harano and Hauglosk as an once-per-story-ability. It would be interesting if the Harano and Hauglosk trackers had more ways to be reduced but they don't. This idea of playing an eco-fascist who flirts with Hauglosk is more a recipe for disaster. Especially since Hauglosk is tested when Chronicle Tenets are broken and assuming that the Chronicle Tenets aren't eco-fascist-friendly this means that said character will succumb to Hauglosk pretty quickly and become an NPC. The mechanics don't support what's suggested here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, clearly the friend is an NPC, who wants to tell a story about a PC getting better?<br /> <br /> Though, I think the CoF loresheet IS that?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:46:54-07:00","id":1519755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519753#post1519753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, clearly the friend is an NPC, who wants to tell a story about a PC getting better?<br /> <br /> Though, I think the CoF loresheet IS that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's someone who turned back before it was too late for them. Not someone who was consumed by the ideology and Rage. I do wonder if this might work if they for instance had a single moment of clarity or something like that?<br /> <br /> <img width=\"325\" height=\"448\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9vfWngu.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9vfWngu.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9vfWngu.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> This is also a way to cure harano or Hauglosk, but it seems to be a legendary rarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T09:57:28-07:00","id":1519756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519753#post1519753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, clearly the friend is an NPC, who wants to tell a story about a PC getting better?<br /> <br /> Though, I think the CoF loresheet IS that?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's weird that they didn't turn something like &quot;The Renunciation of Fenris&quot; or something into an actual Rite with mechanics that allows you to sever the link between a Cult of Fenris member and their Patron Spirit. But with that Loresheet it's specifically about leaving the CoF. And Hauglosk is something every Garou can potentially succumb to so the Hauglosk/fascism-combo should go beyond just the CoF in theory.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger issue is that bringing fascism into a game demands more nuance than &quot;Do the players want to see fascism portrayed in the game? Yes or no?&quot;. There are a lot of sensitive topics attached to fascism. Even if the players say yes there should be more discussion going on to clarify what the ST thinks &quot;portraying fascism&quot; means and seeing where the boundaries for players are exactly on that topic. And if this book wants to enable that, it should've gone into way more detail in guiding STs to do just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:10:31-07:00","id":1519757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519750#post1519750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaand, once you think KM has dropped the matter;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"599\" height=\"201\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> P.322.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, its very much not dropped, the CoF is just the Swords by another name and the current scenario is one where the Cult/Swords are the entire of the Tribe which is what he always believed anyway.<br /> <br /> Hauglusk basically states that if ANY werewolf has a bad day often enough ( 5x) they become a facist....its kinda sad....your guaranteed end states are either violent death, Notsee or Depression so deep that you will never emerge in a functional state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:19:16-07:00","id":1519758,"title":"","content":"two things <br /> <br /> one, i absolutely love the idea of an anti-hanaro, especially considering its just as damaging as, or even more so than Hanaro.<br /> <br /> and a question. Does the release of W5 mean that there gonna stop making W20 stuff? Cause W5 is essentially a reboot like Werewolf the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:26:25-07:00","id":1519759,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen any mention of it but how were Black Furies treated? I'll admit that my expectations are very low due to the revealed opinions the developers had regarding indigenous and women's issues.<br /> <br /> I assume the tribe isn't all women any more because the developers decided that the issues feminism addresses have all been solved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:33:26-07:00","id":1519761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519759#post1519759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen any mention of it but how were Black Furies treated? I'll admit that my expectations are very low due to the revealed opinions the developers had regarding indigenous and women's issues.<br /> <br /> I assume the tribe isn't all women any more because the developers decided that the issues feminism addresses have all been solved?</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 Furies are all about injustice but the book really pushes that they are 'too radical' in how they fight against it and doesn't seem to understand how intersectionality works. So you could make something decent out of it but you'll meed to do the heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the example Furies are predominantly male.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 08-04-2023, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:35:47-07:00","id":1519762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519759#post1519759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen any mention of it but how were Black Furies treated? I'll admit that my expectations are very low due to the revealed opinions the developers had regarding indigenous and women's issues.<br /> <br /> I assume the tribe isn't all women any more because the developers decided that the issues feminism addresses have all been solved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm. Well...<br /> <br /> <img width=\"342\" height=\"526\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"345\" height=\"324\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:37:19-07:00","id":1519763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519759#post1519759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen any mention of it but how were Black Furies treated? I'll admit that my expectations are very low due to the revealed opinions the developers had regarding indigenous and women's issues.<br /> <br /> I assume the tribe isn't all women any more because the developers decided that the issues feminism addresses have all been solved?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what others think but Black Furies (like Red Talons) from how they are described sound to me like another candidate who I could see joining the cause of the CoF (because of how the Tribe is portrayed in their section).<br /> <br /> In W5 the Black Furies aren't an all-female Tribe anymore and are all about addressing injustice. And that's injustice in general. You could still picture feminists being part of this Tribe, for example. And all sorts of causes you could classify as injustice are mentioned. But the reason I talked about the CoF before is this bit in their section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, \u201cset things right\u201d often has a very different meaning for Garou than it does for humans, and not every Black Fury gives a fuck about fair wages if, in their opinion, fair wages equate to \u201ctoo many humans.\u201d Numerous Black Furies hold perspectives that might charitably be described as Darwinian.\u200b<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a role that requires vigilance and self-criticism. All too easily, empathy can turn to pity, and pity to disdain, and Black Furies who long ago took on noble causes can find themselves worn down by the constant need of those who have been marginalized. At the same time, righteousness can turn to hatred, and a Black Fury may have enemies for the sake of having enemies, even where none truly exist \u2014 a perilous risk when mixed with Garou politics and caern meetings.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:37:25-07:00","id":1519764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519758#post1519758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two things<br /> <br /> one, i absolutely love the idea of an anti-hanaro, especially considering its just as damaging as, or even more so than Hanaro.<br /> <br /> and a question. Does the release of W5 mean that there gonna stop making W20 stuff? Cause W5 is essentially a reboot like Werewolf the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the IDEA of an opposite state to Harano......not so much of a fan of it being essentially Dramatic Facism as written. Or that you lose your PC if it claims you.<br /> <br /> W20 was killed by Paradox and The Apocalyptic Record and the two associated books were the last W20 books that were allowed to be published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:42:30-07:00","id":1519765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519757#post1519757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, its very much not dropped, the CoF is just the Swords by another name and the current scenario is one where the Cult/Swords are the entire of the Tribe which is what he always believed anyway.<br /> <br /> Hauglusk basically states that if ANY werewolf has a bad day often enough ( 5x) they become a facist....its kinda sad....your guaranteed end states are either violent death, Notsee or Depression so deep that you will never emerge in a functional state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but Hauglosk/CoF basically imply that deciding to take direct action and causing some harm is the same as being a fascist. You know, like riots, protesting pipelines, general antifa stuff. <i>Punching neo-nazi.</i> And these are just things humans do, never mind stuff garou can do like destroying the spirit of pollution in a factory which causes it to crumble in the real world.<br /> <br /> Plus, since tribes are no longer tied to cultures, how can the CoF be ecofascists? Unless they are the only tribe that is solely white?<br /> <br /> The way this game punishes wanting to do more than just small-scale stuff is really tiring. ESPECIALLY since Red Talons and Black Furies are still stated to take drastic actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:46:21-07:00","id":1519766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519764#post1519764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the IDEA of an opposite state to Harano......not so much of a fan of it being essentially Dramatic Facism as written. Or that you lose your PC if it claims you.<br /> <br /> W20 was killed by Paradox and The Apocalyptic Record and the two associated books were the last W20 books that were allowed to be published.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'd love that. But it would have to act like an actual mental illness like Harano does and not &quot;You want to Eat the Rich and you are not Red Talon/Black Fury.&quot; Stuff like Ratkin's Wyld euphoria would be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T10:53:48-07:00","id":1519767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519764#post1519764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the IDEA of an opposite state to Harano......not so much of a fan of it being essentially Dramatic Facism as written. Or that you lose your PC if it claims you.<br /> <br /> W20 was killed by Paradox and The Apocalyptic Record and the two associated books were the last W20 books that were allowed to be published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. Losing your PC when you get the anti-hanaro is not a good thing.<br /> <br /> well that sucks royal. at least fan stuff can still be made. Right?<br /> <br /> By which i mean homebrew pdfs like on storypath nexus/storyteller vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":". 08-04-2023, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:05:01-07:00","id":1519768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519765#post1519765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that, but Hauglosk/CoF basically imply that deciding to take direct action and causing some harm is the same as being a fascist. You know, like riots, protesting pipelines, general antifa stuff. <i>Punching neo-nazi.</i> And these are just things humans do, never mind stuff garou can do like destroying the spirit of pollution in a factory which causes it to crumble in the real world.<br /> <br /> Plus, since tribes are no longer tied to cultures, how can the CoF be ecofascists? Unless they are the only tribe that is solely white?<br /> <br /> The way this game punishes wanting to do more than just small-scale stuff is really tiring. ESPECIALLY since Red Talons and Black Furies are still stated to take drastic actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what the game is trying to get at is that section on pg 202 called &quot;The Real Problem With Garou&quot;. And it all boils down to saying &quot;What is required to save the world is for Garou to do stuff they can't, won't or find very hard to do.&quot;. And what's special about PC-Garou is that they're firmly situated in the third category of &quot;They have to try <i>very hard</i> to make a difference... maybe, just maybe they make a <i>tiny </i>bit of a difference...&quot;. All the other Garou are on the &quot;can't do it&quot; to &quot;won't do it&quot; spectrum when it comes to doing what's necessary to save the world.<br /> <br /> The challenge this game is focusing on is the idea that the tools/powers/issues Garou have are all there to illustrate how inadequate to the task of saving the world they are. And somehow PC-Garou are supposed to get past that and (maybe) make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:29:34-07:00","id":1519773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519768#post1519768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what the game is trying to get at is that section on pg 202 called &quot;The Real Problem With Garou&quot;. And it all boils down to saying &quot;What is required to save the world is for Garou to do stuff they can't, won't or find very hard to do.&quot;. And what's special about PC-Garou is that they're firmly situated in the third category of &quot;They have to try <i>very hard</i> to make a difference... maybe, just maybe they make a <i>tiny </i>bit of a difference...&quot;. All the other Garou are on the &quot;can't do it&quot; to &quot;won't do it&quot; spectrum when it comes to doing what's necessary to save the world.<br /> <br /> The challenge this game is focusing on is the idea that the tools/powers/issues Garou have are all there to illustrate how inadequate to the task of saving the world they are. And somehow PC-Garou are supposed to get past that and (maybe) make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> its an interesting contrast with revised which explored the garou nation doing what it suggested here and how that was the way forward with the implicit that it was doable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:41:18-07:00","id":1519775,"title":"","content":"To elaborate a bit more... I think a core-designing-principle in writing this book was to take every element and first ask questions like: &quot;How do the Garou fuck this up? How are Garou bad at this task? What counterproductive strategy/tactic is employed by the Garou?&quot;. The idea wasn't, for example, to say that direct action in battling climate-change is bad but instead to make the whole thing about explaining why Garou are bad at it, do the wrong thing or employ some counterproductive strategy or something. The point is always to show that Garou aren't up to the task and depending on the context in the book you get an explanation for how they fuck up.<br /> <br /> That's how you get sections like the Black Furies and Red Talons. You say they're about fighting injustice and protecting animals... but immediately what that followed up with is explaining how this Tribe fucked up, is counterproductive etc.<br /> <br /> And for whatever reason, this game asks you to be one of those guys...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:51:24-07:00","id":1519777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519768#post1519768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what the game is trying to get at is that section on pg 202 called &quot;The Real Problem With Garou&quot;. And it all boils down to saying &quot;What is required to save the world is for Garou to do stuff they can't, won't or find very hard to do.&quot;. And what's special about PC-Garou is that they're firmly situated in the third category of &quot;They have to try <i>very hard</i> to make a difference... maybe, just maybe they make a <i>tiny </i>bit of a difference...&quot;. All the other Garou are on the &quot;can't do it&quot; to &quot;won't do it&quot; spectrum when it comes to doing what's necessary to save the world.<br /> <br /> The challenge this game is focusing on is the idea that the tools/powers/issues Garou have are all there to illustrate how inadequate to the task of saving the world they are. And somehow PC-Garou are supposed to get past that and (maybe) make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is, from the sound of it? The reason it won't work...is author fiat.<br /> <br /> No real reason, just the idea that being genuinely angry about something and being disruptive at all is a bad thing because *mumble mumble.*<br /> <br /> Like, there's a strike going on in my country right now, and it comes off as something that would be Hauglosk-triggering because its refusal to come to the bosses until they come to them is causing massive amounts of disruption to the industry and bleeding millions of dollars, which is hurting people who aren't part of the strike incidentally as the bosses turn to cannibalism to keep the numbers up. Or...well, I'm going to not finger anything here, but there's a way worse example that comes off as Hauglosk that reminds me of certain forms online discourse that has disillusioned me about radical pacifism, and more specifically its more contrarian aspects. (PM me for more.)<br /> <br /> And more importantly - it's way, <i>way </i>too easy to pick up, and not nearly enough to drop it. Like, just one simple rule - &quot;at 5 Hauglosk, your character becomes paranoid, angered, and fearful, and thus may easily be roped into a simplistic but self-destructive schema like the Cult of Fenris' extremism. They are not unplayable, but here are massive penalties to avoid being taken in and against Rage, and you will have to do a story about them coming out of this emotional rut before it becomes self-sustaining.&quot; There, now it's a looming threat, but existential crises are now a thing - and the personal horror is intact <i>while </i>making it playable and the final fall being in the choice of players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:59:25-07:00","id":1519778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519775#post1519775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate a bit more... I think a core-designing-principle in writing this book was to take every element and first ask questions like: &quot;How do the Garou fuck this up? How are Garou bad at this task? What counterproductive strategy/tactic is employed by the Garou?&quot;. The idea wasn't, for example, to say that direct action in battling climate-change is bad but instead to make the whole thing about explaining why Garou are bad at it, do the wrong thing or employ some counterproductive strategy or something. The point is always to show that Garou aren't up to the task and depending on the context in the book you get an explanation for how they fuck up.<br /> <br /> That's how you get sections like the Black Furies and Red Talons. You say they're about fighting injustice and protecting animals... but immediately what that followed up with is explaining how this Tribe fucked up, is counterproductive etc.<br /> <br /> And for whatever reason, this game asks you to be one of those guys...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which then brings up quite a few questions.<br /> <br /> For one, if this truly is a reboot, why is so much of the book focused on waving the shame-bell at the way the Nation works? It doesn't read as explaining the setting, it reads like a 'take that' at the older editions and how ignorant they were.<br /> <br /> The second, so why should you play this game? With vampire, the fantasy of being a vampire is baked in. For hunter, you are protecting humanity from monsters. For garou...uh, you are TRYING?<br /> <br /> It reads like the Hunter Org no bueno sections, except towards the player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T12:03:09-07:00","id":1519779,"title":"","content":"Heads-up to those of you who pre-ordered: Got my hardcopy today... They were faster than I thought. I got the V5 Players Guide just last week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T12:17:39-07:00","id":1519781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519777#post1519777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is, from the sound of it? The reason it won't work...is author fiat.<br /> <br /> No real reason, just the idea that being genuinely angry about something and being disruptive at all is a bad thing because *mumble mumble.*<br /> <br /> Like, there's a strike going on in my country right now, and it comes off as something that would be Hauglosk-triggering because its refusal to come to the bosses until they come to them is causing massive amounts of disruption to the industry and bleeding millions of dollars, which is hurting people who aren't part of the strike incidentally as the bosses turn to cannibalism to keep the numbers up. Or...well, I'm going to not finger anything here, but there's a way worse example that comes off as Hauglosk that reminds me of certain forms online discourse that has disillusioned me about radical pacifism, and more specifically its more contrarian aspects. (PM me for more.)<br /> <br /> And more importantly - it's way, <i>way </i>too easy to pick up, and not nearly enough to drop it. Like, just one simple rule - &quot;at 5 Hauglosk, your character becomes paranoid, angered, and fearful, and thus may easily be roped into a simplistic but self-destructive schema like the Cult of Fenris' extremism. They are not unplayable, but here are massive penalties to avoid being taken in and against Rage, and you will have to do a story about them coming out of this emotional rut before it becomes self-sustaining.&quot; There, now it's a looming threat, but existential crises are now a thing - and the personal horror is intact <i>while </i>making it playable and the final fall being in the choice of players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. It doesn't work. Especially whenever you bring the Garou in contact with real-world-issues it's a bit simplistic to make it all about how terrible Garou are. And this book spends way more time on all the ways in which Garou are incapable of doing the right/necessary thing to save the world. I'm not even sure what the writers think the PC-Garou should do. Like the &quot;hopeful&quot; bit from &quot;The Problem With Garou&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But all is not lost\u2026 at least not yet. As long as the characters are the focus of the scene, hope endures. They do have a veritable arsenal of physical and spiritual tools and weapons at their disposal. The characters \u2014and the Garou Nation as a whole \u2014 are not accidental heroes, but finally acting with decisiveness and direction is sure to be a struggle.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The paragraph reads like a missive from another universe (which actually could be the case... maybe it's a remnant of the first iteration). The Garou-Nation is in shambles, wanting to immediately take action is now a supernatural mental illness (hauglosk) and what direction are they talking about...? This book doesn't even like the Garou-Nation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519778#post1519778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which then brings up quite a few questions.<br /> <br /> For one, if this truly is a reboot, why is so much of the book focused on waving the shame-bell at the way the Nation works? It doesn't read as explaining the setting, it reads like a 'take that' at the older editions and how ignorant they were.<br /> <br /> The second, so why should you play this game? With vampire, the fantasy of being a vampire is baked in. For hunter, you are protecting humanity from monsters. For garou...uh, you are TRYING?<br /> <br /> It reads like the Hunter Org no bueno sections, except towards the player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Well, you are playing this game to learn that Garou suck <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T12:22:50-07:00","id":1519782,"title":"","content":"Paradox is bending over backwards to not make any statements or take a definitive stance on anything and it seems like it's resulted in a bland and wishy washy game with tonal dissonance.<br /> <br /> The world is ending... maybe.<br /> <br /> You are a spiritual warrior for Gaia... maybe, don't get too worked up about that or it's bad.<br /> <br /> Crappy things happened to indigenous peoples historically, but let's just table that for now.<br /> <br /> Generic ideas of injustice are more worthy of the Black Furies' focus than the historical and ongoing oppression of women!<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris believe in the One True Way and are extremists!<br /> <br /> Environmental devastation is bad! Don't fight against it too hard or you'll be like the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> By the way, Red Talons eat people but they are still better than those fanatic Fenrir!<br /> <br /> We like dropping F bombs in our writing because it is edgy and mature and we're all super cool adults!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T17:29:42-07:00","id":1519808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519758#post1519758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and a question. Does the release of W5 mean that there gonna stop making W20 stuff? Cause W5 is essentially a reboot like Werewolf the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cGoing to stop\u201d? What's the last book you know of that was published for W20? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T18:32:45-07:00","id":1519817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519775#post1519775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate a bit more... I think a core-designing-principle in writing this book was to take every element and first ask questions like: &quot;How do the Garou fuck this up? How are Garou bad at this task? What counterproductive strategy/tactic is employed by the Garou?&quot;. The idea wasn't, for example, to say that direct action in battling climate-change is bad but instead to make the whole thing about explaining why Garou are bad at it, do the wrong thing or employ some counterproductive strategy or something. The point is always to show that Garou aren't up to the task and depending on the context in the book you get an explanation for how they fuck up.<br /> <br /> That's how you get sections like the Black Furies and Red Talons. You say they're about fighting injustice and protecting animals... but immediately what that followed up with is explaining how this Tribe fucked up, is counterproductive etc.<br /> <br /> And for whatever reason, this game asks you to be one of those guys...</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself thinking back to the opening comic of W20, and how it revolves a young Garou and the Prophecy of the Phoenix, the prophecy that tells of the Apocalypse, and how the story reframes the meaning of the Prophecy from a portent of doom to a rallying cry for the Garou Nation, that even in the face of the Apocalypse, victory can be achieved. It honestly felt hopeful, that even if they can't stop the Apocalypse from happening, they'll fight it. That even if they all end up dying, they'll fight it. That willingness to fight in the face of the Apocalypse, even it's nothing more than a defiant last stand is noble, heroic.<br /> <br /> And for WtA newcomers, that's something they could sink their teeth in. The heroism of stubbornly fighting in the face of certain doom can be quite appealing. Sure, the Garou have made many, many mistakes over the years and most will end up dying violently. Yet most stand defiant until that end, offering up their lives to prolong the world just a bit longer. And in that refusal to accept defeat there is hope that perhaps the Garou can one day win the war and save the world.<br /> <br /> Do not go gentle into that good night. Rage, rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> Yet everything I've seen and heard about W5 can be summed up as 'You've lost. The Apocalypse is here. Any action to take is at best pointless and ineffectual, at worst only causing more damage. Have fun Garou!' before you even create your PC. So yeah, why should anyone play W5 in that situation? Like even in <i>Apocalypse</i>, the assumption was that you were going to use the book as an end for your ongoing Chronicle, not the starting point.<br /> <br /> Honestly it's a spectacular failure to understand WtA on top of all the other parts of WtA they failed to understand. Frankly I'm almost impressed by not only how clueless about WtA this official WtA book is but also just how much the books seems to have nothing but contempt and hatred for Humans and Garou which is pretty weird given it wants you to play as Human-born Garou.<br /> <br /> At this point I believe W5 is the worst 5E book to ever come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T00:24:07-07:00","id":1519829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519808#post1519808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cGoing to stop\u201d? What's the last book you know of that was published for W20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apocalyptic Record received it's full release this year... though it is obviously an outlier in that regard and there's clearly not going to be any official W20 books after its Kickstarter stuff is fully finished.<br /> <br /> To people that aren't paying as much attention as most forum users here, the release of a book a few months ago give a misleading impression about the state of the 20th books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519817#post1519817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the Garou have made many, many mistakes over the years...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or did they?<br /> <br /> /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T00:46:12-07:00","id":1519830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519817#post1519817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet everything I've seen and heard about W5 can be summed up as 'You've lost. The Apocalypse is here. Any action to take is at best pointless and ineffectual, at worst only causing more damage. Have fun Garou!' before you even create your PC. So yeah, why should anyone play W5 in that situation? Like even in <i>Apocalypse</i>, the assumption was that you were going to use the book as an end for your ongoing Chronicle, not the starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and the way Fenrir are treated as unplayable, even if other tribes do worse. It was more understandable when it was still a &quot;They wanted to avoid controversy&quot; choice, but now that we know it was one guy REALLY pushing for a much worse version and the CoF STILL being hinted to be fascist, it tastes even more bitter. I could buy wanting to avoid controversy, I could buy the glyph being a reason to be careful. That someone wanted to go full-on neo-nazi with them and still made them into unplayable bad guys is not a good reason and barely avoided another controversy.<br /> <br /> As are the many, MANY sidebars telling you how much the garou suck. I don't think V5 or H5 spent that much time literally telling you that your PCs should feel guilty for existing. This reminds me of one online game that spent wikispace putting down anyone not playing an urban garou, only that was a single game trying something new and this is a full ttrpg.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't spend valuable pages telling people why NOT to play this game, you should give them reasons why playing garou could be fun/rewarding.<br /> <br /> Because right now, W5 reads as the book being more interested on decrying its previous editions than actually giving an idea what to play.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T03:26:35-07:00","id":1519836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519830#post1519830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Because right now, W5 reads as the book being more interested on decrying its previous editions than actually giving an idea what to play.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its more a meta attempt to railroad the game into low level urban setting in line with v5....which in turn is proposed to be what vtm is 'supposed' to be. This ultimately leaves w5 lacking identity as a sort of approximation of another splat with the trapping of another more distinct game.<br /> <br /> Moving forward Its very unlikely they'll be able to develop the setting due to design outlook being reductive rather than expansive. They don't really have any ideas (anarch) and won't integrate older ones (sabbat). It's pretty bleak in an interesting way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T04:47:09-07:00","id":1519842,"title":"","content":"Reading the Rites-section... why would anybody even wanna use Rites in this game...? Also great how in that section the game just casually introduces two new Rage-dice-result-types (Brutal failures and &quot;Each Brutal Outcome&quot;). The funny thing about &quot;Each Brutal Outcome&quot; is that it's mentioned four times in that section and only during the fourth and final time (for the Rite of Caern Building) it's explained in parenthesis that &quot;Each Brutal Outcome&quot; means pairs of Rage-Dice with 1s or 2s. If you're not reading carefully, you will be definitely surprised by these new phrases popping up in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:01:32-07:00","id":1519845,"title":"","content":"One thing came to my mind, is the game easier if you lose the wolf like I assumed? I haven't seen any negatives about it aside from lack of gifts/shifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:06:58-07:00","id":1519847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519845#post1519845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing came to my mind, is the game easier if you lose the wolf like I assumed? I haven't seen any negatives about it aside from lack of gifts/shifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It locks you away from most gifts, as most of them require rage, and most of them require you to be in crinos/hisp/glabro to even work.<br /> <br /> So if you are happy with just human traits, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:21:20-07:00","id":1519849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519847#post1519847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It locks you away from most gifts, as most of them require rage, and most of them require you to be in crinos/hisp/glabro to even work.<br /> <br /> So if you are happy with just human traits, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>But hey, no Rage Dice XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:24:27-07:00","id":1519851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519845#post1519845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing came to my mind, is the game easier if you lose the wolf like I assumed? I haven't seen any negatives about it aside from lack of gifts/shifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can still get tagged for Harano (setbacks and Touchstones being harmed/threatened) and Hauglosk tests (breaking Chronicle Tenets). You can still be forced into Frenzy when a severe provocation takes place and you fail the WP-test. Some Tribe-Bans are a real pain in the ass especially since by &quot;losing the wolf&quot; you can't use Gifts and Rites. So the Silent Strider one will be a real problem, for example.<br /> <br /> I think it just goes to show that these negative mechanics are set up in a way where situations can be easily created where your character's just fucked - and it has nothing to do with what you've chosen to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T05:25:08-07:00","id":1519852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519849#post1519849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But hey, no Rage Dice XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh joy. Btw the whole thing with gifts not working outside supernatural forms is utter gibberish to me. It makes keeping the Veil even more absurd and disables the toolkit even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T08:41:51-07:00","id":1519868,"title":"","content":"The fact that the Gale Stalker ban is about consuming meat every day REALLY should have been rethought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T09:20:44-07:00","id":1519869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519868#post1519868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Gale Stalker ban is about consuming meat every day REALLY should have been rethought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's weird. I guess if you have no idea what the Tribe was called in the past, you just scratch your head and wonder why that's the Ban for this Tribe.<br /> <br /> But speaking of weird Tribe-Bans... The Children of Gaia one is also... quite something:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ban: Unicorn is forthright and despises dishonesty. If a Child of Gaia must lie or misdirect, or hides truths specifically for personal gain, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating. <b>(If you have to argue whether it\u2019s \u201cfor personal gain,\u201d that\u2019s maybe an indicator of the intent\u2026)\u200b</b> </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> First, a &quot;you must tell the truth if it helps yourself&quot;-Ban is a bit much but then the passive-aggressive bit at the end... There's certainly one particular writer in this book who seems like an ST I wouldn't wanna play with. Whenever it's that writer, you get this constant refrain about how the ST is the ultimate authority and <i>only </i>the ST is allowed to make judgment calls on decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T09:35:02-07:00","id":1519871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519869#post1519869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But speaking of weird Tribe-Bans... The Children of Gaia one is also... quite something:<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> First, a &quot;you must tell the truth if it helps yourself&quot;-Ban is a bit much but then the passive-aggressive bit at the end... There's certainly one particular writer in this book who seems like an ST I wouldn't wanna play with. Whenever it's that writer, you get this constant refrain about how the ST is the ultimate authority and <i>only </i>the ST is allowed to make judgment calls on decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Veil, people, the VEIL. Also, personal gain can be not getting arrested after frenzying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T09:41:47-07:00","id":1519874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519871#post1519871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Veil, people, the VEIL. Also, personal gain can be not getting arrested after frenzying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally enforcing the joke/myth of &quot;Undercover cops have to tell me if they're a cop when I ask them.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:01:19-07:00","id":1519884,"title":"","content":"Would anything break if one just dumped Tribal bans? None of them are good or add anything to the play experience. I'd rather Players just negotiated their own chiminage individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:17:40-07:00","id":1519888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519884#post1519884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anything break if one just dumped Tribal bans? None of them are good or add anything to the play experience. I'd rather Players just negotiated their own chiminage individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tribal benefits would go with them, which I'm fine with. To me, tribal patrons are beyond controlling every member through bans and boons. Patron versions are shards that can grow powerful, but their need for bans and boons is logical. With Forsaken's tribal bans, they reflect the deal nature of the uratha and their hisil buddies. That and no one is taking Fenris-Ur as a Patron, just his pups.<br /> <br /> Plus to me, the tribal bans and boons in W5 combined with the example concepts hint at how removed from other garou they are and so need spiritual support. In previous versions, lone wolves were looked down on for a reason and I think that is another reason why tribal patrons didn't give their benefits to single garou. They were expected to seek a more personal patron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:31:39-07:00","id":1519890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519884#post1519884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anything break if one just dumped Tribal bans? None of them are good or add anything to the play experience. I'd rather Players just negotiated their own chiminage individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, it could have a place in the game. But the Bans are inconsistent in how they are presented and vary wildly in how restrictive they are. That's why the Pack-Patron-Spirit is just about sharing the Favor with the Pack. They essentially ran into the same problem as with the alternative Clan Banes in the V5 Players Guide. There they foolishly included a Flaw about a vampire having both Clan-Banes and then in a sidebar they had to admit that actually in certain cases that would render the PC unplayable so depending on the Clan you couldn't take the Flaw (because they hadn't written the alternative Clan-Banes with that in mind obviously). Here they just gave up immediately on having a Pack-Patron-Spirit with a Favor/Ban and a Tribe-Patron-Spirit with a Favor/Ban.<br /> <br /> But removing it wouldn't impact anything, I would say. It isn't like you don't need to be mindful of your WP-track even without the Damocles-Sword of a Tribe-Ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:42:45-07:00","id":1519891,"title":"","content":"Was there really much about the Black Spiral Dancers or Pentex? I looked it over, couldn't find much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:45:54-07:00","id":1519892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519891#post1519891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there really much about the Black Spiral Dancers or Pentex? I looked it over, couldn't find much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically; BSD totem is now Bat, BSDs seem to be as they were before. But unlike in W20 where redeeming one is near-mythical, in W5 a loresheet let's you redeem one.<br /> <br /> Pentex is no longer allied with the Wyrm and has its own totem in Fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T15:33:37-07:00","id":1519904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519891#post1519891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there really much about the Black Spiral Dancers or Pentex? I looked it over, couldn't find much.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"359\" height=\"918\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/1FleaWg.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/1FleaWg.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/1FleaWg.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <i>Pentex Group </i>get a lot more than I'm comfortable just pasting in. They are a Shadowy organisation to which any company may actually belong to and who cover themselves up with endless fronts. They have access to Rites, Banes and Fomori. Occasionally Black Spiral Dancers help them, but are quite willing to fuck over Pentex if it suits them. The section has a NBA style conspyramid how the average Pentex front is organised and how to stage a typical chronicle around them. There's less about actual activities, but it's mostly what we'd expect.<br /> <br /> Oh and they get their own patron now - Fly, who allows them to fester and survive in the carcass of Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T16:52:26-07:00","id":1519907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519869#post1519869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it's weird. I guess if you have no idea what the Tribe was called in the past, you just scratch your head and wonder why that's the Ban for this Tribe.<br /> <br /> But speaking of weird Tribe-Bans... The Children of Gaia one is also... quite something:<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> First, a &quot;you must tell the truth if it helps yourself&quot;-Ban is a bit much but then the passive-aggressive bit at the end... There's certainly one particular writer in this book who seems like an ST I wouldn't wanna play with. Whenever it's that writer, you get this constant refrain about how the ST is the ultimate authority and <i>only </i>the ST is allowed to make judgment calls on decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can almost guarantee that writer was Achilli","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T18:42:18-07:00","id":1519913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519904#post1519904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh and they get their own patron now - Fly, who allows them to fester and survive in the carcass of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the text siding with the BSD point of view, and that's terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T18:54:05-07:00","id":1519915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519750#post1519750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaand, once you think KM has dropped the matter;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"599\" height=\"201\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> P.322.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Did anyone on this project spend more than five minutes <i>thinking </i>about fascism before writing, let alone <i>any reasearch</i> on the hows and whys behind it?<br /> <br /> I'm almost vicariously insulted on behalf of fascists with this. There's a lot wrong with the people who are appealed to by paligenetic ultranationalism, but even they deserve better than being reduced down to being understood in terms of &quot;simpleminded morality.&quot;*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519765#post1519765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that, but Hauglosk/CoF basically imply that deciding to take direct action and causing some harm is the same as being a fascist. You know, like riots, protesting pipelines, general antifa stuff. <i>Punching neo-nazi.</i> And these are just things humans do, never mind stuff garou can do like destroying the spirit of pollution in a factory which causes it to crumble in the real world.<br /> <br /> Plus, since tribes are no longer tied to cultures, how can the CoF be ecofascists? Unless they are the only tribe that is solely white?<br /> <br /> The way this game punishes wanting to do more than just small-scale stuff is really tiring. ESPECIALLY since Red Talons and Black Furies are still stated to take drastic actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooow\u200b<br /> <br /> *like, yes, fascism tends to flatten morality and there is an appeal to that, but there is so much more going on with fascists than that, and even if you had to reduce them down to that concept, there's ways you can put it that doesn't make it sound like the writer/s think fascists are just upset children. This phrasing almost goes so far as to suggest they don't think fascism is a serious problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-05-2023, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T19:00:21-07:00","id":1519916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519913#post1519913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the text siding with the BSD point of view, and that's terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a load of weird choices here. The writing is all over the place trying to downplay context and any complex interactions, and the tone implies that they either didn't care about the nuance of old Werewolf or felt that it was not conductive to the kind of game they wanted to have. I think that the most frustrating thing about it is how many words are spent contrasting the old and the new and any time this raises questions writing &quot;nobody knows&quot;. The whole gonzo style of writing is also really not doing it for me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T19:03:06-07:00","id":1519917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519916#post1519916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a load of weird choices here. The writing is all over the place trying to downplay context and any complex interactions, and the tone implies that they either didn't care about the nuance of old Werewolf or felt that it was not conductive to the kind of game they wanted to have. I think that the most frustrating thing about it is how many words are spent contrasting the old and the new and any time this raises questions writing &quot;nobody knows&quot;. The whole <b>gonzo style of writing</b> is also really not doing it for me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly the patron switch for BSDs makes too much sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;We can't stop here. This is Bat country!&quot;<br /> <br /> Can't wait to see what kind of bonuses golf shoes give against reptile-changers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T19:07:32-07:00","id":1519918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519917#post1519917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suddenly the patron switch for BSDs makes too much sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;We can't stop here. This is Bat country!&quot;<br /> <br /> Can't wait to see what kind of bonuses golf shoes give against reptile-changers.</div> </div> </div> </div><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://www.reactiongifs.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/bat-country.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://www.reactiongifs.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/bat-country.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"http://www.reactiongifs.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/bat-country.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Depends, the dude went reptile changer in the end!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T21:25:53-07:00","id":1519928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519915#post1519915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Did anyone on this project spend more than five minutes <i>thinking </i>about fascism before writing, let alone <i>any reasearch</i> on the hows and whys behind it?<br /> <br /> I'm almost vicariously insulted on behalf of fascists with this. There's a lot wrong with the people who are appealed to by paligenetic ultranationalism, but even they deserve better than being reduced down to being understood in terms of &quot;simpleminded morality.&quot;*</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think the discussion started and ended with &quot;The Brand Manager wants Fenrir to be Fascists.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be more fair, this was the <i>third </i>iteration of a game that was announced 6 years ago and had gone through 2 versions already. A lot of the inconsistencies like Rage Dice vs the Archetypes in tribal descs or the Litany being told to be oppressive and yet still having the good tenets in it (Don't eat humans!) could be explained by them just needing this book out.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-06-2023, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T22:49:40-07:00","id":1519933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519750#post1519750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaand, once you think KM has dropped the matter;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"599\" height=\"201\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2mo1oOL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> P.322.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this type of writing is what one might expect of a writer who defines fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; and has not really thought about it much further than that. Thus, there is no particular need for the writer to define fascism, because it <i>obviously </i>consists of the &quot;simpleminded&quot; beliefs of those people who disagree with the far greater intellectual sophistication of the writer all all right-minded people, who will clearly be in agreement. And, since the writer is defining fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; there is a reasonable chance that &quot;fascism may be present in the social realm of the players' characters&quot; because of course it is. In the real world, people who genuinely hold fascist beliefs, and indulge in fascist behaviours, are incredibly rare, as it's more than merely being racist or holding right-wing opinions, but consists of complex belief systems as to how power should be exercised. But, extend the notion of fascism to anyone you dislike, and all of a sudden it becomes incredibly common...<br /> <br /> (Also: the prose in pretty much everything we have seen of W5 is incredibly awful. Phrases like &quot;fascism may be present in the social realm of the players' characters&quot; should never appear in a published book with competent editing. It's not the only offender, and every page has some instance of dreadful prose of the type which should not make it to print in a published book.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T23:11:10-07:00","id":1519937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519933#post1519933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this type of writing is what one might expect of a writer who defines fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; and has not really thought about it much further than that. Thus, there is no particular need for the writer to define fascism, because it <i>obviously </i>consists of the &quot;simpleminded&quot; beliefs of those people who disagree with the far greater intellectual sophistication of the writer all all right-minded people, who will clearly be in agreement. And, since the writer is defining fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; there is a reasonable chance that &quot;fascism may be present in the social realm of the players' characters&quot; because of course it is. In the real world, people who genuinely hold fascist beliefs, and indulge in fascist behaviours, are incredibly rare, as it's more than merely being racist or holding right-wing opinions, but consists of complex belief systems as to how power should be exercised. But, extend the notion of fascism to anyone you dislike, and all of a sudden it becomes incredibly common...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then add to it that the fascist tribe in question is also canonically <b>mentally ill</b> and boy the implications.<br /> <br /> That and ecofascism being mentioned in a game (supposedly) about environmental destruction. It has its place, yes, but the way hauglosk is defined and the fact that tribes no longer have national ties kind of kills the point. Ecofascism requires there to be an idea of certain people being worth sacrificing for the good of the planet, but since the only tribe having those ideas thinks that about every human, it's not really utilized well. It is just another way to finger-wag about being TOO eager.<br /> <br /> I mean, in W20 you could have a LOT of good roleplay over a Fang sept truly being ecofascist to the detriment of other houses in the tribe.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T23:49:35-07:00","id":1519939,"title":"","content":"Another issue that is running through W5 is that while it's mentioning multiple ways to play W5 from time to time, the writers clearly structured the book around <i>one assumed right way</i> to play this game.<br /> <br /> It starts on pg 45 with the sidebar called &quot;Packs In A Modern World&quot; where multiple Pack-types are mentioned. But W5 hasn't taken Coterie-Types from V5 and reproduced them for W5, so that's the first hint of how hollow this effort has been to follow up on what's presented here. And you get the first hint of what the writers think you're supposed to do instead at the end of the sidebar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The most effective kinds of packs for chronicles are proactive \u2014 troublemakers, if you will, but overall the sorts of Garou who investigate where conflict thrives, rather than waiting for it to come to them. Docile werewolves don\u2019t turn back the tide of Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <b>Packs may also find that their initial concept changes over time, or when they acquire resources to protect, such as a caern that ties them to a particular location.</b> That\u2019s great! Not only will the characters themselves change as the chronicle progresses, new dynamics of how those characters work together as a pack can emerge, as well. </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> If you didn't already get the message there, the moment you get to the section on Caerns, the message intensifies and now in a sidebar called &quot;The Players' Pack&quot; (pg 191) this happens:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>As a game, Werewolf: The Apocalypse assumes that the players\u2019 characters will have their own caern, or that their pack will belong to the sept of a specific caern.</b> The assumption exists for multiple reasons.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> This assumption doesn\u2019t have to be true \u2014 the chronicle may well be about a pack that ranges far and wide, across an extensive territory \u2014 but many troupes enjoy having a bit of territory that can show the outcomes of their actions (and the consequences of their choices). </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> In the first sidebar, being tied to a caern was described as something that may happen but now it's already called an &quot;assumption&quot; on the game's part. And even when the last paragraph mentions &quot;The assumption doesn't have to be true&quot;, it's immediately followed up with a &quot;But...!&quot;. And if you're under any illusions whether there's one right way to play W5, the section called &quot;Local Conflicts, Global Implications&quot; (pg 206) disabuses you of that notion:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once the pack has a purpose, establish relevant conflicts so the players\u2019 characters act locally. <b>Where you can, plan for the characters to acquire territory that gives them ties to the local community, such as a caern or participation in a sept.</b><br /> <br /> Local antagonists (both active and passive) provide conflicts in which Garou characters can secure real and meaningful victories, and where their resources can make a difference against the environmental apocalypse. Just because the stakes aren\u2019t epic save-the-world stories, that doesn\u2019t mean they\u2019re not important. Werewolf is very much a game of personal crisis and meaning in the framework of a worldwide catastrophe. And it has all the more meaning if it happens in the context of, say, retaking and then rebuilding a caern, or protecting caern territory as a responsibility to the sept.<br /> <br /> Straight up, the pack won\u2019t defeat the Wyrm (and is unlikely even to confront it directly). However, the packmates can challenge local antagonists who advance the Wyrm\u2019s agenda of greed, selfishness, and destruction, especially when those antagonists threaten what the werewolves have fought hard to attain or recover. </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Now the Storyteller is just straight-up told to make PCs take care of a caern and limit the game to a local conflict. And it's ultimately pointed out that this game isn't even about saving the world in the first place...<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T01:20:47-07:00","id":1519942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519933#post1519933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this type of writing is what one might expect of a writer who defines fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; and has not really thought about it much further than that. Thus, there is no particular need for the writer to define fascism, because it <i>obviously </i>consists of the &quot;simpleminded&quot; beliefs of those people who disagree with the far greater intellectual sophistication of the writer all all right-minded people, who will clearly be in agreement. And, since the writer is defining fascists as &quot;people who disagree with me&quot; there is a reasonable chance that &quot;fascism may be present in the social realm of the players' characters&quot; because of course it is. In the real world, people who genuinely hold fascist beliefs, and indulge in fascist behaviours, are incredibly rare, as it's more than merely being racist or holding right-wing opinions, but consists of complex belief systems as to how power should be exercised. But, extend the notion of fascism to anyone you dislike, and all of a sudden it becomes incredibly common...<br /> <br /> (Also: the prose in pretty much everything we have seen of W5 is incredibly awful. Phrases like &quot;fascism may be present in the social realm of the players' characters&quot; should never appear in a published book with competent editing. It's not the only offender, and every page has some instance of dreadful prose of the type which should not make it to print in a published book.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Its ultimately a product of online nerd culture trauma of late 10's far right ressuragance and the increasingly disconncted nature on online spaces. We're not really engaging with facism here so much as middle class nerds fears of facism hence why fascists are stupid or mentally ill.<br /> <br /> a problem emphasised by the worrying lack of belief in a larger cohesive way of resolving the garou (our?) nations issues were fascist fenris win the arguement <br /> because they're the only ones proposing anything at all.<br /> <br /> I suspect a lot of these people would benifit from getting involved in local politics and actually engaging with people with alternative political stances. Rather than trauma dumping into commercial products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-06-2023, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T01:30:20-07:00","id":1519943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519939#post1519939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue that is running through W5 is that while it's mentioning multiple ways to play W5 from time to time, the writers clearly structured the book around <i>one assumed right way</i> to play this game.<br /> <br /> It starts on pg 45 with the sidebar called &quot;Packs In A Modern World&quot; where multiple Pack-types are mentioned. But W5 hasn't taken Coterie-Types from V5 and reproduced them for W5, so that's the first hint of how hollow this effort has been to follow up on what's presented here. And you get the first hint of what the writers think you're supposed to do instead at the end of the sidebar:<br /> <br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> If you didn't already get the message there, the moment you get to the section on Caerns, the message intensifies and now in a sidebar called &quot;The Players' Pack&quot; (pg 191) this happens:<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> In the first sidebar, being tied to a caern was described as something that may happen but now it's already called an &quot;assumption&quot; on the game's part. And even when the last paragraph mentions &quot;The assumption doesn't have to be true&quot;, it's immediately followed up with a &quot;But...!&quot;. And if you're under any illusions whether there's one right way to play W5, the section called &quot;Local Conflicts, Global Implications&quot; (pg 206) disabuses you of that notion:<br /> <br /> (Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Now the Storyteller is just straight-up told to make PCs take care of a caern and limit the game to a local conflict. And it's ultimately pointed out that this game isn't even about saving the world in the first place...<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Combined with the Q&amp;A with Achilli and how Moonbridges isn't a thing, it is obvious that they want to keep you in one particular area, where you will heavily mingle with humans and as they say, keep being at Street level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T02:15:26-07:00","id":1519944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519943#post1519943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Combined with the Q&amp;A with Achilli and how Moonbridges isn't a thing, it is obvious that they want to keep you in one particular area, where you will heavily mingle with humans and as they say, keep being at Street level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only does this game want you to play at street-level but the focus is very clearly on the physical reality as well. I don't understand why the introduction even lists &quot;explore the mysteries of the Umbra&quot; as something werewolves in this game do. We saw the Loresheet for &quot;Umbral Traveller&quot; during the previews and wondered what would count as a &quot;protracted period of time&quot; for when the Umbra would start damaging the werewolf.<br /> <br /> And here's what being in the Umbra costs you in W5:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While in the Umbra, a Garou requires no food or drink, sustaining their spiritual form through sheer force of will instead. In addition to any other hazards, each scene spent in the Umbra after the first requires the expenditure of a Willpower, or the Garou suffers a level of Aggravated Health damage as their body starts to wither and fade. Werewolves that die in this way sometimes comack as Starving Remnants. (See p. 283)\u200b </div> </div> </div>Considering what a precious resource Willpower is in W5, I don't see any PC wanting to spend a lot of time in the Umbra...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T05:14:38-07:00","id":1519946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519944#post1519944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only does this game want you to play at street-level but the focus is very clearly on the physical reality as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>When thinking about this, I can't help but think of the starting point of a WtF game. The focus is on a group of werewolves claiming a turf and then defending it.<br /> <br /> The difference is that the story of the uratha will not remain in just that one locale or level. Lodges, Hisil quests,etc. can offer a way to move forward. For the W5 garou, though, as stated before I feel the game is designed to last few sessions, because the ceiling comes up FAST.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T07:26:27-07:00","id":1519952,"title":"","content":"So the Umbra is essentially cut off from the Garou then except for short periods of time ( A Scene is bloody short. Thats like an hour generally at most.) and you can't go too far otherwise you risk dying.....I guess Justin and Karim really didn't like Realms....wait....how did the BSDs survive the Spiral then? They must have been in there a while to go completely insane...but they should have died of Agg long before Bat came to get them.....I need to re-read but is there a reason Lion didn't come to get them? Or was the White Howler Patron Bat now?<br /> <br /> I need to read and re-read this book but the writing is so......blargh......it really makes me not want to even open it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 08-06-2023, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T09:40:44-07:00","id":1519964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519952#post1519952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Umbra is essentially cut off from the Garou then except for short periods of time ( A Scene is bloody short. Thats like an hour generally at most.) and you can't go too far otherwise you risk dying.....I guess Justin and Karim really didn't like Realms....wait....how did the BSDs survive the Spiral then? They must have been in there a while to go completely insane...but they should have died of Agg long before Bat came to get them.....I need to re-read but is there a reason Lion didn't come to get them? Or was the White Howler Patron Bat now?<br /> <br /> I need to read and re-read this book but the writing is so......blargh......it really makes me not want to even open it....</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just my theory, but I think the NPCs work under different rules than the PCs. Like the Archetypes in tribe pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T10:50:54-07:00","id":1519971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519964#post1519964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my theory, but I think the NPCs work under different rules than the PCs. Like the Archetypes in tribe pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well....yeah. Otherwise none of the societies work, could you imagine what the Elysium would look like with that many Social Combat rolls going off....just all these Impaired Vamps slumping around and rolling a mass of MCs and BFs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Its just.....weird....takes me right out of the game. But, yeah. Its the only way things can possibly work or every second Garou more than a year past first change would be in Harano or Hauglosk just based on the law of averages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T16:34:38-07:00","id":1519993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519942#post1519942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its ultimately a product of online nerd culture trauma of late 10's far right ressuragance and the increasingly disconncted nature on online spaces. We're not really engaging with facism here so much as middle class nerds fears of facism hence why fascists are stupid or mentally ill.<br /> <br /> a problem emphasised by the worrying lack of belief in a larger cohesive way of resolving the garou (our?) nations issues were fascist fenris win the arguement<br /> because they're the only ones proposing anything at all.<br /> <br /> I suspect a lot of these people would benifit from getting involved in local politics and actually engaging with people with alternative political stances. Rather than trauma dumping into commercial products.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is almost certainly an aspect of this; the writing of W5 in general (and, also, that which has appeared in a fair number of World of Darkness in recent years) has all the hallmarks of being fairly insular, where the authors' frame of reference is gaming, online forums, and other related popular culture. This is quite striking in terms of the evolution of the gaming universe. Back in the 1980s, the people who wrote for <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i> had a very narrow frame of reference. Most people had their notions of a fantasy world informed primarily by Tolkein (albeit a narrow, Americanised version of what Tolkein represented) and a well-read person within this context is someone who might have extended themselves to Edgar Rice Burroughs and Michael Moorcock.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at the beginning of the 1990s <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> appears, and is considered by many gamers to be a breath of fresh air. The authors have, of course, read Bram Stoker and Anne Rice, but also Upton Sinclair and Charles Dickens. They were creating a universe informed by the leading edge of current affairs, talking about environmentalism and racism, and other similar matters. These were games made by people who looked outwards for inspiration, beyond what we would now call &quot;nerd culture&quot;, and came up with interesting, challenging ideas. Of course, over time, the World of Darkness stops being this challenging novelty, and has, itself, become part of nerd culture, with writing driven by insular viewpoints, and too much time spent online. The end point for this trajectory is something like W5, a game written by people who don't quite have the broader context to take it to where it needs to be, and whose viewpoints are dominated by concerns generated within the online world, but which don't quite mesh with reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T16:42:50-07:00","id":1519994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519944#post1519944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only does this game want you to play at street-level but the focus is very clearly on the physical reality as well. I don't understand why the introduction even lists &quot;explore the mysteries of the Umbra&quot; as something werewolves in this game do. We saw the Loresheet for &quot;Umbral Traveller&quot; during the previews and wondered what would count as a &quot;protracted period of time&quot; for when the Umbra would start damaging the werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wondering when this first came up: since there is a larger focus on human society and Kinfolk aren't really a thing, are there rules for playing mortals with ties to the Garou? Like, maybe a shaman with Numina or even access to Gifts? Without having seen the book it still feels weirdly like playing Human: The Apocalypse would cause a lot less headaches.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T20:11:10-07:00","id":1520011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519994#post1519994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering when this first came up: since there is a larger focus on human society and Kinfolk aren't really a thing, are there rules for playing mortals with ties to the Garou? Like, maybe a shaman with Numina or even access to Gifts? Without having seen the book it still feels weirdly like playing Human: The Apocalypse would cause a lot less headaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the book is wishy-washy on the origin of Garou and who gets to be Kin so the idea of it being hereditary comes up a few times. So, I guess, technically you could write something like Kinfolk back into the game if you want. And of course, since it stays away from getting too specific in making any reference to human culture, there's no real discussion of Garou working together with humans. Also, there's the idea of pointing out that the world sees Garou as &quot;monsters&quot; since they often just resort to extreme violence to handle their problems. This is another point to underline how bad Garou are at doing what's necessary to save the world (or just being straight-up bad guys like the Cult of Fenris).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T01:11:28-07:00","id":1520023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519524#post1519524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, there's nothing there specifically about sex. It just attracts attention to them. So you walk into a crowded room and pop the gift and everyone will turn to look at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really no different from the V5 Presence power Awe. It adds dice to certain social rolls. Social rolls aren't mind control. I suppose your GM can play them like they are, but that's kinda creepy. People have free will against something like this. A good social roll might mean you're able to persuade someone or seduce them, but ultimately that person is still the one making the decision you tried to sway them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T01:28:49-07:00","id":1520024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520023#post1520023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's really no different from the V5 Presence power Awe. It adds dice to certain social rolls. Social rolls aren't mind control. I suppose your GM can play them like they are, but that's kinda creepy. People have free will against something like this. A good social roll might mean you're able to persuade someone or seduce them, but ultimately that person is still the one making the decision you tried to sway them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Animal Magnetism has been historically used as a way to breed more werewolves as per the books. There is even a pack tactic in REVISED dedicated to the whole pack using it to get better results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T03:07:26-07:00","id":1520025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520024#post1520024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference is that Animal Magnetism has been historically used as a way to breed more werewolves as per the books. There is even a pack tactic in REVISED dedicated to the whole pack using it to get better results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, in prior editions. It shouldn't be used that way in this edition (or any edition, really).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T03:23:47-07:00","id":1520026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520025#post1520025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, in prior editions. It shouldn't be used that way in this edition (or any edition, really).</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous versions they also had free will about it. That didn't change the perception of what the power is and does. It was broadly panned and considered horrible. That's why it's amusing to see it back with a similar wording in the new and cleaner Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T03:54:18-07:00","id":1520028,"title":"","content":"And, again, previous editions had lots of social buff Gifts to pick from to update as this sort of basic dice-bonus deal. Persuasion is the bread and butter social Gift in old editions, and it's only baggage was how poorly worded it was in terms of the whole &quot;statements have more impact than usual,&quot; was supposed to go. Nobody complains about Persuasion and the whole icky consent part (even though nothing stopped you from using it for seduction attempts) because the Gift didn't draw attention to that.<br /> <br /> There are over 700 Gifts in the legacy editions. Surely they could have picked any of a dozen or so names that are references to old mechanics without picking one that's so strongly linked to sex. Even if it wasn't the name of the creepy sex power that older editions just gave all werewolves, I already pointed out earlier in the thread that the phrase has always been tied to sex. It has those connotations even without knowledge of the older rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T06:22:13-07:00","id":1520031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520025#post1520025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, in prior editions. It shouldn't be used that way in this edition (or any edition, really).</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase is sexual, as Heavy Arms pointed out. In addition, the power/merit/gift has a nasty enough reputation that including it instead of any other convincing gift says something. Its just not a good inclusion due to its history and name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T07:08:44-07:00","id":1520032,"title":"","content":"I think Jay Sherman can sum up my thoughts on W5 better than I ever could...<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=szFj2ROOsio\" data-code=\"szFj2ROOsio\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/szFj2ROOsio/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T07:47:05-07:00","id":1520035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520032#post1520032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Jay Sherman can sum up my thoughts on W5 better than I ever could...<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=szFj2ROOsio\" data-code=\"szFj2ROOsio\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/szFj2ROOsio/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a little more forgiving <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LIFMZl_P4bY\" data-code=\"LIFMZl_P4bY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LIFMZl_P4bY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://youtu.be/LIFMZl_P4bY\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://youtu.be/LIFMZl_P4bY\" data-thumb-url=\"https://youtu.be/LIFMZl_P4bY\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T13:50:11-07:00","id":1520055,"title":"","content":"I think the overbearing reliance of Willpower to cover so much for the Garou in W5, combined with Brutal Outcomes not ever trying for something more narrative like Messy Crits, pushes it over the line from mediocre to &quot;stinks&quot; for me if we're just talking about the text itself (or at least the large amount of previews those with it have shared). H5 is mediocre. It dumps the lore interwoven Hunter Hunted groups, the trying-to-be-something-unique Imbued, and the much more useful sandbox of Vigil for... nothing. The H5 specific rules are odd in places, but generally aren't straining under the weight of so much stuff to deal with.<br /> <br /> Yes, more subjectively and personally, the whole WoD5 has stunk for me because I don't let it off the hook for behind-the-scenes issues, and the increasing lack of respect for the legacy editions despite being a new edition of those games being essential to the brand identity.<br /> <br /> But instead of seeing a steady refinement and improvement on how to leverage the core rules established in V5, we're seeing the opposite where the books seem to be growing less sure of how to translate mechanics into thematic expressions instead of more confidence in how to make their games pop. There's been enough time for them to start down the path the CofD did when Promethean 1e and CtL 1e started really pushing things in a better direction for the larger brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T16:29:39-07:00","id":1520066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520031#post1520031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The phrase is sexual, as Heavy Arms pointed out. In addition, the power/merit/gift has a nasty enough reputation that including it instead of any other convincing gift says something. Its just not a good inclusion due to its history and name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they should have just changed it to something else that doesn't have the same connotations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T17:29:28-07:00","id":1520068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520055#post1520055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But instead of seeing a steady refinement and improvement on how to leverage the core rules established in V5, we're seeing the opposite where the books seem to be growing less sure of how to translate mechanics into thematic expressions instead of more confidence in how to make their games pop. There's been enough time for them to start down the path the CofD did when Promethean 1e and CtL 1e started really pushing things in a better direction for the larger brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what it's feeling like to me. V5 is fairly solid. It has issues with the setting and mechanics, but overall is fairly functional. If someone asked if I wanted to play a V5 game, I'd probably say, &quot;Sure.&quot; I'd rather play a legacy edition, but I'd be willing to play V5. Then Hunter: the Reckoning was just very mediocre. They got rid of the Reckoning Hunters (while keeping the name) but also put all of the cool &quot;normal&quot; Hunter groups out of bounds. If someone asked me if I wanted to play Hunter: the Reckoning, I'd say &quot;Sure, but could we maybe play one of the other Hunter games? And I'd point towards Vigil or Hunters Hunted for playing more normal Hunters. And then W5 just doesn't look interesting from setting or gameplay perspectives. If someone suggested playing W5 I'd say, &quot;Nope. We're playing W20.&quot; <br /> <br /> V5 came out 5 years ago, and it feels like the quality of products has generally been going down ever since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T23:19:09-07:00","id":1520082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520068#post1520068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 came out 5 years ago, and it feels like the quality of products has generally been going down ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it any wonder, though? V5 was made by people who wanted to make it theirs and had clear ideas of how it and its world functioned.<br /> <br /> Hunter was made by an external studio on commission and on the down-low.<br /> <br /> W5 went through THREE tries to make it from three different groups. And according to JS, the internal drama JUST in the second try was immense.<br /> <br /> W5 suffers from being pulled into three different directions and spending valuable page space putting down previous versions for no reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not saying W5 was intentionally messed up, I mean it simply had many cooks trying to make different things out of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-08-2023, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T01:20:10-07:00","id":1520087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520082#post1520082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter was made by an external studio on commission and on the down-low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the same people made h5 as w5. It was the white wolf internal team with the help of freelancers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T03:44:09-07:00","id":1520090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520087#post1520087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly the same people made h5 as w5. It was the white wolf internal team with the help of freelancers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All right, good to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T03:57:32-07:00","id":1520091,"title":"","content":"The idea with H5 had been that the WOD-team with Justin Achilli as lead-dev would release that game first as the team needed more time to work on W5. This is just speculation but I think the development on W5 still ended up getting rushed because instead of focusing on W5 the WOD-team got sidetracked last year by working on the V5 Players Guide. And the way that book ended up, I feel like the majority of its content was written by people on the WOD-team... which is strange since the original arrangement was that Renegade would develop/write the supplements on its own. But the V5 Players Guide was originally supposed to be released in Summer last year and then suddenly it got delayed until earlier this year. And you can see how the WOD-team had taken over for the V5 Players Guide because I doubt anybody on the Renegade-writers-team would come up with an idea like making the introduction a copy-paste of various bits and pieces from the VtM Revised Edition Players Guide (that Justin Achilli also worked on).<br /> <br /> And so then we get to October last year and the writing on W5 is still far from finished. I think if it had been completely up to Justin Achilli this book wouldn't even have come out this year. That's why his statement on the release-date was always &quot;tentatively 2023&quot;. But Paradox was probably like &quot;Take the Hunters-Entertainment-version, finish the goddamn game and release it!&quot;. And the moment Justin Achilli was gone, the release-date immediately became Gen Con 2023.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T04:18:01-07:00","id":1520092,"title":"","content":"The adherence to GenCon releases still baffles me, as it has clearly hurt the WoD5 games a lot. It made sense, well over a decade ago, to do big releases at GenCon. But as e-Commerce has become the norm for so many consumers, releasing for the big trade show for the industry just doesn't matter. Lots and lots of companies are going to be there with books that released between GenCons when the books were ready and fully polished so people are going to be getting a better version than if said companies cut a bunch of months of final work on the books to make sure the games came out on a specific day. There's going to be lots of late beta-test stage games to be presented as previews. There's going to companies showing off books from years ago because it's core to a bunch of new supplements they did. Etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> I cannot imagine any gaming company worrying about getting a book out for GenCon 2023 and rushing it, vs. putting it out in Q2 2024 with a few more months if it needs it. It's just not where the audience is at in terms of their buying priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T04:38:01-07:00","id":1520094,"title":"","content":"Also in this context, there's the whole art-issue where they claim that now after this Gen-Con-release they're gonna re-review all the art and make some changes where necessary.<br /> <br /> And here's another bit of evidence that this book was probably rushed: This book is missing an entire section. Not only that, it's an important one because it's the section on Gaia's Howl.<br /> <br /> From the introduction/Lexicon:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia\u2019s Howl: An audible indicator (capable of sometimes affecting other senses) of the age of Apocalypse, perceptible only by Garou and perhaps some spirits\u200b </div> </div> </div>Then we go to the Umbra-section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether experienced as a literal howl, a painful frisson physically felt while traversing the Gauntlet, intruding visions of Gaia in pain, or an alarming burst of taste or smell, Gaia lets her champions know that they have little time left. (See p. 224 for more information on Gaia\u2019s Howl.)\u200b </div> </div> </div>The issue here...? This quote is on pg 224. And even in the Index Gaia's Howl is referenced as being on 224. But except for those two things I just quoted you above there's no other mention of Gaia's Howl in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T05:56:58-07:00","id":1520097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520094#post1520094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in this context, there's the whole art-issue where they claim that now after this Gen-Con-release they're gonna re-review all the art and make some changes where necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, time to send Paradox few emails.<br /> <br /> But for real, this is really skeevy in terms of picture rights. The book is printed, and the images are on paper. Whatever changes to future printings they make the damage has already been done.<br /> <br /> They also focused on strange things, like the whole Hart Wardens/Fianna thing. Yes, Fianna is not just a word, but you can't just change a tribe name willy nilly ESPECIALLY after you already had a Kickstarter project using the old name. Flyos need to do extra work now to change the name in Retaliation.<br /> <br /> People online will complain, that is what it is. But publishers should not react to everything to damage control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520094#post1520094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here...? This quote is on pg 224. And even in the Index Gaia's Howl is referenced as being on 224. But except for those two things I just quoted you above there's no other mention of Gaia's Howl in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>One wonders if Gaia's Howl is a remnant of an idea that was just left in the manuscript or they just forgot to put it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T06:39:42-07:00","id":1520101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520094#post1520094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in this context, there's the whole art-issue where they claim that now after this Gen-Con-release they're gonna re-review all the art and make some changes where necessary.<br /> <br /> And here's another bit of evidence that this book was probably rushed: This book is missing an entire section. Not only that, it's an important one because it's the section on Gaia's Howl.<br /> <br /> From the introduction/Lexicon:<br /> <br /> <br /> Then we go to the Umbra-section:<br /> <br /> The issue here...? This quote is on pg 224. And even in the Index Gaia's Howl is referenced as being on 224. But except for those two things I just quoted you above there's no other mention of Gaia's Howl in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the kind of mistake I wait to find in the papers of my undergraduate students, not in a $55 book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T06:48:17-07:00","id":1520102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520097#post1520097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, time to send Paradox few emails.<br /> <br /> But for real, this is really skeevy in terms of picture rights. The book is printed, and the images are on paper. Whatever changes to future printings they make the damage has already been done.<br /> <br /> They also focused on strange things, like the whole Hart Wardens/Fianna thing. Yes, Fianna is not just a word, but you can't just change a tribe name willy nilly ESPECIALLY after you already had a Kickstarter project using the old name. Flyos need to do extra work now to change the name in Retaliation.<br /> <br /> People online will complain, that is what it is. But publishers should not react to everything to damage control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original sin was just not following through on the idea of completely severing the links between Tribes and human culture. And then of course Justin Achilli's tonedeaf answer during the Q&amp;A just made it worse. Also, with the new names... We know for example that Ghost Council was James Sambrano's idea. So they just took that as a new name without much thinking. After all, why is the version in this W5 book called Ghost Council...? I'm sure James Sambrano knows why he came up with that name. But this WOD-team in this version just slapped the name on the Tribe and that was it.<br /> <br /> And with Flyos... Yeah, it's not good. But this WOD-team doesn't care. The moment they decided to do the whole &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-bit and made all those changes, they rendered the two werewolf-games Earthblood and Heart of the Forest non-canon/out of step with what this W5 book is doing. And even before the name-change to Hart Wardens, Flyos had the issue that while it was clear that W5 would go into a different direction, this book was still deep in development and so Retaliation already ended up being a strange mix of old and new lore anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520097#post1520097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wonders if Gaia's Howl is a remnant of an idea that was just left in the manuscript or they just forgot to put it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I saw that concept in the previews, I was actually curious about it. Because this is an element which can shed light on the whole Gaia's dead/dying bit and is a show-don't-tell-element for introducing the idea of the age of Apocalypse. Personally, I think this is an essential part of the W5 setting.<br /> <br /> But yeah, now they not only have to replace art but also add this section back into the book which at this stage is quite a bit of work as well... I mean, who knows how big that section was...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:59:11-07:00","id":1520130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1519762#post1519762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm. Well...<br /> <br /> <img width=\"342\" height=\"526\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WdDzvZB.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><img width=\"345\" height=\"324\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/KiUzCBF.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm sure it's been done unconsciously and naively.<br /> Or I just want to believe it.<br /> But it really reads like &quot;All Injustices Matter!&quot;<br /> Which sounds incredibly bad on a few levels, but I'm not accusing authors of anything beside lacking a certain degree of awarness and also courage\u200b.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm badly biased about this game at this point (which I admit is a possibility)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T14:47:01-07:00","id":1520150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520130#post1520130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure it's been done unconsciously and naively.<br /> Or I just want to believe it.<br /> But it really reads like &quot;All Injustices Matter!&quot;<br /> Which sounds incredibly bad on a few levels, but I'm not accusing authors of anything beside lacking a certain degree of awarness and also courage\u200b.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm badly biased about this game at this point (which I admit is a possibility)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what this comes across as to me. Paradox is terrified of alienating any group and this just feels like the cowardly route. Don't try to say anything of substance about Indigenous peoples and don't try to have any social commentary on societal gender roles.<br /> <br /> It really reeks of continued erasure of historically marginalized groups more than anything else.<br /> <br /> Playing it safe by refusing to take a hard stance on any issue in WTA flies in the face of the punk origins of the WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T15:24:01-07:00","id":1520155,"title":"","content":"And, of course, it just ends up alienating plenty of people in the end. I get wanted as broad of an audience as possible, but too safe means there's no reason to pick up your RPG over any other in a very crowded market. You've got to claim a territory and fight t expand it, not try to pretend boundaries don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T17:10:10-07:00","id":1520163,"title":"","content":"Just wanna point out that part of accelerationism is false most accelerationists would try and enforce crypto and enforce techbros<br /> <br /> <br /> The entire concept pushes the idea of accelerating capitalism and technology to uncontrollable levels including the problems.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T03:02:05-07:00","id":1520178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520155#post1520155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, of course, it just ends up alienating plenty of people in the end. I get wanted as broad of an audience as possible, but too safe means there's no reason to pick up your RPG over any other in a very crowded market. You've got to claim a territory and fight t expand it, not try to pretend boundaries don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>And given the game is about fighting back against oppressive forces, going safe is ignoring the reason people play the game in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T07:29:10-07:00","id":1520195,"title":"","content":"It's also misunderstanding WOD as an IP. Whenever you see people talk about the WOD on Youtube or podcasts the thing people talk about is - the lore. There are thousands of YT-videos telling you about the history of various Clans, Tribes, Traditions etc. By thinking they're sort-of streamlining the IP and making it more appealing to the mass-market, they actually end up running away from the one thing the market is telling them they care about - the lore.<br /> <br /> With this &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-bit, they didn't turn over a new page and presented something like CofD but rather just took an old game and gutted its essential elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T08:01:11-07:00","id":1520198,"title":"","content":"[<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520150#post1520150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really reeks of continued erasure of historically marginalized groups more than anything else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go that far, but I agree that reeks of &quot;playing it safe to a fault&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T08:41:50-07:00","id":1520203,"title":"","content":"On the whitewolfrpg reddit a lot of prolific WtA posters seem to be getting bans for commenting on the new release and having a discussion like this one. There are also a number of threads disappearing as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:34:00-07:00","id":1520213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520203#post1520203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whitewolfrpg reddit a lot of prolific WtA posters seem to be getting bans for commenting on the new release and having a discussion like this one. There are also a number of threads disappearing as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was also a thread about it on the werewolves subreddit that seems to have been scrubbed, though I can't say that I'm sad to see it go, since it just seemed to be a swing at James Sembrano for bringing the background shit to public attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:49:50-07:00","id":1520215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520213#post1520213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was also a thread about it on the werewolves subreddit that seems to have been scrubbed, though I can't say that I'm sad to see it go, since it just seemed to be a swing at James Sembrano for bringing the background shit to public attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh. The ways people are just trying to make his complaints irrelevant is just blech. At least here and on rpg.net people are sensible about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T10:34:22-07:00","id":1520220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520195#post1520195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-bit, they didn't turn over a new page and presented something like CofD but rather just took an old game and gutted its essential elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair,it took the 1e CofD books a few year to actually get there. While I liked where 1e was going from the start, with 2e and some hindsight, I have more appreciation for why a lot of fans didn't see the CofD's potential based on the first few 1e cores and related supplements. The arguments that they were taking the old WoD games and gutting the essential elements were made back then, and while I think they were proven wrong in time, it did take proving.<br /> <br /> My lack of faith in Paradox's handling of things,is because they have the last 20 years (nWoD and VtR 1e cores turn twenty next year on release date) of access to what happened in totality with the nWoD swap over, the design iterations of the new systems, the revival and coexistence of both WoD and CofD, and so on... and I don't see any lessons learned from all that. And they're not simply outsiders trying to piece something together by inference to explain it. They've had access to lots of people that have been working on these games from WoD 1e to CofD 2e to consult with directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520198#post1520198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[\u200bI wouldn't go that far, but I agree that reeks of &quot;playing it safe to a fault&quot;\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make the case that they crossed the line into erasure on a simple data point: W5 is still an animist setting. There is no &quot;neutral&quot; animism. Animism is a broad categorical term that loosely describes a ton of very diverse specific belief systems. This has always plagued WtA because it's basically based on a New Age mish-mash of Indigenous animist beliefs; it erases the cultures those beliefs came from by plucking cool ideas and scrubbing them of their cultural context and heritage.<br /> <br /> While we could debate if it's successful (or even possible to be successful) later legacy WtA and WtF tried to be more &quot;transformative&quot; in their take on spirits and spirit worlds. Rather than just be a grab bag of actual beliefs mixed in a blender, they worked to be inspired by real beliefs to come up with a unique fictional version.<br /> <br /> W5 has effectively reversed that. By making the presentation of things very wishy-washy the animism of W5 isn't a fully form fictional animism, but it isn't one that pays any real respect to the real animism it's drawing from at the same time. Thus the label of erasure. There isn't even an attempt to make it seem like the Garou of W5 practice the recognizably Indigenous inspired animism of past editions, and there isn't a replacement fictionalized animism that's explained well enough to use in-play either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T11:04:53-07:00","id":1520222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only speak directly to why a single thread was locked. And that is because of finding out it actually just existed so the poster could run to a certain spot on the internet and make fun of the replies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Thanks for the headsup. I'm slightly confused by this being a thing. I had an inkling who it was when you mentioned the other place, but I had no idea the idea was to shit-stir. I actually meant some more sensible folk, but I guess that they are not being civil enough for the current expectations of the sub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T19:09:16-07:00","id":1520253,"title":"","content":"The new mods of the sub get super ban heavy whenever anyone says anything negative about Paradox, even if you have receipts. I'm not sure if they're worried about blowback or some other reason and they're not particularly open to questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T23:58:40-07:00","id":1520266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520222#post1520222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh. Thanks for the headsup. I'm slightly confused by this being a thing. I had an inkling who it was when you mentioned the other place, but I had no idea the idea was to shit-stir. I actually meant some more sensible folk, but I guess that they are not being civil enough for the current expectations of the sub.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be candid but you lost me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T01:53:49-07:00","id":1520271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520220#post1520220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair,it took the 1e CofD books a few year to actually get there. While I liked where 1e was going from the start, with 2e and some hindsight, I have more appreciation for why a lot of fans didn't see the CofD's potential based on the first few 1e cores and related supplements. The arguments that they were taking the old WoD games and gutting the essential elements were made back then, and while I think they were proven wrong in time, it did take proving.<br /> <br /> My lack of faith in Paradox's handling of things,is because they have the last 20 years (nWoD and VtR 1e cores turn twenty next year on release date) of access to what happened in totality with the nWoD swap over, the design iterations of the new systems, the revival and coexistence of both WoD and CofD, and so on... and I don't see any lessons learned from all that. And they're not simply outsiders trying to piece something together by inference to explain it. They've had access to lots of people that have been working on these games from WoD 1e to CofD 2e to consult with directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Like, you could picture a H5 2.0 so-to-speak where you go &quot;Maybe just limiting it to local hunter-cells wasn't a good idea.&quot;, then you flesh out mechanics like the interplay between Desperation and Danger, you add a system to create your own supernatural antagonists etc. Somebody could take another crack at H5 and W5 and let those games find their footing. H5 may never be like the old Hunter the Reckoning with Imbued but you can still refine the idea of Hunters with Drive.<br /> <br /> But are people really interested to sit around for another decade to wait for WOD5E to do this?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T03:15:15-07:00","id":1520277,"title":"","content":"I mean, some people are. I'm not sure Paradox is, which is ultimately a bigger concern. Whatever Paradox's corporate attitudes towards the TTRPG side of their business is, it doesn't seem to be prioritizing putting out the best TTRPG books they can make. At the same time, it also isn't, &quot;we need to have TTRPG books because that's the core of the franchise, just let some third party do it,&quot; because they could have left OPP to keep things going (even the OPP few WoD5 books are some of the highest regarded ones by fans of the edition) and I don't think anyone would have been upset (even if not everyone happy). <br /> <br /> I don't get what this weird middle ground position actually does them. If they're going to keep a full time in-house WoD staff, they should be putting out really high end books to pair with their distribution channels to maximize sales. If they just want to let other people handle it, they just need a small group to do approvals and then they get paid for other people to make books for them. (and presumably work on much higher profit things like video-games). This isn't '95 where the few competitors in the urban horror TTRPG market are so small compared to the WoD you might not see them at your FLGS. I can go over to Itch.io and find a dozen games for the price of W5 core made by small indie groups that are going to have better writing, equal general production values, and probably far better mechanics for games that are purposefully narrow in what play experience they want to capture..<br /> <br /> People aren't going to keep put down coffee table book prices for games that aren't offering more than what you can get on the indie scene.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm wrong, and Paradox's spreadsheets and ledgers show something in private that I can't puzzle out. But at the same time it's not like their chomping at the bit to hype up how great their TTRPG stuff is doing (they are a publicly traded company with shareholder meetings where they would be bragging about that if it was really some secret sauce they don't want to reveal to the rest of us).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T06:30:36-07:00","id":1520289,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I feel V5 was the only WoD5 book that actually came out as planned. Hunter 5th ed came out of the bushes and W5's drama is well known by now.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think we get sourcebooks or such for W5, because the way it came out hints PDX just wanted it out once and for all. Now, it is out and games/novellas can be placed in it and that's good enough.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T10:44:43-07:00","id":1520311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520277#post1520277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, some people are. I'm not sure Paradox is, which is ultimately a bigger concern. Whatever Paradox's corporate attitudes towards the TTRPG side of their business is, it doesn't seem to be prioritizing putting out the best TTRPG books they can make. At the same time, it also isn't, &quot;we need to have TTRPG books because that's the core of the franchise, just let some third party do it,&quot; because they could have left OPP to keep things going (even the OPP few WoD5 books are some of the highest regarded ones by fans of the edition) and I don't think anyone would have been upset (even if not everyone happy).<br /> <br /> I don't get what this weird middle ground position actually does them. If they're going to keep a full time in-house WoD staff, they should be putting out really high end books to pair with their distribution channels to maximize sales. If they just want to let other people handle it, they just need a small group to do approvals and then they get paid for other people to make books for them. (and presumably work on much higher profit things like video-games). This isn't '95 where the few competitors in the urban horror TTRPG market are so small compared to the WoD you might not see them at your FLGS. I can go over to Itch.io and find a dozen games for the price of W5 core made by small indie groups that are going to have better writing, equal general production values, and probably far better mechanics for games that are purposefully narrow in what play experience they want to capture..<br /> <br /> People aren't going to keep put down coffee table book prices for games that aren't offering more than what you can get on the indie scene.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm wrong, and Paradox's spreadsheets and ledgers show something in private that I can't puzzle out. But at the same time it's not like their chomping at the bit to hype up how great their TTRPG stuff is doing (they are a publicly traded company with shareholder meetings where they would be bragging about that if it was really some secret sauce they don't want to reveal to the rest of us).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just looked it up: The <a href=\"https://icv2.com/articles/markets/view/54819/ogl-mis-step-shakes-up-rpg-business\" target=\"_blank\">sales-numbers</a> put V5 at #4 for Q1 2023. So, it's still in the same position as last Fall. The other Renegade-TTRPGs (Transformers, GI Joe) fell off, though. But it could be that V5 also profiteered from the whole hubbub surrounding D&amp;D and the OGL earlier this year as people were abandoning D&amp;D and looking for alternatives. <br /> <br /> In terms of plans, maybe V5 just becomes the tentpole that finances the support for further work on WOD5E and they're not making profit but they're also not losing money on the project. Paradox is just forging ahead because they know whatever they invest in more WOD-stuff will be covered by the steady revenue of V5. It would also make sense to only publish more V5 books and just ignore the rest of the WOD. Like, if W5 doesn't sell well, just ignore it and focus solely on making new V5 content instead.<br /> <br /> But also about Renegade... I don't know... The way they're grabbing IP left and right and turning them into games. They turned the Good Omens TV-show into a boardgame, they announced a TTRPG for the Welcome To Nightvale podcast... I don't know... Are they really growing so fast and can churn out that much content or is this a bubble in the making and at some point, reality will catch up with them...? I guess we'll see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T10:50:18-07:00","id":1520312,"title":"","content":"Something discussed in another forum, but it deserves to be here as well; W5 seems to treat the garou as amnesiacs to the point where they barely remember ANYTHING about their past. But every other faction does.<br /> <br /> Thing is, there is giving STs freedom and then there is this. W5 isn't giving much to work with, only fragments that don't even work together. The Litany is bad, yet it still has the positive laws and ragabash and philodox exist yet don't seem to play a role in interpreting the Litany.<br /> <br /> Now, if the point of the game was that the information was lost, that would work. But the book doesn't as much treat the information as lost as much as irrelevant. The book doesn't offer any concrete lore to base your game setting on, instead it tells you what lore is WRONG and harmful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T10:55:44-07:00","id":1520313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520312#post1520312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something discussed in another forum, but it deserves to be here as well; W5 seems to treat the garou as amnesiacs to the point where they barely remember ANYTHING about their past. But every other faction does.<br /> <br /> Thing is, there is giving STs freedom and then there is this. W5 isn't giving much to work with, only fragments that don't even work together. The Litany is bad, yet it still has the positive laws and ragabash and philodox exist yet don't seem to play a role in interpreting the Litany.<br /> <br /> Now, if the point of the game was that the information was lost, that would work. But the book doesn't as much treat the information as lost as much as irrelevant. The book doesn't offer any concrete lore to base your game setting on, instead it tells you what lore is WRONG and harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writing-style doesn't help either with all these rhetorical questions and a habit of using 10 words when 5 would suffice (that also annoyed me in the V5 Players Guide at times). There's just way too much waffling around in the text of this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T12:12:46-07:00","id":1520319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520311#post1520311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just looked it up: The <a href=\"https://icv2.com/articles/markets/view/54819/ogl-mis-step-shakes-up-rpg-business\" target=\"_blank\">sales-numbers</a> put V5 at #4 for Q1 2023. So, it's still in the same position as last Fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to be a bit careful wit hthe ICv2 reports; especially the free ones compared to the pro (aka paywalled) versions that are way less detailed (like what the differences are between each entry, and even if something is in the same slot on the chart, is it actually doing the same or just lots of people below it not doing great too).<br /> <br /> What I was referring to, was more things like this: <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/investors/financial-reports\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/i...ancial-reports</a><br /> <br /> Those are what Paradox's CEOs are saying to their shareholders (something we don't get to see with most RPG companies, because so few are publicly traded, or are subsidiaries like nWW was originally structured). The don't mention the WoD.... pretty much at all... Nothing happening with it has merited a line in their big picture reports. The release and then the performance of Bloodhunt doesn't merit an explanation.<br /> <br /> It's hard to infer a lot out of no comments specifically about the WoD properties, except that what is going on, it's not worth bragging about. There's a lot of reasons why that might be the case, but in the end, they don't want their shareholders thinking about the millions spent on buying the various IPs from CCP, and the expenses of setting up an internal division for handling them. Whether it's because massive TTRPG success is still so small that they don't think their investors care, or the WoD team is expecting a big turn around on projects that haven't really been announced yet and don't want to get ahead of their skis, or it's just to paper over that they're not actually making money but it's nothing compared to their profits on their core IPs... it's not worth mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T13:22:12-07:00","id":1520320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520289#post1520289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I feel V5 was the only WoD5 book that actually came out as planned. Hunter 5th ed came out of the bushes and W5's drama is well known by now.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think we get sourcebooks or such for W5, because the way it came out hints PDX just wanted it out once and for all. Now, it is out and games/novellas can be placed in it and that's good enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We just got 2 supplements for H5! I'm pretty sure we will have supplements for W5 too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T22:40:12-07:00","id":1520355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520320#post1520320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We just got 2 supplements for H5! I'm pretty sure we will have supplements for W5 too</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as W5 needs supplements, given the core took 6 years and 3 teams, I feel they will take a break from W5 for a while just to recharge. Plus they have a LOT to clean up with the book still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T23:33:29-07:00","id":1520356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520355#post1520355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as W5 needs supplements, given the core took 6 years and 3 teams, I feel they will take a break from W5 for a while just to recharge. Plus they have a LOT to clean up with the book still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have gone with the &quot;Exalted 2e Errata&quot; dilemma. The early releases of Ex2 definitely needed extra revisions, but would you have trusted it to the people who wrote the first pass, thinking that it was great as they did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T00:19:42-07:00","id":1520359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520356#post1520356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have gone with the &quot;Exalted 2e Errata&quot; dilemma. The early releases of Ex2 definitely needed extra revisions, but would you have trusted it to the people who wrote the first pass, thinking that it was great as they did?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I do not trust them one bit not to screw it up. But with Gaia's Howl not being explained and the art mess, they have to at least do SOMETHING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T09:25:09-07:00","id":1520393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520320#post1520320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We just got 2 supplements for H5! I'm pretty sure we will have supplements for W5 too</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think additional books along those lines are really what people think W5 needs right now.<br /> <br /> There isn't exactly a whole lot of new in the three additional releases for H5:The Free Bonus Material is... just some extra examples of Touchstones, a new monster, and a few play aids, the Storyteller Screen Kit is obviously built around a play aid, the expanded rules are things already available in the V5 stuff, and then it's a bunch of storyhooks and on sample adventure. Lines Drawn in Blood is more of what people would think of as a proper supplement, but even then it's four adventure modules that are capable of being strung together for a larger ongoing game.<br /> <br /> None of that is a bad thing. It's certainly good stuff to have for H5 groups, and W5 groups would benefit from such things for W5 too. But it's not a more comprehensive monster building guide, nor a better explanation of how to implement the Danger tracker in play. It's not something like HtR 1e's First Contact to more fully explore the line between Driven and Jobber, and how orgs that aren't as inherently hostile to Driven cells work in play; it's easy to understand why government Orgs don't like a bunch of vigilantes running around taking government maters into their own hands, but it's a lot harder to understand why the Arcanum wouldn't be fairly amenable to cooperating with Driven cells<br /> <br /> W5 needs books that really expand on a bunch of stuff in the core book, not just offer a bunch of example NPCs and some starter adventures to play. Not that W5 shouldn't do those too, but as people have pointed out, there are a lot of topics that are near unusable because of how much W5 wants to leave things mysterious/open to multiple interpretations.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's an inherently bad thing to try to make the WoD a bit more like the CofD in term of being a toolkit where you pick and choose which elements from the books you want to use. But a toolkit needs to be full of tools... or it's just an empty toolbox. Selling me a bit driver and a single bit just means I have a screwdriver for one type of screw. The fact that I could have dozens of bits for all the different types of screws out there does me nothing until I have more bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T00:05:49-07:00","id":1520433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520355#post1520355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as W5 needs supplements, given the core took 6 years and 3 teams, I feel they will take a break from W5 for a while just to recharge. Plus they have a LOT to clean up with the book still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some bad news for you... The Renegade-team are already working on the first W5 supplement. They immediately started on that when they got the manuscript in January. Now I wonder whether they then also already commissioned art from the same guy who was then involved in the GW-fiasco because that guy has been contributing art to pretty much every book since the switch to the in-house team plus Renegade happened (like I bet there's art from him in the upcoming Blood Sigils book).<br /> <br /> Additionally, this W5-book has its issues but compared to the state these pre-order early-release books are usually like, it's pretty good actually. Both the V5 Players Guide and Lines Drawn in Blood had stuff like repeating paragraphs, paragraphs in the wrong place, paragraphs from a previous draft completely unconnected to the final version, missing paragraphs or rules for little stuff like Merits/Flaws, spelling mistakes... Usually, these early-release pdfs are much worse. But I guess in this case they actually had their act together a bit because it also got a physical release at GenCon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T00:45:48-07:00","id":1520434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520393#post1520393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think additional books along those lines are really what people think W5 needs right now.<br /> <br /> There isn't exactly a whole lot of new in the three additional releases for H5:The Free Bonus Material is... just some extra examples of Touchstones, a new monster, and a few play aids, the Storyteller Screen Kit is obviously built around a play aid, the expanded rules are things already available in the V5 stuff, and then it's a bunch of storyhooks and on sample adventure. Lines Drawn in Blood is more of what people would think of as a proper supplement, but even then it's four adventure modules that are capable of being strung together for a larger ongoing game.<br /> <br /> None of that is a bad thing. It's certainly good stuff to have for H5 groups, and W5 groups would benefit from such things for W5 too. But it's not a more comprehensive monster building guide, nor a better explanation of how to implement the Danger tracker in play. It's not something like HtR 1e's First Contact to more fully explore the line between Driven and Jobber, and how orgs that aren't as inherently hostile to Driven cells work in play; it's easy to understand why government Orgs don't like a bunch of vigilantes running around taking government maters into their own hands, but it's a lot harder to understand why the Arcanum wouldn't be fairly amenable to cooperating with Driven cells<br /> <br /> W5 needs books that really expand on a bunch of stuff in the core book, not just offer a bunch of example NPCs and some starter adventures to play. Not that W5 shouldn't do those too, but as people have pointed out, there are a lot of topics that are near unusable because of how much W5 wants to leave things mysterious/open to multiple interpretations.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's an inherently bad thing to try to make the WoD a bit more like the CofD in term of being a toolkit where you pick and choose which elements from the books you want to use. But a toolkit needs to be full of tools... or it's just an empty toolbox. Selling me a bit driver and a single bit just means I have a screwdriver for one type of screw. The fact that I could have dozens of bits for all the different types of screws out there does me nothing until I have more bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree, don't get me wrong, the Academia Hunter supplement is a bit underwhelming (the 4 adventures are always useful); I was just mentioning that if even a line which was basically launched as a gateway for other games and a filler while we were waiting for Werewolf get a bit of support, W5 will almost surely get much more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T00:47:45-07:00","id":1520650,"title":"","content":"Anyone think it's strange just how much the Wyrm is downplayed in W5? Having read the book now, while the opening makes a big deal about how it's Garou's purpose to fight the Wyrm and whatever, it seems like every time it's mentioned, it has to be followed along with some kind of note that's like &quot;But is the Wyrm really that bad? It's just a force of nature, after all. Maybe it's the Garou who are wrong.&quot;. And while banes and such are still around, the Wyrm has been removed from a lot of enemy factions. Pentex is no longer directly associated, only incidentally working alongside it, and there's a big sidebar that says &quot;oh you don't have to use Pentex there's other real-life evil companies&quot; (which was true in the original game to be fair, but there it was less emphasized and with everything else it just seems to be more of an attempt to distance the game from its original antagonist). The BSDs are here, but they seem to just be a token mention and don't actually come up much. And it feels like everytime the idea of actually fighting the Wyrm comes up, it's always accompanied by the game shrieking that this is a fast-track to Hauglosk and you will be just as bad as the Cult of Fenris. Hell, the Red Talons now explicitly think the Wyrm is the <i>victim</i> so now it's okay to start using its tactics.<br /> <br /> But the game really wants you to know that the Cult of Fenris are always there and always terrible. Hell, the sample adventure at the end, despite having nothing to do with them, really tries to push you into shoehorning them into the plot and gleefully encourages you to steal their artifacts and caern.<br /> <br /> It's just kind of impressive just how blatantly this game doesn't actually want to be Werewolf: the Apocalypse at all, but just a reskinned V5 the way it railroads you into prioritizing petty inter-Garou conflicts instead of. You know. Saving the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T02:29:28-07:00","id":1520653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520650#post1520650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone think it's strange just how much the Wyrm is downplayed in W5? Having read the book now, while the opening makes a big deal about how it's Garou's purpose to fight the Wyrm and whatever, it seems like every time it's mentioned, it has to be followed along with some kind of note that's like &quot;But is the Wyrm really that bad? It's just a force of nature, after all. Maybe it's the Garou who are wrong.&quot;. And while banes and such are still around, the Wyrm has been removed from a lot of enemy factions. Pentex is no longer directly associated, only incidentally working alongside it, and there's a big sidebar that says &quot;oh you don't have to use Pentex there's other real-life evil companies&quot; (which was true in the original game to be fair, but there it was less emphasized and with everything else it just seems to be more of an attempt to distance the game from its original antagonist). The BSDs are here, but they seem to just be a token mention and don't actually come up much. And it feels like everytime the idea of actually fighting the Wyrm comes up, it's always accompanied by the game shrieking that this is a fast-track to Hauglosk and you will be just as bad as the Cult of Fenris. Hell, the Red Talons now explicitly think the Wyrm is the <i>victim</i> so now it's okay to start using its tactics.<br /> <br /> But the game really wants you to know that the Cult of Fenris are always there and always terrible. Hell, the sample adventure at the end, despite having nothing to do with them, really tries to push you into shoehorning them into the plot and gleefully encourages you to steal their artifacts and caern.<br /> <br /> It's just kind of impressive just how blatantly this game doesn't actually want to be Werewolf: the Apocalypse at all, but just a reskinned V5 the way it railroads you into prioritizing petty inter-Garou conflicts instead of. You know. Saving the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, exploring the Umbra is downplayed, Garou having a tight-knit community is downplayed (especially in the way Rites work mechanically) and the potential for Garou to do good is also downplayed... At times, it isn't just that this game doesn't want to be WtA but that the writers are expressing their active dislike of the idea of Garou. Like, your takeaway should be that the right solution to all these issues starts with &quot;Step 1 : Don't be a Garou.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T05:39:30-07:00","id":1520660,"title":"","content":"Its ultimately because w5 wants to be v5. The Get and spiral are the v5 Sabbat/inquisition the broken localised guys are the anarchs, the garou nation are the carmarilla the wyrm is a a vague cosmic force like the 3rd gen.<br /> its the same reason w5 doesn't like umbral adventutes-the game is supposed to be street like v5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-15-2023, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T11:02:33-07:00","id":1520687,"title":"","content":"There's an overview of the quickstart in the back of the core on RPGnet, and, on the main antagonist...uh...<br /> <br /> He's the prickly head of the local horticultural society turned ritual killer fomor. His stats are this:<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1290_1692122244761_49\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1290&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Now, having a raw strength of 8 plus being an absolutely expert brawler, to say nothing of how plants animate to defend him, might make it sound like he's being ridden by a bigwig among banes. The bane...is this:<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1291_1692122348978_503\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1291\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1291\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1291&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> Not even sentient enough to have a name.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTo repost what I said there: and it turns its host into a supervillain. Because this needed to be a boss fight.<br /> <br /> The prickly president of the horticulture club with a slightly nutty old lady (who stores ferns everywhere in her house because something something players are only allowed to ambush him there) being targeted because the totes his fault imp riding him gave him homicidal urges to build a body that sucks less. With no link to roots or even consumption at all, just frustrated growth, so it's not even linked to the mulch he draws his form from.<br /> <br /> ...I'd compare him to something written by Zane Lofton in Slayer X, but even that plot involved Zane realizing his real-life boss as a convenience store supervisor is kind of provincial to make an evil mastermind boss no matter how much of a prick he is.<br /> <br /> Like, what is this? Is there some great horror in gardening culture this is satirizing? Is there ceremonies on makeshift altars of Miracle-Gro in the back of my local Lowe's? And that's long before the solution was apparently ritualistic murders. You could at least link the spirit to his mutations and social role - like, a kudzu-spirit or a periwinkle-spirit, that explicitly links him being a petty tyrant to being an invasive weed, showing how the Wyrm is a force of corrupted ecological balance.<br /> <br /> But we really needed to know the Fenris have a couple of statless hicks whining about their caern being picked up by the PCs because it seemed unoccupied, because Vampire 5th has those and it ties into the link the Cult has to...so as you can tell, the ecofascist group is very important to this story about a serial killer gardener.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/