iledataid=1291\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1291\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1291&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> Not even sentient enough to have a name.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTo repost what I said there: and it turns its host into a supervillain. Because this needed to be a boss fight.<br /> <br /> The prickly president of the horticulture club with a slightly nutty old lady (who stores ferns everywhere in her house because something something players are only allowed to ambush him there) being targeted because the totes his fault imp riding him gave him homicidal urges to build a body that sucks less. With no link to roots or even consumption at all, just frustrated growth, so it's not even linked to the mulch he draws his form from.<br /> <br /> ...I'd compare him to something written by Zane Lofton in Slayer X, but even that plot involved Zane realizing his real-life boss as a convenience store supervisor is kind of provincial to make an evil mastermind boss no matter how much of a prick he is.<br /> <br /> Like, what is this? Is there some great horror in gardening culture this is satirizing? Is there ceremonies on makeshift altars of Miracle-Gro in the back of my local Lowe's? And that's long before the solution was apparently ritualistic murders. You could at least link the spirit to his mutations and social role - like, a kudzu-spirit or a periwinkle-spirit, that explicitly links him being a petty tyrant to being an invasive weed, showing how the Wyrm is a force of corrupted ecological balance.<br /> <br /> But we really needed to know the Fenris have a couple of statless hicks whining about their caern being picked up by the PCs because it seemed unoccupied, because Vampire 5th has those and it ties into the link the Cult has to...so as you can tell, the ecofascist group is very important to this story about a serial killer gardener.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Its so weird because the author writes some brilliant stuff for Savage Age and his other projects......I'm smelling a lot of Developer interference on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T11:36:15-07:00","id":1520779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520696#post1520696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its so weird because the author writes some brilliant stuff for Savage Age and his other projects......I'm smelling a lot of Developer interference on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I love Savage Age. You're right, really does seem like someone who worked on that would have done much better than this without interference. Given that we do have a bit of insight into how development of W5 went, (namely, aggressively railroading it out of being anything other than a shallow V5 clone) I definitely believe that executive meddling happened here.<br /> <br /> I feel so bad for anyone who genuinely cared about WtA that got roped into working on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T05:53:26-07:00","id":1520802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520696#post1520696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its so weird because the author writes some brilliant stuff for Savage Age and his other projects......I'm smelling a lot of Developer interference on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it was the page-count...? But yeah, it isn't good. Plot-wise a lot of things are happening before the player-characters even become involved. I think the moment the city told this &quot;horticulture club&quot; to work on this bit of forest-area, every Garou in the vicinity would've perked up because in that area is <i>a frigging caern</i>. An abandoned caern but a caern all the same. For Garou to get involved only <i>after </i>the club had started working on that area and <i>after </i>the villain of the story had already performed a goddamn Wyrm-ritual in that area should be a problem. And at the next Moot some serious questions need to be asked how this was allowed to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:16:52-07:00","id":1520807,"title":"","content":"Okay so the plots a mess, how well does it illustrate what sort if game they're trying to nudge the players into running and what's the appeal of the sort of game it presents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:27:00-07:00","id":1520808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520807#post1520807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so the plots a mess, how well does it illustrate what sort if game they're trying to nudge the players into running and what's the appeal of the sort of game it presents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<ul><li>it's extremely local and small-scale (PC-Garou against one Fomor) and so the title &quot;No Matter How Small&quot; is a bit on-the-nose</li> <li>there are no named Garou-NPCs (except one person who had just undergone the First Change)</li> <li>the Bane-spirit possesses the main-bad-guy simply because he's a bit of an asshole</li> <li>the Cult of Fenris has human allies for some reason whose description makes them sound like a movie's idea of rednecks</li> <li>part of this oneshot's pitch is (of course) for the player-group to immediately start taking care of the caern after this introduction-oneshot</li> <li>the victim the main-bad-guy is going after is really weird... her one-bedroom-house is full of plants... in fact, so many plants that when her stove broke, she just put more plants into it, her home is hot and humid - and she has named all her plants... but she's supposed to be just a normal person</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:49:30-07:00","id":1520812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520808#post1520808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>tove broke, she just put more plants into it, her home is hot and humid - and she has named all her plants... but she's supposed to be just a normal person</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>It is outright stated she is normal, or might there be a very obvious plot hook for the ST to use in the future?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:57:20-07:00","id":1520814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520812#post1520812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is outright stated she is normal, or might there be a very obvious plot hook for the ST to use in the future?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's outright stated that she's normal. Supposedly she even has a job (senior manager at a publishing company).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T16:48:02-07:00","id":1520844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520814#post1520814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's outright stated that she's normal. Supposedly she even has a job (senior manager at a publishing company).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a referance to someone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T17:37:50-07:00","id":1520849,"title":"","content":"One of the characters in the quickstart scenario in the book: the prime victim the PCs can save from the main antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:36:52-07:00","id":1520866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520844#post1520844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a referance to someone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. It sounds really specific and is probably someone the author has encountered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T14:01:36-07:00","id":1520898,"title":"","content":"I find it rather funny that, had Paradox not been so married to the 'garou are BAD' take on the lore, W5 could have had an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> What if the PCs first change and basically have to figure out things on their own. Digging up old lore of the Nation where they can find it and trying to repair spirit relations with what skills they have.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't even take away from the intended villany of the Nation, as the PCs could uncover old wrongs and TRY to figure out how to fix them.<br /> <br /> Basically, play up the ignorance and don't go out of your way stating which lore is bad, what factions are evil etc. Let the PCs decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T14:53:05-07:00","id":1520900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520898#post1520898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it rather funny that, had Paradox not been so married to the 'garou are BAD' take on the lore, W5 could have had an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> What if the PCs first change and basically have to figure out things on their own. Digging up old lore of the Nation where they can find it and trying to repair spirit relations with what skills they have.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't even take away from the intended villany of the Nation, as the PCs could uncover old wrongs and TRY to figure out how to fix them.<br /> <br /> Basically, play up the ignorance and don't go out of your way stating which lore is bad, what factions are evil etc. Let the PCs decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is they won the apocalypse scenario 1 but most of the nation was wiped. But it didn't undo the wyrms and weavers damage to the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T09:23:41-07:00","id":1520952,"title":"","content":"So far I didn't end reading the book. The game is in my wiev closer to Kult themes. The core concept is about 85% I saw in 2 ed. They put 1:1 scale real problems in the game as WtA 1 and 2 ed put 90's problems then. Many known lore from previews editions is myth or legend now. Reading between the lines I thionk that they are more garou before first change then in previews ed and it remindes me prophecy of the Phoenix in W20 about young garou.<br /> The game have lot of gaps for GM to fill. <br /> What I'd like to see now: <br /> 1. some book filled with lot of BN's, caern /sept, lore, some rage across New York. <br /> 2. players guide/companion filled with talismans, rites, gifts, new backgrounds and loresheets.<br /> 3. Book of the Wyrm/book of the Pentex group.<br /> <br /> Game needs them rather quick. W20 was complete for me. This book give many tools and clues but I prefer specified area of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T11:42:14-07:00","id":1520966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520898#post1520898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it rather funny that, had Paradox not been so married to the 'garou are BAD' take on the lore, W5 could have had an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> What if the PCs first change and basically have to figure out things on their own. Digging up old lore of the Nation where they can find it and trying to repair spirit relations with what skills they have.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't even take away from the intended villany of the Nation, as the PCs could uncover old wrongs and TRY to figure out how to fix them.<br /> <br /> Basically, play up the ignorance and don't go out of your way stating which lore is bad, what factions are evil etc. Let the PCs decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in the book, though, Garou are stated to be the bad guys, nor the Nation to be villainous. <br /> <br /> They are both said to have failed at their duty to save Gaia from the Wyrm, and the Litany is said to be something easily abused.<br /> <br /> Which, I would say, is surely a shift in tone from the prior editions, but it's not something unseen or unknown before. Or a huge stretch like casting the Garou as villains. To be fair, the genocidal role of the Garou in the War of Rage is greatly reduced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 08-19-2023, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T11:56:44-07:00","id":1520967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520660#post1520660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its ultimately because w5 wants to be v5. The Get and spiral are the v5 Sabbat/inquisition the broken localised guys are the anarchs, the garou nation are the carmarilla the wyrm is a a vague cosmic force like the 3rd gen.<br /> its the same reason w5 doesn't like umbral adventutes-the game is supposed to be street like v5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, the book is not written like this. <br /> <br /> There is a fairly relevant chapter about the Umbra, and llot hooks about the Umbra are costantly underlined and brought about. I would say most of the plot hooks presented in the book involve spirits.<br /> <br /> The marked difference is in a reboot of the Umbra concept and in a lore element<br /> <br /> 1. Reboot- The Umbra doesn't have a map or a geography, it's a shadow of our world but it's marked by different events, so it is constantly changing; you are not traveling in different Umbral realms with a map, you are reaching a place of spiritual importance and enter the Umbra to deal with the relevant spirits<br /> <br /> 2. Lore- The Umbra is suffering at human hands, so it's strengthtening the Gauntlet to try separate itself from the ever growing power of the Wyrm in the real world<br /> <br /> the Garou Nation is not something distinct from the players, and it's not even depicted particularly bad, it's a preApocalypse alliance which was shattered by continued defeats and the walkouts of Fenris and Stargazers, and whose laws (the Litany) were abused by ingenious leaders.<br /> <br /> The setup is much closer, I'd say, to a Year Zero game (the Fria Ligan post apocaliptic signature game) , where you defend and reclaim your territory, and clear the Umbra.<br /> <br /> BSDs are presented as nihilists, not just corrupted monsters, and Cult of Fenris as a cautionary lesson in militant factionalism and extremism.<br /> <br /> Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld are not vague, they are cosmic forces, but the influence and presence of their spirits is the moving force of the game.<br /> <br /> By the way, &quot;street level&quot; doesn't really mean &quot;everything is fucked, you as well, just hide to survive&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is presented as &quot; Build your legend fighting for your territory&quot;. You are not gonna charge in the maws of the Wyrm, but you are gonna do the very same things you were doing in earlier editions, you are just assumed to do them in your hunting ground, instead of globetrotting around the Amazons.<br /> <br /> (And still, the game says you can go globetrotting around if you want)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 08-19-2023, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T12:30:55-07:00","id":1520968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520966#post1520966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere in the book, though, Garou are stated to be the bad guys, nor the Nation to be villainous.<br /> <br /> They are both said to have failed at their duty to save Gaia from the Wyrm, and the Litany is said to be something easily abused.<br /> <br /> Which, I would say, is surely a shift in tone from the prior editions, but it's not something unseen or unknown before. Or a huge stretch like casting the Garou as villains. To be fair, the genocidal role of the Garou in the War of Rage is greatly reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is everywhere in the book. Look how the Litany is discussed, count the times the garou are written as incompetent or randomly forgetting important details when others don't.<br /> <br /> Especially in the Litany section, look at the laws of the Litany and then look how it is said to be used. Then take note how the philodox auspice is not mentioned once nor is ragabash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T12:34:50-07:00","id":1520969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520968#post1520968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is everywhere in the book. Look how the Litany is discussed, count the times the garou are written as incompetent or randomly forgetting important details when others don't.<br /> <br /> Especially in the Litany section, look at the laws of the Litany and then look how it is said to be used. Then take note how the philodox auspice is not mentioned once nor is ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being bad at saving the world is not the same as being bad, that's my point \ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> The Litany is said to have been abused, just like every Constitution in the world, that doesn't mean Constitutions are bad. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 08-19-2023, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:42:15-07:00","id":1520976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520969#post1520969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being bad at saving the world is not the same as being bad, that's my point \ud83d\ude03<br /> <br /> The Litany is said to have been abused, just like every Constitution in the world, that doesn't mean Constitutions are bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the book is not offering a discussion. It is stating facts and leads you towards one conclusion about the garou.<br /> <br /> The Litany section is a great example of this for me. It is presenting the way the Litany is abused, but it isn't discussing the positive sides nor bringing up that the philodox are responsible for interpreting the Litany and ragabash have a duty to question it. It only brings up the negatives and leaves out the positives and the freedom a philodox has in applying the law. Because W5's focus is on presenting the garou as incompetent first, PCs second.<br /> <br /> Basically, there is a difference between presenting a group as flawed and omitting information to prove they are flawed. W5 does the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:54:00-07:00","id":1520978,"title":"","content":"In previous editions, the Garou were anti-heroes. Their brutality, violence, and danger to innocent bystanders was countered by the overwhelming importance of their fight.<br /> <br /> When you take away the &quot;heroic&quot; parts, an anti-hero just becomes a villain. If the Garou are so bad at everything they're supposed to be doing, they're just a bunch of ticking time-bombs of Rage fueled murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:57:30-07:00","id":1520979,"title":"","content":"Weaver and Wyld in W5 are treated with a tone of pronounced superficiality in an effort to remove interesting bits of past lore (Drones or Gorgons are never mentioned, for example). Also, the street level perspective is heavily enforced by the book literally making assumptions about your chosen mode of play (street level and taking care of a caern). Other modes are mentioned... but the book is very clear what it wants players to do instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T14:00:10-07:00","id":1520981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520978#post1520978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions, the Garou were anti-heroes. Their brutality, violence, and danger to innocent bystanders was countered by the overwhelming importance of their fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is still the case, and repeated times and times in the book. The book is just stressing the &quot;so far, we were losing&quot; side more than in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T14:19:49-07:00","id":1520982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520981#post1520981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is still the case, and repeated times and times in the book. The book is just stressing the &quot;so far, we were losing&quot; side more than in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;More than the past&quot; is an understatement of the tone and thematic approach to Garou in the book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T14:23:08-07:00","id":1520983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be fair, the book is not written like this.<br /> <br /> There is a fairly relevant chapter about the Umbra, and llot hooks about the Umbra are costantly underlined and brought about. I would say most of the plot hooks presented in the book involve spirits.<br /> <br /> The marked difference is in a reboot of the Umbra concept and in a lore element<br /> <br /> 1. Reboot- The Umbra doesn't have a map or a geography, it's a shadow of our world but it's marked by different events, so it is constantly changing; you are not traveling in different Umbral realms with a map, you are reaching a place of spiritual importance and enter the Umbra to deal with the relevant spirits<br /> <br /> 2. Lore- The Umbra is suffering at human hands, so it's strengthtening the Gauntlet to try separate itself from the ever growing power of the Wyrm in the real world</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a locking off of the potential for the Weaver to be the party at fault and the villain. This takes something very important away from the setting, and positions the Wyld as less troubled. This has decreased the possibilities for conflict.<br /> <br /> Also, the Umbra being indistinct just doesn't work out well. If it's really the soul of the world, it ought to be a bit more substantive, especially since its well-being in the prior lore kept the physical world from crumbling. Spirit was viscerally important because without it, Matter could not last.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Garou Nation is not something distinct from the players, and it's not even depicted particularly bad, it's a preApocalypse alliance which was shattered by continued defeats and the walkouts of Fenris and Stargazers, and whose laws (the Litany) were abused by ingenious leaders.<br /> <br /> The setup is much closer, I'd say, to a Year Zero game (the Fria Ligan post apocaliptic signature game) , where you defend and reclaim your territory, and clear the Umbra.<br /> <br /> BSDs are presented as nihilists, not just corrupted monsters, and Cult of Fenris as a cautionary lesson in militant factionalism and extremism. </div> </div> </div>The last bit also does not make fucking sense, and we all know that it's just a thin wallpaper over Karim's desire to make the Swords of Heimdall the dominant portion of the Get. Somehow. In spite of being very, very dead and generally as capable, it seems, as the Neo-Nazis from Black Lagoon. After all, we didn't hear many casualties when the Get fell on them like a hammer. Well, not for the main body of Fenrir; just the Swords, at near 100%. And afterword, if anyone had any sympathies for the fallen, they made sure to keep their damned shameful heads down and shut the fuck up.<br /> <br /> De-platforming - it works!<br /> <br /> Also, the BSDs are never worth listening to. They don't have any greater depth, and it doesn't serve the narrative to try and make them look deep and meaningful. They've decided that the world is already gone, and so, to them, it is, along with everything that might be worth preserving. This is not the truth, but they believe it. Looking at the self-loathing of the Wyrm, they became infected by it, and are more tools for it to blindly lash out at the world to try and free itself from a prison it can no longer comprehend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld are not vague, they are cosmic forces, but the influence and presence of their spirits is the moving force of the game. </div> </div> </div>And somehow their influence isn't something that can be read or sensed in the slightest? Not even one track from where the Weaver bound everything too tightly, or where the Defiler squirmed through more easily for it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, &quot;street level&quot; doesn't really mean &quot;everything is fucked, you as well, just hide to survive&quot;. </div> </div> </div>In this game, it does, because the street is a dangerous place, and being de-powered and having capability removed makes the protagonists significantly more vulnerable. You absolutely need that cool head in Crinos to not be a temporary thing, because this is a game about a war, and wars require going the distance with your armor on, because the consequences of taking it off are way worse. Just another way trying to match it on Vampire systems is doing it a grave disservice. Vampire is holding it back from what it could be, and here, it's a particularly strong and visible binding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is presented as &quot; Build your legend fighting for your territory&quot;. You are not gonna charge in the maws of the Wyrm, but you are gonna do the very same things you were doing in earlier editions, you are just assumed to do them in your hunting ground, instead of globetrotting around the Amazons.<br /> <br /> (And still, the game says you can go globetrotting around if you want) </div> </div> </div>Who the hell is going to remember your legend? Who, in a setting where the talekeepers aparently don't bother to remember anything? Your legend will be washed away by some inept Galliard's weekly consumption of Natty Light or Schlitz. There are no ancestors to contact, and no spirits with a sworn pact to recognize your achievements. When they took the Nation away, Renown stopped being a sensible Trait to keep. As something external, it has no holder in this setting. Keeping a measure of spiritual connection would have made way more sense, because it existed internally for all the Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> But no. Renown, somehow. Probably only because of Forsaken. None of these mechanical bits is really original; they're just adapted from Paradox, from Humanity, from every game that's about as far thematically from W:tA as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T14:26:06-07:00","id":1520984,"title":"","content":"My copy just came in, and it looks like they went cheap on the printer, like they used the standard option from Drive-through. All the art is washed out, and darker.<br /> BTW I'm comparing the quality to Used 1st Edition Pathfinder and my old NWoD/CoD and my 2nd AD&amp;D books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T14:59:13-07:00","id":1520985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be fair, the book is not written like this.<br /> <br /> There is a fairly relevant chapter about the Umbra, and llot hooks about the Umbra are costantly underlined and brought about. I would say most of the plot hooks presented in the book involve spirits.<br /> <br /> The marked difference is in a reboot of the Umbra concept and in a lore element<br /> <br /> 1. Reboot- The Umbra doesn't have a map or a geography, it's a shadow of our world but it's marked by different events, so it is constantly changing; you are not traveling in different Umbral realms with a map, you are reaching a place of spiritual importance and enter the Umbra to deal with the relevant spirits<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The umbra was previously a place you could/had to visit for days, weeks or even years. Lot of characters in the lore were lost in it for decades if not centuries, with at least one lupus losing himself somewhen during the middle ages and getting back on earth in modern day.<br /> <br /> Now you have to use a willpower point every scene to not take damages for simply being there. It's a clear indication that the devs want the games to be little involved with the umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Lore- The Umbra is suffering at human hands, so it's strengthtening the Gauntlet to try separate itself from the ever growing power of the Wyrm in the real world<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> My, oh my. Another massive reboot. This goes against the nature of the umbra and the gauntlet. The umbra doesn't have a will. At most, the only reference to some sort of desire is when the game states that the worlds of flesh and spirit yearn to join again.<br /> <br /> And the gauntlet was never an umbra thing, it was directly created by the Weaver, and it's strenghtening by human presence not because &quot;human bad&quot; but because humans attracts weaver spirits that strenghen the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Also, the umbra tries to &quot;separate itself from the wyrm power in the material world&quot;? But the Wyrm is a spiritual presence. If it's present in our world, it is by necessity equally present in the umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Garou Nation is not something distinct from the players, and it's not even depicted particularly bad, it's a preApocalypse alliance which was shattered by continued defeats and the walkouts of Fenris and Stargazers, and whose laws (the Litany) were abused by ingenious leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> That makes it sound like the Fenrir and Stargazers were fundamental pillars of the nation. Going against every previous lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld are not vague, they are cosmic forces, but the influence and presence of their spirits is the moving force of the game.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> But that was always the case. This description match every edition of the game, what actually changed?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520967#post1520967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, &quot;street level&quot; doesn't really mean &quot;everything is fucked, you as well, just hide to survive&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is presented as &quot; Build your legend fighting for your territory&quot;. You are not gonna charge in the maws of the Wyrm, but you are gonna do the very same things you were doing in earlier editions, you are just assumed to do them in your hunting ground, instead of globetrotting around the Amazons.<br /> <br /> (And still, the game says you can go globetrotting around if you want)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that sounds like &quot;everything is fucked&quot;. The apocalypse was always a global problem, analoguous to climate change. Going local makes no sense. Charging in the maws of the Wyrm IS the solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T15:59:59-07:00","id":1520990,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520985#post1520985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My, oh my. Another massive reboot. This goes against the nature of the umbra and the gauntlet. The umbra doesn't have a will. At most, the only reference to some sort of desire is when the game states that the worlds of flesh and spirit yearn to join again.<br /> <br /> And the gauntlet was never an umbra thing, it was directly created by the Weaver, and it's strenghtening by human presence not because &quot;human bad&quot; but because humans attracts weaver spirits that strenghen the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Also, the umbra tries to &quot;separate itself from the wyrm power in the material world&quot;? But the Wyrm is a spiritual presence. If it's present in our world, it is by necessity equally present in the umbra..<br /> <br /> <br /> That makes it sound like the Fenrir and Stargazers were fundamental pillars of the nation. Going against every previous lore. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for your lore losses, but as this is a reboot, things do contradict old lore. <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520985#post1520985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that sounds like &quot;everything is fucked&quot;. The apocalypse was always a global problem, analoguous to climate change. Going local makes no sense. Charging in the maws of the Wyrm IS the solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, ask the White Howlers how did it go the last time they charged in the maws of the Wyrm. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T16:04:52-07:00","id":1520992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520990#post1520990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry for your lore losses, but as this is a reboot, things do contradict old lore.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>A reboot without a cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, yes, ask the White Howlers how did it go the last time they charged in the maws of the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>You mean when they decided to rush in without waiting for anyone else to even field a second opinion? When they thought that the Apocalypse was nigh and jumped the gun? That time?<br /> <br /> If you don't go in trying to dance the spiral labyrinth, you might just fare better. It certainly seemed to be possible with prep in more than one Apocalypse scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T16:19:42-07:00","id":1520994,"title":"","content":"I can mostly say that much of your fears are dealt with and solved in the core book, I will try to answer in detail below. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520983#post1520983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a locking off of the potential for the Weaver to be the party at fault and the villain. This takes something very important away from the setting, and positions the Wyld as less troubled. This has decreased the possibilities for conflict.<br /> <br /> Also, the Umbra being indistinct just doesn't work out well. If it's really the soul of the world, it ought to be a bit more substantive, especially since its well-being in the prior lore kept the physical world from crumbling. Spirit was viscerally important because without it, Matter could not last.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no party at fault, or at least the Garou do not have a clear indication of who's the fault for Wyrm ascendancy. <br /> <br /> There are those think it's the Humies' fault, those who think it's the Weaver's, those who think &quot;ehy, it's the cosmic cycle&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is laid out pretty clearly in the Tribes' sections and again stressed in the Umbra section. <br /> <br /> The Wyld is also quite troublesome, as it basically positioned as the source of natural catastrophes. <br /> <br /> The Umbra is not indistinct, nor separate from the world. It's literally the reflection of our world and of its most important elements. <br /> <br /> So, the point is, most of the time to interact with the Umbra you just need to summon the spirits, to go in the Umbra it is to enter their kingdom, which is probably something you are going to do for climax. <br /> <br /> It's different from the past? Yes. But the setting and the game are still animistic, I would say more so than the old &quot;Multiverse&quot; Umbra. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520983#post1520983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last bit also does not make fucking sense, and we all know that it's just a thin wallpaper over Karim's desire to make the Swords of Heimdall the dominant portion of the Get. Somehow. In spite of being very, very dead and generally as capable, it seems, as the Neo-Nazis from Black Lagoon. After all, we didn't hear many casualties when the Get fell on them like a hammer. Well, not for the main body of Fenrir; just the Swords, at near 100%. And afterword, if anyone had any sympathies for the fallen, they made sure to keep their damned shameful heads down and shut the fuck up.<br /> <br /> De-platforming - it works!<br /> <br /> Also, the BSDs are never worth listening to. They don't have any greater depth, and it doesn't serve the narrative to try and make them look deep and meaningful. They've decided that the world is already gone, and so, to them, it is, along with everything that might be worth preserving. This is not the truth, but they believe it. Looking at the self-loathing of the Wyrm, they became infected by it, and are more tools for it to blindly lash out at the world to try and free itself from a prison it can no longer comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;WE ALL KNOW WHAT KARIM WANTED&quot; and what is actually written in the book are two different things. <br /> <br /> Fascism as a Fenris connection gets mentioned in the Appendix on Fascism, at the end of the book, literally in the line of the Cult as a cautionary tale. There is probably a sarcastic connection in the Get loresheet, with one level named &quot;Bootlicker&quot; and that's all.<br /> <br /> Nowhere are Nazi werewolves mentioned, nowhere the Sword of Heimdall is ever mentioned, nowhere the Fenris are White Suprematists. <br /> <br /> They are a metaphor for AltRight radicalization? Very much so. But never are Nazis or Heimdall presented, and if you are a newbie player or someone who doesn't know a lot about them, you will never know. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520983#post1520983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And somehow their influence isn't something that can be read or sensed in the slightest? Not even one track from where the Weaver bound everything too tightly, or where the Defiler squirmed through more easily for it? </div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot &quot;detect evil&quot; at will, but the core of the game is exactly to discover these things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520983#post1520983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this game, it does, because the street is a dangerous place, and being de-powered and having capability removed makes the protagonists significantly more vulnerable. You absolutely need that cool head in Crinos to not be a temporary thing, because this is a game about a war, and wars require going the distance with your armor on, because the consequences of taking it off are way worse. Just another way trying to match it on Vampire systems is doing it a grave disservice. Vampire is holding it back from what it could be, and here, it's a particularly strong and visible binding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core math of the game is different, and Gifts are still strong power multipliers. So in the ruleset of 5th edition, Garous are still combat monkeys. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520983#post1520983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Who the hell is going to remember your legend? Who, in a setting where the talekeepers aparently don't bother to remember anything? Your legend will be washed away by some inept Galliard's weekly consumption of Natty Light or Schlitz. There are no ancestors to contact, and no spirits with a sworn pact to recognize your achievements. When they took the Nation away, Renown stopped being a sensible Trait to keep. As something external, it has no holder in this setting. Keeping a measure of spiritual connection would have made way more sense, because it existed internally for all the Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> But no. Renown, somehow. Probably only because of Forsaken. None of these mechanical bits is really original; they're just adapted from Paradox, from Humanity, from every game that's about as far thematically from W:tA as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the corebool doesn't tell you everything which has happened before doesn't mean there isn't memory. <br /> <br /> That the Garou have strong oral traditions is repeatedly stressed. As they are not a single culture anymore, these stories vary by Tribe and Caern. <br /> <br /> Also, Spirits are very much bound by duties, contracts and obligations with Garou, it's the central Gift mechanic and repeatedly stressed in the Umbra, Gift and Renown sections. <br /> <br /> So, really... I understand you don't like the tone of the game, its development and developers, and it's fair. <br /> <br /> But many of your critics are not aimed at the actual product, but at its public perception and supposed behind the door drama. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T17:47:11-07:00","id":1520997,"title":"","content":"I've read the book cover-to-cover by this point. And this is a &quot;reboot&quot; that mostly just exists to wave towards things in the original while actively locking players out of getting to do anything with them, mechanically enforce the idea that the Garou of past editions were incompetent villains (it doesn't have to outright say this if every single thing about Garou in the book heavily implies this and the entire rage dice/harano/hauglosk system is built around it), and we should all just play Vampire: the Masquerade 5th Edition 2: This Time It's Werewolves because Paradox thinks anything more complicated than that will apparently melt the fragile brains of modern TTRPG players. Not to mention all the racism and other gross things that went on behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> I'm open to the idea of a fresh start to clear out the vast pileup of metaplot, but this lazy, spiteful showing ain't it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 08-19-2023, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T20:03:27-07:00","id":1521004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520990#post1520990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry for your lore losses, but as this is a reboot, things do contradict old lore.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they should have called it &quot;Werewolf the Apocalypse: revamped&quot;. Not pretend it's a new edition.<br /> <br /> At this stage, it's clearly an attempt to sell the poorly imagined games that the authors wanted to make by surfing on the success and reputation of the previous ones.<br /> <br /> It's especially terrible because with their new lore, even ignoring the original game, their cosmology makes no sense.<br /> Just look at this very exemple. W5 keeps claiming that garou are being of spirits and flesh.<br /> But if that's the case, why the world of spirits target them as soon as they stay a few hours in? And if that's the case, how did garou ever achieve anything in the umbra?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520990#post1520990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yes, ask the White Howlers how did it go the last time they charged in the maws of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The garou made multiple successful attacks on Malfeas. The most known exemple is when they were tricked into attacking the prison of Ananasa. That and all the maeljins, the pretty litteral heads of the hydra, are all killable. <br /> Charging into Malfeas with clear objectives is actually the best tactic as far as stopping the Apocalypse goes. W20 gives a pretty list of clear target that would impede the Wyrm if eliminated. Including the entrance to the black spiral labyrinth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T00:44:04-07:00","id":1521013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1520990#post1520990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry for your lore losses, but as this is a reboot, things do contradict old lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>As was discussed on this thread before, what helped CofD to grow into its own was bringing new ideas and concepts to the table and embrace those rather than ruminating on the old WOD. Concepts like &quot;The wolf must hunt.&quot; for WtF, for example. With W5 it feels like we're right back in time and we witness the same issues yet again that plagued CofD 1E at the beginning back then. Too many ties to the legacy games, underdeveloped new ideas or uninteresting new takes on old ideas etc. ...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T23:13:12-07:00","id":1521099,"title":"","content":"At the very core of this all, the problem with W5 is that it is not really clear what of its lore the players should use and see as positive.<br /> <br /> Ignore all the 'this is why the garou are bad' and what exactly is left to use? You are a werewolf with spirit powers and you must protect sacred places from threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T00:16:37-07:00","id":1521102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521099#post1521099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very core of this all, the problem with W5 is that it is not really clear what of its lore the players should use and see as positive.<br /> <br /> Ignore all the 'this is why the garou are bad' and what exactly is left to use? You are a werewolf with spirit powers and you must protect sacred places from threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted H5 with its aversion to hunter-orgs in any form runs into a similar issue: So you're a local hunter-cell who has just taken out their first supernatural monster... and then what? You can upgrade your stuff and whatnot but at some point you're gonna run into other hunter-orgs or become more hunter-like maybe even - but those are fundamentally evil in H5. Or at least that's how the H5 corebook sees it. Because the supplement Lines Drawn By Blood written by the Renegade writers team isn't quite as extreme in how hunter-orgs are portrayed. So it wouldn't surprise me if the first W5 supplement written by the Renegade team takes its foot off the gas in really hammering home how dysfunctional and bad Garou are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T00:34:45-07:00","id":1521103,"title":"","content":"More than anything, I just wish the 5th editions would just commit to being completely fresh starts instead of dangling all the interesting past lore over players' heads and then telling them that, no, you can't be trusted with this kind of stuff. The hunter-orgs are there, but they're all evil and bad and you don't want to be a bad person, do you? You don't want to play this game the wrong way, right? Stay in your little circle of friends and pick off the occasional caitiff. Here's this entire spirit world that you're told your Garou character is fundamentally a part of. Except no, that might not <i>really</i> be the truth and besides we've made it to where you die if you stay there for more than a few hours. We're going to hint at all this vast history and lore but you don't get to know about any of it, because your character is stupid and incompetent. Go back to fighting over caerns. There's two big warring vampire factions, one of which explores trying to navigate a new society of barely-contained monsters while not letting humans know and another that embraces their new bestial state, but like. They're too complicated for you. You should play the faction that does nothing but dick around fighting over turf.<br /> <br /> These games are just so small to the point where there really isn't anything to do. There's nothing wrong with small-scale games, but WoD5e has a way of being so condescending about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T00:53:53-07:00","id":1521105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521103#post1521103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More than anything, I just wish the 5th editions would just commit to being completely fresh starts instead of dangling all the interesting past lore over players' heads and then telling them that, no, you can't be trusted with this kind of stuff. The hunter-orgs are there, but they're all evil and bad and you don't want to be a bad person, do you? You don't want to play this game the wrong way, right? Stay in your little circle of friends and pick off the occasional caitiff. Here's this entire spirit world that you're told your Garou character is fundamentally a part of. Except no, that might not <i>really</i> be the truth and besides we've made it to where you die if you stay there for more than a few hours. We're going to hint at all this vast history and lore but you don't get to know about any of it, because your character is stupid and incompetent. Go back to fighting over caerns. There's two big warring vampire factions, one of which explores trying to navigate a new society of barely-contained monsters while not letting humans know and another that embraces their new bestial state, but like. They're too complicated for you. You should play the faction that does nothing but dick around fighting over turf.<br /> <br /> These games are just so small to the point where there really isn't anything to do. There's nothing wrong with small-scale games, but WoD5e has a way of being so condescending about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the whole reboot-thing doesn't work, to begin with, when you come in with hot takes like &quot;All hunter-orgs are evil.&quot; and &quot;The Get are an evil Tribe who have to be antagonists.&quot;. These writers had the freedom of it being a reboot and yet there's still so much here that clings to the legacy-stuff, wants to comment on it, &quot;correct&quot; it or something. For example, Karim Muammar's opinion on the Get of Fenris adds <i>nothing </i>to the game once it has become a reboot. The only reason to make that Tribe antagonists is that KM wants to have a meta-dialogue with previous editions while to the edition he's writing on, it's nothing but a hindrance. Rather than considering the rebooted setting and making that work, W5 is stuck making comments on previous editions. Or how &quot;anybody can join any Tribe&quot; makes more sense as a comment from the writers about what they think of previous WtA editions than an actual bit of worldbuilding that makes sense in the W5 setting.<br /> <br /> The overall lore and worldbuilding in W5 without the context of previous editions is terrible. A lot of concepts don't seem very well-thought-out or are undercut by the consistent lack of effort to create a setting for these werewolf-characters to live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:02:36-07:00","id":1521108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521105#post1521105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or how &quot;anybody can join any Tribe&quot; makes more sense as a comment from the writers about what they think of previous WtA editions than an actual bit of worldbuilding that makes sense in the W5 setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its also genrally not true, firstly the previous edition restrictions were far less strict than has genrally been presented.<br /> <br /> Red talon- no homid (metis permitted)<br /> <br /> Black furies- no male lupus or homid.<br /> <br /> Silver fangs- pure breed over 2.<br /> <br /> That's pretty much the only hard rules. Everything else is open with some basic writting for example my very british jamican ex could easily qualify as fianna with her Irish grandmother and extrovert artistic personality. To say nothing of a totem liking the cut of your gib regardless.<br /> <br /> Its also not strictly speaking true that anyone anyone be any tribe even in w5, unless you're deliberately being subversive their are plenty of characters who won't fit into a tribe for example a luddite glass walker or a humanitarian red talon. So it's a bit of a none statement over all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:38:52-07:00","id":1521109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521108#post1521108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its also genrally not true, firstly the previous edition restrictions were far less strict than has genrally been presented.<br /> <br /> Red talon- no homid (metis permitted)<br /> <br /> Black furies- no male lupus or homid.<br /> <br /> Silver fangs- pure breed over 2.<br /> <br /> That's pretty much the only hard rules. Everything else is open with some basic writting for example my very british jamican ex could easily qualify as fianna with her Irish grandmother and extrovert artistic personality. To say nothing of a totem liking the cut of your gib regardless.<br /> <br /> Its also not strictly speaking true that anyone anyone be any tribe even in w5, unless you're deliberately being subversive their are plenty of characters who won't fit into a tribe for example a luddite glass walker or a humanitarian red talon. So it's a bit of a none statement over all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the next issue right there: One, it's based on a bad understanding of the lore from previous editions. Two, it's inconsistently applied and not really thought through in terms of what this means specifically for W5 worldbuilding. This sentiment is the basis for removing the Younger and Older Brother Tribe as we know it and changing the Black Furies to be focused on injustice in general. But what about describing Silver Fangs as an &quot;aristocratic&quot; Tribe despite all the changes? Or sticking with the focus on wolves with Red Talons? That's a real one-two-punch for any WtA-fan right there: First, it presents the reader with an insufficient understanding of old lore and second the new lore feels half-assed and underdeveloped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:56:17-07:00","id":1521113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521109#post1521109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Furies to be focused on injustice in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>something that occurs is that injustice us a reactive to a somewhat subjective concept. For example a mob lynching of an sex offender can be percieved as both just and unjust depending on an individuals outlook. Philopsohers and legalists have struggled with the nature of justice since forever (to say nothinh of the possibility justice doesnt exist). This leaves the tribe somewhat rudderless. The writters would probably suggest this is an opertunity to reflect on what in/justice is but this denies the fandom a collective idea of what black furies stand for and expects a lot out if the players.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-21-2023, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T03:04:33-07:00","id":1521114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521113#post1521113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> something that occurs is that injustice us a reactive to a somewhat subjective concept. For example a mob lynching of an sex offender can be percieved as both just and unjust depending on an individuals outlook. Philopsohers and legalists have struggled with the nature of justice since forever. This leaves the tribe somewhat rudderless.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Does it though? Their ideals of justice just like their outlooks fit in well with the presented &quot;Garou fuck things up&quot; and &quot;Garou don't have tools to do anything but violence&quot;. It makes the Black Furies reactionary and deeply split. One could easily argue that a group of Proud Boys Black Furies is viable with this outlook, as they are &quot;only there to protect western culture and oppressed values from the corrupt system&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T04:11:10-07:00","id":1521119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521114#post1521114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it though? Their ideals of justice just like their outlooks fit in well with the presented &quot;Garou fuck things up&quot; and &quot;Garou don't have tools to do anything but violence&quot;. It makes the Black Furies reactionary and deeply split. One could easily argue that a group of Proud Boys Black Furies is viable with this outlook, as they are &quot;only there to protect western culture and oppressed values from the corrupt system&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly if the objective is to discredit the tribe which is an.....interesting choice for a tribe previously established as advocates of women.<br /> <br /> Yeah Proud boys would be an obvious example of the vagueness of injustice. Terfs too, tankies even. Historically oppressors try to frame themselves as oppressed, St augustine stated that the existence of non believers is an oppression.<br /> <br /> I mean theoretically their isn't really a great deal from stopping a gm from assuming a truly grotesque outlook as acceptable. The &quot;no fascists allowed&quot; is ultimately can't really be enforced and their plenty of nasty ugly outlooks which arnt fascist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-21-2023, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T05:09:40-07:00","id":1521122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521119#post1521119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly if the objective is to discredit the tribe which is an.....interesting choice for a tribe previously established as advocates of women's.<br /> <br /> Yeah Proud boys would be an obvious example of the vagueness of injustice. Terfs too, tankies even. Historically oppressors try to frame themselves as oppressed, St augustine stated that the existence on non believers is an oppression.<br /> <br /> I mean theoretically their isn't really a great deal from stopping a gm from assuming a truly grotesque outlook as acceptable. The &quot;no fascists allowed&quot; is ultimately can't really be enforced and their plenty of nasty ugly outlooks which arnt fascist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also really doesn't help matters that the Black Fury tribe description in the book says that a good number of them become Social Darwinists. Which is uhhh pretty much the exact opposite thing you'd expect from a tribe supposedly focused on &quot;injustice&quot;. In fact it's pretty damn fascist. But it's only fascism when the Fenrir do it, I guess.<br /> <br /> I still wonder what the goal was to make the game spiteful to this level. Newbies aren't given anything appealing to latch onto because the game really wants you to know that Garou are pointless, and as a long-time player the mere fact that this game would let you use Proud Boy as a reasonable Black Fury concept because &quot;injustice&quot; is so poorly-defined and the whole social darwinism thing makes my skin crawl. Too much time is spent over-correcting and whining about perceived flaws from previous editions to hold any appeal for anyone coming over from VtM5e. Who is this game even for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T06:04:09-07:00","id":1521124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521122#post1521122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still wonder what the goal was to make the game spiteful to this level. Newbies aren't given anything appealing to latch onto because the game really wants you to know that Garou are pointless, and as a long-time player the mere fact that this game would let you use Proud Boy as a reasonable Black Fury concept because &quot;injustice&quot; is so poorly-defined and the whole social darwinism thing makes my skin crawl. Too much time is spent over-correcting and whining about perceived flaws from previous editions to hold any appeal for anyone coming over from VtM5e. Who is this game even for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think its more bad writting than anything. Black furies as classically written had some darker impulses (misandry, terfs etc) so a logically 5th Black Furies will to. The trouble is since w5 lacks a well defined frame of referance of what is 'good' to the tribe it means that both in and out the universe.<br /> To give you an example me and my partner recently disagreed on the punishment for teenage girps who committed a monstrous crime (attempted human sacrifice). I felt her indefinate incarceration was too severe for a number of issues while my partner believed it just. Considering we largely have very simular views on morality. Realistically how is the clan supposed to have a cohesive identity?<br /> <br /> I suppose they could be going for werewolf brujah but the brujah deliberately align with radical philosophies in general and opposition to the ventrue and its been a huge detriment to the clan. Both in game and out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T06:45:41-07:00","id":1521128,"title":"","content":"You'll note the removal of female empowerment groups or factions or writing them as extremist or incompetent is pretty standard for X5 properties so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T11:50:11-07:00","id":1521139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521128#post1521128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note the removal of female empowerment groups or factions or writing them as extremist or incompetent is pretty standard for X5 properties so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the cultural question theory is correct, it should come as no surprise that they do the same with political groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T13:46:19-07:00","id":1521148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521124#post1521124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think its more bad writting than anything. Black furies as classically written had some darker impulses (misandry, terfs etc) so a logically 5th Black Furies will to. The trouble is since w5 lacks a well defined frame of referance of what is 'good' to the tribe it means that both in and out the universe.<br /> To give you an example me and my partner recently disagreed on the punishment for teenage girps who committed a monstrous crime (attempted human sacrifice). I felt her indefinate incarceration was too severe for a number of issues while my partner believed it just. Considering we largely have very simular views on morality. Realistically how is the clan supposed to have a cohesive identity?<br /> <br /> I suppose they could be going for werewolf brujah but the brujah deliberately align with radical philosophies in general and opposition to the ventrue and its been a huge detriment to the clan. Both in game and out</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, didn't mean to imply that the Furies never had negative aspects or extremists before. They clearly did, but they were at least consistent with the tribe's core idea before. It's more the idea that the way they're doing it here makes no sense and runs so counter to what the tribe once was while still keeping the name that I wondered why they even bothered.<br /> <br /> I think you're onto something with the Brujah thing, though. Shame they didn' t seem to learn anything from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T01:28:14-07:00","id":1521167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521148#post1521148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, didn't mean to imply that the Furies never had negative aspects or extremists before. They clearly did, but they were at least consistent with the tribe's core idea before. It's more the idea that the way they're doing it here makes no sense and runs so counter to what the tribe once was while still keeping the name that I wondered why they even bothered.<br /> <br /> I think you're onto something with the Brujah thing, though. Shame they didn' t seem to learn anything from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True I think its ultimately bad writting, they knew they had an idea of what they wanted to do with the tribes and they were just unable to pull it off.<br /> <br /> yeah the brujah have simular issues as do the anarchs in general (freedom rather than justice but simular problems) wod has the weird thing were they both romantise dissidence and rebellion (to an absurd degree) but seem unable to give then definitive objectives or wins.<br /> the furies in previous editions had a better established objective as a dissident underdog group. They could even reflect that things have improved for women over the centuries and discussion on transgender women is a solid plot hook. Frankly black furies in previous edition did what 5th ed wants to do better than they do now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T02:06:26-07:00","id":1521169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521167#post1521167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True I think its ultimately bad writting, they knew they had an idea of what they wanted to do with the tribes and they were just unable to pull it off.<br /> <br /> yeah the brujah have simular issues as do the anarchs in general (freedom rather than justice but simular problems) wod has the weird thing were they both romantise dissidence and rebellion (to an absurd degree) but seem unable to give then definitive objectives or wins.<br /> the furies in previous editions had a better established objective as a dissident underdog group. They could even reflect that things have improved for women over the centuries and discussion on transgender women is a solid plot hook. Frankly black furies in previous edition did what 5th ed wants to do better than they do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutley. I don't endorse the Proud Boys Furies as a concept, I'm just confused how is that a fully viable concept for who the Furies used to be and stand for. They were fighting for good causes and had darker and questionable facets that could provoke a discussion or conflict in ways that would enhance play.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T03:10:37-07:00","id":1521172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521169#post1521169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, absolutley. I don't endorse the Proud Boys Furies as a concept, I'm just confused how is that a fully viable concept for who the Furies used to be and stand for. They were fighting for good causes and had darker and questionable facets that could provoke a discussion or conflict in ways that would enhance play.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its more a meta observation, the proud boys are more an extreme example of how weak the vague appeal to injustice is a more normal example would be say my mothers view child molesters should be executed vs my own disapproval of the death penalty both understandable as justice but irreconcilable.<br /> Its a very vague concept, now you could go existentialist and say it's up the individual but this is unsatisfying for a tribe collectively dedicated to the idea.<br /> <br /> Wereas women's rights while very complex is a clear solid banner to rally around.<br /> <br /> to clarify on my own thoughts on the previous edition Furies I really liked the terf issue within the tribe partly because I like some wrongs to right and it opens up to the more complex ideas of what it means to be a woman. I would have also liked to see how the tribe reacted to sex positive femminism or difficulties of intersectional praxis. If we're going to do 'woke' let's actually do woke and not arse around with vagueries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T03:28:21-07:00","id":1521174,"title":"","content":"From what James Sambrano has written there were two issues at play that laid the groundwork for the version we got in this book: The first was Karim Muammar's surface reading of the Black Furies as the &quot;feminist Tribe&quot;. There's a lot more going on with the Black Furies in the lore than them just being a bunch of feminist activists. The second issue is that the professed solution was to get away from politics. And I guess &quot;injustice&quot; doesn't seem &quot;political&quot; in the immediate sense so that's why that was the chosen alternative. But of course, if you start to think about what sort of topics and themes are covered by something as broad as &quot;injustice&quot;, ironically the Tribe isn't getting away from human politics but is being dragged into that arena even more now. With the focus on womanhood, you also could connect it to its place in mystical and occult lore - so that it isn't about human politics all the time. &quot;Injustice&quot;, though...? That topic always gets political quickly once you try to apply it to any given situation. Like, for example, having a weird take on justice and survival in nature and then coming up with something troubling like &quot;social Darwinism&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I still can't get over the fact that they ran away from feminism only to bring up that &quot;numerous&quot; members of the Tribe believe in social Darwinism... what a boneheaded idea...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T04:04:55-07:00","id":1521178,"title":"","content":"I see that train of thought clearly. The problem for me is even more with the words &quot;percieved injustice&quot;. If they were a tribe od judges that dealt with the ideal of justice - i.e. euthanatos meets Nagah meets lords of doom - they would be less open to negative interpretations and relativity of justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T04:31:39-07:00","id":1521179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521178#post1521178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that train of thought clearly. The problem for me is even more with the words &quot;percieved injustice&quot;. If they were a tribe od judges that dealt with the ideal of justice - i.e. euthanatos meets Nagah meets lords of doom - they would be less open to negative interpretations and relativity of justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm gonna take &quot;Euthanatos meets Nagah&quot; as my fanon for Black Furies now lol (dunno who the lords of doom are) - they'll be about divine vengeance and holy retribution much like their Tribal namesake, with Pegasus serving as a calming and balancing influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T04:37:09-07:00","id":1521180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521174#post1521174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (I still can't get over the fact that they ran away from feminism only to bring up that &quot;numerous&quot; members of the Tribe believe in social Darwinism... what a boneheaded idea...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Im beginning to wonder if they actually know what social darwinism considering they also suggested the lasombras defection from the Sabbat (surrendering massive amounts of power, credabilty, dignity, ideology, long term objectives and dying in massive numbers for a position at the botton of the totem pole) was something the clan would be okay with because they're social darwinists.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they think it means &quot;survive&quot; rather than what it actually means.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T05:07:42-07:00","id":1521181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521179#post1521179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'm gonna take &quot;Euthanatos meets Nagah&quot; as my fanon for Black Furies now lol (dunno who the lords of doom are) - they'll be about divine vengeance and holy retribution much like their Tribal namesake, with Pegasus serving as a calming and balancing influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a camp of Shadow Lords that has a similar creed to the Nagah. They hunt and judge those who are not judged by Garou Justice.<br /> <br /> And if you like that connection, consider that the Erineyes/Furies are cthonic goddesses of justice and vengeance to the unjust. They could easily be the central totem of the new Black Furies. And if you want a more singular figure you have the three defined Erineyes - Megaera, Tisiphone and Aelecto. Or even the links with Demeter and Nyx.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T08:53:55-07:00","id":1521190,"title":"","content":"Just the idea of trying to ' get away from politics' in a game like WtA that is so inherently political right down to its core bamboozles the living fuck out of me.<br /> <br /> Was there no one telling the Developers ' If your not up to the task its ok to hand it on to someone else' because they very clearly were not up to the task and persisted regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T09:00:12-07:00","id":1521191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521190#post1521190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the idea of trying to ' get away from politics' in a game like WtA that is so inherently political right down to its core bamboozles the living fuck out of me.<br /> <br /> Was there no one telling the Developers ' If your not up to the task its ok to hand it on to someone else' because they very clearly were not up to the task and persisted regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, consider that Paradox already dealt with ONE political kerfluffle.<br /> <br /> But what JS has revealed of the second try at W5, it seems like the focus was on removing any positive political stuff and keeping the negative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T09:03:51-07:00","id":1521192,"title":"","content":"James Sambrano went on a podcast (together with &quot;A Bunch Of Gamers&quot; and Josh Heath from High Level Games who used to host a Werewolf the Apocalypse podcast) talking about the W5 corebook and his experiences writing on the Hunters Entertainment version. I think this would be of interest to the readers of this thread as it gives more insight on this book and some design-choices, so here it is:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrH7EZXzWmw\" data-code=\"DrH7EZXzWmw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DrH7EZXzWmw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T13:19:09-07:00","id":1521219,"title":"","content":"THey addressed a lot of things that I've pondered about W5, even the 'Screw you guys I'm 0 Rage!&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, listening to them go through the tribes and pointing out auspices don't matter really showcases how little the tribes outside CoF mattered. There is so much stuff that is reliant on legacy knowledge to work.<br /> <br /> The Whip Poor Will being an omen of death in Indigenous cultures of the area it lives in is a good point. My main issue with WPW has always been that it is an American bird for a Scottish tribe, but we aren't given any in-between patrons for BSDs to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 08-22-2023, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T00:36:45-07:00","id":1521237,"title":"","content":"One idea that stuck out to me that I hadn't really considered before is how the whole pitch of &quot;The Garou of the past fucked up and now it's my place as a young Garou to fix it!&quot; lines up with the idea of &quot;white guilt&quot;. And it also connects to how there are no ancestor-spirits in W5 apparently.<br /> <br /> The way W5 also focuses mostly on humans being the reason for things being bad makes it unintentionally (or I hope it's that) seem like one of the big sins of the Garou is that they ever stopped with the Impergium.<br /> <br /> But another thing that shocked me a bit was when Josh Heath (who was one of the playtesters for W5) revealed that the Rage-Dice-mechanic we get in this book is a toned-down (!) version of what he played. Now it really makes sense why in one session where Outstar was the ST nobody changed into Crinos... Man, if previous versions were even harsher in making PCs involuntarily act out violently... It really feels like the overall direction of development was spearheaded by people more invested in &quot;settling a score&quot; with WtA (its past editions and lore) than actually developing an interesting game you'd wanna play.<br /> <br /> What's also interesting is how James Sambrano mentioned that the whole &quot;WOD5E has to be street-level&quot;-idea is handed down from Paradox. And at this point, I really gotta wonder how much of Justin Achilli's explanations for development-decisions were just PR-speak for Paradox as a company. Like, &quot;Fenrir are antagonists because of verbs.&quot; or when he said &quot;You can't tell personal stories when there are epic stakes like saving the world involved.&quot;... What truly was going on, though, was that Fenrir as antagonists was a remnant of the Hunter Entertainment version they were using without crediting anyone involved in that and the insistence on &quot;street-level-play&quot; was a Paradox corporate decision for the direction of the IP. In both cases, though, Justin Achilli pretended like the development-team made those decisions on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T01:40:11-07:00","id":1521239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521237#post1521237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's also interesting is how James Sambrano mentioned that the whole &quot;WOD5E has to be street-level&quot;-idea is handed down from Paradox. And at this point, I really gotta wonder how much of Justin Achilli's explanations for development-decisions were just PR-speak for Paradox as a company. Like, &quot;Fenrir are antagonists because of verbs.&quot; or when he said &quot;You can't tell personal stories when there are epic stakes like saving the world involved.&quot;... What truly was going on, though, was that Fenrir as antagonists was a remnant of the Hunter Entertainment version they were using without crediting anyone involved in that and the insistence on &quot;street-level-play&quot; was a Paradox corporate decision for the direction of the IP. In both cases, though, Justin Achilli pretended like the development-team made those decisions on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah the Paradox thing did surprise me, I'd assumed it was a decision established as some sort of private obessesion with Justin from his previous writtings.<br /> <br /> That certainly doesn't bode well for m5 if mismanagement is coming from the top.<br /> <br /> <br /> its also a little disheartening that justins dubious statements about are coming from corporate. Considering how white wolf started reminds me of how dissidence and counter culture has slowly become just another grift from some soulless Corp and writters I used to respect might just be a mouthpiece for them.<br /> <br /> .....I need a drink and it's only 11am","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-23-2023, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T02:06:26-07:00","id":1521240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521239#post1521239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah the Paradox thing did surprise me, I'd assumed it was a decision established as some sort of private obessesion with Justin from his previous writtings.<br /> <br /> That certainly doesn't bode well for m5 if mismanagement is coming from the top.<br /> <br /> <br /> its also a little disheartening that justins dubious statements about are coming from corporate. Considering how white wolf started reminds me of how dissidence and counter culture has slowly become just another grift from some soulless Corp and writters I used to respect might just be a mouthpiece for them.<br /> <br /> .....I need a drink and it's only 11am</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and it makes you wonder how much it even matters who the next lead-developer is gonna be. Not only are there corporate-mandated decisions involved in what WOD5E is like but you see in a case like Apocalyptic Record where the writers wanted to change some things (like renaming Tribes) and Paradox simply said no that these efforts by Paradox are also very heavy-handed. They don't bring writers on-board to have a discussion about the direction of WOD5E, they bring them aboard to merely turn a pre-planned vision for the IP into a sellable product, it seems.<br /> <br /> That really doesn't bode well for how things will develop for WOD5E in the future...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T04:31:14-07:00","id":1521246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521237#post1521237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea that stuck out to me that I hadn't really considered before is how the whole pitch of &quot;The Garou of the past fucked up and now it's my place as a young Garou to fix it!&quot; lines up with the idea of &quot;white guilt&quot;. And it also connects to how there are no ancestor-spirits in W5 apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the ancestor thing goes into a very Christian and scientific concept of things. It's not even Western, because there have been many ancestor-worshipping faiths here in Europe. There is this concept that since you can't scientifically prove that you can connect to your ancestors outside changes in genetics, they are only vague memories if even that. Or rather, they are a BURDEN upon you and their actions damn you.<br /> <br /> Essentially, there is no relationship with your ancestors, because they aren't ACTUALLY there.<br /> <br /> And while WtA had that, it also had a connection to one's history and heritage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T05:35:03-07:00","id":1521249,"title":"","content":"Its also probably worth noting in a meta sense you probably can't fix it. Afterall were on 30 years of the game now were the upcoming new generation youre playing as havnt been able to dent the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a meta sense it even speaks to a naivety about one's own responsibilities and the moral and intellectual purity of the current generation irl. Its up all of us to make things better not some idealised vision of the kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T05:41:56-07:00","id":1521251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521246#post1521246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the ancestor thing goes into a very Christian and scientific concept of things. It's not even Western, because there have been many ancestor-worshipping faiths here in Europe. There is this concept that since you can't scientifically prove that you can connect to your ancestors outside changes in genetics, they are only vague memories if even that. Or rather, they are a BURDEN upon you and their actions damn you.<br /> <br /> Essentially, there is no relationship with your ancestors, because they aren't ACTUALLY there.<br /> <br /> And while WtA had that, it also had a connection to one's history and heritage.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you don't have a religious aspect with ancestor-worship, you still got things like remembrance culture and how that's linked to national identity. And with Christianity... well, it always depends on what particular sort of Christianity we're talking about but there the focus is more on the afterlife.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it doesn't particularly matter because to me it doesn't feel like the W5 book is invested in any particular perspective on these matters. There's no deeper meaning to be grasped here other than the worldbuilding was sloppily put together. So you just get this mix of some default opinions and spur-of-the-moment hot takes that were thrown together to write this book. Then some corporate-mandates like &quot;Make it street-level&quot; and downplaying the Umbra are added and that's about it. James Sambrano mentioned this as well that along with all the vagueness in this book there are even basic questions like &quot;When did the Apocalypse start?&quot; that are never answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:18:41-07:00","id":1521384,"title":"","content":"Some more design thoughts from Justin:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img width=\"1162\" height=\"328\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/toGdWKI.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/toGdWKI.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/toGdWKI.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<img width=\"1165\" height=\"319\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6QgH700.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/6QgH700.jpg\" data