title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f_baloTGt5M\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;...here's the galliards and how they work...&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention Galiards.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1328\" height=\"72\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/NzESKgA.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/NzESKgA.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/NzESKgA.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <img width=\"1292\" height=\"48\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/YilgbbH.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/YilgbbH.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/YilgbbH.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:10:02-07:00","id":1521392,"title":"","content":"Oh man... It's the whole &quot;H5 is a heist-game&quot;-thing all over again. Also, he should just go on Outstar's show and talk about W5. Sure, he left his job with Paradox/WOD. But apparently, without Justin Achilli there isn't a single writer/developer of W5 who's willing to come on her show. And even if it's just PR-speak... but just letting your community-manager do a news-show online and then there isn't a single person from the WOD-team (after one person left) willing to come on and talk to her about W5... that's just sad.<ul><li>That &quot;religion vs god&quot;-thing is such a strange high-fantasy-conception of religion. You need a particular kind of fantasy-setting where you can be like &quot;Well, that's what you say, priest of god x. But before that... let me check in with your god and see what they think, okay...?&quot;</li> <li>And of course, religion in our world doesn't work like that. Even in legacy WtA Garou didn't just constantly go to Gaia questioning her on what she wants Garou to do.</li> <li>His stance on mysteries is way too extreme as exhibited by this book. I can understand the intention. A pbtA-game doesn't want to delve too deeply into a setting and it's more about setting up parameters for a genre or sub-genre narrative (and leaving lots of room in the worldbuilding for people at the table to fill out). Honestly, if that's his actual beliefs and that's the kind of games he wanted to make, then taking on the mantle of developing the new edition of WOD-games was possibly the worst choice he could've made.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:34:39-07:00","id":1521394,"title":"","content":"Honestly, JA can talk all he wants, it is clear a lot of his stuff comes from way higher up.<br /> <br /> Also, if one of your auspices is a historian/tale teller, that history does need to be fleshed out. Same with when there is a lawkeeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T12:05:58-07:00","id":1521400,"title":"","content":"I mean, he put lore in airquotes... It really does seem like he's at a point where he believes games shouldn't have <i>any lore</i>. Or at least that's what it feels like reading these comments and what he has said in the last few years.<br /> <br /> If that is another thing Paradox mandates (while JA tries to obscure this), then WOD5E will just be bad... Every time a new 5th edition version of a splat comes out we're just gonna come here and list all the ways WOD5E has got it all wrong again. And at the same time, WOD5E can't do its own thing because it's supposed to be WOD5E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T14:33:48-07:00","id":1521402,"title":"","content":"Why is Justin even commenting ( not that I'm sure any of that waffle counts as commenting)? He left.<br /> <br /> All these comments really do is absolutely nail down that he and Karim never actually read the books.....or if they did didn't recall any of it past early 2nd Ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T14:47:05-07:00","id":1521403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521402#post1521402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Justin even commenting ( not that I'm sure any of that waffle counts as commenting)? He left.<br /> <br /> All these comments really do is absolutely nail down that he and Karim never actually read the books.....or if they did didn't recall any of it past early 2nd Ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered the same thing myself months ago when he re-started the whole &quot;Fenrir are antagonists because of verbs&quot;-thing. And even before that, he had a very strange PR-strategy of just posting on Twitter willy-nilly, it seemed. Whatever caught his fancy that day, he would just talk about it. There was no PR-strategy to it. Sometimes he would suddenly respond to a comment from another Twitter-user.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can understand why he's still doing this: You don't see Karim Muammar or Khaldoun Khelil doing any PR-work. Jason Carl is only doing V5. Not really sure why it is like that but without Justin Achilli there's apparently nobody on the WOD-team who wants to step into the public and talk about what the development-process of W5 has been like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:00:02-07:00","id":1521405,"title":"","content":"I think Justin is proud of his baby and feels obligated to explain what and why they did. It's how he is. And I'm glad for the insights but we shouldn't read anything about his character there. Just about the design decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:14:46-07:00","id":1521407,"title":"","content":"There's a reason lots of game designers differentiate between lore and fluff, based on a simple criteria: can a player use this information in play. If yes, it's lore, and you should put it in. If no, it's fluff, and you can get rid of it. W5 is choking on fluff by trying to be &quot;mysterious&quot; since what few things it does say, are things players can really use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T15:21:52-07:00","id":1521411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521174#post1521174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what James Sambrano has written there were two issues at play that laid the groundwork for the version we got in this book: The first was Karim Muammar's surface reading of the Black Furies as the &quot;feminist Tribe&quot;. There's a lot more going on with the Black Furies in the lore than them just being a bunch of feminist activists. The second issue is that the professed solution was to get away from politics. And I guess &quot;injustice&quot; doesn't seem &quot;political&quot; in the immediate sense so that's why that was the chosen alternative. But of course, if you start to think about what sort of topics and themes are covered by something as broad as &quot;injustice&quot;, ironically the Tribe isn't getting away from human politics but is being dragged into that arena even more now. With the focus on womanhood, you also could connect it to its place in mystical and occult lore - so that it isn't about human politics all the time. &quot;Injustice&quot;, though...? That topic always gets political quickly once you try to apply it to any given situation. Like, for example, having a weird take on justice and survival in nature and then coming up with something troubling like &quot;social Darwinism&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I still can't get over the fact that they ran away from feminism only to bring up that &quot;numerous&quot; members of the Tribe believe in social Darwinism... what a boneheaded idea...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I think this is enough to avoid problems, after all they are not claiming anything, technically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T13:41:32-07:00","id":1521444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521403#post1521403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026 You don't see Karim Muammar or Khaldoun Khelil doing any PR-work. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness to Khaldoun he\u2019s a freelancer, not a WoD staff member. In addition, like several folks who freelanced on the book, he put out a couple of tweets talking about it when it came out. Promoting the book isn\u2019t a freelancer\u2019s job though, that\u2019s why WoD/Paradox presumably has an advertising budget and social media people. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T01:09:52-07:00","id":1521454,"title":"","content":"Did anyone like the V5 and H5 go on sales?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T01:21:04-07:00","id":1521455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521444#post1521444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fairness to Khaldoun he\u2019s a freelancer, not a WoD staff member. In addition, like several folks who freelanced on the book, he put out a couple of tweets talking about it when it came out. Promoting the book isn\u2019t a freelancer\u2019s job though, that\u2019s why WoD/Paradox presumably has an advertising budget and social media people.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I was just thinking if not Justin Achilli, who else could you put on the WOD-news to talk about the development of W5. It just seems strange to me that since Justin Achilli isn't doing it, there's nobody else who could do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521411#post1521411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I think this is enough to avoid problems, after all they are not claiming anything, technically.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Only question is then why use the kind of terminology you found in that section in the first place? On one page the Age of Apocalypse is described as the &quot;Capitalocene era&quot;, on another, you get a sidebar explaining how companies and accumulations of capital aren't bad by definition and how the whole thing is an &quot;emotional issue&quot;, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T03:44:20-07:00","id":1521460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521454#post1521454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone like the V5 and H5 go on sales?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tons of people liked V5 when it came out. That's why there were holy wars. I don't think anyone cared about H5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T05:08:53-07:00","id":1521462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521460#post1521460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tons of people liked V5 when it came out. That's why there were holy wars. I don't think anyone cared about H5.</div> </div> </div> </div>pretty much V5 was a game which slowly undermined itself with bad release after bad release. The corebook had some really neat idea's which needed refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T05:11:07-07:00","id":1521463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521462#post1521462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> pretty much V5 was a game which slowly undermined itself with bad release after bad release. The corebook had some really neat idea's which needed refinement.</div> </div> </div> </div>And world's worst layout for a high end release <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-27-2023, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T06:00:45-07:00","id":1521466,"title":"","content":"I find it really sad that W5's core concept is so great for many different types of examination of the Nation. The problem is that the book doesn't want you to do THAT.<br /> <br /> Like, I might just write this up as a proper setting, but the Nation fractures and now 50 years has passed. A bunch of cubs get the mission to unite the Nation once more. The problem is that within those 50 years, what being a garou is has changed and there is no longer one answer.<br /> <br /> There are garou who refuse their wolf entirely and treat what they have as a sickness.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are damned and so embrace their Rage every full moon to commit atrocities.<br /> <br /> There are garou who feel God gave them a mission to hunt down evildoers and so they do. Whether they capture the right ones is another question entirely.<br /> <br /> There are garou who see their new state as a blessing and bully others to get what they want.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are Stolen Moons ascended, performing a ritual 'correctly' and now trying to get their followers to ascend as well.<br /> <br /> And this is just using basic werewolf lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T10:26:18-07:00","id":1521471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521466#post1521466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it really sad that W5's core concept is so great for many different types of examination of the Nation. The problem is that the book doesn't want you to do THAT.<br /> <br /> Like, I might just write this up as a proper setting, but the Nation fractures and now 50 years has passed. A bunch of cubs get the mission to unite the Nation once more. The problem is that within those 50 years, what being a garou is has changed and there is no longer one answer.<br /> <br /> There are garou who refuse their wolf entirely and treat what they have as a sickness.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are damned and so embrace their Rage every full moon to commit atrocities.<br /> <br /> There are garou who feel God gave them a mission to hunt down evildoers and so they do. Whether they capture the right ones is another question entirely.<br /> <br /> There are garou who see their new state as a blessing and bully others to get what they want.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are Stolen Moons ascended, performing a ritual 'correctly' and now trying to get their followers to ascend as well.<br /> <br /> And this is just using basic werewolf lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, I find these reactions quite realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T10:45:29-07:00","id":1521472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521471#post1521471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worse, I find these reactions quite realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and it creates a lot of drama. How do you explain to someone who thinks they are without control that eating humans is bad? Or to someone who had RELISHED on the ability to feed on corpses when other food was unavailable.<br /> <br /> Or things like fighting the Wyrm, Respecting the territory of others or not killing others in a challenge?<br /> <br /> And how tenous and fragile is the trust in a Nation, and how its past can easily drive others off.<br /> <br /> But in order to have this setting, there first has to be value in the Litany and in a Nation in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T12:12:32-07:00","id":1521476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521466#post1521466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it really sad that W5's core concept is so great for many different types of examination of the Nation. The problem is that the book doesn't want you to do THAT.<br /> <br /> Like, I might just write this up as a proper setting, but the Nation fractures and now 50 years has passed. A bunch of cubs get the mission to unite the Nation once more. The problem is that within those 50 years, what being a garou is has changed and there is no longer one answer.<br /> <br /> There are garou who refuse their wolf entirely and treat what they have as a sickness.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are damned and so embrace their Rage every full moon to commit atrocities.<br /> <br /> There are garou who feel God gave them a mission to hunt down evildoers and so they do. Whether they capture the right ones is another question entirely.<br /> <br /> There are garou who see their new state as a blessing and bully others to get what they want.<br /> <br /> There are garou who think they are Stolen Moons ascended, performing a ritual 'correctly' and now trying to get their followers to ascend as well.<br /> <br /> And this is just using basic werewolf lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what I would add is have all these factions as a category of werewolves who are focused on the material world but then you have a whole other category of werewolves who work with Spirits. Those are remnants of Garou-traditionalists, those who are lost to the Triat in some fashion (BSD, Cyberdogs/Weaver, something &quot;Cult of Fenris&quot;-esque but more grounded) and just all the werewolves who have a Patron-Spirit. And now Patron-Spirits who used to be stewards of Garou-Tribes are overseeing cults or more disorganized followings and the Patron-Spirits in this apocalyptic era have gone insane or have become &quot;weird&quot; to various degrees as well. But the Patron-Spirits are so disoriented and deranged to various degrees that your Pact as werewolf with them is also partly about helping them make sense of the world and making sure they listen more to werewolves with some common sense then the ones who abuse the Patron-Spirit's trust or don't sufficiently fight back against or correct the bad qualities/behaviors of the Patron-Spirit.<br /> <br /> And another category I also think would be interesting is a pack of young Garou whose Patron-Spirit is an ancestor-spirit (maybe related to one of the werewolf-PCs or maybe not) - but bring in the ideals of Garou as well as their failings through a ghost-mentor-figure. It's a bit hokey but personally I think it's a neat little roleplaying-scenario that requires less buy-in than roleplaying being a Garou who has to navigate Garou-society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T14:20:41-07:00","id":1521479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521472#post1521472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, and it creates a lot of drama. How do you explain to someone who thinks they are without control that eating humans is bad? Or to someone who had RELISHED on the ability to feed on corpses when other food was unavailable.<br /> <br /> Or things like fighting the Wyrm, Respecting the territory of others or not killing others in a challenge?<br /> <br /> And how tenous and fragile is the trust in a Nation, and how its past can easily drive others off.<br /> <br /> But in order to have this setting, there first has to be value in the Litany and in a Nation in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep imagining, for some reason, someone sending this argument to one of the developers and he replying that you are free to make the game with that thought in mind, but other people will prefer not to delve into it and want something lighter and more action-packed, while a third group will prefer to be a group of herds that patrol the streets, another that struggles to survive, another to discover the mysteries of the supernatural little by little and that is the game's proposal, thus satisfying all tastes, both old and new players.<br /> <br /> After that it doesn't necessarily need the Garou nation or the litany, only groups even if smaller and isolated have an already established common sense for these matters, for example, it would be as if each city or territory had a prince or baron as in VTM, and they established rules of coexistence and common sense and they are responsible for the newcomers that appear in their territory, in one way or another. Of course, they don't need to be from a larger sect, just a group that defends a hunting ground or haven.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T15:40:42-07:00","id":1521483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521479#post1521479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep imagining, for some reason, someone sending this argument to one of the developers and he replying that you are free to make the game with that thought in mind, but other people will prefer not to delve into it and want something lighter and more action-packed, while a third group will prefer to be a group of herds that patrol the streets, another that struggles to survive, another to discover the mysteries of the supernatural little by little and that is the game's proposal, thus satisfying all tastes, both old and new players.<br /> <br /> After that it doesn't necessarily need the Garou nation or the litany, only groups even if smaller and isolated have an already established common sense for these matters, for example, it would be as if each city or territory had a prince or baron as in VTM, and they established rules of coexistence and common sense and they are responsible for the newcomers that appear in their territory, in one way or another. Of course, they don't need to be from a larger sect, just a group that defends a hunting ground or haven.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine for Vampire, but Werewolf is fundamentally not Vampire. Vampire is about squatting in the world and cornering temporal powers to make your existence easier in power games with other vampires; it is about perpetuating stasis. Werewolf is about a desperate battle to break some center of your foes' power, to gain a toehold in a war; it is about fighting stasis to produce change, even when the Garou Nation doesn't change all that much. This is even without the more expansive parts that make Vampire's perspective seem so small and empty - the spiritual world, the twisted nature of the cosmos, the trust that exists among Garou that Vampire never even get near.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, this is like &quot;Blue Does Not Understand Orange&quot;. Diehard Vampire LARPists, as it turns out, make for terrible tabletop book developers working on a complementary and not very orthogonal setting. Rather than accept the differences and let the games breathe like they used to, they have decided that everything has to be remade to suit Vampire, and only Vampire, with any themes of their own washed away and forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T22:48:10-07:00","id":1521493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521483#post1521483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fine for Vampire, but Werewolf is fundamentally not Vampire. Vampire is about squatting in the world and cornering temporal powers to make your existence easier in power games with other vampires; it is about perpetuating stasis. Werewolf is about a desperate battle to break some center of your foes' power, to gain a toehold in a war; it is about fighting stasis to produce change, even when the Garou Nation doesn't change all that much. This is even without the more expansive parts that make Vampire's perspective seem so small and empty - the spiritual world, the twisted nature of the cosmos, the trust that exists among Garou that Vampire never even get near.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, this is like &quot;Blue Does Not Understand Orange&quot;. Diehard Vampire LARPists, as it turns out, make for terrible tabletop book developers working on a complementary and not very orthogonal setting. Rather than accept the differences and let the games breathe like they used to, they have decided that everything has to be remade to suit Vampire, and only Vampire, with any themes of their own washed away and forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense, but it's that thing, if V5 worked then let's launch V5 with a werewolf skin and see if it works, and at least here where I live it seems to be working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T10:38:05-07:00","id":1521517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521493#post1521493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes sense, but it's that thing, if V5 worked then let's launch V5 with a werewolf skin and see if it works, and at least here where I live it seems to be working.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plural of &quot;anecdote&quot; is not &quot;data&quot;, and even if it's selling okay now...where is the staying power? H5 seems to have evaporated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T10:45:39-07:00","id":1521518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521517#post1521517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The plural of &quot;anecdote&quot; is not &quot;data&quot;, and even if it's selling okay now...where is the staying power? H5 seems to have evaporated.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do we even know if it is selling? The book isn't out yet for a few days, unless you preordered it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T11:07:35-07:00","id":1521520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521518#post1521518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do we even know if it is selling? The book isn't out yet for a few days, unless you preordered it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, if they had actually sold all the physical copies they had at GenCon we would've heard about it... shrug... but other than that... who knows...<br /> <br /> I mean, one of the biggest impediments both H5 and W5 face is the comparatively expensive Renegade-pricing for these books. Not only will people on the internet probably immediately tell you that you should pick HtV 2E over H5 but the difference in prices also impacts that choice.<br /> <br /> With the official W5 release date coming up this week, I'm also wondering if this is when more official reviews from various outlets/websites will show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T12:23:42-07:00","id":1521523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521518#post1521518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do we even know if it is selling? The book isn't out yet for a few days, unless you preordered it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly thought it had...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T14:19:15-07:00","id":1521534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">After years of seeing a certain subsection of the fanbase inundate social media with posts about the supposed poor sales of CofD I can't really find anything but skepticism anymore when it comes to sales talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the only sure thing is &quot;however many get solid, it's probably nowhere near as many as the 5e PHB&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T14:47:20-07:00","id":1521535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521517#post1521517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The plural of &quot;anecdote&quot; is not &quot;data&quot;, and even if it's selling okay now...where is the staying power? H5 seems to have evaporated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that, but seeing it makes me skittish anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T15:19:33-07:00","id":1521698,"title":"","content":"I wish Justin wrote all of this into a blog.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1525\" height=\"804\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5L5PO3N.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5L5PO3N.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5L5PO3N.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <img width=\"1523\" height=\"118\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T15:59:27-07:00","id":1521699,"title":"","content":"Still baffled by Justin's design-philosophy... I get what he's trying to do. I always got the sense what he wants to do is some sort of story-first game with a blank-space setting and the game is mainly setting up a framework for people at the table to create the setting through collaborative storytelling. The problem is that at the time he signed up to WOD5E V5 had already set up a different paradigm for what WOD5E looks like. Not to mention the expectations that are summoned by invoking all the old WOD-lines like HtR and WtA. If it were all up to him, he would've run in the opposite direction as quickly as possible... away from the lore, the mechanics, the legacy... all of it. But alas, the situation with WOD5E is quite different and so we got H5 (with its hard anti-hunter-org-stance while abandoning the original premise of HtR) and W5 (with its hard aversion to &quot;lore&quot; of any kind to the point that it doesn't even want to touch Garou-history with a ten-foot-pole).<br /> <br /> I guess, maybe it wasn't surprising he ended up quitting prematurely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T17:18:21-07:00","id":1521706,"title":"","content":"The design philosophy works fine when you're making a new gameline (such as when White Wolf rolled out CofD). It doesn't work nearly as well when you take an existing gameline with decades of lore that fans and players have been following and you throw it all in the trash. Wizards of the Coast attempted to do this with 4th edition D&amp;D, throwing much of the lore of the Forgotten Realms in the trash because they felt it was too difficult for new players to get into the setting. They ended up losing many of the old players who were invested in the setting but did not gain the number of new players to balance out the loss. During that time period D&amp;D was dethroned as the best selling RPG on the market, and when 5th edition rolled around they immediately began reverting most of those lore changes and started bringing back the material that the long-time players enjoyed. <br /> <br /> I suspect you'll see something similar with W5, where it will be considered less successful than W20, especially as word of mouth gets around to fans about the significant retcons and changes they've made to the setting the lore - that this is so different it's less of a new edition building on what existed and more of a game taking pieces of the lore but being set in a parallel universe. Rather than being V5, which is a direct continuation to the gameline, W5 is a bit closer in many respects to H5 - it's a very different game that just uses some of the old ideas and names to pull in fans of the previous work but it isn't meant to be a continuation of the old game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T19:02:43-07:00","id":1521715,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure he realises from the last bit that giving players no guidance or boundaries just leads to decision paralysis and providing essentially no setting info foists everything onto the ST.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how new STs are supposed to know how to run this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T19:17:43-07:00","id":1521717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521715#post1521715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure he realises from the last bit that giving players no guidance or boundaries just leads to decision paralysis and providing essentially no setting info foists everything onto the ST.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how new STs are supposed to know how to run this.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T19:44:42-07:00","id":1521720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521715#post1521715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure he realises from the last bit that giving players no guidance or boundaries just leads to decision paralysis and providing essentially no setting info foists everything onto the ST.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how new STs are supposed to know how to run this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same problem that a lot of CofD (especially 1e) games had. Like I love Promethean to death, but even my game troupe, with over a decade of experience running TTRPGs, has a lot of trouble actually playing it and one of the big reasons why is that it just gives STs almost no useful guidance, just drowning them under waves of fluff while also giving very little structure. But at least Promethean's fluff is very engaging. Even if the game is very hard to run, I still want to make Promethean characters. W5 not only gives players, new or old, nothing to work with, but also spends most of its time harping on the perceived flaws of previous editions. Old players are offended, and new players have no idea what half of these references are or why the text is so inconsistent and negative.<br /> <br /> I guess people will still play it in the sense that a lot of TTRPG players refuse to engage with anything but the newest editions of anything. But I do sincerely hope this game fails on word of mouth because new players really do deserve better than this.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside I don't really care for his implying that people not liking WoD5e are &quot;grognards&quot;. WoD as a whole has, in my experience, been one of the least grognard-y TTRPG communities out there. Maybe 5e just isn't very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 08-31-2023, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T20:53:35-07:00","id":1521722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521715#post1521715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure he realises from the last bit that giving players no guidance or boundaries just leads to decision paralysis and providing essentially no setting info foists everything onto the ST.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how new STs are supposed to know how to run this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also leads too why the hell should I buy your book, if I have to do all the work I'm paying you for.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I'm wrong but I thought the point of buying your book, was so that I had something to actually work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3647-eric-ericson","name":"Eric Ericson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T21:28:48-07:00","id":1521725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Ericson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521722#post1521722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also leads too why the hell should I buy your book, if I have to do all the work I'm paying you for.<br /> <br /> Forgive me if I'm wrong but I thought the point of buying your book, was so that I had something to actually work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels backwards to me too. It's like the idea is that it's easier for STs, especially new STs, to create a deep and enticing setting filled with lore, than it is to simply ignore the parts of the setting or lore that you don't like. As an ST I've never had any issue with ignoring parts of the setting I don't care for and replacing pieces of it with my own. But coming up with all (or most) of the lore and the setting for a gameline is incredibly daunting. That's why I prefer games with already existent settings and lore that I can modify than games where you get the mechanics but little to no useable lore. <br /> <br /> Ultimately I believe it's better for games to include a section that says, &quot;Your game, your rules. Everything in here are ideas and tools for you to use, but you can, and should, ignore, change or modify any part of the game, settings or mechanics that you don't like. You have our permission and any players who are unhappy with that should find a new ST.&quot; I think that's better than dropping the burden of the creative process into the lap of the ST, especially new STs who are still trying to get a handle on the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T00:25:58-07:00","id":1521731,"title":"","content":"I've had the pleasure of experiencing when WtF was released and I have my core from the first printing. I know how a new Werewolf game coming out feels.<br /> <br /> But WtF 1st ed. for all its faults, still made me want to create characters for the game. It still gave me an idea of a potential story.<br /> <br /> W5's lore is actively harmed by the book constantly pushing for ignorance. It isn't leaving holes for the ST and players to fill stuff in, it is actively saying you should not bother. I point at the way the Litany is presented once more, it isn't giving a neutral &quot;some abuse it, some don't&quot; explanation. Instead, we are told the Litany is all about abuse and younger garou ignore it and Elders abuse it.<br /> <br /> Basically, it might not be saying it outright, but it is clearly still saying this; The Litany is bad and you should not bother with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T01:46:12-07:00","id":1521732,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand how he even can claim that this was his design-philosophy and that he saw it through with this game. After all, it immediately got undermined when Paradox mandated the game had to be street-level only and then Karim Muammar brought in his ideas from the Hunter Entertainment version (like the Fenrir having to be antagonists). And the whole desire for offering a broad framework that gets filled in by the people at the table just gets further undermined by the game being called Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> With the Litany, he probably would've preferred two or three very broad rules (Like &quot;Fight the Wyrm&quot;, &quot;Keep your existence secret from humanity&quot; and &quot;Protect Gaia and caerns&quot;) and then just vaguely added &quot;Depending on what Tribe is dominant various Septs add additional rules linked to what the local threats are.&quot;. But since it's still a game called WtA, he instead got saddled with &quot;The Litany&quot;. And as a setting-element it's probably way too detailed for his tastes, so what gets focused on instead how it can be circumvented/ignored in the game in order to not &quot;take control away from the people at the table&quot; or that's how it seems he looks at something like that.<br /> <br /> And despite the disclaimer this book still has a lot of &quot;continuation&quot; in its DNA but instead of trying to get away from that by coming up with new stuff, the book is just constantly trying to undermine all the legacy-stuff that is still very present in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T03:44:22-07:00","id":1521740,"title":"","content":"I particularly grate at the idea that &quot;nay-sayers&quot; can't have valid opinions because we've never played this specific game. The conflation of how many people bought old WW books to read them instead of play with them has no bearing on those of us that played the games for decades and our ability to apply that experience to the new edition and spot flaws.<br /> <br /> I have played in some for or another 15 different iterations of the same family of rules (I'm counting Storypath here, but only once). I've had characters that I played for almost a decade of continuous play. I've lost count of how many stories, settings, and so on I've been part of building through these games. If I read a new WoD/CofD/Exalted/etc. book and immediately nope out of it without giving it a try... it's for better reasons than what he's using to justify his statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T04:30:51-07:00","id":1521741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521732#post1521732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand how he even can claim that this was his design-philosophy and that he saw it through with this game. After all, it immediately got undermined when Paradox mandated the game had to be street-level only and then Karim Muammar brought in his ideas from the Hunter Entertainment version (like the Fenrir having to be antagonists). And the whole desire for offering a broad framework that gets filled in by the people at the table just gets further undermined by the game being called Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> With the Litany, he probably would've preferred two or three very broad rules (Like &quot;Fight the Wyrm&quot;, &quot;Keep your existence secret from humanity&quot; and &quot;Protect Gaia and caerns&quot;) and then just vaguely added &quot;Depending on what Tribe is dominant various Septs add additional rules linked to what the local threats are.&quot;. But since it's still a game called WtA, he instead got saddled with &quot;The Litany&quot;. And as a setting-element it's probably way too detailed for his tastes, so what gets focused on instead how it can be circumvented/ignored in the game in order to not &quot;take control away from the people at the table&quot; or that's how it seems he looks at something like that.<br /> <br /> And despite the disclaimer this book still has a lot of &quot;continuation&quot; in its DNA but instead of trying to get away from that by coming up with new stuff, the book is just constantly trying to undermine all the legacy-stuff that is still very present in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its the contradictions are a byproduct of two things<br /> <br /> 1) theirs a very clear corporate mandate on what w5 should be with mind to franchise building as part of wod rather than a project in its own right.<br /> <br /> 2)a lot of statements from the game designers are explicitly corporate pr and cannot be taken as factual or even in extreme cases, relavent.<br /> <br /> <br /> On reflection i think its clear that paradox are slowly becoming another ea or Activision so should be treated with a degree of disdain. I probably won't be buying their products going forward on any front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-31-2023, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T04:48:45-07:00","id":1521742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521741#post1521741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its the contradictions are a byproduct of two things<br /> <br /> 1) theirs a very clear corporate mandate on what w5 should be with mind to franchise building as part of wod rather than a project in its own right.<br /> <br /> 2)a lot of statements from the game designers are explicitly corporate pr and cannot be taken as factual or even in extreme cases, relavent.<br /> <br /> <br /> On reflection i think its clear that paradox are slowly becoming another ea or Activision so should be treated with a degree of disdain. I probably won't be buying their products going forward on any front.</div> </div> </div> </div>A third point might be that what also can't be acknowledged is that W5 ended up like this because they rushed the development of this version as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T05:04:15-07:00","id":1521743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521698#post1521698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img width=\"1523\" height=\"118\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>He does know that, indirectly, this means 5th Edition doesn't even say thanks to previous players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T05:40:11-07:00","id":1521744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521743#post1521743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He does know that, indirectly, this means 5th Edition doesn't even say thanks to previous players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its also worth noting it's ultimately incorrect. W5 isn't newbie friendly at all. It's vaguely written, railroady relies heavily of meta knowledge of how the games 'supposed' to be played and has the usual issues of wod mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T05:58:16-07:00","id":1521745,"title":"","content":"W5 requires an insane amount of WtA knowledge for a new edition.<br /> <br /> For one, how to play auspice.<br /> <br /> For another, Silent Striders are Cursed... how? And why keep that in?<br /> <br /> How BSDs function is entirely left vague, when knowing how they function would make that loresheet a bit bigger of a thing.<br /> <br /> Things aren't left vague in a way that helps worldbuilding, because it is still the crust of WtA... but all the breadmeat is removed. You can stuff the crust, sure, but only the breadmeat of the crust fills it well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T22:33:22-07:00","id":1521948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521743#post1521743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He does know that, indirectly, this means 5th Edition doesn't even say thanks to previous players?</div> </div> </div> </div>The: By Contrast WOD20 are the &quot;ones with everything<br /> <br /> Should tell everything about the way paradox is using the IP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T01:41:14-07:00","id":1521958,"title":"","content":"I ran at a local convention the ready-made adventure in th corebook.<br /> I used the pre-gen advice in the back of the corebook, and assembled a 5-Auspices Pack with a Black Fury Ahroun, a Ghost Council Theurge, a Silver Fang Philodox, a Galestalker Galliard and a Children of Gaia Ragabash.<br /> <br /> Their day-to-day identities were a eco-activist back from London, a midwife, a local gentry, a closeted artist and the local constabulary (I set the game in a generic English shire).<br /> <br /> I have passing knowledge of the old setting (what Tribes, Triat and Auspices are, I'm more versed in Pentex subsidiaries and Fomori because I use them in VtM too; for instance, I have a very confuse idea of how the old Umbra was meant to work, and zero knowledge of old Gifts or Renown mechanics).<br /> <br /> \u200bNo player at the table was familiar with old WtA or Wod5e, they had all played old VtM.<br /> <br /> Introduction to the setting was quick and in broad strokes, they had &quot;something&quot; manifesting in them, became aware of the spirit world and of their dual nature, and their tribal spirits found and lead them to others of their choice for mentorship. This was framed as background info, with then a quick explanation of the Triat, of the losing battle against the Wyrm, and of the dissent within the Garou Nation, including dissenting opinions whether it was better to wait the end, cull the humans, or charge into the Wyrm's maw.<br /> <br /> I presented the Auspices as &quot;traditional society&quot; roles, and Garou as a warlike culture, and the characters as a small group of newbies tending to a self-assigned territory. I didn't present all the Tribes, only the existence of other Spirit Totems and of their shared cultures.<br /> <br /> The adventure ran smoothly, I just skipped the Cult of Fenris part due to time running out.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, the only main subsystems we didn't have the chance to use were Harano / Hauglosk and Chagrin. Rage Economy worked quite easily, with some negotiations between me and the players on how to acquire it.<br /> <br /> Brutal Outcomes recurred three times, two of them in dealing with the Spirits and one in combat. I portrayed the Spirit outcomes as the Spirits resentful of general Garou defeats in defending their homelands and particularly of not preventing the Bane from infesting the area, it led to quite an heated verbal confrontation with characters.<br /> The Combat Brutal Outcome was when they were trying yo deal with the newly transformed Werewolf, and I made them trample her poor husband, leaving him seriously injured.<br /> <br /> They used Crinos twice, to stop the new Wolf and to crush the Bane, and Glabro once.<br /> <br /> I relied, in descriptions, on the fact that they have richer perceptions and can superficially perceive the presence of the Spirit World, and this led them to interact a lot with Spirits and the Umbra, using Gifts and Rites. The presence of Weaver-themed Gifts and the Ghost Council ambiguity towards studying what had allowed the Bane to enter the World created some small interesting tensions between the Theurge, the Ragabash and the Ahroun.<br /> <br /> All in all, my experience with both setting and rules worked well. I will run the game again in a couple of sessions to my regular V5 group of newbies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-03-2023, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1259