oice for mentorship. This was framed as background info, with then a quick explanation of the Triat, of the losing battle against the Wyrm, and of the dissent within the Garou Nation, including dissenting opinions whether it was better to wait the end, cull the humans, or charge into the Wyrm's maw.<br /> <br /> I presented the Auspices as &quot;traditional society&quot; roles, and Garou as a warlike culture, and the characters as a small group of newbies tending to a self-assigned territory. I didn't present all the Tribes, only the existence of other Spirit Totems and of their shared cultures.<br /> <br /> The adventure ran smoothly, I just skipped the Cult of Fenris part due to time running out.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, the only main subsystems we didn't have the chance to use were Harano / Hauglosk and Chagrin. Rage Economy worked quite easily, with some negotiations between me and the players on how to acquire it.<br /> <br /> Brutal Outcomes recurred three times, two of them in dealing with the Spirits and one in combat. I portrayed the Spirit outcomes as the Spirits resentful of general Garou defeats in defending their homelands and particularly of not preventing the Bane from infesting the area, it led to quite an heated verbal confrontation with characters.<br /> The Combat Brutal Outcome was when they were trying yo deal with the newly transformed Werewolf, and I made them trample her poor husband, leaving him seriously injured.<br /> <br /> They used Crinos twice, to stop the new Wolf and to crush the Bane, and Glabro once.<br /> <br /> I relied, in descriptions, on the fact that they have richer perceptions and can superficially perceive the presence of the Spirit World, and this led them to interact a lot with Spirits and the Umbra, using Gifts and Rites. The presence of Weaver-themed Gifts and the Ghost Council ambiguity towards studying what had allowed the Bane to enter the World created some small interesting tensions between the Theurge, the Ragabash and the Ahroun.<br /> <br /> All in all, my experience with both setting and rules worked well. I will run the game again in a couple of sessions to my regular V5 group of newbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you use Chronicle Tenets for the oneshot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T02:33:21-07:00","id":1521963,"title":"","content":"Yep, the classic Humanistic tenets, they mostly behaved properly though \ud83d\ude01 and abundantly moaned and remorsed about the comatous victim.<br /> <br /> They also used a lot Favors and Bans as moral guidelines. <br /> <br /> I didn't use Convinctions and Touchstones, however, I don't like to introduce them if I don't have the time to frame appropriate scenes.<br /> <br /> Some other notes:<br /> <br /> I was very late with other event assignments, so sheets were made late night during the pauses of a massive multi-table event. I can say that making a set of quick characters was quite easy, even though I'm well acquainted with V5 so I have an advantage here.<br /> <br /> They used Willpower a lot, and also rolled a lot. I presented them &quot;take half&quot; and other narrative solutions, but they preferred to go through problems the old dicey way. This made the Rage economy quite relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> That said, it surely worked into reinforcing the concept of Savage Horror, they were actively courting Rage to deal with Spirits and smash through threats, but they were always watching out for how to minimize possible collateral damage.<br /> <br /> One of the characters Frenzied while in Rage.<br /> <br /> We were lacking the Philodox character, so Litany and Garou duties did come into play as something the Spirits wanted then to abide to, this still created Justin-intended societal tensions.<br /> <br /> When I will run the story for my table, I will probably try to make it into three or four acts: First Change and introduction, setup of the mistery and preliminary investigations, the new Werewolf (perhaps as a way to introduce a new character) and the Cult appearing, final confrontation and aftermath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-03-2023, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T02:54:38-07:00","id":1521964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521963#post1521963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the classic Humanistic tenets, they mostly behaved properly though \ud83d\ude01 and abundantly moaned and remorsed about the comatous victim.<br /> <br /> They also used a lot Favors and Bans as moral guidelines.<br /> <br /> I didn't use Convinctions and Touchstones, however, I don't like to introduce them if I don't have the time to frame appropriate scenes.<br /> <br /> Some other notes:<br /> <br /> I was very late with other event assignments, so sheets were made late night during the pauses of a massive multi-table event. I can say that making a set of quick characters was quite easy, even though I'm well acquainted with V5 so I have an advantage here.<br /> <br /> They used Willpower a lot, and also rolled a lot. I presented them &quot;take half&quot; and other narrative solutions, but they preferred to go through problems the old dicey way. This made the Rage economy quite relevant to the game.<br /> <br /> That said, it surely worked into reinforcing the concept of Savage Horror, they were actively courting Rage to deal with Spirits and smash through threats, but they were always watching out for how to minimize possible collateral damage.<br /> <br /> One of the characters Frenzied while in Rage.<br /> <br /> We were lacking the Philodox character, so Litany and Garou duties did come into play as something the Spirits wanted then to abide to, this still created Justin-intended societal tensions.<br /> <br /> When I will run the story for my table, I will probably try to make it into three or four acts: First Change and introduction, setup of the mistery and preliminary investigations, the new Werewolf (perhaps as a way to introduce a new character) and the Cult appearing, final confrontation and aftermath.</div> </div> </div> </div>One note: When you bring in all the other systems using the Humanist Chronicle Tenets for your table might introduce some issues. Going against Tenets is what triggers Hauglosk-tests. Not harming innocents and not trying to kill something (except in self-defense) will come up during the one-shot. And since it's so hard to reduce Harano/Hauglosk gaining even one point is a huge deal if you're playing W5 as a chronicle. But ultimately it's up to your table how you guys want to handle this.<br /> <br /> There are no Convictions in W5, so you don't have to worry about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T04:22:24-07:00","id":1521970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521964#post1521964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One note: When you bring in all the other systems using the Humanist Chronicle Tenets for your table might introduce some issues. Going against Tenets is what triggers Hauglosk-tests. Not harming innocents and not trying to kill something (except in self-defense) will come up during the one-shot. And since it's so hard to reduce Harano/Hauglosk gaining even one point is a huge deal if you're playing W5 as a chronicle. But ultimately it's up to your table how you guys want to handle this.<br /> <br /> There are no Convictions in W5, so you don't have to worry about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are definitely right, should it be a Chronicle I would have them discussed at the table in Session 0.<br /> <br /> I'm planning mostly one shots and short three-to-five sessions, so harsher Tenets could be useful to bring Hauglosk to the table \ud83e\udd14.<br /> <br /> Werewolf it's a bit of uncharted territory both for me and my local association, so we are definitely still exploring options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T06:00:41-07:00","id":1521975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521970#post1521970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you are definitely right, should it be a Chronicle I would have them discussed at the table in Session 0.<br /> <br /> I'm planning mostly one shots and short three-to-five sessions, so harsher Tenets could be useful to bring Hauglosk to the table \ud83e\udd14.<br /> <br /> Werewolf it's a bit of uncharted territory both for me and my local association, so we are definitely still exploring options.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you guys want more lore for the tribes, like how the Fangs are aristocrats and what the Strider Curse IS, I recommend checking revised tribebooks. Even if W5 is a reboot, the tribes aren't THAT different.<br /> <br /> But if you guys are okay with making your own lore of why, more more to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T10:08:50-07:00","id":1522407,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or does it feel like Paradox/WOD is close to doing zero PR for W5 after its official release...? They pushed for that physical Gen-Con-release but there hasn't been anything going on in an official capacity to promote the game since then... It doesn't seem like they send out review-copies to outlets for reviews, there's no official actual-play to show off the game and since Justin Achilli has gone, apparently there will be no official sitdowns/interviews with developers of W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T10:31:31-07:00","id":1522411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522407#post1522407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me or does it feel like Paradox/WOD is close to doing zero PR for W5 after its official release...? They pushed for that physical Gen-Con-release but there hasn't been anything going on in an official capacity to promote the game since then... It doesn't seem like they send out review-copies to outlets for reviews, there's no official actual-play to show off the game and since Justin Achilli has gone, apparently there will be no official sitdowns/interviews with developers of W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple: all of their creative energy is now being spent on creating the ULTIMATE W5 Tribe Bingo Cards!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> What? It's only logical!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T11:29:09-07:00","id":1522414,"title":"","content":"I thought I had just missed a lot of it because we got so much discussion about it with the early PDFs going out before the full release day... but yeah. They're doing basically nothing to promote the book now that it's fully on sale.<br /> <br /> The official World of Darkness website hasn't even been updated to say that the book was released. There's a single post about it on their X-Twitter feed. It feels like the BL2 announcement has completely overshadowed anything WtA related. I do kinda get that for Paradox, BL 2 is probably a bi make-or-break moment for them, while W5 is not. But it does feel very strange to not even try to promote the book for general sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T12:05:04-07:00","id":1522417,"title":"","content":"You know what's really weird: Comparatively, H5 had more PR than W5. Back then I always thought H5 arrived with less fanfare than V5 because, well, it's H5 (and there's the tiny issue of it not even being a follow-up to the old HtR). But I always thought back then that the release of W5 would be the moment when they would try to make WOD5E a thing with popular appeal again.<br /> <br /> Instead... we got this...<br /> <br /> Also, what just baffles me... Why did W5 need to be released at Gen-Con 2023 then...? Pushing for that release-date clearly led to some issues (like the art being problematic). But Paradox pushed for that only to follow it up with... nothing?! Same as with H5, I think the game should've seen more playtesting in order to make sure that the mechanics don't feel so half-baked. Instead, same as H5 the fifth edition of WtA is also a game where house-rules are a requirement instead of an option. Both H5 and W5 have mechanics that are <i>un-fun</i> to play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T13:08:35-07:00","id":1522420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522417#post1522417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's really weird: Comparatively, H5 had more PR than W5. Back then I always thought H5 arrived with less fanfare than V5 because, well, it's H5 (and there's the tiny issue of it not even being a follow-up to the old HtR). But I always thought back then that the release of W5 would be the moment when they would try to make WOD5E a thing with popular appeal again.<br /> <br /> Instead... we got this...<br /> <br /> Also, what just baffles me... Why did W5 need to be released at Gen-Con 2023 then...? Pushing for that release-date clearly led to some issues (like the art being problematic). But Paradox pushed for that only to follow it up with... nothing?! Same as with H5, I think the game should've seen more playtesting in order to make sure that the mechanics don't feel so half-baked. Instead, same as H5 the fifth edition of WtA is also a game where house-rules are a requirement instead of an option. Both H5 and W5 have mechanics that are <i>un-fun</i> to play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it's because development has already gone on too long and they want to take advantage of the Gen-con period. Normally when an employee or studio doesn't meet a goal it makes them look bad, so they need to show results, otherwise... You get the idea, you know, business stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T14:13:44-07:00","id":1522424,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but part of &quot;business stuff,&quot; is pacing your schedule of releases and news. Unless Paradox wants people to forget about W5, they shouldn't have had a major BL 2 announcement just after W5's release. What happened basically has three potential reasons on the business side of things:<br /> <br /> 1) Bad management of the brand where scheduling has lead to PR overlaps and internal competition for marketing resources.<br /> <br /> 2) A lack of confidence in future growth for a product. Or, in other words, Paradox thinks that W5's sales goals were adequately hit in pre-orders, and all future sales are just extras for their targets, so there isn't a need to invest more marketing into it.<br /> <br /> 3) Active dissatisfaction with the product internally, meaning that the goal is in fact to bury W5 because they don't like how it's doing, and are moving focus onto other things to keep customers focused on positive PR.<br /> <br /> 2 and 3 are similar, and externally we really don't have a way to judge that until much farther along in the future. The big difference is going to be in supplements and how much attention those get. 2 implies there will be supplements with at least a level of marketing previous V5 and H5 books have received, while 3 implies even if there are supplements, there isn't going to be a lot of pushing from Paradox of them (Renegade might opt to take up the slack there though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T15:05:00-07:00","id":1522432,"title":"","content":"I bet in the third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T17:33:08-07:00","id":1522438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522417#post1522417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's really weird: Comparatively, H5 had more PR than W5. Back then I always thought H5 arrived with less fanfare than V5 because, well, it's H5 (and there's the tiny issue of it not even being a follow-up to the old HtR). But I always thought back then that the release of W5 would be the moment when they would try to make WOD5E a thing with popular appeal again.<br /> <br /> Instead... we got this...<br /> <br /> Also, what just baffles me... Why did W5 need to be released at Gen-Con 2023 then...? Pushing for that release-date clearly led to some issues (like the art being problematic). But Paradox pushed for that only to follow it up with... nothing?! Same as with H5, I think the game should've seen more playtesting in order to make sure that the mechanics don't feel so half-baked. Instead, same as H5 the fifth edition of WtA is also a game where house-rules are a requirement instead of an option. Both H5 and W5 have mechanics that are <i>un-fun</i> to play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely because V5 released at Gen Con, and W5 was an attempt to try and recreate that hype as part of the &quot;Big Three&quot; of 90s White Wolf. Style over substance, always (even considering there's not much style and as little substance as they could manage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T21:53:47-07:00","id":1522443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522438#post1522438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most likely because V5 released at Gen Con, and W5 was an attempt to try and recreate that hype as part of the &quot;Big Three&quot; of 90s White Wolf. Style over substance, always (even considering there's not much style and as little substance as they could manage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic, because many of us here on the forum guessed that V5's initial mechanical, text, and narrative problems arose directly from rushing publication to make that year's GenCon.<br /> <br /> So the owners of WoD5 have succeeded in making the <i>same mistake twice</i>.<br /> <br /> Unlike with Vampire, though, you have neither the brand recognition, nor the marketing, nor the customer benefit-of-the-doubt with W5. It's a less well known part of the World of Darkness, that got much less publicity, at a time when customer confidence in Paradox's management of the IP in general is at an all-time low.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T23:16:11-07:00","id":1522445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522424#post1522424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) Active dissatisfaction with the product internally, meaning that the goal is in fact to bury W5 because they don't like how it's doing, and are moving focus onto other things to keep customers focused on positive PR.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say 3 easily, for the reasons you gave but ALSO because all the drama surrounding W5. While the Discord server can play off the accusations as people starting drama, the truth is that aspects of W5 were exposed to be in opposition with its intended goals and the revelations also raked the name of the brand manager through the mud.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the revelations about the traced art from clearly non-stock image sources.<br /> <br /> W5 simply has too much of a bad reputation to try and sell it more than it already does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T04:02:59-07:00","id":1522450,"title":"","content":"Looking at Discord.....which is pretty much the only online space Paradox has interest in the only person doing promo posts and interacting with fans about W5 is Justin........who doesn't even work there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 09-12-2023, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:05:10-07:00","id":1522461,"title":"","content":"Just as a note for people laying down markers for my three options: they're not actually mutually exclusive beyond the most extreme cases. As I would do whenever it's possible, I would say the most likely cause is actually a mix of all three. Justin's departure from Paradox has clearly left a management position that isn't being handled, making judgements on pre-sales with minimal later hype is fairly common in the TTRPG space even if we don't call something a pre-sale (Onyx Path is pretty transparent that many of their books basically hit baseline sales goals on crowdfunding alone, so they don't do a lot of hyping up of when books get fully released on DTRPG/etc.), and moving on to BL 2 news instead of dwelling on W5's negative PR - that they can't really do anything about immediately even if they do want to address it - is a sensible business move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:14:40-07:00","id":1522463,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Justin and the design ideas:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1843\" height=\"256\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:37:11-07:00","id":1522465,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, that sure was scope creep, going from (looks at 1e) a cosmic horror story to more cosmic horror. I'd post a lengthy rant about it, but we all know that everything he posts is probably a smokescreen mandated by an NDA and has no bearing on what's actually going on or anything relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:41:37-07:00","id":1522468,"title":"","content":"Oddly, I do feel this sentiment he is positing is what he believes and what they wanted to do. You don't go making a game without wanting to say something and making something that the audience will like. As personal as some comments and changes sound, I doubt the concerns of the legacy fans were seen as relevant.<br /> <br /> It's just that this vision of how all this connects together is missing out on what made Werewolf great","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:49:03-07:00","id":1522471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522463#post1522463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Justin and the design ideas:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1843\" height=\"256\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/u8Yv8hE.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>But there's a clear issue with what Justin is outlining there: Okay, the game may be for new players who know next to nothing about WtA and their characters similarly know little... but then where is the Storyteller's knowledge of things like the Litany, Garou-Nation and other lore/worldbuilding supposed to come from...? How is anybody supposed to introduce lore/worldbuilding when the game doesn't provide explicit details or even supports a framework for STs to come up with their own lore/worldbuilding?<br /> <br /> And &quot;player knowledge inhibits character stakes&quot;...? Even if you know a lot about the setting... it's still a game where you roll dice. The narrative stakes don't disappear just because a player has some knowledge about the setting. Also, that would mean by that logic the player and their character should never learn anything about the setting. So would he consider any player who wants to learn more about the setting they're playing in a &quot;bad player&quot;? Is the ideal state of playing W5 supposed to be that you started knowing next to nothing about WtA and you end the Chronicle by still knowing next to nothing about WtA? Because otherwise the character-stakes would be... lowered?<br /> <br /> Also the obvious contradictions are still there... &quot;It's all about what the people at the table want to play - but it has to be a street-level game!&quot; and &quot;The game isn't about lore and instead it's about what sort of story you want to tell... also this game is about Garou, the Umbra, war against the Wyrm, Pentex, the Litany, the Garou-Nation, there's also something called the Impergium and there are other shifters as well in the setting, so good luck figuring out how this all fits together because it's your story after all.&quot;.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522465#post1522465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, that sure was scope creep, going from (looks at 1e) a cosmic horror story to more cosmic horror. I'd post a lengthy rant about it, but we all know that everything he posts is probably a smokescreen mandated by an NDA and has no bearing on what's actually going on or anything relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're probably right... It's just so weird that this is apparently the hill he wants to die on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T09:32:37-07:00","id":1522515,"title":"","content":"Renegade is pushing quite a lot, I receive a couple of emails a week presenting W5 and they are also active on social networks, as well as adding bonus content to the W5 page.<br /> <br /> Official Paradox silence is strange, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T09:34:50-07:00","id":1522516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1521975#post1521975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you guys want more lore for the tribes, like how the Fangs are aristocrats and what the Strider Curse IS, I recommend checking revised tribebooks. Even if W5 is a reboot, the tribes aren't THAT different.<br /> <br /> But if you guys are okay with making your own lore of why, more more to you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like to mine legacy lore for ideas, if I can give the adventure the span of a short chronicle I will surely give them a look!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-13-2023, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T11:32:11-07:00","id":1522523,"title":"","content":"Well, there was a review on Goonhammer about W5... The title: <a href=\"https://www.goonhammer.com/werewolf-the-apocalypse-takes-one-step-forward-and-two-steps-back/\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Apocalypse Takes One Step Forward and Two Steps Back</a>. Nothing in it will come as much of a surprise to readers of this thread but the complaints about picking Gifts from all those pages of Gifts and the allusions to V5 just made me think again just how little actual &quot;re-imagining&quot; is going on in W5. What even is there that isn't derivative of V5 or WtA-legacy-stuff...? The biggest differences stem from W5 doing less than V5 and legacy-WtA. &quot;New&quot; ideas like making the Fenrir antagonists are more of a response to legacy-stuff than an actual new idea or you just get stuff like &quot;What is the Garou-Nation? Who knows! And it's gone now anyway...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:00:22-07:00","id":1522524,"title":"","content":"Theres some truly wacky shit in the free W5 downloads from Renegade....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:12:42-07:00","id":1522526,"title":"","content":"So. They put out some bonus content for the game. And really, really managed to piss me off with one of their random &quot;inspiration tables&quot;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"413\" height=\"1112\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I'd like to single out<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot; You weren\u2019t expecting them to lock the doors at the wedding. It was at that moment the long line of Garou in your family bloodline revealed their strange tradition about the First Change. To prove you were worthy of the wolf you had to kill your way out of the room after they triggered the change. After that, nothing the Wyrm can do fazes you.&quot;<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>What the flying fuck. This is some BSD level shit. We knew the authors view of Garou was quite bleak, but this really puts the Garou into a different light. Also it reinforces the familial connections, but hey there's no familial links to becoming a Garou!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:17:30-07:00","id":1522528,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thats the most egregious one but theres a couple of others.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, thats a BSD tradition........well a W5 BSD tradition...I'm unsure Legacy BSDs would let that many Kinfolk just go to waste....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:20:09-07:00","id":1522529,"title":"","content":"I think I've had a PC go through pretty much all of the other ones ( or something somewhat similar) over the years except 8....maybe not 4. But DEFINITELY not 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:38:54-07:00","id":1522530,"title":"","content":"Note how, in addition to all these being disturbingly dark, none of them position the First Change in anything resembling a good or liberating light.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Werewolf can't be a positive development for you, the PC. You <i>must</i> have angst. Preferably also with a bodycount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T15:34:22-07:00","id":1522537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522528#post1522528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, thats the most egregious one but theres a couple of others.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, thats a BSD tradition........well a W5 BSD tradition...I'm unsure Legacy BSDs would let that many Kinfolk just go to waste....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohoho no, there is no kinfolk anymore. The PC has to kill other GAROU.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T15:44:07-07:00","id":1522539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522526#post1522526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. They put out some bonus content for the game. And really, really managed to piss me off with one of their random &quot;inspiration tables&quot;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"413\" height=\"1112\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/nHIhgmE.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I'd like to single out<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What the flying fuck. This is some BSD level shit. We knew the authors view of Garou was quite bleak, but this really puts the Garou into a different light. Also it reinforces the familial connections, but hey there's no familial links to becoming a Garou!</div> </div> </div> </div>No one asked, but I will give my two cents:<br /> <br /> 1 - 4: Good enough.<br /> <br /> 5: That was different.<br /> <br /> 6: Good, but need some work.<br /> <br /> 7: That is crazy in the bad way.<br /> <br /> 8: Also good.<br /> <br /> 9: This is heavy and sick, I guess.<br /> <br /> 10: I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T16:18:05-07:00","id":1522540,"title":"","content":"And 90s Edgelords have a seat at the table again I see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T16:32:05-07:00","id":1522541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522530#post1522530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note how, in addition to all these being disturbingly dark, none of them position the First Change in anything resembling a good or liberating light.<br /> Becoming a Werewolf can't be a positive development for you, the PC. You <i>must</i> have angst. Preferably also with a bodycount.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as we've heard from Justin Achilli one of the core-ideas of WOD5E is &quot;I'm a monster, what now?&quot;, so I assume that was the direction the writer was given. But that really makes me wonder how they're even gonna approach all the other splats... This is just gonna get increasingly weirder the more Paradox enforces this idea that all WOD-splats need to be VtM-esque.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522537#post1522537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohoho no, there is no kinfolk anymore. The PC has to kill other GAROU.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than having consistent worldbuilding, the whole &quot;Who gets to be a Garou?&quot;-thing is another shrug. And so it's pretty much all sorts of ideas happening at once. It's random people turning into Garou at random times, it's hereditary, it's caused by personal experiences or the socio-economic position you and your family have found yourselves in... Technically I guess anything can trigger someone becoming a Kin and at whatever point in a person's life this turns into a First Change. Like number 5 is just &quot;random&quot;. Something happened to the character and suddenly said character is a werewolf.<br /> <br /> But when it's this random, all these scenarios where it feels like other werewolves are trying to &quot;trigger&quot; you, it just comes across as psychopathic behavior. And this just goes back to how negative W5's portrayal of Garou in general is. You really get the sense from what Justin Achilli has said and the way this is handled that actually if anything all the Garou (and not just the Fenrir) are viewed as bad guys by the writers of this version of W5 we've gotten now. And the way you're supposed to play this version of W5 is have player-characters who are werewolves but couldn't care less about the Garou-Nation, the Litany and being sacred warriors for Gaia. That's all bad. But the game also can't offer an alternative because that would require worldbuilding (which according to Justin Achilli is inherently bad).<br /> <br /> And so the same way H5 is a game of local hunter-cells incapable of envisioning anything beyond that, W5 is a game of young werewolves who have just become &quot;Garou&quot; (more or less) who struggle with their position in the world. But the horizon of imagination in the game's writing ends right there. W5 can't imagine the player-characters saving the world or becoming leaders of a Sept. The mechanics are even pushing against that (like with Rites, for example). Same as with H5, there's no vision to go beyond these beginning-stages of having new players who know next to nothing play the game. Try to do anything else with this and you start running into issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T17:52:29-07:00","id":1522544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522537#post1522537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ohoho no, there is no kinfolk anymore. The PC has to kill other GAROU.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Surely the majority of the guests would be ordinary humans, and as the First Change is often accompanied by Frenzy.....thats a lot of dead people....plus your spouse, flower girls, ushers etc.<br /> <br /> This is solidly BSD territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T18:25:28-07:00","id":1522547,"title":"","content":"I think the authors intend it to be solidly in Cult of Fenris territory... but with redeemable BSDs who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T20:30:45-07:00","id":1522552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522541#post1522541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as we've heard from Justin Achilli one of the core-ideas of WOD5E is &quot;I'm a monster, what now?&quot;, so I assume that was the direction the writer was given. But that really makes me wonder how they're even gonna approach all the other splats... This is just gonna get increasingly weirder the more Paradox enforces this idea that all WOD-splats need to be VtM-esque.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a huge WtA buff, so I must defer to those more knowledgeable than I: was &quot;I'm a monster, what now?&quot; ever a major theme in the older editions of Werewolf?<br /> <br /> Because that seems like more specifically a VtM theme. &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, this also gives me misgivings about, say, M5. While Hubris was always a theme in Mage, are we going to see M5 frame the Awakened as inherently monstrous too? Because classic Mage was very much of the opinion that, Ascension War and Paradox (the force, not the company) aside, being a Mage kind of rocks. Except for being alienated from the rest of humanity, due to your unique experiences that unAwakened can't really grok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T22:04:12-07:00","id":1522557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522552#post1522552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a huge WtA buff, so I must defer to those more knowledgeable than I: was &quot;I'm a monster, what now?&quot; ever a major theme in the older editions of Werewolf?<br /> <br /> Because that seems like more specifically a VtM theme. &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become&quot;.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. While you could have your First Change outside of Garou society, it was also just as, if not more, likely that you were either born within it or were quickly scooped up and taught what was going on. WtA was never all that much about personal horror like Vampire, but about external threats like the Wyrm, Weaver, pollution, the Umbra, conflicts with other groups, Garou or not, and all that stuff. So while coming to terms with your werewolf nature could be a theme if you wanted to take that angle, it's not really the focus of the game as a whole, and trying to shoehorn WtA into that box just completely neuters the larger scale it's supposed to have and is already causing problems because Paradox has given the game no room to breathe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T22:48:06-07:00","id":1522559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522552#post1522552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a huge WtA buff, so I must defer to those more knowledgeable than I: was &quot;I'm a monster, what now?&quot; ever a major theme in the older editions of Werewolf?<br /> <br /> Because that seems like more specifically a VtM theme. &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was not, and yes, you are right, everything about this is quite sus in how similar it is to how Vampire operates. The answer to &quot;Now what?&quot; in prior editions of W:tA was &quot;do something about the hideous coils of corruption threatening to snuff you out&quot;, which, while admittedly wide-open and perhaps even overwhelming, was a much more satisfying answer than the constant shrugs that this game supplies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, this also gives me misgivings about, say, M5. While Hubris was always a theme in Mage, are we going to see M5 frame the Awakened as inherently monstrous too? Because classic Mage was very much of the opinion that, Ascension War and Paradox (the force, not the company) aside, being a Mage kind of rocks. Except for being alienated from the rest of humanity, due to your unique experiences that unAwakened can't really grok. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably. By the estimation of most metrics, angst is likely going to be imposed on Mage in ways that make the Revised edition look optimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T23:15:04-07:00","id":1522560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522544#post1522544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely the majority of the guests would be ordinary humans, and as the First Change is often accompanied by Frenzy.....thats a lot of dead people....plus your spouse, flower girls, ushers etc.<br /> <br /> This is solidly BSD territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling that the PC must fight through his family to get back to his bride. But further reading, you are right.<br /> <br /> Which is even MORE fucked up.<br /> <br /> It feels like the writers legit are just thinking W5 as a V5 but with werewolves. The funny thing is, that according to one of the developers of WtA 1st ed, they TRIED the cursed angle but found it weird to not engage with the name of the game. Hence why WtA legacy is like it is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, the way this is copying V5 is actually ignoring the difference between a garou and a vampire.<br /> <br /> Because a vampire is STUCK dealing with this stuff, they are now an undead monster and there is no cure.<br /> <br /> BUT, a garou in W5 is not so unlucky. They can spend all their Rage and lose the wolf and just... leave. Ignore the Wyrm, the Fenrir, the BSDs and such.<br /> <br /> If a garou in W5 is faced with this? They can leave and so these traditions truly would have to be from BSDs as no other tribe would have the resources nor cruelty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 09-14-2023, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T00:09:24-07:00","id":1522561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522560#post1522560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the feeling that the PC must fight through his family to get back to his bride. But further reading, you are right.<br /> <br /> Which is even MORE fucked up.<br /> <br /> It feels like the writers legit are just thinking W5 as a V5 but with werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of the things in the list feel like things you'd see the Sabbat do to someone before Embracing them, so well beyond even what most vampires go through. If this list is meant to be a fairly typical set of examples that characters go through, then Garou society is seriously fucked up, beyond even what you see in something like the Camarilla. In that case, it's understandable why young Garou would hate Garou society - it's an attitude that would be similar to what you might see from a shovelhead vampire that was forced to go through Sabbat rites but never had the Vinculum to force loyalty to their tormenters. But it definitely creates a tonal shift when you have, apparently, a not-insignificant portion of Garou society engaging in the sorts of actions you would expect to see from a group like the Sabbat, that's so evil and wicked, in V5 they've become NPC only with no rules for being allowed to play them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T00:14:22-07:00","id":1522562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522561#post1522561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several of the things in the list feel like things you'd see the Sabbat do to someone before Embracing them, so well beyond even what most vampires go through. If this list is meant to be a fairly typical set of examples that characters go through, then Garou society is seriously fucked up, beyond even what you see in something like the Camarilla. In that case, it's understandable why young Garou would hate Garou society - it's an attitude that would be similar to what you might see from a shovelhead vampire that was forced to go through Sabbat rites but never had the Vinculum to force loyalty to their tormenters. But it definitely creates a tonal shift when you have, apparently, a not-insignificant portion of Garou society engaging in the sorts of actions you would expect to see from a group like the Sabbat, that's so evil and wicked, in V5 they've become NPC only with no rules for being allowed to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling there is very little idea of how to apply the Nation in W5. Because the text constantly says it is bad, but then turns around and says PCs might be part of it. So you get these weird extra dark things written by people who assume the Nation is like That.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T01:05:13-07:00","id":1522563,"title":"","content":"Also, the list of example-Garou-relationships have some issues as well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lisa Meyers, Philodox Silver Fang. Head nurse at St. Anne retirement community </div> </div> </div>Yeah, having a Garou with Rage run a retirement-home doesn't sound like a recipe for disaster at all...<br /> <br /> Also in general the Tribes of the example-characters are weird...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jeremy Bondeau, Galliard Glass Walker. Author of the Moonlight Mysteries supernatural romance novel series </div> </div> </div>A Glass Walker...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neel Eggers, Ragabash Silent Strider. IT specialist building secure communications networks for Garou Nation </div> </div> </div>But this is a Silent Strider...? (also the writer of this thing seems to think the Garou Nation is still a thing in W5)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Margot Moreau, Theurge Hart Warden. Tarot reader, spiritual healer, and confidence woman extraordinaire </div> </div> </div>And this is a Hart Warden...?<br /> <br /> It's like the writer took the idea of &quot;anybody can join any Tribe&quot; a bit too far... Both with the archetypes in the book and with these examples here, the choice of Tribe is rendered meaningless when there's no flavorful throughline for these character-types.<br /> <br /> And of course, you just had to throw the obligatory \u201cGalliard musician\u201d into the mix\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Julia Estes, Galliard Ghost Council. Bass player of the band Wicked Church Ladies </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T08:08:31-07:00","id":1522573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522547#post1522547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the authors intend it to be solidly in Cult of Fenris territory... but with redeemable BSDs who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs are usually pretty freaking awful but I feel like shredding an entire wedding party by tooth and claw would be pushing it even for them. Not that they would view the murder as bad, but that a whole building of people torn to shreds would risk too much attention. I would think they would stage a mass shooting if anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T08:21:55-07:00","id":1522574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522561#post1522561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several of the things in the list feel like things you'd see the Sabbat do to someone before Embracing them, so well beyond even what most vampires go through. If this list is meant to be a fairly typical set of examples that characters go through, then Garou society is seriously fucked up, beyond even what you see in something like the Camarilla. In that case, it's understandable why young Garou would hate Garou society - it's an attitude that would be similar to what you might see from a shovelhead vampire that was forced to go through Sabbat rites but never had the Vinculum to force loyalty to their tormenters. But it definitely creates a tonal shift when you have, apparently, a not-insignificant portion of Garou society engaging in the sorts of actions you would expect to see from a group like the Sabbat, that's so evil and wicked, in V5 they've become NPC only with no rules for being allowed to play them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I was so aggravated. These seem to be &quot;typical&quot; first change experiences. That speaks volumes of what the Garou are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T09:52:13-07:00","id":1522579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522574#post1522574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I was so aggravated. These seem to be &quot;typical&quot; first change experiences. That speaks volumes of what the Garou are like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are qualified as &quot;Dramatic&quot; turning points, so they are not necessarily typical. This would imply that they are botched, or at least problematic, turning situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T11:04:16-07:00","id":1522582,"title":"","content":"I don't know about your sensibility guys but the things in the list to me looks totally horror werewolf.<br /> the one with the marriage is super silver Fang or shadow lord to me. I don't know how you play and how you depict the sabbat, and I RESPECT IT, but to me here nothing new at all. Garou have a culture of war and violence and many tribes have to prove their members strong enough. With more violence which is, surprise, the thing that fucks up garou every time and they still chose it because hey, that's the tragedy about a game filled with righteous battles but wrong answers. Violence creates violent culture, might is right, brutal traditions to keep the standard. Imagine if you are a murderhobo 3mtrs tall killing machine with anger management problems. <br /> in first editions shadow lords ended up killing other garou with silver, get of fenris and others killed off their metis forcing the mother to do so (there is also an illustration somewhere) , there are black furies that wants to go serial killing on men, wendigo that advocates Total War against homids, Fianna that decide who have to get pregnant and Fenris at least two rage across that are actually far right sympathizer. Where is the Sabbat like stuff here in the list of DRAMATIC turning points ? Because I see none.<br /> There are a lot of sabbat examples where those vamps are far worst than a family brawl in crinos during a marriage. Montreal by night where there is also depicted a rape with a dildo to get blood, among the various infernalist fucked up practices. Various killing spree forms in the guide to the Sabbat. Elders that drink only children's blood. Giovanni that... well you know.<br /> <br /> I read a lot of 20th stuff and of course, all the garou seems really much more soft. But still, I can't see any exceptional fucked up thing from garou.<br /> also, brutal invitation rites are perfect to start a long term campaign about problems with the elders when the pc realize some stuff.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents. I have no much time these days, working a lot. I will answer when I can if someone will quote me.<br /> <br /> Again, read and read again: I'm not attacking your game play mood. Everyone is free to play according to its own sensibility and favored theme.<br /> I only clearly remember FAR more fucked up stuff from the wod. The problem is mine, take this post like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:34:00-07:00","id":1522584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522582#post1522582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about your sensibility guys but the things in the list to me looks totally horror werewolf.<br /> the one with the marriage is super silver Fang or shadow lord to me. I don't know how you play and how you depict the sabbat, and I RESPECT IT, but to me here nothing new at all. Garou have a culture of war and violence and many tribes have to prove their members strong enough. With more violence which is, surprise, the thing that fucks up garou every time and they still chose it because hey, that's the tragedy about a game filled with righteous battles but wrong answers. Violence creates violent culture, might is right, brutal traditions to keep the standard. Imagine if you are a murderhobo 3mtrs tall killing machine with anger management problems.<br /> in first editions shadow lords ended up killing other garou with silver, get of fenris and others killed off their metis forcing the mother to do so (there is also an illustration somewhere) , there are black furies that wants to go serial killing on men, wendigo that advocates Total War against homids, Fianna that decide who have to get pregnant and Fenris at least two rage across that are actually far right sympathizer. Where is the Sabbat like stuff here in the list of DRAMATIC turning points ? Because I see none.<br /> There are a lot of sabbat examples where those vamps are far worst than a family brawl in crinos during a marriage. Montreal by night where there is also depicted a rape with a dildo to get blood, among the various infernalist fucked up practices. Various killing spree forms in the guide to the Sabbat. Elders that drink only children's blood. Giovanni that... well you know.<br /> <br /> I read a lot of 20th stuff and of course, all the garou seems really much more soft. But still, I can't see any exceptional fucked up thing from garou.<br /> also, brutal invitation rites are perfect to start a long term campaign about problems with the elders when the pc realize some stuff.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents. I have no much time these days, working a lot. I will answer when I can if someone will quote me.<br /> <br /> Again, read and read again: I'm not attacking your game play mood. Everyone is free to play according to its own sensibility and favored theme.<br /> I only clearly remember FAR more fucked up stuff from the wod. The problem is mine, take this post like this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The thing is, no tribes you mentionned ever put their kin in such a danger just in case to trigger a first change.<br /> <br /> If anything, garou are overprotective of their kinfolks. Putting then in a trapped wedding hoping to trigger a first change that'll kill many of them is against everything every editions told us about the relationship between garou and kinfolks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:34:19-07:00","id":1522585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522582#post1522582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about your sensibility guys but the things in the list to me looks totally horror werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately though, you seem to be taking things out of context of all the other changes made in W5. Even if you like this level of cultural violence in your Werewolf games, most of what your defending doesn't make sense with all the changes W5 has done in rebooting the game: W5 Garou don't have to prove themselves to Tribes to join, the Patron spirits pick Garou they think are good fits; W5 doesn't force Garou to undergo initiation rites to join a Tribe. W5 has stripped answers, right or wrong, in favor of vague uncertainty; there are no commonly held misguided beliefs for Garou to insist on as a larger group to justify their actions and there isn't even a functional Garou Nation anyway anymore. There is nobody to enforce &quot;brutal traditions&quot; and nobody believes in the old &quot;standards&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> I could argue with you plenty about your estimation of WtA back in 1e/early 2e, but that doesn't really matter: these examples are for W5, and W5 doesn't want to be early WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:44:39-07:00","id":1522587,"title":"","content":"As for the idea in W5 that everyo'e can be secretly a garou and goes through a first change, this has some massive setting breaking implications.<br /> <br /> <br /> If being a garou is now due to random or unknown circonstances, or worse, if every human can be one if they rage enough, we end up with a very effed up world.<br /> <br /> Imagine a garou pack attacking a pentex owned company. The fear and trauma causes two pentex employees to go through first change.<br /> <br /> A glass walker creates a blackout to cover for the pack escape. In the now dark block, a teen is panicked inside the now immobile and dark elevator and transform.<br /> <br /> Every teen getting intimate for the first time is now playing russian roulette. Will I shift and kill my partner, or vice versa?<br /> <br /> And, to add some irony in the nonsense, every werewolf hunter is only one adrenaline filled hunt away from becoming one of the beings he decided to kill.<br /> <br /> In many ways, it mimic one of the issues with mage, where anyone can awaken. Howether at least for mage, awakening is typically not triggered by simply feeling extreme emotions<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 09-14-2023, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:45:51-07:00","id":1522588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522585#post1522585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ultimately though, you seem to be taking things out of context of all the other changes made in W5. Even if you like this level of cultural violence in your Werewolf games, most of what your defending doesn't make sense with all the changes W5 has done in rebooting the game: W5 Garou don't have to prove themselves to Tribes to join, the Patron spirits pick Garou they think are good fits; W5 doesn't force Garou to undergo initiation rites to join a Tribe. W5 has stripped answers, right or wrong, in favor of vague uncertainty; there are no commonly held misguided beliefs for Garou to insist on as a larger group to justify their actions and there isn't even a functional Garou Nation anyway anymore. There is nobody to enforce &quot;brutal traditions&quot; and nobody believes in the old &quot;standards&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> I could argue with you plenty about your estimation of WtA back in 1e/early 2e, but that doesn't really matter: these examples are for W5, and W5 doesn't want to be early WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core w5 says clearly that garou ''can be'' from a bloodline, and all the material about how you join a tribe or the tribe choses you, is very vague. Nothing can stop me to create a local version of a tribe where the totem choses from certain culture/bloodlines/families, or where some hardcore members looks for kin in order to force them into the tribe to make it bigger. The book suggest various times the danger of autoritarianism from the litany, and after all, it totally do not forbid or deny my examples.<br /> Gorgon can chose some honest activists in New York, and a ruthless mafia family in Seattle. The fact that the tribal concepts are more vague doesn't mean you can't play a lot with them instead of let them being just grey areas. The description of the Silver Fangs can perfectly fit the marriage example on a local level. <br /> Falcon maybe will not ask a single trial to join, but his children, in that specific place, maybe are a bit fucked up in the head. <br /> <br /> btw, it's clear your overall position on it, i'm not here for arguing, because after all is also clearly a matter of taste. Again, I'm sorry for who can't enjoy a new edition of werewolf, and I'm not ironic, I know what does it mean when you feel something for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T12:46:56-07:00","id":1522589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522579#post1522579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they are qualified as &quot;Dramatic&quot; turning points, so they are not necessarily typical. This would imply that they are botched, or at least problematic, turning situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition any First Change is dramatic. Considering this is a player facing supplement with additional tools and quick tables to generate who you are and where you came from, these are typical experiences that you should base your character on. You can decide to be incredibly charitable towards the reading, but considering the portrayal of the Garou in the W5 book, it does feel on brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T13:27:28-07:00","id":1522593,"title":"","content":"I don't know, perhaps it's because English is not my native language and I'm failing to read between the lines, but the text says &quot;If you want a First Change with lasting effects... &quot;<br /> <br /> There is an If and a determined condition, so it doesn't sound as the baseline to me. <br /> <br /> That said, I mostly agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3773_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3773\" data-vbnamecard=\"3773\">Helur</a> here: as a reboot on lore and plot, W5 is pretty soft, most of old stuff still apply but in vaguer terms. What has changed is that Garou existence is presented much more clearly in monstrous terms. Of course, this can't sit well with those who prefer a cosmic warrior approach, but still I would say it doesn't make Garou baddies. It makes them flawed heroes in the vein of ancient Greek heroes of the Iliad and Odissey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T13:40:53-07:00","id":1522595,"title":"","content":"Considering the vagueries of W5, a scenario like number 7 only makes sense if you want to set up Garou as amoral psychopaths. Because that scenario is a good combination of &quot;Kinseeking plus wanting to trigger a First Change&quot; and W5's completely pessimistic view of the Garou-Nation. It's also striking how none of the 10 examples involve spirits and/or any sort of animistic view-point. Well, at least it's just more of the same: erasure instead of representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T13:56:39-07:00","id":1522596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522593#post1522593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has changed is that Garou existence is presented much more clearly in monstrous terms. Of course, this can't sit well with those who prefer a cosmic warrior approach, but still I would say it doesn't make Garou baddies. It makes them flawed heroes in the vein of ancient Greek heroes of the Iliad and Odissey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that you lurk in these discussions and have seen that I use similar comparisons to the narrative role of the Garou. However, I do feel that a hero must have more positive to them than the negative, and usually the heroes of Greek Myth are pretty damn good at that. The Garou of W5 are just dysfunctional assholes which are actually underscored in the storyteller section will never change or become better. While Vampire might revel in its angst, Werewolf did not. It was about trying to make things better. And the previous writers understood that better than the current crop does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T13:59:35-07:00","id":1522597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522582#post1522582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about your sensibility guys but the things in the list to me looks totally horror werewolf.<br /> the one with the marriage is super silver Fang or shadow lord to me. I don't know how you play and how you depict the sabbat, and I RESPECT IT, but to me here nothing new at all. Garou have a culture of war and violence and many tribes have to prove their members strong enough. With more violence which is, surprise, the thing that fucks up garou every time and they still chose it because hey, that's the tragedy about a game filled with righteous battles but wrong answers. Violence creates violent culture, might is right, brutal traditions to keep the standard. Imagine if you are a murderhobo 3mtrs tall killing machine with anger management problems.<br /> in first editions shadow lords ended up killing other garou with silver, get of fenris and others killed off their metis forcing the mother to do so (there is also an illustration somewhere) , there are black furies that wants to go serial killing on men, wendigo that advocates Total War against homids, Fianna that decide who have to get pregnant and Fenris at least two rage across that are actually far right sympathizer. Where is the Sabbat like stuff here in the list of DRAMATIC turning points ? Because I see none.<br /> There are a lot of sabbat examples where those vamps are far worst than a family brawl in crinos during a marriage. Montreal by night where there is also depicted a rape with a dildo to get blood, among the various infernalist fucked up practices. Various killing spree forms in the guide to the Sabbat. Elders that drink only children's blood. Giovanni that... well you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's get back to this example.<ul><li>They trigger your first change</li> <li>They lock you in either at your own or someone else's wedding</li> <li>They don't let you out until you murder your way out</li> <li>You proceed to kill 20-150 people in a massacre of people who cannot do anything to you</li> <li>You are scarred for life, because after this you don't even care about what the Wyrm does</li> </ul>This makes Sabbat look cuddly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T14:09:53-07:00","id":1522598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522596#post1522596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that you lurk in these discussions and have seen that I use similar comparisons to the narrative role of the Garou. However, I do feel that a hero must have more positive to them than the negative, and usually the heroes of Greek Myth are pretty damn good at that. The Garou of W5 are just dysfunctional assholes which are actually underscored in the storyteller section will never change or become better. While Vampire might revel in its angst, Werewolf did not. It was about trying to make things better. And the previous writers understood that better than the current crop does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Greek heroes usually have pretty huge failings on their backs, from Heracles killing his family to the likes of Agamemnon, Aiax, Diomedes and Achilles, whose actions in the War of Troy are surely brave and paragon of warlike values, but are also... well, what very dysfunctional assholes would do. <br /> <br /> Werewolf, I feel, is still about trying to make things better, it's &quot;just&quot; that you are burdened by something which osore present in the narrative.<br /> <br /> I fully understand that it's not everyone's cup of tea, I like it more but it's quite a radical departure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-14-2023, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T14:34:44-07:00","id":1522600,"title":"","content":"Scenario 7 just does not work as a &quot;First Change&quot;-scenario... unless it's about joining the BSD. The emotional hurt of the werewolf killing his way out plus who he has to kill in the process... Also in W5 you don't know if any number of people in the audience also experience their First Change. It doesn't feel like scenario 7 is in line with W5 lore.<br /> <br /> W5 is very vague with who gets to be Kin. So any sort of mass-slaughter should be an obvious no-no for Garou. And something like this Renegade-document needs to run with this super-vague definition, so the focus should've been all about personal experiences and/or spirits interacting with a Kin. The whole &quot;Kinseeking&quot;-aspect and how one might do that... That should've been developed in the corebook... which it wasn't (of course... since ye know,&quot;worldbuilding=bad&quot; according to the lead-dev Justin Achilli). So bringing up psychopathic examples of &quot;Kinseeking&quot; is a really bad idea in my opinion. There's no actual baseline for what &quot;Kinseeking&quot; is like in W5. Like a lot of stuff in W5 it's way too vague and so to introduce psychopath-stuff like scenario 7 is just poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> Just think it through... Is this document actually suggesting that you should play this...? Or that it's something that happened in the character's past? And somehow a character who has gone through scenario 7 would still call themselves a &quot;Garou&quot; actually...? Come on... that scenario really only makes sense if we're talking about BSD...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T14:52:34-07:00","id":1522601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522600#post1522600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario 7 just does not work as a &quot;First Change&quot;-scenario... unless it's about joining the BSD. The emotional hurt of the werewolf killing his way out plus who he has to kill in the process... Also in W5 you don't know if any number of people in the audience also experience their First Change. It doesn't feel like scenario 7 is in line with W5 lore.<br /> <br /> W5 is very vague with who gets to be Kin. So any sort of mass-slaughter should be an obvious no-no for Garou. And something like this Renegade-document needs to run with this super-vague definition, so the focus should've been all about personal experiences and/or spirits interacting with a Kin. The whole &quot;Kinseeking&quot;-aspect and how one might do that... That should've been developed in the corebook... which it wasn't (of course... since ye know,&quot;worldbuilding=bad&quot; according to the lead-dev Justin Achilli). So bringing up psychopathic examples of &quot;Kinseeking&quot; is a really bad idea in my opinion. There's no actual baseline for what &quot;Kinseeking&quot; is like in W5. Like a lot of stuff in W5 it's way too vague and so to introduce psychopath-stuff like scenario 7 is just poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> Just think it through... Is this document actually suggesting that you should play this...? Or that it's something that happened in the character's past? And somehow a character who has gone through scenario 7 would still call themselves a &quot;Garou&quot; actually...? Come on... that scenario really only makes sense if we're talking about BSD...</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we say it's a BSD Kinseeking, that the BSD tried to recruit you wouldn't be such a strange backstory even in legacy Wta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:13:29-07:00","id":1522603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522601#post1522601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we say it's a BSD Kinseeking, that the BSD tried to recruit you wouldn't be such a strange backstory even in legacy Wta.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be strange for something that's supposed to help you set up a game. This is supposed to be a tool for beginners. Any sort of &quot;outlier&quot;-scenarios or extreme scenarios like &quot;BSD-Kinseekings&quot; shouldn't be part of the &quot;introduction-package&quot;.<br /> <br /> Especially because of how little worldbuilding you get from the actual W5 corebook. Even just characterizing it as a BSD-Kinseeking is us <i>adding </i>detail to this. Neither the Renegade-document nor the W5 corebook deal with these matters in a thoughtful manner. But without the BSD-detail... what sort of play is encouraged here? That killing innocents is fine on occasion...? That it's okay to ally with the guys who made you slaughter innocent people? Of course, neither the Renegade-document nor the W5 corebook will help you answering these questions.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, I think scenario 7 doesn't add anything to your game in W5. And we're talking only about W5 here. Why would you need that particular First Change scenario in W5? What is it about W5 that this should be one of the proposed standard-options for a starting-character/player...?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:56:26-07:00","id":1522605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522598#post1522598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Greek heroes usually have pretty huge failings on their backs, from Heracles killing his family to the likes of Agamemnon, Aiax, Diomedes and Achilles, whose actions in the War of Troy are surely brave and paragon of warlike values, but are also... well, what very dysfunctional assholes would do.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, I feel, is still about trying to make things better, it's &quot;just&quot; that you are burdened by something which osore present in the narrative.<br /> <br /> I fully understand that it's not everyone's cup of tea, I like it more but it's quite a radical departure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually you wait until after a hero is established to introduce their hamartia. This? With the First Change? This is pre-made right out of the gate. It's a cheap shot with no heat and no agency on the part of the werewolf-to-be in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:00:00-07:00","id":1522608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522603#post1522603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But without the BSD-detail... what sort of play is encouraged here? That killing innocents is fine on occasion...? That it's okay to ally with the guys who made you slaughter innocent people? Of course, neither the Renegade-document nor the W5 corebook will help you answering these questions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the corebook answers these questions quite a lot: it repeatedly says that Werewolves are flawed heroes, whose Rage and desperation might lead some of them in very dark places. The PCs are meant to fight against these dark sides, born of their defeats, but they themselves are not immune to these failings. <br /> <br /> Again, W5 is a game where heroes are risking their morality: if someone's tastes are more towards heroes who stand true and strong to their ideas, the game as presented<br /> is pivoted towards different themes.<br /> <br /> But it's a coherent concept, which is explained again and again in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:01:09-07:00","id":1522609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522605#post1522605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Usually you wait until after a hero is established to introduce their hamartia. This? With the First Change? This is pre-made right out of the gate. It's a cheap shot with no heat and no agency on the part of the werewolf-to-be in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a rule, it's a plot hook you may use, not use, modify, adapt, discuss etc etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:02:12-07:00","id":1522610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522608#post1522608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the corebook answers these questions quite a lot: it repeatedly says that Werewolves are flawed heroes, whose Rage and desperation might lead some of them in very dark places. The PCs are meant to fight against these dark sides, born of their defeats, but they themselves are not immune to these failings.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, &quot;We just copied V5 and changed some minor details to avoid being too much like Twilight Life and Death.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, W5 is a game where heroes are risking their morality: if someone's tastes are more towards heroes who stand true and strong to their ideas, the game as presented<br /> is pivoted towards different themes.<br /> <br /> But it's a coherent concept, which is explained again and again in the book. </div> </div> </div>A concept that they already did for Vampire. It's rather tiresome to see in any version of Werewolf, since the original creators tried it out and found out that it was fucking boring as hell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:04:24-07:00","id":1522611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522609#post1522609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a rule, it's a plot hook you may use, not use, modify, adapt, discuss etc etc</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter if it's a rule or not. As an example, it's terrible and simply just there for the weirdest kind of angst. I swear, it's a wonder that everyone - vampire, hunter, werewolf, and more - doesn't have a Shadow in WoD5, because they surely want everyone to have a trackable amount of Angst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:19:45-07:00","id":1522615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522610#post1522610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In other words, &quot;We just copied V5 and changed some minor details to avoid being too much like Twilight Life and Death.&quot;<br /> <br /> A concept that they already did for Vampire. It's rather tiresome to see in any version of Werewolf, since the original creators tried it out and found out that it was fucking boring as hell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your cup of tea. My cup of tea, I'm pretty happy to have a set of similar and relatable mechanics, and I also appreciate that monsters (and monster hunters) are walking a thin line between using their power and abusing it.<br /> <br /> Saying they are the same would be like saying Mutant Year Zero and Coriolis are the same game because they are set in a distant future, they rely on the pushing mechanic, and the PCs are actively managing something. \ud83d\ude03","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T16:35:17-07:00","id":1522616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522608#post1522608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the corebook answers these questions quite a lot: it repeatedly says that Werewolves are flawed heroes, whose Rage and desperation might lead some of them in very dark places. The PCs are meant to fight against these dark sides, born of their defeats, but they themselves are not immune to these failings.<br /> <br /> Again, W5 is a game where heroes are risking their morality: if someone's tastes are more towards heroes who stand true and strong to their ideas, the game as presented<br /> is pivoted towards different themes.<br /> <br /> But it's a coherent concept, which is explained again and again in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on a second... You're getting distracted. Are you telling me that the sort of introduction to W5 you're envisioning is trapping unknowing PCs in a scenario where they're asked to kill dozens of innocents during their First Change...?! You want the introduction to W5 to be about killing innocent people...?! Rather than the animistic worldview of WtA and how that interlocks with all sorts of issues in the world, you want to defend the idea that what <i>really </i>needs to be foregrounded is death and slaughter...?<br /> <br /> The Garou-Nation and Garou in general aren't supposed to be squeaky clean in terms of morals but they are the defenders of Gaia and have a holy mission. All the imperfections of Garou is where the grimdark comes in.<br /> <br /> If you go with &quot;First, the Garou are <i>just bad</i>...&quot;, then... okay, now what...? The whole game is nonsense and pointless at that point. Even if it's some sort of deconstructive commentary on the past... okay, congratulations, you've deconstructed it to the point of pointlessness. If you go too negative with Garou as &quot;holy warriors defending Gaia&quot; then having Garou in the game is pointless. The whole setup just falls apart.<br /> <br /> It's just setting up yet another self-destructive horizon like how anything beyond &quot;local hunter-cells&quot; is unimaginable in H5. W5's version of that is trying to be anything else than a singular pack of Garou hunkering down in a caern. Just a profound lack of variety and vision when it comes to gameplay here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T17:53:11-07:00","id":1522619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522615#post1522615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your cup of tea. My cup of tea, I'm pretty happy to have a set of similar and relatable mechanics, and I also appreciate that monsters (and monster hunters) are walking a thin line between using their power and abusing it.<br /> <br /> Saying they are the same would be like saying Mutant Year Zero and Coriolis are the same game because they are set in a distant future, they rely on the pushing mechanic, and the PCs are actively managing something. \ud83d\ude03</div> </div> </div> </div>You had both V:tM in the WoD and most of the CoD for that. W:tA didn't need to also be it; it is an entirely different game with different struggles in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T23:57:24-07:00","id":1522622,"title":"","content":"Garou are monsters and what they do is at times awful. But I feel the wedding example takes away from the intended play in W5.<br /> <br /> Because the PCs should still want to protect their Caern, they still should want to guard their territory. They should still believe that what they are doing is helping.<br /> <br /> But if your starting point is that garou happily sacrifice innocent lives for one first change, why should the PC want anything to do with the garou? Remember, unlike in V5 or in legacy WtA, a W5 garou can just LEAVE. They can just spend all their rage and never howl at the moon and be done with it.<br /> <br /> In W5, the PCs aren't forced into any roles by the Nation, they have to choose to commit to being a werewolf. So their experiences with garou society should be positive, especially for new players. You can play with more complex relations later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To give a more concrete example, say a PC decides that they rather not garou. They spend their Rage and then just return to everyday life. In Legacy, Rage, the Nation and the Wyrm made quitting nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> In W5, once you lose the wolf you legit can just coast by without gaining Rage as long as you don't howl at the moon, the Nation hasn't got much of a reach and the Wyrm's influence is massively lessened. Sure, a ST can throw baddies at the PC, but by lore and mechanics, they can just quit if they want to return to normal life.<br /> <br /> Plus, W5 still assumes your PCs WANT to be in a pack, that they WANT to guard the Caern and they WANT to make things better. A vampire in V5 has no choice, a garou in W5 as I stated above has very much a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 09-15-2023, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T05:17:58-07:00","id":1522699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522622#post1522622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In W5, once you lose the wolf you legit can just coast by without gaining Rage as long as you don't howl at the moon, the Nation hasn't got much of a reach and the Wyrm's influence is massively lessened. Sure, a ST can throw baddies at the PC, but by lore and mechanics, they can just quit if they want to return to normal life.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200bI'm trying to remember if their are actually any plot points that you'd even know about the moon thing if you'd turned with no werewolf peers around. You could theoretically just burn through your rage during the first few hours then spend your life as some guy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T07:05:33-07:00","id":1522701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522699#post1522699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b\u200bI'm trying to remember if their are actually any plot points that you'd even know about the moon thing if you'd turned with no werewolf peers around. You could theoretically just burn through your rage during the first few hours then spend your life as some guy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given the Rage pool is 5 and how many things cost Rage, yep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T08:17:51-07:00","id":1522705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522699#post1522699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b\u200bI'm trying to remember if their are actually any plot points that you'd even know about the moon thing if you'd turned with no werewolf peers around. You could theoretically just burn through your rage during the first few hours then spend your life as some guy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's the &quot;Starving Remnant&quot;-thing from the Antagonists-section: &quot;The First Change is frightful, and many fledgling Garou do not survive it. Even more frightful is the prospect of those Kin who experience their First Change and become lost in the Umbra, whether having lost contact with a spiritual guide who brought them there, or those who somehow crossed them Gauntlet themselves and were unable to make their way back.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> What I find strange about them is that they are these fledgling Garou &quot;winnowed to nothing&quot; in the Umbra and all that remains is their hunger. But then they are described as trying to &quot;lure&quot; Garou into the Umbra (by pretending to need help and whatnot) where they then stage an ambush. The way I would picture this concept is them being these malformed werewolves wandering the Umbra and taking every opportunity to attack stuff that seems weak. Like they're just a bunch of feral spirit-mutants roaming the Umbra. I wouldn't have figured that the described process would turn them into these tricksters who try to lure things into the Umbra in order to ambush them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T08:51:02-07:00","id":1522707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522705#post1522705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's the &quot;Starving Remnant&quot;-thing from the Antagonists-section: &quot;The First Change is frightful, and many fledgling Garou do not survive it. Even more frightful is the prospect of those Kin who experience their First Change and become lost in the Umbra, whether having lost contact with a spiritual guide who brought them there, or those who somehow crossed them Gauntlet themselves and were unable to make their way back.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> What I find strange about them is that they are these fledgling Garou &quot;winnowed to nothing&quot; in the Umbra and all that remains is their hunger. But then they are described as trying to &quot;lure&quot; Garou into the Umbra (by pretending to need help and whatnot) where they then stage an ambush. The way I would picture this concept is them being these malformed werewolves wandering the Umbra and taking every opportunity to attack stuff that seems weak. Like they're just a bunch of feral spirit-mutants roaming the Umbra. I wouldn't have figured that the described process would turn them into these tricksters who try to lure things into the Umbra in order to ambush them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they decided to half-heartedly rip off the Innocents that tormented the Mokole, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T09:59:29-07:00","id":1522708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522705#post1522705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's the &quot;Starving Remnant&quot;-thing from the Antagonists-section: &quot;The First Change is frightful, and many fledgling Garou do not survive it. Even more frightful is the prospect of those Kin who experience their First Change and become lost in the Umbra, whether having lost contact with a spiritual guide who brought them there, or those who somehow crossed them Gauntlet themselves and were unable to make their way back.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> What I find strange about them is that they are these fledgling Garou &quot;winnowed to nothing&quot; in the Umbra and all that remains is their hunger. But then they are described as trying to &quot;lure&quot; Garou into the Umbra (by pretending to need help and whatnot) where they then stage an ambush. The way I would picture this concept is them being these malformed werewolves wandering the Umbra and taking every opportunity to attack stuff that seems weak. Like they're just a bunch of feral spirit-mutants roaming the Umbra. I wouldn't have figured that the described process would turn them into these tricksters who try to lure things into the Umbra in order to ambush them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, they survived in the umbra? Doesn't staying there cost willpower per scene or the character takes agravated damage?<br /> <br /> Please tell me I misread and it's not a case of the writers forgetting their own rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T10:42:52-07:00","id":1522710,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this means anything, but I think I should mention it. I belong to a Werewolf group on Facebook. As such, the W5 group keeps popping up in my Suggestions feed, and I occasionally lurk on it to gauge the opinion on the new game. Just as the game was coming out, the opinion was overall <b><i><u>very</u></i></b> positive. Members hated anyone who had anything negative to say, even those who had carefully detailed reasons. After awhile, the positions became a little more nuanced and balanced, but still this hatred lingered towards those who hated the game. Now, after too many haters started posting to the group, it has splintered due to the original moderator not catching more of these types of posts. Well, I tried to check in on some of the members to get a deeper feeling last to why there was so much hatred, as something felt off to me.<br /> <br /> There were people who worked for game companies in the group. I didn't check to see if they were connected to Paradox or their subsidiaries, but it might not mean anything. Someone can like a game for a competitor without any issue. However, at least one member of the group only had a few pictures posted, and not really anything else. It's as if they only were on Facebook to be a part of this group. There was nothing in their profile about any other interests or even public information. Now, maybe they found a way to make such info private. Maybe they just skipped some steps as they felt it was unimportant. I've seen it happen. Maybe I'm just horrible at internet research in this regard. I am getting the same vibes I get whenever I receive a request from a woman from another country whose profile is just pictures of her in barely any clothing. Or less.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't want to make any accusations or draw a wrong conclusion, but you can see where I'm heading with this. With the original group splitting after more detailed opinions are spreading, this could mean something big is going on behind the scenes involving the game. I will keep investigating, but I am not sure what I will find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T12:00:09-07:00","id":1522717,"title":"","content":"Let's not purport conspiracy theories on this forum. People are entitled to like or dislike any game, regardless of the company they work for or how much or how little information is on their Facebook profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T13:18:45-07:00","id":1522721,"title":"","content":"Fair.<br /> <br /> Yeah I don't think it's deliberate. Their seem to be rather polarised on the subject, I suspect mod culture may be shaping the communities.<br /> <br /> From my observstions<br /> <br /> Discord-pro<br /> Oynx path-anti<br /> rpgnet-anti<br /> facebook-mixed, some pro some anti<br /> reddit theoretically mixed but very little discussion full stop.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T13:50:33-07:00","id":1522722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522721#post1522721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair.<br /> <br /> Yeah I don't think it's deliberate. Their seem to be rather polarised on the subject, I suspect mod culture may be shaping the communities.<br /> <br /> From my observstions<br /> <br /> Discord-pro<br /> Oynx path-anti<br /> rpgnet-anti<br /> facebook-mixed, some pro some anti<br /> reddit theoretically mixed but very little discussion full stop.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> can confirm your theory at least on discord. The mods have the banhammer easy on anyone criticising 5th edition in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T15:27:22-07:00","id":1522724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522721#post1522721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair.<br /> <br /> <br /> reddit theoretically mixed but very little discussion full stop.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Reddit is a bit complex. The site has two different subreddits for WoD. One, r/WhiteWolf, which is the biggest of the two, tended to be mixed but favored more the legacy stuff, but now there are new mods and I don't know what the situation are nowadays (but the last time I visited the site was like three months ago and I don't expect a real change than a more strict policy about edition wars maybe.It's true that I heard rumors about banhammer to all the people who dares to criticize W5 but take this with a grain of salt). In the other hand we have r/vtm which was pro 5th edition all the way around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","user":"Metalbird","date":". 09-17-2023, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T16:17:35-07:00","id":1522725,"title":"","content":"I am suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T16:44:26-07:00","id":1522726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metalbird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522724#post1522724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reddit is a bit complex. The site has two different subreddits for WoD. One, r/WhiteWolf, which is the biggest of the two, tended to be mixed but favored more the legacy stuff, but now there are new mods and I don't know what the situation are nowadays (but the last time I visited the site was like three months ago and I don't expect a real change than a more strict policy about edition wars maybe.It's true that I heard rumors about banhammer to all the people who dares to criticize W5 but take this with a grain of salt). In the other hand we have r/vtm which was pro 5th edition all the way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were super strict just as it landed, but things loosened up. I do feel it may have been partially due to the fact that things were really volatile with active shit stirring on both ends. For instance, someone was intentionally provoking drama with legacy folks just to put it on the official discord. The discussion and the dialogue now seems polite, even if my impression is that W5 isn't really well liked, but is accepted as a fact there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T04:43:15-07:00","id":1522821,"title":"","content":"Further thinking of this, I feel really weirded out by the changes made to the BSD and that one loresheet.<br /> <br /> For one, I know W5's main goal was to distance itself from the legacy, but the redemption of Bat could have been used as a way to show what the PCs can do without the Nation. A patron was rescued from the brink and now offers its patronage to garou. Yet, it still has to fight hard to keep its mind. A great way to showcase what garou CAN do when the Nation is not beating them down with its traditions.<br /> <br /> The loresheet baffles me, even if you aren't aware of legacy, just one look at any BSD art will tell you what they are like. While obviously it is bad to base morality on someone's appearance, BSDs even in W5 art still signal very strongly that they are just Wrong. Look at Retaliation's <a href=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/039/237/478/301ff9d0649a4068487ace0db40d5a83_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;w=700&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1668543977&amp;gif-q=50&amp;q=92&amp;s=934583b2d84b7a2b9c134347c6a9f014\" target=\"_blank\">BSD models</a> compared to its <a href=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/039/277/941/4039888191220c16e65db94f65d99b75_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;w=700&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1668953747&amp;gif-q=50&amp;q=92&amp;s=b03a48834e90009d24576a78aa503209\" target=\"_blank\">CoF</a> models. While neither is exactly pretty, the CoF lupus doesn't have SPIKES coming from its body. Nevermind that the lore isn't exactly saying they are too changed by their behaviour.<br /> <br /> So, who looks at a BSD and decides &quot;Oh, THESE guys can be redeemed&quot;? And not through a great quest or a costly spirit deal. No, in a loresheet you can max out at chargen. Even ignoring the fact that CoF can't be redeemed, this choice is so baffling given everything else W5 says and shows about BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T06:54:30-07:00","id":1522825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522821#post1522821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further thinking of this, I feel really weirded out by the changes made to the BSD and that one loresheet.<br /> <br /> For one, I know W5's main goal was to distance itself from the legacy, but the redemption of Bat could have been used as a way to show what the PCs can do without the Nation. A patron was rescued from the brink and now offers its patronage to garou. Yet, it still has to fight hard to keep its mind. A great way to showcase what garou CAN do when the Nation is not beating them down with its traditions.<br /> <br /> The loresheet baffles me, even if you aren't aware of legacy, just one look at any BSD art will tell you what they are like. While obviously it is bad to base morality on someone's appearance, BSDs even in W5 art still signal very strongly that they are just Wrong. Look at Retaliation's <a href=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/039/237/478/301ff9d0649a4068487ace0db40d5a83_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;w=700&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1668543977&amp;gif-q=50&amp;q=92&amp;s=934583b2d84b7a2b9c134347c6a9f014\" target=\"_blank\">BSD models</a> compared to its <a href=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/039/277/941/4039888191220c16e65db94f65d99b75_original.jpg?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&amp;w=700&amp;fit=max&amp;v=1668953747&amp;gif-q=50&amp;q=92&amp;s=b03a48834e90009d24576a78aa503209\" target=\"_blank\">CoF</a> models. While neither is exactly pretty, the CoF lupus doesn't have SPIKES coming from its body. Nevermind that the lore isn't exactly saying they are too changed by their behaviour.<br /> <br /> So, who looks at a BSD and decides &quot;Oh, THESE guys can be redeemed&quot;? And not through a great quest or a costly spirit deal. No, in a loresheet you can max out at chargen. Even ignoring the fact that CoF can't be redeemed, this choice is so baffling given everything else W5 says and shows about BSDs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they say on pg 277 in the antagonist section: &quot;Tonight the Black Spiral Dancers remain Garou, but Wyrm-twisted aberrations of those things the Garou themselves hold dear. Their bodies have been tortured into shapes resembling bats, feral dogs, rats, and even things unspeakable, as much as they resemble wolves. And though they still possess the ability to change shape, as do Gaian Garou, those shapes are hideous and unnatural.\u200b&quot; But the loresheet has this tone of &quot;Your character is friends with some bad kids on the schoolyard - but watch out, nobody likes seeing you hang out with the 'wrong crowd'!&quot;. The issue is more how &quot;scandalous&quot; your association with Wyrm-followers is (it's always about how other Garou will react badly when they find out just how close to the Wyrm-people-crowd you are). But on the other hand, you get descriptions like &quot;remarkably stable fomor&quot; (for the 2-dot-&quot;You have a contact&quot;-bit) or the phrasing for the 5-dot redemption &quot;Once per story, you can attempt to persuade a Black Spiral Dancer to <i>emancipate </i>themselves\u200b&quot;. The text on that loresheet comes off as surprisingly blas\u00e8 about the whole &quot;Wyrm-follower&quot;-bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T11:28:50-07:00","id":1522840,"title":"","content":"Today the new Loresheet is out. It's essentially The Winchesters Sisters hunting rogue werewolves and collecting werewolf and other monster lore. There's a lot of Supernatural cues in the Emissaries of Athena writeup, but something else popped up to me.<br /> <br /> There was a <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/werewolf-the-apocalypse-reboots-the-moonlight.699079/\" target=\"_blank\">glowing review on ENWorld about W5</a>. I didn't give it much weight at the description sounded like the person was writing a puff piece and wasn't really aware of older Werewolf material. I assumed they wanted to enjoy it in a vacuum and thought that was a good thing that someone could enjoy the game on its own. The only thing is... this glowing review is written by the same author who has been writing all these new bonus pieces for W5, Rob Wieland. He had to have known his work was going to be published for W5 not even a month ago, and I'm just confused how come he didn't let someone else handle the review!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:07:30-07:00","id":1522845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>New Loresheet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spiral Scar:<br /> You fought the Black Spiral Dancers alongside the Emissaries and have a scar to prove it. Once per session, when you discover evidence of any Black Spiral Dancer presence or a Storyteller character brings them up in conversation, set your rage to whatever level you desire from 0 to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wha? Now losing the wolf is a BENEFIT???<br /> <br /> ETA: Also, what sort of effect is this? &quot;I feel the BSDs presence so much I'm going to-be actually calm.&quot;<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 09-20-2023, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:21:48-07:00","id":1522846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522840#post1522840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today the new Loresheet is out. It's essentially The Winchesters Sisters hunting rogue werewolves and collecting werewolf and other monster lore. There's a lot of Supernatural cues in the Emissaries of Athena writeup, but something else popped up to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I figured when I saw the title and the image that this would be the first time the idea of &quot;camps&quot; would be re-introduced to W5 and this would be about a Black Furies Camp with a feminist focus. Instead... yeah, it not only sounds like it was inspired by Supernatural but the overall flair reminds me of &quot;mortal hunters vs supernatural&quot;. And it's noticeable how it never covers what these characters' struggle with Rage looks like. This portrayal of them as these adventurous do-gooders is quite at odds with the negative portrayal of Garou in the W5 corebook. Really doesn't feel like whoever wrote this was of the opinion that they are the &quot;wrong tool&quot; to fix the problems of the world...<br /> <br /> What bothers me the most is the cavalier attitude towards W5 as a system:<ul><li>They are a Pack with Athena as their Pack-Patron-Spirit... must be nice to be able to pick Pack-Patron-Spirits that aren't Tribal Patron-Spirits...</li> <li>&quot;when you discover evidence of any Black Spiral Dancer presence or a Storyteller character brings them up in conversation, set your rage to whatever level you desire from 0 to 5.\u200b&quot;... Really, &quot;when a ST-character brings them up in conversation&quot;?! And once per session setting your Rage at whatever level you desire is <i>really </i>good. Also, on a narrative level just a really weird mechanic...</li> <li>&quot;Gifts that use Wisdom in their dice pools cost two fewer experience points to learn to a minimum of one experience point.\u200b&quot; Gifts in W5 never cost 1 XP - even with two point reduction. The XP-cost for Gifts is &quot;New Gift amount x2&quot;. A player-character starts with three Gifts. Even if you started out with a character with no Gifts this sub-clause will only ever be relevant for the first Gift you theoretically buy a Gift with XP. And this sort of XP-reduction is also way too good as a mechanic, I feel like...</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:28:02-07:00","id":1522848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522846#post1522846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bothers me the most is the cavalier attitude towards W5 as a system:<ul><li>They are a Pack with Athena as their Pack-Patron-Spirit... must be nice to be able to pick Pack-Patron-Spirits that aren't Tribal Patron-Spirits...</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Especially given the core doesn't even have tools to create a custom totem spirit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:41:42-07:00","id":1522850,"title":"","content":"These are very strange Black Furies indeed if they follow <i>Athena</i> as a patron. Almost like something really important got lost on the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:43:31-07:00","id":1522852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522850#post1522850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are very strange Black Furies indeed if they follow <i>Athena</i> as a patron. Almost like something really important got lost on the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I thought that somebody would do that...<br /> <br /> But the pair of werewolves in this Loresheet are Silent Striders who have chosen Athena as their Pack-Patron-Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T13:01:11-07:00","id":1522853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522852#post1522852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I thought that somebody would do that...<br /> <br /> But the pair of werewolves in this Loresheet are Silent Striders who have chosen Athena as their Pack-Patron-Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right. The Owl thing. Do they still follow Owl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T13:06:05-07:00","id":1522855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522853#post1522853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, right. The Owl thing. Do they still follow Owl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> But the Loresheet neither addresses the Silent-Strider-curse which is this &quot;Who knows what's up with that...?&quot;-thing in the W5-version (but it still forces Silent Striders to wander). Sure, they wander but it doesn't seem like it's because they are Silent Striders and more because Supernatural is the inspiration here. And it also never addresses the W5-Tribe-Ban of the Silent Striders which is &quot;Owl remains ever alert to the return of the rival spirit-haunt that tormented his tribe in the past, and he makes sure to do so by honoring the presence of this \u201cother\u201d sort of spirit. If a Silent Strider causes, participates in, or even witnesses death but doesn\u2019t perform a commemorative rite to acknowledge it, they may recover only a single Willpower at the start of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b&quot;. Would've been interesting to see someone incorporate that in the depiction of a W5 Silent Strider NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T22:45:30-07:00","id":1522879,"title":"","content":"Somehow I missed a short story published by Renegade, could someone paste link here? Thank You.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T05:18:55-07:00","id":1522886,"title":"","content":"I still wonder why Garou is so in the dark about their past.<br /> Like, how is it possible that literally no one wrote or talked about the things from the past?<br /> In the previous editions, even killing a major foe would warrant a song, or tale or book to be written about them. Nevermind things like War of Rage or Set cursing the Slilent Striders or Mithras slaughtering hundreds of Werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:29:17-07:00","id":1522899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522886#post1522886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras slaughtering hundreds of Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras killed a large impromptu pack. That's most likely 10-20 garou. And the fight left him crippled enough to be eaten by a Neonate. Still impressive, but not ridiculous like &quot;slaughtering hundreds&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, one wonders what the Gallilards are even for in W5.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T08:57:04-07:00","id":1522901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522899#post1522899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mithras killed a large impromptu pack. That's most likely 10-20 garou. And the fight left him crippled enough to be eaten by a Neonate. Still impressive, but not ridiculous like &quot;slaughtering hundreds&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, one wonders what the Gallilards are even for in W5.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To repeatedly tell people, &quot;No one knows, it's a mystery!&quot;, when asked a question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T09:09:32-07:00","id":1522902,"title":"","content":"I think what makes it so bizarre is that this is a book that opens with &quot;re-imagination not continuation&quot;. So the writers have already given themselves license to reboot, remove and keep whatever they want. But then they've taken possibly the weirdest route to &quot;re-imagine&quot; these things. Like the Silent Strider curse or War of Rage. First, they aren't changed or removed, it's still there. But the way it's kept in the book is via this weird decision of removing context/knowledge but not the thing itself. The Silent Striders still have the same curse but... nobody knows why. The War of Rage happened and all the other changing breeds know that - except the Garou (for whatever reason). And because that's how it's presented, it isn't a mystery or a story-hook because the only question it evokes is &quot;Wait, but how did it come to be like that...?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The thing with the Stargazers and their new Patron-Spirit is similar: The Garou know Chimera isn't their Patron-Spirit anymore - but they have no idea who their new Patron-Spirit is... and that's all you get from the text. It would have been SO easy to just add &quot;The Stargazers refuse to talk about it and are very secretive.&quot;. Done, that's all you would've needed. But the text doesn't give you that.<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of Galliards... One of the Emissaries of Athena is a Galliard and I don't think it hits the right tone of oral storytelling/remembrance being this pillar of Garou culture with sentences like &quot;Tallulah loves to swap stories with fellow Galliards&quot; or the two-dot-bit &quot;You learned to love the stories of the Garou Nation from Tallulah. Especially the dirty ones.\u200b&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also this bit where I'm not sure what this even is supposed to mean in the context of WtA: &quot;While a lot of mythology centers on the history of the Garou Nation tribes, the information on other werewolves is less concrete. These enemies must be understood before they are destroyed, so the next time they appear they can be destroyed more efficiently.\u200b&quot; I mean... &quot;Other werewolves&quot;...? And this is in the context of why the two chose Athena, so what does &quot;While a lot of mythology...&quot; mean here? I don't think Greek mythology has a lot to say about the Garou Nation... Just weird...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T11:50:42-07:00","id":1522913,"title":"","content":"In terms of how W5 is, looking at how it has panned out I get this feeling it might be succeeding in its goal; For those who know only V5, W5 seems to be a good game to pick up and play. There are people saying this around.<br /> <br /> And I feel that might be one reason why W5 is so vague, because we've had vampire players come to this forum for years stating that WtA lore should be more vague. Here is WtA with vague lore.<br /> <br /> Of course, this still resulted in a rather shallow game, since a lot of the lore is not opened at all. Such as the Litany tenets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T13:43:54-07:00","id":1522920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522913#post1522913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of how W5 is, looking at how it has panned out I get this feeling it might be succeeding in its goal; For those who know only V5, W5 seems to be a good game to pick up and play. There are people saying this around.<br /> <br /> And I feel that might be one reason why W5 is so vague, because we've had vampire players come to this forum for years stating that WtA lore should be more vague. Here is WtA with vague lore.<br /> <br /> Of course, this still resulted in a rather shallow game, since a lot of the lore is not opened at all. Such as the Litany tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say that V:tM is into S&amp;M - being shallow and meaningless. Superficial isn't just its middle name, it's also a damage type!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T15:19:39-07:00","id":1522926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522913#post1522913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of how W5 is, looking at how it has panned out I get this feeling it might be succeeding in its goal; For those who know only V5, W5 seems to be a good game to pick up and play. There are people saying this around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean like if you put in those terms a comparable situation is the latest C&amp;C game being mobile games, like sure you can easily pick up and play and the game play might be pretty fun but it lacks something that attracted fans to the game in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T15:25:06-07:00","id":1522927,"title":"","content":"I think one of the big issues W5 will have to deal with is less the lore and more the system itself. Like H5, this is a game that should've been playtested more thoroughly. Take the Rage-economy in the game's system, for example. You see Rage-checks being mentioned here and there and since Rage is doing double-duty for parts of Gnosis of previous editions, it's now the battery for various powers as well. So that makes sense but certain provisions to when you can do what create hidden wrinkles to this system which lead to a pile-up of Rage-checks. Gifts can only be used in Glabro, Crinos and Hispo (unless otherwise stated). But if the cost of activating a Gift is a Rage-check this provision means the actual cost isn't one Rage-check but two (or 3 in Crinos). Same with Regeneration: You want to make use of supernaturally fast Regeneration? Shift into a supernatural form first and then do a Rage-check to regenerate... but similarly, this means the actual cost isn't just one Rage-check.<br /> <br /> And here's where the more punishing nature of W5's Rage-system compared to V5's Hunger-system comes in. In V5 the push/pull is the cost of keeping your Hunger low but if your Hunger's low... good for you. Not so in W5. Here you're kinda always screwed but in different ways depending on the situation. You keep your Rage too low and whatever the ST might throw at you might lead to your character ending up with Rage 0 / losing the wolf. You building up Rage to avoid that might screw up non-combat-scenes as Brutal Outcomes lead to automatic failures on rolls... unless... the character is acting aggressively and/or violently.<br /> <br /> And that's the part where the game kinda falls apart, I think. What's missing from the system here is the &quot;Humanity&quot;-part.<br /> <br /> Without that push from something like &quot;Humanity&quot;, the question is how players will respond to experiencing the downside of Rage 0/losing the wolf and high Rage disrupting non-aggressive/-violent actions in non-combat-scenes. If you run this game with RAW, it's entirely possible that the most effective way to play this game is to play the Garou-PCs exactly as the kind of overly volatile knuckleheads that are the &quot;wrong tool&quot; to save the world as the book says. And rather than the aspirational quality of Humanity, you get Harano and Hauglosk which are just two types of downward-spirals for your character. It's like the system was conceived to say that the Garou simply <i>can't </i>save the world no matter what they do.<br /> <br /> Also, this isn't just not fun for the player. If the players are unaware of all the hidden costs that pile up with Rage-checks and aren't too sensitive to how much Rage they should have built up before dealing with combat then the ST on behalf of the system has to punish the player for ending up with Rage 0. Or if a player wants to solve stuff non-violently but still has too much Rage then it's up to the ST to explain on behalf of the system why a Brutal Outcome has rendered their efforts futile. And the irony is: The player who plays their Garou-PC as this super-aggressive dickhead who has always high Rage, seeks constantly conflict, is aggressive and always treats violence like a viable solution... there's no punishment awaiting that guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T22:18:01-07:00","id":1522937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522899#post1522899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mithras killed a large impromptu pack. That's most likely 10-20 garou. And the fight left him crippled enough to be eaten by a Neonate. Still impressive, but not ridiculous like &quot;slaughtering hundreds&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, one wonders what the Gallilards are even for in W5.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about that stupid plot point. (Hell, I killed more Werewolves in a single fight as a younger Methuselah in a ToJ chronicle). I was talking about the times of Albion and Romans, see below;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps it was the growth of his cult, or perhaps the bloodshed of the war with the Iceni, but something drew Mithras\u2019 attention to these Isles.<br /> In AD 71, he revealed himself to his worshippers. As the legions marched against Venutius of the Celtic Brigantes tribe in the north, Mithras went with them. He inspired the troops to greater heights of bravery and bloodshed. Mithras, whatever else he is, is an ancient, and ancients need copious amounts of vitae. And Mithras was hungry. In the Caledonian wilderness, the legions fought against Celtic and Pictish tribes. In the cold damp nights, the Lupines descended upon the legion camps\u2026but Mithras slew them all. Hundreds died by his hand alone, it is said.The Romans cowered in fear at the sight of a god made flesh, but he protected them from the things of the darkness. He stood with the legate Gnaeus Julius Agricola\u2019s legions when the Caledonian resistance was finally broken.<br /> Though the Romans shattered British resistance, it never truly ended. A full tenth of the Roman military was stationed in this distant province, but there were always threats to Roman order. Opposition was never unified, but this was a mixed blessing; the barbarians attacked Imperial territory piecemeal, but a victory over one foe rarely guaranteed peace. Through it all stood Mithras, reveling in the carnage.<br /> Mithras was of greater age and puissance than any of his contemporaries. Making his headquarters under the Roman city of Londinium, his influence reached out to all parts of the Roman province of Britannia. Mithras in turn threatened the Roman vampires with extinction, having purged most of the older vampires from the Isles. He made London his domain, but all other cities were allowed remain independent, with their own princes, so long as they agreed to pay tribute to him. </div> </div> </div><br /> I miss how Garou remembered their history from their defeats to victories to their shames.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>As told by Michael Stonebrow, Galliard Adren of the Fianna to Burntfoot, his cliath nephew</i><br /> Forget what you think you know, cub. You know halftruths and fictions as told to you by your packmates. They claim events as fact that are fiction, and are ignorant of some of the Garou\u2019s greatest triumphs. The humans remember little of the first people to walk in the Isles now known as Britain, myth and legend serving as a veil to hide the truth from those who can\u2019t stand to know it. Only we Garou maintain a true history, sung by the wisest of our people and handed down from elder to cub over the centuries. It is an epic tale of great adventure and heroism, of the Tuatha de Danann, the conflict against the Fomorians, the Impergium, the War of Rage and the birth of the Rule of Man. Come closer, and listen to the tale. </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","user":"Technoma","date":". 09-22-2023, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T22:49:14-07:00","id":1522938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522937#post1522937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't talking about that stupid plot point. (Hell, I killed more Werewolves in a single fight as a younger Methuselah in a ToJ chronicle). I was talking about the times of Albion and Romans, see below;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...it is said <span style=\"font-size:8px\">by Vampire authors reaching for cheap heat.</span>...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T22:54:44-07:00","id":1522939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522938#post1522938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...it is said <span style=\"font-size:8px\">by Vampire authors reaching for cheap heat.</span>...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It was from Dark Ages: British Isles. It is a multi splat book and even the second quote from my post is from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-21T23:48:49-07:00","id":1522941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522939#post1522939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was from Dark Ages: British Isles. It is a multi splat book and even the second quote from my post is from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...yeah...but hundreds of Garou deaths empties large swathes of Europe leaving dozens of Caerns emptied even back in the DA. It's an event that potentially wipes out the majority of the Protectorates on the continent.....and yet is never mentioned in any other book.<br /> <br /> Besides, we've all seen Mithras statblocks...two dozen Garou is a big stretch for godboy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T00:16:06-07:00","id":1522945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522941#post1522941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...yeah...but hundreds of Garou deaths empties large swathes of Europe leaving dozens of Caerns emptied even back in the DA. It's an event that potentially wipes out the majority of the Protectorates on the continent.....and yet is never mentioned in any other book.<br /> <br /> Besides, we've all seen Mithras statblocks...two dozen Garou is a big stretch for godboy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We also never hear things like Tezghul the Insane ravaging the Europe, burning cities left and right and creating wastelands outside of a book or two with the justification of Order of Reason aka the Technocracy suppressing it.<br /> <br /> There are lots of things, for one reason or another, only mentioned briefly through out the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T01:36:04-07:00","id":1522949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522926#post1522926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean like if you put in those terms a comparable situation is the latest C&amp;C game being mobile games, like sure you can easily pick up and play and the game play might be pretty fun but it lacks something that attracted fans to the game in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it was intentional, but yes. Given how the latest loresheet works, it seems some writers aren't even engaging with the core mechanics at all. Because mention of BSDs= Free max or zero Rage and a custom totem feel odd.The game says you should only have tribal totems and anything else is for more experienced characters and given how Rage going up and down is a core mechanic, it feels like the writer wasn't beholden to how the game is supposed to function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T02:09:43-07:00","id":1522950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522949#post1522949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it was intentional, but yes. Given how the latest loresheet works, it seems some writers aren't even engaging with the core mechanics at all. Because mention of BSDs= Free max or zero Rage and a custom totem feel odd.The game says you should only have tribal totems and anything else is for more experienced characters and given how Rage going up and down is a core mechanic, it feels like the writer wasn't beholden to how the game is supposed to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it also seems the writer is thinking of the more descriptive variety of the Mentor-Background and not the somewhat busted version in the W5-corebook. Because according to this Loresheet the Emissaries would be equivalent to 1-dot-Mentor individually and a 2-dot if combined. The text acknowledges that they have low Renown but I don't think it's quite understood in that section just how low the described amount of Renown for the first two dots of the Mentor-Background is. Essentially any starting character would have the same amount of Renown as these Emissaries.<br /> <br /> Also, it's mentioned two times, the one time on the first page and then on the second one &quot;The Emissaries hunt non-tribal shapeshifters and have become experts on the subject.\u200b&quot;. This Loresheet acts like non-Tribal/non-Garou werewolves are a faction in the setting and they're... bad somehow? Or maybe this is supposed to be about the Stolen Moons...? But then why not say that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T07:16:17-07:00","id":1522956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522913#post1522913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of how W5 is, looking at how it has panned out I get this feeling it might be succeeding in its goal; For those who know only V5, W5 seems to be a good game to pick up and play. There are people saying this around.<br /> <br /> And I feel that might be one reason why W5 is so vague, because we've had vampire players come to this forum for years stating that WtA lore should be more vague. Here is WtA with vague lore.<br /> <br /> Of course, this still resulted in a rather shallow game, since a lot of the lore is not opened at all. Such as the Litany tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm one of those players, and I'd say that I do not want tge lore to be vague: I want the lore to be easily understandable and approached in different steps and with different intensity. <br /> <br /> There was a lot to study properly in old Wta and also old Wtf (as there was in VtM), which I felt intimidating to approach even as a VtM metaplot geek: generally speaking, I prefer lore to be modular. <br /> <br /> For my tastes and needs, W5 is optimal: there is a familiar setup, but with enough open spots that I can fill in, and I'm not getting the impression that to enter the game I have to master a very distinct and specialistic body of lore. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T07:57:23-07:00","id":1522958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522956#post1522956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm one of those players, and I'd say that I do not want tge lore to be vague: I want the lore to be easily understandable and approached in different steps and with different intensity.<br /> <br /> There was a lot to study properly in old Wta and also old Wtf (as there was in VtM), which I felt intimidating to approach even as a VtM metaplot geek: generally speaking, I prefer lore to be modular.<br /> <br /> For my tastes and needs, W5 is optimal: there is a familiar setup, but with enough open spots that I can fill in, and I'm not getting the impression that to enter the game I have to master a very distinct and specialistic body of lore.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel W5 does allow a much easier intro to WtA than Legacy.<br /> <br /> Though, I need to ask, how do you feel about the Litany not being explained outside &quot;It is bad and abused?&quot; Because in Legacy, each tenet was explained thoroughly. In W5 its just a list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T09:48:08-07:00","id":1522961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522939#post1522939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was from Dark Ages: British Isles. It is a multi splat book and even the second quote from my post is from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages treated its Vampire core as the single master core for its line, so the true multi-splatness is sus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T09:56:01-07:00","id":1522964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522958#post1522958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel W5 does allow a much easier intro to WtA than Legacy.<br /> <br /> Though, I need to ask, how do you feel about the Litany not being explained outside &quot;It is bad and abused?&quot; Because in Legacy, each tenet was explained thoroughly. In W5 its just a list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've understood it a bit like the Traditions in Masquerade - a connective tissue between Garou communities which is often interpreted locally or accordingly to power relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T10:38:06-07:00","id":1522967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522964#post1522964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've understood it a bit like the Traditions in Masquerade - a connective tissue between Garou communities which is often interpreted locally or accordingly to power relations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse this facetious question, but given how the book presents the Litany, how would you deal with a player character who decides that since the Litany is moot, they can freely engage in eating humans?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T11:07:05-07:00","id":1522968,"title":"","content":"Actually this would be a nice plot for a simple chronicle: there is a Garou - or small group of Garou - that have went full post-apocalyptic and are eating humans; they are seen as bulwarks against some rigid Elders, but they are increasingly violent and cannibalistic. What do the characters do?<br /> <br /> For a PC, besides Hauglosk checks? Well, depending on how organized is it, I suppose the local Garou community would still frown on this and punish the offender, unless there is a sizeable chunk of fanatic Red Talons, Second Inquisition would close in, killing after killing, and in the end probably Wyrm spirits would start crawling around him and the places where he kills.<br /> <br /> To use again a probably unpopular paragon with the Masquerade, even if the Traditions are constantly abused by the Elders, even the Anarchs and most of the Sabbat observe some common sense derivations of them. The same should be said of the Litany, even if the Nation is in disarray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-22-2023, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T11:10:08-07:00","id":1522969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522964#post1522964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've understood it a bit like the Traditions in Masquerade - a connective tissue between Garou communities which is often interpreted locally or accordingly to power relations.</div> </div> </div> </div>But surely the V:tM core goes into detail about the Traditions and expects them to be followed in a Cam city. W5 does neither.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T11:32:30-07:00","id":1522972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522968#post1522968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use again a probably unpopular paragon with the Masquerade, even if the Traditions are constantly abused by the Elders, even the Anarchs and most of the Sabbat observe some common sense derivations of them. The same should be said of the Litany, even if the Nation is in disarray.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book offers you a man-eater as a player character, so I assume that long pig is not that strange of a prey. Yes, it was a Red Talon, but even in Legacy you didn't have a Talon example character so focused on human-eating. Especially as Wyrm taint is seemingly no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> Plus, unlike Camarilla, Anarchs and the Sabbat, the Nation is not on the ropes, it is said to be gone.<br /> <br /> I personally find it really interesting to explore the idea of a bunch of garou who decide to hunt humans as their prey and even share hunting grounds with some vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T13:45:34-07:00","id":1522977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522972#post1522972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book offers you a man-eater as a player character, so I assume that long pig is not that strange of a prey. Yes, it was a Red Talon, but even in Legacy you didn't have a Talon example character so focused on human-eating. Especially as Wyrm taint is seemingly no longer a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting option, each Tribe has some more monstrous and inhuman example characters.<br /> <br /> I still see it as a borderline character in terms of degeneration, but it creates interesting narrative challenges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522972#post1522972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, unlike Camarilla, Anarchs and the Sabbat, the Nation is not on the ropes, it is said to be gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about the functioning of the old Nation, how cohesive it was at national and supranational level?<br /> From W5 core, I got the impression that the two main axes of sociopolitical action are local Caerns and Septs, and tribes as shared philosophies.<br /> <br /> The Litany, as the old law of the land, would still probably the default social arrangement, like the Traditions were still mostly respected during the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> To make a more post-apocalyptic comparison, I picture Garou communities a bit like survivor polities in a game like Twilight 2000: there are bits and remains of the old governments, sometimes not even communicating between them, independent warlords and those who simply try to live another day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522972#post1522972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally find it really interesting to explore the idea of a bunch of garou who decide to hunt humans as their prey and even share hunting grounds with some vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an absolutely neat concept!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-23-2023, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T14:09:21-07:00","id":1522978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522977#post1522977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about the functioning of the old Nation, how cohesive it was at national and supranational level?<br /> From W5 core, I got the impression that the two main axes of sociopolitical action are local Caerns and Septs, and tribes as shared philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>While septs were their own thing with their own cultures, there was this overarching sense of a nation. As garou are born and die and aren't immortal, the culture was taught from generation to generation in a much longer line than Camarilla traditions.<br /> <br /> More importantly, if sept A was in trouble, sept B could and was encouraged to help. While there was competition over caerns, generally everyone was working towards a single goal.<br /> <br /> Then there were the spirits, who could serve as a first warning in case of of Wyrmtaint. Of course there were pockets of such and anyone could fall. But if sept X was heard breaking the Litany, sept G could send judges to see if the rumour was true.<br /> <br /> Unlike Camarilla, the Nation had an unified goal of fighting the Wyrm which went over every single other thing.<br /> <br /> When I say the Nation is gone, I mean there is no longer this large spiritual and global oversight over the Litany being followed. There is no longer this unified goal that allowed garou to move from caern to caern. There is no longer any reason for each tribe to TRY and work together. The spirits have peaced out. First Changes no longer get covered up by a vast network of garou and garou relatives. And so on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T22:21:27-07:00","id":1522992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522968#post1522968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually this would be a nice plot for a simple chronicle: there is a Garou - or small group of Garou - that have went full post-apocalyptic and are eating humans; they are seen as bulwarks against some rigid Elders, but they are increasingly violent and cannibalistic. What do the characters do?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If This adventure doesn't end with a garou quoting captain Titus on the subject of the lantry (&quot;The Lantry is a set of rules. They guide us, shape us as Garous, teach us to place duty and honour above all. But how we live with those rules is the true test of a Garou&quot;). It would be a missed opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T01:26:41-07:00","id":1522996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522972#post1522972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally find it really interesting to explore the idea of a bunch of garou who decide to hunt humans as their prey and even share hunting grounds with some vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine vampires and Garou would willingly share hunting grounds. Setting aside that both are territorial - especially against each other - our hypothetical cannibal Garou pack would be directly depleting the &quot;herd&quot; of the vampires. Vampires, at least, don't need to kill their prey. Whereas these cannibal werewolves must, by definition.<br /> <br /> Plus, while a vampire can feed on people while drawing minimal attention to herself, if people start straight up disappearing (or showing up skeletonized), that attracts much more attention. There would be investigations. Even if people assume it's just man-eating wolves, that can create hunting parties of angry humans looking to purge the man-eaters in their area. People may also get scared, and stay at home more or travel in groups for protection.<br /> <br /> All this makes it very inconvenient for vampires (and werewolves) just looking to survive in peace. It doesn't matter if it actually causes problems. Just the possibility that any of this could happen is enough for the vampire(s) in the area to get pissed. Hence, being territorial.<br /> <br /> This is true regardless of what vampire sect we're talking about. Even the Sabbat don't &quot;shit where they eat&quot; if they can help it. And when they do kill people, they tend to either do it elsewhere (like in Camarilla territory, to make headaches for them), or dispose of it properly. They can't trust anyone else to deal with bodies piling up. Moreover, they're even more sensitive about other parties &quot;poaching&quot; their herds, because they also like to kill them. Can't have someone else literally eating into their numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> (One may argue, &quot;What if the Sabbat gives the bodies they drain to the werewolves? Win win!&quot;. The Garou would probably respond, &quot;WE DON'T NEED HANDOUTS! ESPECIALLY FROM SOME F***ING LEECHES! WE CAN HUNT FOR OURSELVES!&quot; Their pride wouldn't tolerate this kind of arrangement, no matter how beneficial.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T03:12:00-07:00","id":1523000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522937#post1522937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't talking about that stupid plot point. (Hell, I killed more Werewolves in a single fight as a younger Methuselah in a ToJ chronicle). I was talking about the times of Albion and Romans, see below;<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I do have that book and have read it a long time ago, but I probably just rolled my eyes and kept going. Hundreds of Lupines under his own hands does sound like an epic embellishment. I can see him being pivotal in helping the Romans against the White Howlers. But if he had killed hundreds and the rest of his legions and followers killed many as well, there wouldn't even be any White Howlers left by the time he was done. It's one of those things where people want to make insane Vampire NPC's unstoppable and then completely miss what that means in the context of another game. I'd chalk that down to a story vampires tell about him, rather than actual fact, as it's not supported by anything else in Werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T04:33:18-07:00","id":1523007,"title":"","content":"The thing with the Litany like with many other lore/worldbuilding-elements is that it's still mostly the same - except now it's defunct/worthless and in its presentation poorly explained. You could go by what the text says, focus on how Garou elders exploit it, how young Garou don't care for it, how Rage makes any interaction between Garou violent and difficult, how there are also young Garou who don't know the Litany at all... Okay, you do all that as ST, go into the same direction as the book describes, you present the same arguments as in the book and then you show the Litany as listed in the book to the players. And then when the ST talks about how elders abuse the part that says &quot;Submit to Those of Higher Station&quot;, a player then might just point to the same Litany and say &quot;Well, what about the one right underneath 'Respect Those of Lower Station, for All Are of Gaia.\u200b' ? The Litany doesn't seem that bad to me.&quot;. Of course, the text in the W5 corebook doesn't go into it because it's almost exclusively focused on the negative parts. And the text also gives short shrift to the interplay between the Litany and the Philodox- and Ragabash-Auspice. Not that this is an isolated problem, the book doesn't offer a lot of help with depicting Septs and Moots either.<br /> <br /> It's also that issue again that it isn't really cutting down on worldbuilding/lore because even the reduced list of the Litany still has a lot of tenets. VtM has six traditions while even with the reduction the Litany has eleven. And the V5-core-book (as it should have been done here) goes through the traditions one by one and gives some short comments. You got the old Litany here and yet it just gets this overly negative dismissive commentary while poorly explaining all the parts that are still right there. And since it's a reboot, it's strange that it was done this way. Since it seems the direction was so averse to the idea of worldbuilding/lore, they could've simply rewritten the Litany and simplified it for the sake of accessibility. But they didn't.<br /> <br /> Rather than re-imagination, the style of changes made in this edition are merely cutting out the context and depth of previous editions. And the ST is burdened to make sense of all these various setting-elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T05:23:11-07:00","id":1523010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1522978#post1522978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While septs were their own thing with their own cultures, there was this overarching sense of a nation. As garou are born and die and aren't immortal, the culture was taught from generation to generation in a much longer line than Camarilla traditions.<br /> <br /> More importantly, if sept A was in trouble, sept B could and was encouraged to help. While there was competition over caerns, generally everyone was working towards a single goal.<br /> <br /> Then there were the spirits, who could serve as a first warning in case of of Wyrmtaint. Of course there were pockets of such and anyone could fall. But if sept X was heard breaking the Litany, sept G could send judges to see if the rumour was true.<br /> <br /> Unlike Camarilla, the Nation had an unified goal of fighting the Wyrm which went over every single other thing.<br /> <br /> When I say the Nation is gone, I mean there is no longer this large spiritual and global oversight over the Litany being followed. There is no longer this unified goal that allowed garou to move from caern to caern. There is no longer any reason for each tribe to TRY and work together. The spirits have peaced out. First Changes no longer get covered up by a vast network of garou and garou relatives. And so on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the unified Nation fell apart as Gaia started to send his mysterious Howl: Stargazers quit, the Cult of Fenris rose and probably a number of Septs and Caerns fell to civil war or millenaristic gloom.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think that the fall of the Nation would instantly mean total anarchy: spirits still respect Renown and ancient binds, even though many of them may be resentful of Garou failures. Tribal spirits, of course, are the more important: they actively recruit Garou in their ranks, I think it's implied, and their Ban and Favors provide a rough sort of moral code to recruits.<br /> <br /> Septs and Caerns will maintain old ties and alliances, and in most instances, to facilitate relations, the Litany will probably just be the equivalent of Lex Mercatorum or other Common Law set of shared norms which have emerged from constant interaction.<br /> <br /> Of course, differing political setups will probably result in different interpretations of the Litany, and there will be pockets of dissidence, apostasy or total rejection and autarky- but even when the Core says that the Litany was often abused, those who try to uphold it are not defined as &quot;the villains&quot; or the abusers, mostly as utopians. So, it's not like the Litany is totally discredited, I think it's mostly seen as something like &quot;real Communism was never tried&quot; or &quot;Yes, capitalism gave us CIA death squads, but also development and wealth&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Garou live in a post-apocalyptic society hidden within daily routine - which adds to the feeling of isolation and urgency - and the more I think of it, the more taking some cues fromTwilight 2000 seems interesting -<br /> <br /> I know this is not going to be everyone's setting of choice, but I rather like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T05:56:19-07:00","id":1523013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523010#post1523010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose the unified Nation fell apart as Gaia started to send his mysterious Howl: Stargazers quit, the Cult of Fenris rose and probably a number of Septs and Caerns fell to civil war or millenaristic gloom.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think that the fall of the Nation would instantly mean total anarchy: spirits still respect Renown and ancient binds, even though many of them may be resentful of Garou failures. Tribal spirits, of course, are the more important: they actively recruit Garou in their ranks, I think it's implied, and their Ban and Favors provide a rough sort of moral code to recruits.<br /> <br /> Septs and Caerns will maintain old ties and alliances, and in most instances, to facilitate relations, the Litany will probably just be the equivalent of Lex Mercatorum or other Common Law set of shared norms which have emerged from constant interaction.<br /> <br /> Of course, differing political setups will probably result in different interpretations of the Litany, and there will be pockets of dissidence, apostasy or total rejection and autarky- but even when the Core says that the Litany was often abused, those who try to uphold it are not defined as &quot;the villains&quot; or the abusers, mostly as utopians. So, it's not like the Litany is totally discredited, I think it's mostly seen as something like &quot;real Communism was never tried&quot; or &quot;Yes, capitalism gave us CIA death squads, but also development and wealth&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Garou live in a post-apocalyptic society hidden within daily routine - which adds to the feeling of isolation and urgency - and the more I think of it, the more taking some cues fromTwilight 2000 seems interesting -<br /> <br /> I know this is not going to be everyone's setting of choice, but I rather like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that none of that is in the book? You're building this on past context that's not relevant here. Which is fine for your table, but does not give a common context to play in.<br /> <br /> Beside that the Litany is supposed to be a set of laws interpreted and enforced by the Garou society for untold times. How is this done by the Ragabash and Philodilox of W5? And considering the attitude towards the litany, why would the players bother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:07:46-07:00","id":1523015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523013#post1523013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise that none of that is in the book? You're building this on past context that's not relevant here. Which is fine for your table, but does not give a common context to play in.<br /> <br /> Beside that the Litany is supposed to be a set of laws interpreted and enforced by the Garou society for untold times. How is this done by the Ragabash and Philodilox of W5? And considering the attitude towards the litany, why would the players bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this (the spirits) is in the core, the rest is mostly extrapolation based on common sense. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm really sick and tired of this militant tone. &quot;I do realize&quot; that most of the time I'm not allowed to like the game or to even discuss it creatively, because you don't like it? <br /> <br /> Ok, then, what's the point of having a discussion about it? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:25:52-07:00","id":1523017,"title":"","content":"Oh by all means enjoy the game if you like it. But do not expect that you will change our minds or expectations just because you think &quot;it's common sense&quot;. You're consistantly arguing against criticisms of the writing with the logic of &quot;it works for me!&quot;. That's not addressing or engaging with the topic.<br /> <br /> For instance, your idea of how this should work is quite reasonable, but it's not in the book that came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:29:29-07:00","id":1523018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523017#post1523017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh by all means enjoy the game if you like it. But do not expect that you will change our minds or expectations just because you think &quot;it's common sense&quot;. You're consistantly arguing against criticisms of the writing with the logic of &quot;it works for me!&quot;. That's not addressing or engaging with the topic.<br /> <br /> For instance, your idea of how this should work is quite reasonable, but it's not in the book that came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not remotely interested in changing your minds, but there are users willing to discuss the game even if they don't like it, and others who are more interested in policing the thread. <br /> <br /> If someone asks me &quot;how do you envision the thing X&quot;, and I answer accordingly to what I've read and what I would do, silencing me with &quot; You do realize it's not written in the book&quot; it's not meaningful engagement neither.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-23-2023, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:48:57-07:00","id":1523021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523018#post1523018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not remotely interested in changing your minds, but there are users willing to discuss the game even if they don't like it, and others who are more interested in policing the thread.<br /> <br /> If someone asks me &quot;how do you envision the thing X&quot;, and I answer accordingly to what I've read and what I would do, silencing me with &quot; You do realize it's not written in the book&quot; it's not meaningful engagement neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't just that it's not in the book, it's that very, very little is in the book, and the ST is now required to spend all the energy of a D&amp;D 5e DM for a game that doesn't have the popularity of D&amp;D 5e. That may on-board some players, but it's going to burn out STs, and that's probably not going to be good for the game in the long run.<br /> <br /> Also, why the fuck are you paying 50 USD for a book that has so little in it that you have to do most of the work? It seems like a bad return. You might get one game up and running, but what about after that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:59:14-07:00","id":1523025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523021#post1523021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't just that it's not in the book, it's that very, very little is in the book, and the ST is now required to spend all the energy of a D&amp;D 5e DM for a game that doesn't have the popularity of D&amp;D 5e. That may on-board some players, but it's going to burn out STs, and that's probably not going to be good for the game in the long run.<br /> <br /> Also, why the fuck are you paying 50 USD for a book that has so little in it that you have to do most of the work? It seems like a bad return. You might get one game up and running, but what about after that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, outburning storytellers is a risk when you have to create a lot, but it may also be a risk when you have to over-study existing materials, especially if at the table there are experienced players with command over the lore. <br /> <br /> When you have a broad setup, you can get creative without the need for double checking. <br /> <br /> 50 dollars for a 350 pages book, btw, is a fair price, I would say, there are quite worse deals out there in the rpg world, both in the WoD (I'm looking at you, Sabbat V5 book), and in the general Rpg market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T07:28:41-07:00","id":1523026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523025#post1523025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, outburning storytellers is a risk when you have to create a lot, but it may also be a risk when you have to over-study existing materials, especially if at the table there are experienced players with command over the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sessions zero. Agree on what to use and what not to. It's easier to cut from a larger whole than to try and produce material to fill the yawning void.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you have a broad setup, you can get creative without the need for double checking.<br /> <br /> 50 dollars for a 350 pages book, btw, is a fair price, I would say, there are quite worse deals out there in the rpg world, both in the WoD (I'm looking at you, Sabbat V5 book), and in the general Rpg market. </div> </div> </div>It isn't about the page count. Some very thin books have been very dense with useful content. W5 is 350 pages of abandonment of the responsibilities of a core setting book. It is aggressively against telling you anything. If you can get something out of that, great, but you could potentially have gotten it out of anything, like Agent Mulder of the X-Files solving cases by way of zoning out while watching <i>Plan Nine From Outer Space</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T09:27:20-07:00","id":1523034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523026#post1523026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sessions zero. Agree on what to use and what not to. It's easier to cut from a larger whole than to try and produce material to fill the yawning void.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, changing/challenging the metaplot is way more difficult than creating from nothing. Players can get attached to what they find in the books and could react badly when the storyteller changes something because &quot;It's not the GAME anymore&quot;. Sometimes the along-the-line messages become &quot;How dare you change something that I spend time learning&quot; or even &quot;How dare you change something that I studied making me equal to the novices&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T10:05:28-07:00","id":1523035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523034#post1523034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience, changing/challenging the metaplot is way more difficult than creating from nothing. Players can get attached to what they find in the books and could react badly when the storyteller changes something because &quot;It's not the GAME anymore&quot;. Sometimes the along-the-line messages become &quot;How dare you change something that I spend time learning&quot; or even &quot;How dare you change something that I studied making me equal to the novices&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flipside of that is that due to poor worldbuilding you ask four people what their takeaway is from reading the book and you get four different answers. That's why in those situations the burden of worldbuilding is shifted either completely onto the Storyteller or it's something you have to address during Session Zero. Like the book says it's happening during the Age of Apocalypse... so when did it start? Then if someone's read the book closely, you're probably gonna have a discussion about the capitalocene era and when people think that started. Or the event of the Fenrir and the Stargazers leaving? Or the Garou-Nation falling? When did this happen, ten years ago, fifty, a thousand...? Who knows...<br /> <br /> And W5 isn't like an Apocalypse World where beyond some tentpoles in worldbuilding (the post-apocalypse genre, the Maelstrom and what the Playbooks imply) you're mostly working with a blank canvas. W5 has a lot of distinct concepts but there are a lot of questions left unanswered as to how these concepts work. Also, unlike any good PbtA-game the game just either shrugs about giving information or just ignores it. There's no point in the book where it gives guidance on how to fill out the blank spaces or what sort of questions you might ask in Session Zero for the sake of completing the process of worldbuilding. When you play this game and in the fourth session somebody asks the ST about how long the Garou-Nation lasted, I certainly don't think giving an answer like &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia?&quot; would be satisfactory. \u200bAnd you can't move it too far back into the past because that would imply the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers left the Garou-Nation thousands of years ago. But if you put it too close to the present, you start to wonder why nobody knows a damn thing about it. And that's an example of how you're not working with a blank canvas here because &quot;Fall of Garou-Nation&quot;, &quot;Cult of Fenris/Stargazers leaving&quot; and &quot;What was the Garou-Nation like?&quot; are all tied together while also being hamstrung by the book's careless &quot;Who knows&quot;-attitude towards worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> W5 is in the tricky spot where it does too much worldbuilding to allow the sort of freewheeling collaborative worldbuilding you do in a lot of PbtA-games but it does too little to serve as a reliable guide to how its setting works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T10:12:00-07:00","id":1523036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523034#post1523034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience, changing/challenging the metaplot is way more difficult than creating from nothing. Players can get attached to what they find in the books and could react badly when the storyteller changes something because &quot;It's not the GAME anymore&quot;. Sometimes the along-the-line messages become &quot;How dare you change something that I spend time learning&quot; or even &quot;How dare you change something that I studied making me equal to the novices&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone plays how they play and I'm not trying to say the way you play is wrong.<br /> <br /> But as someone on RPG.net so well pointed out; W5 is not a generic werewolf game.<br /> <br /> You can do Interview with Vampire in VtM, you can do Lost Boys in VtM, you can do Nosferatu in VtM. The game, though filled with a lot of lore, is not reliant on it.<br /> <br /> You can't do Teen Wolf in WtA, you can't do American Werewolf in London in WtA, you can't do The Howling in WtA. Unlike VtM which has no one true type of vampire, WtA has exactly one type of werewolf as playable, with Stolen Moon as pure antagonists that are not expanded on much.<br /> <br /> Trying to be a more open-to-interpretation setting is hampered by the fact that the garou still have auspices, still have five forms, still are implied to be born and still have tribes and patrons. Making up stuff is cool, but how easy it is to fall back on Legacy which already has every answer the players might be asking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T12:17:45-07:00","id":1523042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523034#post1523034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience, changing/challenging the metaplot is way more difficult than creating from nothing. Players can get attached to what they find in the books and could react badly when the storyteller changes something because &quot;It's not the GAME anymore&quot;. Sometimes the along-the-line messages become &quot;How dare you change something that I spend time learning&quot; or even &quot;How dare you change something that I studied making me equal to the novices&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaplot? Of all the games to complain about the metaplot, you pick Werewolf? The game where the overarching stories were drawn in deliberately broad strokes to incorporate player characters? The game where, even when the Stargazer leadership was gone from the Garou Nation, there were still an allowance to play Stargazers because packmates don't just pack up and leave so easily? That metaplot?<br /> <br /> The most heavy-handed thing that ever happened for Werewolf was arguably the Week of Nightmares, and that was because everyone had to deal with Vampire's baggage, since it always wants to make an Important NPC the center of action while players watch hopelessly and without agency from the sidelines. That is crap, and that's why it's really great that Werewolf didn't ever do it, even with Albrecht.<br /> <br /> Oh, I suppose that the Swords of Heimdall players were also out of luck, but in the words of Abridged Yajirobe, <i>they're weird</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T15:36:35-07:00","id":1523052,"title":"","content":"It speaks volume of how your setting is setup when you establish character X is the King of all the Werewolves and can order them or organise them in any way possible. And he proceeds to fuck off and have his own little projects so he doesn't meddle in PC affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T20:54:26-07:00","id":1523066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523035#post1523035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flipside of that is that due to poor worldbuilding you ask four people what their takeaway is from reading the book and you get four different answers. That's why in those situations the burden of worldbuilding is shifted either completely onto the Storyteller or it's something you have to address during Session Zero. Like the book says it's happening during the Age of Apocalypse... so when did it start? Then if someone's read the book closely, you're probably gonna have a discussion about the capitalocene era and when people think that started. Or the event of the Fenrir and the Stargazers leaving? Or the Garou-Nation falling? When did this happen, ten years ago, fifty, a thousand...? Who knows...<br /> <br /> And W5 isn't like an Apocalypse World where beyond some tentpoles in worldbuilding (the post-apocalypse genre, the Maelstrom and what the Playbooks imply) you're mostly working with a blank canvas. W5 has a lot of distinct concepts but there are a lot of questions left unanswered as to how these concepts work. Also, unlike any good PbtA-game the game just either shrugs about giving information or just ignores it. There's no point in the book where it gives guidance on how to fill out the blank spaces or what sort of questions you might ask in Session Zero for the sake of completing the process of worldbuilding. When you play this game and in the fourth session somebody asks the ST about how long the Garou-Nation lasted, I certainly don't think giving an answer like &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia?&quot; would be satisfactory. \u200bAnd you can't move it too far back into the past because that would imply the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers left the Garou-Nation thousands of years ago. But if you put it too close to the present, you start to wonder why nobody knows a damn thing about it. And that's an example of how you're not working with a blank canvas here because &quot;Fall of Garou-Nation&quot;, &quot;Cult of Fenris/Stargazers leaving&quot; and &quot;What was the Garou-Nation like?&quot; are all tied together while also being hamstrung by the book's careless &quot;Who knows&quot;-attitude towards worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> W5 is in the tricky spot where it does too much worldbuilding to allow the sort of freewheeling collaborative worldbuilding you do in a lot of PbtA-games but it does too little to serve as a reliable guide to how its setting works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, to me it seemed like they just meant that these questions don't need to be relevant and you can just play without having to worry about the Garou nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T21:53:01-07:00","id":1523068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523066#post1523066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, to me it seemed like they just meant that these questions don't need to be relevant and you can just play without having to worry about the Garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it isn't relevant you wouldn't dedicate a whole sub-section to it. And since you're playing a Garou in this game, it <i>is </i>relevant. Also this attitude in the book of &quot;Who knows&quot; lands in a category of authoritative anti-world-building. After all, rather than giving a detailed explanation for how to portray something or offering questions about the world that need to be resolved during session zero, this style of description is saying &quot;Yeah, this element in the setting is like... whatever... so do <i>not </i>care about this in your game, understood?&quot;. The moment you got a player who cares about the worldbuilding and is asking questions about the Garou Nation, you can't just be like &quot;Ah, not relevant, who cares... let's move on.&quot;. And the point of a book like the W5 corebook is to help STs with that. Telling them to not worry about it isn't a solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T23:59:54-07:00","id":1523069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523035#post1523035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flipside of that is that due to poor worldbuilding you ask four people what their takeaway is from reading the book and you get four different answers. That's why in those situations the burden of worldbuilding is shifted either completely onto the Storyteller or it's something you have to address during Session Zero.<br /> [...]<br /> When you play this game and in the fourth session somebody asks the ST about how long the Garou-Nation lasted, I certainly don't think giving an answer like &quot;The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia?&quot; would be satisfactory. \u200bAnd you can't move it too far back into the past because that would imply the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers left the Garou-Nation thousands of years ago. But if you put it too close to the present, you start to wonder why nobody knows a damn thing about it. And that's an example of how you're not working with a blank canvas here because &quot;Fall of Garou-Nation&quot;, &quot;Cult of Fenris/Stargazers leaving&quot; and &quot;What was the Garou-Nation like?&quot; are all tied together while also being hamstrung by the book's careless &quot;Who knows&quot;-attitude towards worldbuilding.<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I do not see the problem in getting different answers to that specific question. There could be different takeaways from an RPG book based on personal taste and interest. People could have significantly different takeaways from the meaning (but also on the role of different characters or what the authors would like to say and so on) of stories it will be surprising if they do not get different takeaways from books that describe the background that they should you use to build their stories. Also, it seems that up until now people are getting sensible takeaways from W5 in terms of game mood and theme.<br /> 2) If the question is in the game you should respond from the NPC point of view, if it is outside of the game you can point out that the book is not clear on this topic and that you choose a certain event. Nevertheless, I would like to encourage you to consider another point of view, the ends of a huge societal construct like the Garou Nation is not a clear process, think of the fall of the Roman Empire, there are multiple interpretations for this long and complex events. Things get more complicated when you look at the Roman Empire's succession. If you prefer a (minor) modern example the formation and evolution of the Italian state(Now it is the second or the third republic? Which are the relationships between monarchical and republican institutions?).<br /> Sure they can provide a timeline but I do not think that the lack of it could constitute a fatal flow for W5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T04:12:29-07:00","id":1523074,"title":"","content":"All I'm seeing are 6-8 hour session zeros as every single player brings their own interpretation of the nebulous language used in W5 to the table and its up to the ST to sort it all into some sort of semblance of sanity. Thats way too much work to foist onto a new ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T05:31:39-07:00","id":1523075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523069#post1523069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) I do not see the problem in getting different answers to that specific question. There could be different takeaways from an RPG book based on personal taste and interest. People could have significantly different takeaways from the meaning (but also on the role of different characters or what the authors would like to say and so on) of stories it will be surprising if they do not get different takeaways from books that describe the background that they should you use to build their stories. Also, it seems that up until now people are getting sensible takeaways from W5 in terms of game mood and theme.<br /> 2) If the question is in the game you should respond from the NPC point of view, if it is outside of the game you can point out that the book is not clear on this topic and that you choose a certain event. Nevertheless, I would like to encourage you to consider another point of view, the ends of a huge societal construct like the Garou Nation is not a clear process, think of the fall of the Roman Empire, there are multiple interpretations for this long and complex events. Things get more complicated when you look at the Roman Empire's succession. If you prefer a (minor) modern example the formation and evolution of the Italian state(Now it is the second or the third republic? Which are the relationships between monarchical and republican institutions?).<br /> Sure they can provide a timeline but I do not think that the lack of it could constitute a fatal flow for W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I mean the only takeaway I've seen is the book creates more work for people who play this game. And most times what instead happens is that people are just looking at the previous editions for explanations instead. Because at the end of the day, you just get a reference from the previous editions but in a way that's poorly explained. And the W5-setting has trouble standing on its own.<br /> <br /> 2) The comparisons you mention work insofar as they show off the bad worldbuilding in this book. There's a ton of rememberance-culture about Rome and its fall in the centuries afterwards. Nobody was like &quot;Rome was successful for a time. How long did it last? A decade? A century? Who knows...&quot;. The fall of Rome didn't erase Rome from everybody's memory unlike what this book has to say about the Garou-Nation.<br /> <br /> And sure you can choose a certain event to find your own explanation which again points to the book creating more work for the ST through its lackluster efforts. And there's nothing worthwhile about having to do worldbuilding on such a basic level. This isn't about the ST working off of a story-seed that inspires what happens in the next gaming-session, this is the ST finishing the job the corebook should have done.<br /> <br /> I think the whole thing is only a fatal flaw in the sense that, for example, it feels superficial that you have this book which is all about the &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; and yet even something basic as that is so vaguely defined that the book doesn't tell you when it started. Same as with the Garou-Nation we're talking here about a scale of vagueness that is mindboggling. Giving an important event in the setting a possibility-range between it happening thousands of years ago and it happening ten years ago is just shrugging and refusing to do basic worldbuilding. Especially since it's also supposed to happen in the context of the real world and with one of the Auspices, the Galliards, being supposedly dedicated to storytelling and lorekeeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T06:51:38-07:00","id":1523077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523068#post1523068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it isn't relevant you wouldn't dedicate a whole sub-section to it. And since you're playing a Garou in this game, it <i>is </i>relevant. Also this attitude in the book of &quot;Who knows&quot; lands in a category of authoritative anti-world-building. After all, rather than giving a detailed explanation for how to portray something or offering questions about the world that need to be resolved during session zero, this style of description is saying &quot;Yeah, this element in the setting is like... whatever... so do <i>not </i>care about this in your game, understood?&quot;. The moment you got a player who cares about the worldbuilding and is asking questions about the Garou Nation, you can't just be like &quot;Ah, not relevant, who cares... let's move on.&quot;. And the point of a book like the W5 corebook is to help STs with that. Telling them to not worry about it isn't a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant is that their possible intention was that you don't need to play as a werewolf from the Garou nation, or care about the Garou nation, if that's your wish, you can ignore all that and just be a werewolf. using the powers for personal gain or whatever cause you want while facing off against other werewolves or hunters. It's not an attitude that I approve of, especially because it takes away what WTA highlighted, but anyone can use this argument saying that the book gives you total freedom to make the type of story you want, including one based on the old WOD and that you are wrong for restricting others from wanting different stories and I think it's difficult for this version to have been made without having that thought in mind. Regardless of the truth, this is what it seems like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T11:02:12-07:00","id":1523083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523077#post1523077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I meant is that their possible intention was that you don't need to play as a werewolf from the Garou nation, or care about the Garou nation, if that's your wish, you can ignore all that and just be a werewolf. using the powers for personal gain or whatever cause you want while facing off against other werewolves or hunters. It's not an attitude that I approve of, especially because it takes away what WTA highlighted, but anyone can use this argument saying that the book gives you total freedom to make the type of story you want, including one based on the old WOD and that you are wrong for restricting others from wanting different stories and I think it's difficult for this version to have been made without having that thought in mind. Regardless of the truth, this is what it seems like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, we circle back to &quot;if this W:tA core doesn't want to be W:tA, why bother buying it or using it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T11:31:30-07:00","id":1523087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523083#post1523083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again, we circle back to &quot;if this W:tA core doesn't want to be W:tA, why bother buying it or using it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I've seen by comparing it to our association copies of WtA revised and W20, this WtA is still very much WtA.<br /> <br /> It's still an animistic game of savage warriors fighting to save a dying planet from the forces of Entropy and greed. There are still tribes, forms, Gaia and the Umbra, and most of the basic old assumptions still apply.<br /> <br /> The main variations are in tone, and in the social setup of the game, but not to the point of making the game basically unplayable, as it's often argued.<br /> <br /> It's a darker WtA, but it's still recognizably WtA. It doesn't want Garou to be a cohesive army on march in a difficult conflict, but a scattered motley of partisans currently overwhelmed by the enemy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:04:09-07:00","id":1523092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523087#post1523087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I've seen by comparing it to our association copies of WtA revised and W20, this WtA is still very much WtA.<br /> <br /> It's still an animistic game of savage warriors fighting to save a dying planet from the forces of Entropy and greed. There are still tribes, forms, Gaia and the Umbra, and most of the basic old assumptions still apply.<br /> <br /> The main variations are in tone, and in the social setup of the game, but not to the point of making the game basically unplayable, as it's often argued.<br /> <br /> It's a darker WtA, but it's still recognizably WtA. It doesn't want Garou to be a cohesive army on march in a difficult conflict, but a scattered motley of partisans currently overwhelmed by the enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you stick to incredibly broad descriptors I suppose anything could be similar. Also, the fact that it doesn't want Garou to be a cohesive army on the march, at least from time to time, makes it very, very much <b>not</b> W:tA.<br /> <br /> Edit: The rules that have been dissected online don't seem to really encourage being a group of partisans, either, since you can just burn out your rage and leave, and you don't have a culture to rally around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-24-2023, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:21:52-07:00","id":1523094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523092#post1523092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: The rules that have been dissected online don't seem to really encourage being a group of partisans, either, since you can just burn out your rage and leave, and you don't have a culture to rally around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Burning your Rage and quitting is more theory than practice: you acquire Rage by provocation, so losing the Wolf is granted to be temporary. <br /> <br /> You have a culture, which is falling apart, and a subculture, which gives you a modus operandi, a favor and a ban which are both practical and moral elements. <br /> <br /> Seems to me very close to the real-life experience of partisan groups with differing ideologies but a shared enemy... which may be enough not to fight between themselves, or not. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:22:58-07:00","id":1523095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523092#post1523092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you stick to incredibly broad descriptors I suppose anything could be similar. Also, the fact that it doesn't want Garou to be a cohesive army on the march, at least from time to time, makes it very, very much <b>not</b> W:tA.<br /> <br /> Edit: The rules that have been dissected online don't seem to really encourage being a group of partisans, either, since you can just burn out your rage and leave, and you don't have a culture to rally around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Burning your Rage and quitting is more theory than practice: you acquire Rage by provocation, so losing the Wolf is granted to be temporary. <br /> You have a culture, which is falling apart, and a subculture, which gives you a modus operandi, a favor and a ban which are both practical and moral elements.<br /> <br /> Seems to me very close to the real-life experience of partisan groups with differing ideologies but a shared enemy... which may be enough not to fight between themselves, or not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:41:08-07:00","id":1523096,"title":"","content":"Well, a crumbling culture and several ideological subcultures with a shared enemy and a degree of diffidence on what to do afterwards, it's basically the description of every Partisan movement in WW2 Europe (except Yugoslavia, where the Communists dominated the Resistance due to the Chetnicks ending up cooperating with the occupiers against them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:46:21-07:00","id":1523097,"title":"","content":"For all of the broad discussions of a lot of the game, the &quot;get to Rage 0 and then go be a normal human for as long as you want,&quot; thing really does seem to be the biggest self-defeating aspect to how W5's mechanics and themes interact. Even if the setting has plenty of reasons to dip back into Rage.. you can shed it and return to your normal life easily enough after whatever. You don't need Rage to be an environmental activist.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Comparing the psychology of partisans in a war that lasted for a few years, to a war that's been going on for thousands (maybe?) and that's apparently a lost cause anyway (maybe?) doesn't really work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-24-2023, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T17:59:39-07:00","id":1523109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523097#post1523097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all of the broad discussions of a lot of the game, the &quot;get to Rage 0 and then go be a normal human for as long as you want,&quot; thing really does seem to be the biggest self-defeating aspect to how W5's mechanics and themes interact. Even if the setting has plenty of reasons to dip back into Rage.. you can shed it and return to your normal life easily enough after whatever. You don't need Rage to be an environmental activist.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Comparing the psychology of partisans in a war that lasted for a few years, to a war that's been going on for thousands (maybe?) and that's apparently a lost cause anyway (maybe?) doesn't really work.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in fact without Kinfolk to be the human facing sector of the Cause, Losing the Wolf and doing the hard yards of lobbying, protesting, legislating and directly actioning against invested interests yourself is pretty much the only soft tool in the Garous box. In Legacy they could work with Kinfolk in a two pronged assault with the Kinfolk doing all the ground work and ' mundane' activities whilst the Garou worked on the spiritual aspect and attacking those parts of the issue that would simply eat humans that investigated.<br /> <br /> Now this means that W5 Garou are far less effective at achieving meaningful change as they can only work one side of the issue at a time and cannot work as a united front, they can ally with human NGOs but those organisations are working with only half the information maximum and so are far, far less effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T19:44:45-07:00","id":1523114,"title":"","content":"Also, I don't know how &quot;Partisan&quot; W5 really encourages, when it's stated attitude is a paternalistic, condescending denial of the efficacy of Direct Action. The edition doesn't want you doing traditional Partisan activities, like being disruptive or engaging in asymmetrical guerilla warfare. It honestly doesn't even want you engaging in positive change through &quot;official&quot; channels, by the way it frames the fight as being lost.<br /> <br /> What W5 seems to want, tonally and textually, is for Garou to hunker down in the werewolf equivalent of apocalypse bunkers and try to survive a little longer. That's not being a Partisan, that's at best being a prepper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T22:17:17-07:00","id":1523121,"title":"","content":"From historical military context, the get are probably the closer to partisans in terms of mo and outlook. Conventional garou packs are more like social collapse warbands guarding their petty territories which could be an interesting idea to develop since eventually these coalesce into regional and later, national powers but I don't think 5th ed has any interest in developing it that way since it has an aversion to large scale success or even effort in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T23:32:43-07:00","id":1523123,"title":"","content":"@<b>Knightingale</b>\u200b:<br /> 1) You should probably read the post by Manfr on page 25 number 369 and page 33 number 491. He provides a sensible interpretation of the setting and an example of how to explain it to novices in less than 6-8 hours. Also, it seems a sensible amount of work for a storyteller.<br /> 2) There were plenty of people discussing when the fall of Rome happened, but there wasn't a shared consciousness of an exact and single time point for the fall of Rome. For example, Byzantine emperors considered themself Roman emperors, not their successor. Ottoman emperors considered themself Roman Emperors by right of conquest (part of the orthodox church accepted them as Roman emperors for several reasons).<br /> <br /> Is &quot;How long did it last? A decade? A century? Who knows&quot; a verbatim citation from the book? Could you please provide the context for the citation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T00:29:56-07:00","id":1523124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523123#post1523123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b>Knightingale</b>\u200b:<br /> 1) You should probably read the post by Manfr on page 25 number 369 and page 33 number 491. He provides a sensible interpretation of the setting and an example of how to explain it to novices in less than 6-8 hours. Also, it seems a sensible amount of work for a storyteller.<br /> 2) There were plenty of people discussing when the fall of Rome happened, but there wasn't a shared consciousness of an exact and single time point for the fall of Rome. For example, Byzantine emperors considered themself Roman emperors, not their successor. Ottoman emperors considered themself Roman Emperors by right of conquest (part of the orthodox church accepted them as Roman emperors for several reasons).<br /> <br /> Is &quot;How long did it last? A decade? A century? Who knows&quot; a verbatim citation from the book? Could you please provide the context for the citation?</div> </div> </div> </div>By this logic I can think that it is something similar to that statement that dinosaurs are only terrestrial and aquatic and winged ones are just reptiles that lived at the same time, however there are those who consider them all to be dinosaurs, at the end of the day it doesn't make a difference.<br /> <br /> Applying it here, it seems like the nation has fallen and everyone left has a different idea about how, why and when, in the end everything is so lost that knowledge hasn't even been passed on, and yes I read Manfr's comment, he read the that he had there and filled in the gaps with what he found amusing and made a more or less cohesive story (my English isn't perfect), but you can't even say that he's right, because if it's really vague it's just his interpretation, another type of person may interpret it differently, which again falls into that thing that's why it's &quot;good&quot; and you should feel bad for not agreeing.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, what I think I want to say is that this game seems like it was made to be a werewolf V5, which doesn't make it bad, I actually like V5, it has some good ideas, but when you see everything that he had to throw away, and that's the right term, to get to that, it's just seems like a waste and at the end of the night like the dinossaurs, it's don't matter. You can laught now.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T00:36:30-07:00","id":1523125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523123#post1523123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b>Knightingale</b>\u200b:<br /> 1) You should probably read the post by Manfr on page 25 number 369 and page 33 number 491. He provides a sensible interpretation of the setting and an example of how to explain it to novices in less than 6-8 hours. Also, it seems a sensible amount of work for a storyteller.<br /> 2) There were plenty of people discussing when the fall of Rome happened, but there wasn't a shared consciousness of an exact and single time point for the fall of Rome. For example, Byzantine emperors considered themself Roman emperors, not their successor. Ottoman emperors considered themself Roman Emperors by right of conquest (part of the orthodox church accepted them as Roman emperors for several reasons).<br /> <br /> Is &quot;How long did it last? A decade? A century? Who knows&quot; a verbatim citation from the book? Could you please provide the context for the citation?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) In the context of story-first games that have come out, the way the book expects STs to shoulder this burden isn't sensible. And it isn't like the supplements will carry on acting like the blank spaces left by the corebook are intentional and the burden put on the STs was part of the design. No, Renegade will write supplements with a very distinct interpretation of the setting. Rather, the W5-book doesn't help STs with filling the blank space either and just forces the issue through its lackluster efforts instead. The reason somebody has to figure out how to handle the Silent Strider curse of having to wander around, for example, is just the result of the W5 corebook not putting in an adequate amount of work to fit it into the setting. &quot;Nobody knows, maybe it's a curse...?&quot; isn't satisfactory. It's not a storyhook, it's not evocative and it doesn't add character to the Silent Striders.<br /> <br /> 2) And wouldn't that be nice to know enough to have a discussion... But that's not the case here. The book doesn't give enough detail for that. And the Fall of Rome isn't remotely comparable to what the W5 corebook does with the Fall of the Garou Nation. Like I said, with what the W5 corebook tells you the possible range of when that could've happened stretches between thousands of years ago and a decade ago. Events like the Cult of Fenrir and the Stargazers leaving and Gaia's Howl are just these free-floating story-points with no context or reference-points that the book has just thrown out there. That's just bad worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's a quote from pg 37.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T05:36:14-07:00","id":1523130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523123#post1523123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b>Knightingale</b>\u200b:<br /> 2) There were plenty of people discussing when the fall of Rome happened, but there wasn't a shared consciousness of an exact and single time point for the fall of Rome. For example, Byzantine emperors considered themself Roman emperors, not their successor. Ottoman emperors considered themself Roman Emperors by right of conquest (part of the orthodox church accepted them as Roman emperors for several reasons).<br /> <br /> Is &quot;How long did it last? A decade? A century? Who knows&quot; a verbatim citation from the book? Could you please provide the context for the citation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Byzantine emperors are Roman emperors, the distinction between the classical empire and the medieval one is an artificial construct.<br /> <br /> Its also isnt a great comparison, while we can and do argue on the semantics of empire, we are quite aware of the timeline, events and nature of the empires history. Itd be closer to say islam collapsing and us losing all info on it in under a generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T01:39:33-07:00","id":1523199,"title":"","content":"To bring up another issue: Renown being tied to Gifts and Rites. The particular issue is that starting with Theurge-Gifts til the Rites all powers related to dealing with Spirits use Honor. But the Tribes who are according to the text most interested in the Umbra and Spirits are the Ghost Council and the Children Of Gaia - which are Wisdom-Tribes. From a starting-character-perspective that means they are less well-equipped to deal with Spirits than, for example, a Bone Gnawer Garou. And continuing from there using your XP to invest in Honor means you're not investing in Wisdom and since these are Wisdom-Tribes all their Gifts use Wisdom for their dice-pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T09:57:02-07:00","id":1523214,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know if there is any mention of vampires or SI in W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T10:30:38-07:00","id":1523216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523214#post1523214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know if there is any mention of vampires or SI in W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a short bit on vampires in the antagonist-section with two example-antagonists, the &quot;Dimebag-Dracula&quot; and &quot;Count Orlock or some shit&quot;. And personally, I think the writing on those two antagonists is the most flavorful and evocative writing you can find in the book. As the names already imply it has this sardonic tone and judgmental perspective on what vampires are. But it's evocative in the sense that despite just spending a couple dozen words on it, you can picture the NPC it's talking about and it's flavorful because the text sells the sardonic tone.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition is mentioned and is part of the larger portrayal of mortal hunters as &quot;agents of the Weaver&quot; in W5. Considering that H5 makes a huge fuss about how bad hunter-orgs are and how they're really just another force reinforcing the status-quo, it follows the logic of that book. Project Twilight gets a loresheet and mentioned as a werewolf-specific hunter-org but in W5 it has been officially disbanded by the director of the Special Affairs Division - and yet somehow still exists (another infamous &quot;Who knows&quot;-bit).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T10:45:28-07:00","id":1523219,"title":"","content":"Okay, aside from the right wingness of the recent free pdf, I like Track Morrisson. A good non-garou werewolf with a fitting rite. This is something W5 NEEDED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T11:54:56-07:00","id":1523226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523219#post1523219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, aside from the right wingness of the recent free pdf, I like Track Morrisson. A good non-garou werewolf with a fitting rite. This is something W5 NEEDED.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolen Moons are another of James uncredited additions to W5, I quite like Track as an Antagonist though I don't think he'd last overly long vs remotely competent Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T12:11:09-07:00","id":1523228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523226#post1523226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stolen Moons are another of James uncredited additions to W5, I quite like Track as an Antagonist though I don't think he'd last overly long vs remotely competent Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he starts teaching the ritual onwards to his followers, maybe he could. A sort of puppetmaster behind a bunch of rowdy Stolen Moons who thrive on being 'free' of humanity's chains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T14:01:34-07:00","id":1523233,"title":"","content":"A good antagonist. Mixes the social challenge of him being famous and having a loyal following with the spiritual powers he acquired and is trying to increase. Although my first reaction was more &quot;Oh, this would be a great WtF-setup.&quot;.<br /> <br /> But it does make me wonder if it reflects what the Renegade-development-team thinks of W5 in general or if it's just this one writer in particular. Both with the Emissaries, the character-introduction-stuff and now this antagonist... the general direction feels more like &quot;You happen to be a monstrous werewolf and now you deal with some local problems.&quot;. And it's that instead of more usual WtA-Wyrm-stuff or W5-specific story-beats like Age of Apocalypse, Cult of Fenris or Garou suck at working together. Especially the Fenrir... the way the corebook was written I could've pictured this guy also as a Fenrir or one of their &quot;human allies&quot; (which show up in the one-shot within the corebook).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T14:27:16-07:00","id":1523236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523228#post1523228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he starts teaching the ritual onwards to his followers, maybe he could. A sort of puppetmaster behind a bunch of rowdy Stolen Moons who thrive on being 'free' of humanity's chains.</div> </div> </div> </div>True...my players have been dismantling cults for a few decades now so they'd likely roll through them still...but a good low level background threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:01:08-07:00","id":1523241,"title":"","content":"so,my own w5 chronicles started a few weeks back. the players are going after a Black Fury who betrayed them and have crossed into Jacksonville's Umbra or the first time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:02:38-07:00","id":1523242,"title":"","content":"here's session 1 Recap<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We arrive at a cemetery within Jacksonville. We are there for Jacob\u2019s Mom\u2019s funeral. There is an older woman who lets us in and takes our names. There is a man who comes up to us, wearing a scarf, which Jacob notes is odd \u2013 the man is his brother, Saul. They were fighting last they spoke. Underneath the scarf is a large scar on his neck, as if a large animal attacked him. The funeral itself is small; not many have shown up beyond Jacob\u2019s close family, such as his brother, Saul, and their Grandmother, Alice. Gran suggests Jacob gets \u2018things in order\u2019 as they talk. Saul also seems thinner, but doesn\u2019t seem to recall when he last ate. Jacob asks Owen and Cassie to investigate how his mother died and who did this to her, then the three head out to lunch. Cassie has a Spiritual Companion, Panther. She can communicate mentally with her so long as Cassie stays on the Physical Realm. Jacob\u2019s mother is named Sylvia. She died in a car accident or other some such car wreck. Cassie goes to sus out the security footage, and the computer crashes. The security guard recommends seeking out her Insurance Company; Oliver Gavins, the owner of the Company, seemed to want to find a loophole for the money to go to her family. The Insurance Company is called In The Shade, which seems to reference Thunder in its slogan. It seems to be a family-owned company; the secretary is named Jamie Gavins. Oliver is Jamie\u2019s grandfather. As Owen and Cassie meet the CEO of the Insurance Company, he wears a nice white-gray suit and is quite tall. His office is at the end of a long corridor, which strikes us as odd. Cassie tries to pull information from Oliver, who claims that someone named Sandro Phillips attempted to embezzle funds from the company. Oliver is a Shadow Lord. While we don\u2019t know what is up with him specifically, he asks us about whether or not we\u2019ve ever taken human life. Cassie answers, Owen does notBack at lunch, Jacob notes that Saul still doesn\u2019t mention the scar; however he seems to hold onto the silver cross still. Saul taps his pockets frequently enough that Jacob asks about it. Saul explains that while in Iraq he began to pray. He seems to have trouble explaining that he was hit while on duty there and it hurt him so much that he began to read the bible. Jacob learns that the scar was created not by a Vampire; but perhaps a werewolf. Then finally Saul reveals how he got the scar in Iraq. He helped a few kids get water from a well when a large man with a rune tattoo by his eye arrived. The man was aggressive and yelled at the kids but Saul tried to stop him; this caused the enraged man to attack him. Saul doesn\u2019t know if he was high on drugs, but the man bit into his neck before running away. Jacob hacks into the security system and discovers that his mother was possessed by a spirit. Specifically, she has been possessed by a rogue Wyld spirit. We\u2019re also warned that Hunters are all over Jacksonville. With Spindle\u2019s help, Jacob discovers the IP of the Black Fury who edited the footage. Cassie speaks with Panther, who appears to be injured. There is a Wyld Spirit, called Haze, who pretends to be a cigarette in the physical realm; in the Umbra, a purple smoke. When smoked, Haze will possess its Host and makes them do \u2018dumb shit\u2019. Jacob searches local smoke shops and discovers a man, seemingly soaked with blood. Other customers don\u2019t seem to notice this man. He buys a pack of cigarettes and then heads to an alleyway to smoke. The smoke appears as a deep purple and we realize that we are looking at Haze. </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:03:51-07:00","id":1523243,"title":"","content":"Here's the recap for Session 2<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We follow the man on cameras to Sawgrass, where he just hangs out under a streetlamp and smokes more of the purple smoke. We debate how to deal with Haze; figuring out how powerful the spirit might be. We capture and interrogate Haze. He claims that the murders and \u2018dumb shit\u2019 were just trial runs; he was learning how to possess others. He also claims that he was summoned by a woman who seemingly wants to thin the gauntlet; believed to be the Black Fury as mentioned prior. We convinced \u2013 rather intimidated \u2013 Haze to go back to the Umbra. Cassie arrests the man, as he was still covered in blood; though Owen gives him a Blessed Brew to hopefully sober him up. \u2014 Time passes and we go to the Elders to speak with them about Jacob\u2019s brother\u2019s attacker; theoretically a Cultist of Fenris. The Elder of the Glass Walkers is a man named Kevin Narik. He is waiting for us, reading a plain book. He is 50 and known for being a good architect before moving to Jacksonville; he took down some Pentex in New York and took down a pit of Black Spiral Dancers. Jacob speaks with Kevin about his brother and mother. Kevin explains that the Elders are aware of some sort of Cult presence\u2026 though Elder Narik has not found any evidence of them as of yet. Perhaps, then, the Cult may be attempting to kill Saul or have other goals in Jacksonville. Owen and Jacob head with Kevin to gather the rest of the Elders. Meanwhile, Cassie goes to another of her tribe. A woman named Laura is there using a punching bag. She looks upset\u2026 though not rage filled. Cassie explains the situation and then Laura is truly pissed. Cassie further explains the importance of the situation, but Laura claims it was not her. Laura does fess up to something however; she knows another Black Fury who she is suspicious of as she is good with technology and computers. The woman\u2019s name is Kayene Robertson. Cassie says that she will not sell out Laura. At this, Laura turns and runs into the woods in her Lupus form. Cass then comes back to the Elders and the rest of the Pack. Kevin tells us about the other two Elders there; Mama Ayunerak, the Black Fury Elder. She is a very spiritual Native woman. The other, Mocking Scarlet, the Red Talon Elder. He received his name due to goading others into fights; enemies and allies alike. Kevin nearly takes Mocking Scarlet\u2019s bait; nearly fighting with the man\u2026. however Owen speaks up to attempt to calm the Elders down by asking them to see to the matters at hand; fighting would not aid anything right now. Mama Ayunerak asks the pack to seek out Kayene Robertson and bring her to the Elders for judgement in three days time. We learn that Kayene is on a Native Reservation in Seminole. We are let in and Cassandra explains Kayene\u2019s crimes against the litany. Kayene attempts to escape but we hold her down and knock her out \u2013 but not before reinforcements arrive from the Umbra. A storm brews and as we try to escape with Kayene there is an earthquake on the road. We escape into the Umbra which appears rocky. We follow panther. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:08:06-07:00","id":1523244,"title":"","content":"Panther and Spindle btw,are the Spirit Allies of the pack. since the word &quot;Totem&quot; is not used Panther is a Gaian Panther spirit,Spinder is something very close to a Pattern Spider","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-27-2023, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T23:09:08-07:00","id":1523260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523233#post1523233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good antagonist. Mixes the social challenge of him being famous and having a loyal following with the spiritual powers he acquired and is trying to increase. Although my first reaction was more &quot;Oh, this would be a great WtF-setup.&quot;.<br /> <br /> But it does make me wonder if it reflects what the Renegade-development-team thinks of W5 in general or if it's just this one writer in particular. Both with the Emissaries, the character-introduction-stuff and now this antagonist... the general direction feels more like &quot;You happen to be a monstrous werewolf and now you deal with some local problems.&quot;. And it's that instead of more usual WtA-Wyrm-stuff or W5-specific story-beats like Age of Apocalypse, Cult of Fenris or Garou suck at working together. Especially the Fenrir... the way the corebook was written I could've pictured this guy also as a Fenrir or one of their &quot;human allies&quot; (which show up in the one-shot within the corebook).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is intentional, giving the PCs low level and lone wold threats to fight to ease them into the setting. With CoF and BSDs reserved for more serious encounters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T00:28:16-07:00","id":1523261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523260#post1523260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel this is intentional, giving the PCs low level and lone wold threats to fight to ease them into the setting. With CoF and BSDs reserved for more serious encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, personally I think there would be two things I would add/change to bring it more in line with W5: The first would be to make the Bone Witch the real villain of this story. &quot;Who is that spirit and what does it want?&quot; should be a bigger driving force and lead to encourage players to explore the Umbra. And the other thing is that with the Rite it says that Track is absorbing the memories and abilities (including supernatural ones) of the Garou when he eats their hearts. I think what I would add is that the most important part is actually that in this particular variation of the Stolen Moons phenomenon, he's also taking on their Rage - and it's driving him insane. So while he may have a bit of a wacky show with a conservative bend at the start, the more hearts he consumes the more it turns into an Alex-Jones-type of show (conspiracy-theories, culture war outrage, all sorts of prejudices being pursued etc.). And this happens to make players reflect on how when Rage is doing that to this guy, how Rage has impacted Garou-society in the past. That brings it more in line with the critical perspective W5 has when it comes to Garou, I think.<br /> <br /> Also, in the way he's been described, I think he would also serve as a good antagonist for H5. Because in a way he is a Hunter with Drive. Now the text of H5 is all about local hunter-cells=good vs hunter-orgs=bad but the Drives listed in the book include some bad ones. And the Drive of Envy is all about the Hunter trying to join the supernatural community. So what started out as a local hunter-cell organized by him utilizing his podcast would slowly turn into the Vigilante-type hunter-org as described in the book. And you could have a three-way-conflict between the player-Hunter-group, Track and his followers and the Garou. Or this could even become a four-way-conflict if hunter-orgs get involved. Similarly, if the players are Garou you could bring in Project Twilight to complicate the situation as these mortal hunters don't differentiate between Track's werewolf-activities and the player-group's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T02:58:07-07:00","id":1523266,"title":"","content":"One thing I would change in a heartbeat would be to make his podcast's leanings up to the ST. Maybe the story has had issues with people with good intentions but bad actions and Right Track is a liberal &quot;Look how shitty the world is! But I know a way to fix it!&quot; podcast.<br /> <br /> I must say I love the idea of a pack of Stolen Moons thinking they are true werewolves and acting accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T03:32:57-07:00","id":1523267,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the exact nature of his podcast doesn't really matter. It's not like the player-characters are gonna start a debate-club with the guy or something. He's gonna use his tools and abilities to go after the player-characters and the player-characters are gonna use their abilities to go after him. Simple as that. Actually, thinking about it, that makes me think it would be more interesting if dispatching Track is fairly easy but then you play out the consequences of his death (the followers radicalizing and treating him like a martyr, various followers picking up the Rite) and all the while the Bone Witch is in the background doing her own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T09:53:58-07:00","id":1523311,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> 1) I think you are overestimating the amount of work needed to fill the hole in W5. D&amp;D requires much more work for the Master if played using only the 3 big books and yet D&amp;D 5ed is probably the best-selling RPG of all time, with a thriving fan base of novice players who are starting to play RPG.<br /> In revisited the Silent Strider curse description was &quot; No Garou trucks with the undead if he's wise, but the Striders are the Leeches' bitter foes, although few outside the tribe know why. Tribal legend holds that long ago, the tribe fought against an army of vampires led by the dark god-monster known as Sutekh. At the final battle, Sutekh wove a mighty curse that drove them from their homeland of Egypt and scattered them to the four winds. To this day, the land of the Nile is the one land where they can find no rest. But worse still, the curse severed all contact with the ancestor-spirits of the tribe. No Striders have been able to find their forbears, even though many have searched both spirit world and ' Underworld for some sign. Many Striders take an Egyptian name in honor of their lost heritage&quot;.<br /> There is still uncertainty about what happened (it is a legend and not tribal history), and there is a forced connection with vampires and the fact that you are cursed as a tribe.<br /> If the W5 edition leaves more room for ST and players to explore the reason and the meaning of the Silent Strider's wandering more power to the W5. There are several opportunities:<br /> - Curse<br /> -Spirit Quest<br /> -Act of contrition to atone for something<br /> -Act of devotion<br /> -Act of self enlightenment<br /> - Strategical/Tactical decision that loses its meaning with the passing of time and now it is a tradition<br /> All of them interact differently with the verbs that describe the Silent Strider and the Auspices.<br /> And if the ST or the player aren't interested in the origin/explanation of Silent Strider's wandering they can just ignore it until they feel that it has become an interesting topic to address in play.<br /> <br /> 2) So there are multiple free-floating story-points that you can use to depict the fall of the Garou Nation and that the ST could discuss in and out of the game with your players based on their common interests and inspiration. If a ST and the players would like to centre their chronicle on the topic of large-scale social construct they can answer the following question both before and during play:<br /> - Why do we need a large-scale social construct in the Garou society?<br /> - What should it do?<br /> - Was Garou Nation able to achieve its raison d'\u00eatre? If not why?<br /> - Should we resurrect the Garou Nation or should we start something new?<br /> - Which were the turning points in the Garou Nation's fall?<br /> - Can we do something about it?<br /> - Which were the inherent weaknesses of the GN that we should address?<br /> <br /> There are so many possibilities out there for ST and players to explore and different ways to tell the fall of Garou Nation. If the facts are fixed you could only discuss them but if there is not only one set of facts you can have a wider range of stories. In principle, you could also rebuild the Garou Nation or its successor.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T12:15:48-07:00","id":1523316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523311#post1523311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> 1) I think you are overestimating the amount of work needed to fill the hole in W5. D&amp;D requires much more work for the Master if played using only the 3 big books and yet D&amp;D 5ed is probably the best-selling RPG of all time, with a thriving fan base of novice players who are starting to play RPG.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the setting proposed by the D&amp;D-books and the one suggested by the W5 corebook aren't remotely the same. D&amp;D taps into stereotypes (including ones established by D&amp;D's popularity itself), WtA meanwhile has a very distinct setting. The whole idea of Garou goes hard against a stereotypical conception of werewolf-horror. There's nothing about a werewolf-game that immediately would link it to things like animism and environmental activism and yet that very thing is a <i>crucial </i>part of WtA, for example.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there are plenty of setting-books for D&amp;D which are popular (Forgotten Realms isn't a burden, for example) so that's a good indication that W5's aversion to worldbuilding can be called wrongheaded at best. Especially in the context of what made the WOD so distinct in the past, it feels like a dead end to embrace hating lore/worldbuilding as WOD5E has done in recent years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In revisited the Silent Strider curse description was &quot; No Garou trucks with the undead if he's wise, but the Striders are the Leeches' bitter foes, although few outside the tribe know why. Tribal legend holds that long ago, the tribe fought against an army of vampires led by the dark god-monster known as Sutekh. At the final battle, Sutekh wove a mighty curse that drove them from their homeland of Egypt and scattered them to the four winds. To this day, the land of the Nile is the one land where they can find no rest. But worse still, the curse severed all contact with the ancestor-spirits of the tribe. No Striders have been able to find their forbears, even though many have searched both spirit world and ' Underworld for some sign. Many Striders take an Egyptian name in honor of their lost heritage&quot;.<br /> There is still uncertainty about what happened (it is a legend and not tribal history), and there is a forced connection with vampires and the fact that you are cursed as a tribe.<br /> If the W5 edition leaves more room for ST and players to explore the reason and the meaning of the Silent Strider's wandering more power to the W5. There are several opportunities:<br /> - Curse<br /> -Spirit Quest<br /> -Act of contrition to atone for something<br /> -Act of devotion<br /> -Act of self enlightenment<br /> - Strategical/Tactical decision that loses its meaning with the passing of time and now it is a tradition<br /> All of them interact differently with the verbs that describe the Silent Strider and the Auspices.<br /> And if the ST or the player aren't interested in the origin/explanation of Silent Strider's wandering they can just ignore it until they feel that it has become an interesting topic to address in play. </div> </div> </div>Well, what you quoted is a storyhook. Of course, it's vague because it's a mystery, a starting-point for a story but at least there's a story there. What you get in the W5 corebook is plain bad writing instead. Because it's written like it offers you a blank page. &quot;It's whatever you want&quot;... that's the claim that goes alongside presenting it in such a &quot;Who knows?&quot;-manner - except it isn't. The Silent Striders don't exist in a vacuum. They are Garou who are part of the Garou Nation who suffer from Rage who were involved in the Impergium etc., etc. ...<br /> <br /> The reason you do something like what you quoted is because it isn't a blank page you're working with once you get to the lore of a Tribe. This Tribe can't be &quot;whatever you want&quot;. There's a concept and you need to make sure said concept works with the other concepts in the game. And you do worldbuilding where you balance an intriguing setting with leaving room for players to explore.<br /> <br /> W5 didn't do that. It wants to give you a blank page. And it doesn't. Why do Silent Striders need to suffer any sort of thing that makes them wander, to begin with? Why? After all, it says it right there at the beginning &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;. It takes the old lore away... but where's the re-imagination...? They still have to wander! Only now it doesn't get explained! That's absolutely terrible worldbuilding! And taking an old idea and be just like &quot;What if we don't explain it at all this time around...?&quot; is such a boring and bland take on old Silent Strider lore.<br /> <br /> Taking an old idea and making it worse is certainly not my interpretation of &quot;re-imagination&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) So there are multiple free-floating story-points that you can use to depict the fall of the Garou Nation and that the ST could discuss in and out of the game with your players based on their common interests and inspiration. If a ST and the players would like to centre their chronicle on the topic of large-scale social construct they can answer the following question both before and during play:<br /> - Why do we need a large-scale social construct in the Garou society?<br /> - What should it do?<br /> - Was Garou Nation able to achieve its raison d'\u00eatre? If not why?<br /> - Should we resurrect the Garou Nation or should we start something new?<br /> - Which were the turning points in the Garou Nation's fall?<br /> - Can we do something about it?<br /> - Which were the inherent weaknesses of the GN that we should address? </div> </div> </div>A <i>good </i>game puts what you describe in its corebook. W5 didn't.<br /> <br /> Take any PbtA-game... There's a reason there are questions on the Playbooks. You don't just throw concepts at the people at the table and be like &quot;You go figure it out.&quot;. Games were of course developed with distinct ideas in mind (even the most ambiguous ones) so you can't just be like &quot;Who knows...?&quot;. The questions aren't just about making inquiries, they're about setting up what the game cares about, where the game wants to focus on, what sorts of questions are the interesting ones, what's the point of this element... W5 instead chooses to say &quot;Who knows...?&quot;. There's a purposefulness to questions you find in PbtA-games.<br /> <br /> But you won't find such purposefulness in W5. That game just... shrugs. A shrug. Nothing more. And a gesture that lacks effort is a good metaphor for a book that doesn't put a lot of effort into its worldbuilding, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are so many possibilities out there for ST and players to explore and different ways to tell the fall of Garou Nation. If the facts are fixed you could only discuss them but if there is not only one set of facts you can have a wider range of stories. In principle, you could also rebuild the Garou Nation or its successor. </div> </div> </div>Hang on, W5 is still a game with a <i>very </i>fixed setting. Garou aren't just werewolves, the Impergium isn't just stereotypical werewolf-folklore-stuff, the Umbra and animism isn't standard-werewolf-stuff... The game already establishes plenty of facts about the world. There's plenty of WtA-specific stuff in this game. The problem is that its presented with this &quot;Who knows&quot;-attitude in a lot of places that is just bad worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T12:47:35-07:00","id":1523319,"title":"","content":"It'd probably be better to put what D&amp;D does out of your mind. D&amp;D is the beneficiary of what could be called a conspiracy to destroy its competition - the OGL, which caused a massive influx of D20 shovelware in the oughties that tanked most RPG sellers. Its long-reaching effects are such that even when 4e was not selling as strongly as its owners wanted it to, it was still outselling Pathfinder in every month except for the ones where it wasn't releasing anything because it had been capped in the back of the head early and replaced with something more appealing to grognards. At present, it's basically a monopoly, and it has a lot of hold on people who don't want to learn more than one system because no one is playing anything but 5e, hence why spend time on anything else?<br /> <br /> The present landscape can't really be broken without billions of dollars and/or a truly epic revolt of the market and audience. The best that WoD can manage is to stay as true to itself as it can be, and W5 is a resounding failure in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T13:08:56-07:00","id":1523321,"title":"","content":"Or, to pick something closer to WtA as an example:<br /> <br /> In the CofD 2e core book, Integrity (the replacement for Morality from 1e) is a very vague trait. It's purposefully so. The books tell you it's that way on purpose. What challenges the Integrity of a hardened detective isn't the same as what challenges a freshman college student from a protected upper class background. <br /> <br /> What the CofD 2e core does, and what a lot of us don't think W5 accomplishes, is summed up in what's generally referred to as &quot;the questionnaire.&quot; This is a list of questions the player answers to establish what Integrity means to their character, so they and the ST can establish a shared idea of what does and doesn't challenge the character's Integrity (and also serves as a way to establish that &quot;hard&quot; characters are not safe from said challenges just because their experiences are different and players shouldn't expect to get a free pass just because they make worldly characters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T23:03:30-07:00","id":1523341,"title":"","content":"W5 also doesn't give players the tools to make things of their own which is typical of games that have vague settings. You don't have the tools to make the pack a custom totem, there is no guide how to do that. You can't create a custom tribe, there are no tools for that. You can't even be a tribeless werewolf if we go by RAW.<br /> <br /> This is made worse by the free add-ons including a custom totem for two NPCs. One that is not even given stats for the players to use.<br /> <br /> Heck, the newest add-on has a cool Stolen Moon concept... but doesn't give the mechanics for the rite he uses to become one.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Werewolf the Forsaken, which is meant to be a more open game than Legacy WtA, offers every rite and trick the antagonists use so the ST can also use them.<br /> <br /> Yes, you CAN make these things up yourself, but in a game that relies on mechanics like W5 you shouldn't have to do the work of the devs for you.<br /> <br /> And this is W5's issue; It hints of things, but then doesn't give the ST tools or hints of how to use them. That is why the phrase &quot;Who knows&quot; is parroted so much on the thread, because that is how W5 treats its lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 09-30-2023, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T05:29:28-07:00","id":1523347,"title":"","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've never been as much of a werewolf guy as I've been a V:TM guy but my friend and co-author, Michael Suttkus, absolutely loves them. So, I'm going to go over both his and my thoughts on the matter from what I could tell.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>I don't mind the vilification of the Garou Nation</b><br /> <br /> I think some of the complaints aren't particularly valid. As early as my 2nd Edition Werewolf Storyteller's Guide, the dark and awful parts of the Garou Nation were a major part of the story. Albretch was doing his best to reform things but it was a place where all of the abuse of kinfolk, subtle corruption of the Wyrm, and so on was there. Garou shouldn't be &quot;good guys.&quot; All WOD protagonists are antiheroes against worse.<br /> <br /> I don't get the complaints about the wedidng. Garou frenzy. They kill innocent people. It's why they're monsters. Monsters fighting something worse.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>The vilification of the Get of Fenris isn't too surprising but disappointing</b><br /> <br /> I once had a conversation with a developer about how W:TF had a white supremacy problem, particularly in Europe. It was were assholes took advantage of Pure Breed, the violence, and elements in the game to advocate their own nasty views while claiming to be &quot;just playing in character.&quot; Addressing this with things like wiping out the Swords and other groups in Revised felt heavy handed because, &quot;I mean, are fans too dumb to realize these are the bad guys?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, it turns out player comfort getting compromised and bringing RL hate to the game was a bad idea and they put RL player comfort over in-game and I don't blame them for that. Still, I think they could have done this better.<br /> <br /> Still, if I was the writer, I would have split the Get rather than wholly corrupted them. I would have made them The Defenders of Joro (Norse Earth Goddess) and had the &quot;evil&quot; Get join with Red Talons and Silver Fang to make the The Pure equivalent. That way you can have your decent Get and just say, &quot;We hate the racists. A lot of us are Slavs, gays, or other minorities.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. <b>I feel a lot of these changes would have been fine in-universe</b><br /> <br /> The Black Furies accepting men, the Fianna being the Hart folk, and so on didn't have to be retcons and could have been described as happening as the result of reforms within the Garou. They could also have been what helped bring about the split.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>I like redeeming BSD</b><br /> <br /> I feel like the BSD being redeemable is something that adds an interesting story arc. I'm pretty sure that redeeming Fenris should be much-much easier, though, because I view the latter as a political decision but they seem to have gone full spiritual corruption.<br /> Still, I think it makes a hell of a fun potential PC background.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>The Umbra being off limits</b><br /> <br /> I think this reminds me of what happened to Mage: The Ascension. People want gritty street level games and feel like adventuring in the Umbra detracts from that.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>No Genetic Component</b><br /> <br /> My headcanon is this is mote just an acknowledgement that the Garou being with humanity since the Impergium means everyone has a little werewolf blood in them.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The Fera are now all mysterious</b><br /> <br /> This is just bullshit and ruins my games where the players played a lot of Fera.\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2023, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T06:32:30-07:00","id":1523349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've never been as much of a werewolf guy as I've been a V:TM guy but my friend and co-author, Michael Suttkus, absolutely loves them. So, I'm going to go over both his and my thoughts on the matter from what I could tell.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest, W5 still isn't the generic werewolf game it could have been. It still relies on Auspice and Gaia and that is all stuff most Werewolf media lacks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou shouldn't be &quot;good guys.&quot; All WOD protagonists are antiheroes against worse.<br /> <br /> I don't get the complaints about the wedidng. Garou frenzy. They kill innocent people. It's why they're monsters. Monsters fighting something worse.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The vilification of the Garou Nation is not as much of a problem for me as that the book simply shrugs when it comes to alternative ways of being a garou. Page space is spent ranting about the Nation, but no other way is offered and as I stated above there isn't even a chance to play a tribeless garou OR make a custom totem.<br /> <br /> As for the wedding, as much as the garou are monsters, they are not the same type of monsters that vampires are. W5 is still very heavily focused on the environmentalist angle and the (non-CoF) foes still are mostly polluters. So a way to force a First Change through killing innocent humans, when the game pushes HEAVILY for human connections even more than Legacy, rings a bit extreme.<br /> <br /> Plus, W5 accidentally gives a VERY easy way out of being a werewolf. Just spend all your Rage and never howl at the moon. No more Rage, no more spirit stuff. As such, the PCs should at least WANT to be involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>The vilification of the Get of Fenris isn't too surprising but disappointing</b><br /> <br /> I once had a conversation with a developer about how W:TF had a white supremacy problem, particularly in Europe. It was were assholes took advantage of Pure Breed, the violence, and elements in the game to advocate their own nasty views while claiming to be &quot;just playing in character.&quot; Addressing this with things like wiping out the Swords and other groups in Revised felt heavy handed because, &quot;I mean, are fans too dumb to realize these are the bad guys?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, it turns out player comfort getting compromised and bringing RL hate to the game was a bad idea and they put RL player comfort over in-game and I don't blame them for that. Still, I think they could have done this better.<br /> <br /> Still, if I was the writer, I would have split the Get rather than wholly corrupted them. I would have made them The Defenders of Joro (Norse Earth Goddess) and had the &quot;evil&quot; Get join with Red Talons and Silver Fang to make the The Pure equivalent. That way you can have your decent Get and just say, &quot;We hate the racists. A lot of us are Slavs, gays, or other minorities.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is made even worse by the fact that making the Get into the Cult of Fenris wasn't a unified decision between the devs. It was one guy pushing for it while also wanting the Younger Brother to be entirely destroyed and Feminism removed from Black Furies.<br /> <br /> And as we can see from the finished book, tribes like Silver Fangs and Red Talons can be played. Even if the Talons are WAY worse than in Legacy. So even if I fully understand why the idea was offered, the method of the excecution and ignoring of a MUCH easier tribe to make into Right Wingers all makes it extra sour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. <b>I like redeeming BSD</b><br /> <br /> I feel like the BSD being redeemable is something that adds an interesting story arc. I'm pretty sure that redeeming Fenris should be much-much easier, though, because I view the latter as a political decision but they seem to have gone full spiritual corruption.<br /> Still, I think it makes a hell of a fun potential PC background.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind BSD redemption on its own, even if it is treated like a massive snowflake trait in certain circles.<br /> <br /> It is, as you said, the fact that a BSD can be redeemed but a CoF member can't be.<br /> <br /> Especially as the CoF are NOT corrupted, they are NOT of the Wyrm. Instead, they as a tribe are suffering from a case of 'Insane with righteousness', in addition to the brand manager being gun-ho about making them all fascists and right wingers.<br /> <br /> So you have this REALLY awkward situation where a tribe of corrupted mutant torturers can be redeemed. But a person caught up in a movement needs a rare magical item to be saved. Aka, &quot;I can forgive a rapist torturer, but I draw the line at right wing.&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T07:31:23-07:00","id":1523350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. <b>The Umbra being off limits</b><br /> <br /> I think this reminds me of what happened to Mage: The Ascension. People want gritty street level games and feel like adventuring in the Umbra detracts from that.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;People want&quot; is doing a lot of heavy lifting here.<br /> <br /> The designers certainly wanted gritty street level games, to the point they made that the default and <i>functionally</i> only playstyle. (Double emphasis on &quot;functional&quot;. You CAN go to the Umbra, the game just doesn't want you to and punishes you for it.)<br /> <br /> As with Mage: The Ascension, there's also a not insignificant contingent who <b>like</b> the Umbra, think it's fun to adventure there (at least some of the time), and resent having that taken away from them. Then, as now, those people are not incorrect for feeling that way.<br /> <br /> In earlier editions, you could play street level or Umbra adventures. Both were supported. There was no conflict.<br /> <br /> Now, in W5, you're playing street level whether you like it or not.<br /> <br /> As I'm fond of saying, all else being equal, more options is better than fewer options, categorically. You need a damn good reason to limit options, especially when they were options already in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, raising the specter of the Avatar Storm just underscores how much of a bad idea this aspect of W5 was, and how little its designers learned. The Avatar Storm was not merely poorly received. It <b>broke the base</b>. White Wolf spent the latter parts of Revised jumping through hoops to walk back how severe its effects were and give ways to circumvent it, because it was so hated.<br /> <br /> Doing that in Werewolf is, in short, not a clever move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-30-2023, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T07:42:09-07:00","id":1523351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the complaints about the wedidng. Garou frenzy. They kill innocent people. It's why they're monsters. Monsters fighting something worse.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This issue on this, at least, is the idea that the werewolves would intentionally be triggering a frenzy in someone for the purpose of getting him to kill a bunch of people he cares about, and then trying to recruit him. As a VtM example, that's the sort of thing you'd expect to see as a suggestion for a typical Sabbat PC and how they were Embraced - forced to wake up and drain all of their loved ones during a wedding. But it would raise some eyebrows if that was used as an example of the sort of Embrace that a typical Camarilla vampire could have been expected to go through. The Garou nation has always been a bad place, but it's never been presented at around the same level of the Sabbat or worse. It's a pretty big change. <br /> <br /> And that's not getting into the fact that the idea doesn't even work in W5 - &quot;It was at that moment the long line of Garou in your family bloodline revealed their strange tradition about the First Change.&quot; - werewolves in V5 don't have bloodlines. It's an important part of the setting that you can't predict who will be a werewolf, the change doesn't run in the blood, and that it just couldn't happen the way it's written. And even if it were meant to be inspired by the previous setting only the most utterly deranged Garou would sacrifice multiple kinfolk just for the chance of maybe triggering someone into being a werewolf - like that's not something even the Black Spirals would readily do.<br /> <br /> In short this is a terrible backstory hook for a number of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T08:19:47-07:00","id":1523353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. <b>I don't mind the vilification of the Garou Nation</b><br /> <br /> I think some of the complaints aren't particularly valid. As early as my 2nd Edition Werewolf Storyteller's Guide, the dark and awful parts of the Garou Nation were a major part of the story. Albretch was doing his best to reform things but it was a place where all of the abuse of kinfolk, subtle corruption of the Wyrm, and so on was there. Garou shouldn't be &quot;good guys.&quot; All WOD protagonists are antiheroes against worse.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it doesn't come off like you're expected to even play anti-heroes. It's the Age of Apocalypse, the Garou-Nation has fallen, the Garou of the past are failures, the older Garou are all obstacles to changing things for the better and young Garou aren't invested in Garou-traditions like the Litany. Somehow the PCs are still Garou in that environment and expected to make a difference... well, a little bit of a difference because W5 doesn't think PCs can solve &quot;systemic issues&quot;. And Garou are specificially called out for being the wrong tools to fix the issues of the world. There's so much pessimism and dismissal in how Garou are described that it's really hard to believe the authors of the book even consider it possible for Garou to be heroes (anti- or otherwise).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. <b>I feel a lot of these changes would have been fine in-universe</b><br /> <br /> The Black Furies accepting men, the Fianna being the Hart folk, and so on didn't have to be retcons and could have been described as happening as the result of reforms within the Garou. They could also have been what helped bring about the split. </div> </div> </div>It certainly would've also brought it closer to how the V5 corebook dealt with its lore. Despite all the changes, V5 still wanted to be seen as a continuation. For W5 the motto instead was &quot;re-imagination not continuation&quot; but even on that front it doesn't quite succeed because there's still a lot of leftovers of old lore that don't quite make sense in the new setup anymore. And the Hart Wardens are a good example because it took quite a bit of pushback from the community to make that change happen. If it had been just up to the developers, the Tribe still would have been called Fianna while having nothing to do with the British Isles. But then again they completely reworked the Black Furies and yet their Gifts still have those cultural names invoking the previous version of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> The writing really should've been more thorough in making a clear decision in which direction they wanted to take this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. <b>I like redeeming BSD</b><br /> <br /> I feel like the BSD being redeemable is something that adds an interesting story arc. I'm pretty sure that redeeming Fenris should be much-much easier, though, because I view the latter as a political decision but they seem to have gone full spiritual corruption.<br /> Still, I think it makes a hell of a fun potential PC background. </div> </div> </div>I don't have an issue with redeeming BSD as an option but I feel like the writing of the Black Spiral Loresheet was a little bit too glib for my tastes. These are followers of the Wyrm and not just some rowdy fanclub you have some interactions with. Especially with WtA supposed to be a game with an animistic worldview redeeming a BSD should be about more than using some psychology to convince them to change sides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. <b>The Umbra being off limits</b><br /> <br /> I think this reminds me of what happened to Mage: The Ascension. People want gritty street level games and feel like adventuring in the Umbra detracts from that. </div> </div> </div>I think the spiritual side is essential to WtA. You're not just an environmental activist, you care about the environment because you fight for its spiritual representation in Gaia. And that's what makes WtA distinct. The flavor of the game just gets diluted by running away from the Umbra as a presence in the game. And according to the Introduction, &quot;exploring the Umbra&quot; is even something the game thinks PCs do in this game but then the mechanics are all about gatekeeping and making it as hard as possible to interact with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. <b>No Genetic Component</b><br /> <br /> My headcanon is this is mote just an acknowledgement that the Garou being with humanity since the Impergium means everyone has a little werewolf blood in them. </div> </div> </div>What irks me about the wishy-washy way in which Kin are described that then in that context the Silver Fangs make no sense. They shouldn't be this &quot;aristocratic Tribe&quot; of leaders that they are somehow still described as in W5. Anybody could end up being a Silver Fang and yet the description still hints very much at what Silver Fangs used to be rather than presenting a new version that fits into W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. <b>The Fera are now all mysterious</b><br /> <br /> This is just bullshit and ruins my games where the players played a lot of Fera.\u200b </div> </div> </div>That and the fact that apparently the War of Rage has happened in W5 but all the Garou have forgotten about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T08:55:28-07:00","id":1523355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5. <b>The Umbra being off limits</b><br /> <br /> I think this reminds me of what happened to Mage: The Ascension. People want gritty street level games and feel like adventuring in the Umbra detracts from that.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hate to pile on since I like you, but nothing I've ever seen backs this up and its known to be corporate mandateed. Plus 5th eds interpretation of the street is nothing like the street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-30-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T08:56:57-07:00","id":1523356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523353#post1523353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What irks me about the wishy-washy way in which Kin are described that then in that context the Silver Fangs make no sense. They shouldn't be this &quot;aristocratic Tribe&quot; of leaders that they are somehow still described as in W5. Anybody could end up being a Silver Fang and yet the description still hints very much at what Silver Fangs used to be rather than presenting a new version that fits into W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons why I think there were certain goals set for W5 (make the Fenrir all fascists, street level, no more Nation) and the rest could just... be. Because Fangs, even in revised, still had more vulnerability to fascism than Fenrir.<br /> <br /> It especially shows since for all W5 took from WtF, it didn't take the solution for a non-bloodline leadership tribe. Storm Lords lay their claim at leadership because they all have gone through hell and their tribal oath is NEVER to show weakness.<br /> <br /> Fangs not changing much shows they weren't much considered at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T09:10:29-07:00","id":1523357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've never been as much of a werewolf guy as I've been a V:TM guy<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>We know. This sub-forum is basically littered with odd takes that you had about W:tA on account of being a V:tM main. It's been about eight years, so it's really no mystery.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T13:37:30-07:00","id":1523366,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was a really long post that either didn't read or understand the points raised in this thread. Which is fine but doesn't really add anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T15:31:23-07:00","id":1523373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523366#post1523366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that was a really long post that either didn't read or understand the points raised in this thread. Which is fine but doesn't really add anything.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not attempting to respond to 37 pages of response but give my own reaction to the book I just read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523355#post1523355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hate to pile on since I like you, but nothing I've ever seen backs this up and its known to be corporate mandateed. Plus 5th eds interpretation of the street is nothing like the street.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I'm not sure why you'd think it's piling on. I don't think anyone has been disagreeing with what I've said. Mostly because I was just giving my hot takes.<br /> <br /> I was initially a big booster of V5 but the thing that finally turned me against it was the very casual way they disregarded continuity and it does feel like they just didn't care to follow up on the continuity.<br /> <br /> Indeed. the gist of my post was meant to be, &quot;There's no reason this had to be so shoddy in its handling of lore.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-30-2023, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T16:23:49-07:00","id":1523377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. <b>I don't mind the vilification of the Garou Nation</b><br /> <br /> I think some of the complaints aren't particularly valid. As early as my 2nd Edition Werewolf Storyteller's Guide, the dark and awful parts of the Garou Nation were a major part of the story. Albretch was doing his best to reform things but it was a place where all of the abuse of kinfolk, subtle corruption of the Wyrm, and so on was there. Garou shouldn't be &quot;good guys.&quot; All WOD protagonists are antiheroes against worse.<br /> <br /> I don't get the complaints about the wedidng. Garou frenzy. They kill innocent people. It's why they're monsters. Monsters fighting something worse.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Previous edition formulated harsh criticism of the nation, but these critics were always accompanied with calls to do better, to acknowledge the errors of the past and atone for previous sins. <br /> <br /> And while the hypocrisies of the nation were evident, the game also portrayed it's right fullness, the value of it's goals, and the hope they are for the world. <br /> <br /> Here's the nation is belittled constantly as some utterly failed system. Every notion of garou culture is portrayed mostly in the negative. <br /> <br /> <br /> And I think you completely miss the point in the wedding. <br /> It's not &quot;garou raging in a wedding and killing people is horrible&quot;. <br /> It's &quot;garou traps a potential garou inside the place of a wedding, hopping they kill everyone, hence becoming a jaded killer&quot; <br /> <br /> Not only does it breaks everything the game told us about new garou, but this is exactly the behavior of BSDs, not of common garou. <br /> <br /> Yes, garou are killers, yes, innocents are killed during frenzy or because they're in the way of garou's sacred missions. <br /> But these are casualties. Unless you're a red talon, the carnage is never the goal. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b. <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. <b>The vilification of the Get of Fenris isn't too surprising but disappointing</b><br /> <br /> I once had a conversation with a developer about how W:TF had a white supremacy problem, particularly in Europe. It was were assholes took advantage of Pure Breed, the violence, and elements in the game to advocate their own nasty views while claiming to be &quot;just playing in character.&quot; Addressing this with things like wiping out the Swords and other groups in Revised felt heavy handed because, &quot;I mean, are fans too dumb to realize these are the bad guys?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, it turns out player comfort getting compromised and bringing RL hate to the game was a bad idea and they put RL player comfort over in-game and I don't blame them for that. Still, I think they could have done this better.<br /> <br /> Still, if I was the writer, I would have split the Get rather than wholly corrupted them. I would have made them The Defenders of Joro (Norse Earth Goddess) and had the &quot;evil&quot; Get join with Red Talons and Silver Fang to make the The Pure equivalent. That way you can have your decent Get and just say, &quot;We hate the racists. A lot of us are Slavs, gays, or other minorities.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a common issue with writers. They think they can control what will happen in the table. <br /> <br /> Did we already forgot that ttrpg is mainly build by the DM and players, and that the game systems are technically advises?<br /> <br /> There will always be terrible players, that's no reason to amputate one's game universe, and making it less fun for the majority because a few bad apple. <br /> <br /> Idiots who use in universe prejudice to be assholes will always find a way to do it. It's up to other players to stand up against them. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, all you'll end up is games with the most innofensive player character options and the most heavy handed cartoonishly evil antagonists, which pretty much kills the idea of role-playing. <br /> <br /> <br /> I've played, and have had players in my games playing, some of the characters with the most prejudiced and immoral mindset possible, and there never was any issue. While I've seen assholes fucking up everything while playing typical goody two shoes characters constantly belittling other PCs using their sense of moral superiority to a point that sabotaged the game and the mood at the table. <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not up to writers to do that works, otherwise, we'll end up with the next editions of the Warhammer 40 K ttrpgs where playing anything but Tau, salamanders and eldars is forbidden<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. <b>I feel a lot of these changes would have been fine in-universe</b><br /> <br /> The Black Furies accepting men, the Fianna being the Hart folk, and so on didn't have to be retcons and could have been described as happening as the result of reforms within the Garou. They could also have been what helped bring about the split.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly agrees. Well, most of W5 changes are bullshit regardless, but like for V5 (at least when it was announces) , I would be perfectly willing to accept massive in universe change as long as they're well written and logical. <br /> <br /> But that would have required efforts and more importantly, knowledge and appreciation for the decades of previous lore. Something the team clearly lacked. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4. <b>I like redeeming BSD</b><br /> <br /> I feel like the BSD being redeemable is something that adds an interesting story arc. I'm pretty sure that redeeming Fenris should be much-much easier, though, because I view the latter as a political decision but they seem to have gone full spiritual corruption.<br /> Still, I think it makes a hell of a fun potential PC background.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is really not bad in itself. The execution is terrible. Leaving the BSDs should be a terrible return from the deepest darkness, a constant fight to regain one's inner purity, and it should involve heavy spirit quest. <br /> <br /> That it's easier to do that than leaving the fenrir, which are just separated from other tribes by pure ideology is nonsense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5. <b>The Umbra being off limits</b><br /> <br /> I think this reminds me of what happened to Mage: The Ascension. People want gritty street level games and feel like adventuring in the Umbra detracts from that.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nonsense. The *dev team* wanted that, not *people* in general. <br /> <br /> You just have to look at the reaction of the MtA community in revised. The edition backlash was massive. <br /> The avatar storm was the single worst metaplot decision that white wolf ever made for their game both in story or gameplay terms. <br /> <br /> Let's be clear. Some people want gritty street level games. Most don't, for every word games, most players aren't playing that. It's a niche. Not saying it's a bad thing and that they should get material, but that must never be the lens through which the whole playerbase must be forced to play. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 6. <b>No Genetic Component</b><br /> <br /> My headcanon is this is mote just an acknowledgement that the Garou being with humanity since the Impergium means everyone has a little werewolf blood in them.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Not a bad headcannon. <br /> <br /> How ether, this remind me of how the &quot;who knows who can be a garou&quot; narrative is damaging the themes of the game. <br /> <br /> Now garou's are no longuer a species, but a phenomenom, like mages. Everyone can theorically be one, anywhere. That pentex accountant may first change when you attack the secret office, that beautiful lady met on the dancefloor you're taking to your bedroom might first change during lovemaking, etc<br /> <br /> One might say it was already the case in previous editions (I would know, I made it happen that a pentex scientist first changed while threatened by one of my player) but when it happened, it indicated the character is in fact a lost kin, that they're part of a garou bloodline lost from knowledge. And these are rare, since garou and kinfolk are rare. People with garou blood being an extreme minority of the population, increasingly so with each generation without mating with garou or other kinfolks. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now everyone of the 8 billions of humans can be secretly a garou. <br /> Nice horror though for the poor vampire wondering if his next meal with butcher him<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523347#post1523347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 7. <b>The Fera are now all mysterious</b><br /> <br /> This is just bullshit and ruins my games where the players played a lot of Fera.\u200b<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel your pain, howether, and sorry for being a bit snarky, but now you feel how many people feel with 5th edition in general. <br /> It does not support most playstyles. V5 does not allow transition from previous edition of sabbat games, elder games, any game with blood sorcerers etc. <br /> And W5 does not support most transition. No high adventures in the umbra, no epic fight against the wyrm, no campaign about garou nation's repr\u00e9sentants trying to find peace and allyship with the fera, and of course, no campaign with the fenrir. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T16:42:59-07:00","id":1523379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523373#post1523373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not attempting to respond to 37 pages of response but give my own reaction to the book I just read.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> I'm not sure why you'd think it's piling on. I don't think anyone has been disagreeing with what I've said. Mostly because I was just giving my hot takes.<br /> <br /> I was initially a big booster of V5 but the thing that finally turned me against it was the very casual way they disregarded continuity and it does feel like they just didn't care to follow up on the continuity.<br /> <br /> Indeed. the gist of my post was meant to be, &quot;There's no reason this had to be so shoddy in its handling of lore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't describe them as hot takes. They're mostly some of the milder contentions that people that favor Vampire over Werewolf have with Werewolf. The stronger ones, regrettably, have become integral to W5, or as one could rightly call it, VV5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T17:02:30-07:00","id":1523380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523377#post1523377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel your pain, howether, and sorry for being a bit snarky, but now you feel how many people feel with 5th edition in general.<br /> It does not support most playstyles. V5 does not allow transition from previous edition of sabbat games, elder games, any game with blood sorcerers etc.<br /> And W5 does not support most transition. No high adventures in the umbra, no epic fight against the wyrm, no campaign about garou nation's repr\u00e9sentants trying to find peace and allyship with the fera, and of course, no campaign with the fenrir.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it wasn't clear from my observations, I wasn't a big fan of W5 from the very beginning. Some of the changes I like but I don't think it was very well done overall.<br /> <br /> The Fera thing is just an utter dealbreaker for me.<br /> <br /> I also find some amusement in the fact the &quot;Hart Wardens&quot; mixes with my homebrew Weredeer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T17:11:32-07:00","id":1523381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523373#post1523373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not attempting to respond to 37 pages of response but give my own reaction to the book I just read.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> I'm not sure why you'd think it's piling on. I don't think anyone has been disagreeing with what I've said. Mostly because I was just giving my hot takes.<br /> <br /> I was initially a big booster of V5 but the thing that finally turned me against it was the very casual way they disregarded continuity and it does feel like they just didn't care to follow up on the continuity.<br /> <br /> Indeed. the gist of my post was meant to be, &quot;There's no reason this had to be so shoddy in its handling of lore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think we're running into the old problem we had communicating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cos that was not at all what I got from your post.<br /> <br /> All good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T17:21:43-07:00","id":1523382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523381#post1523381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think we're running into the old problem we had communicating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cos that was not at all what I got from your post.<br /> <br /> All good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.<br /> <br /> I think the TLDR version is that I was a booster of V5 for so long people are taking a bit to catch up with the fact I'm now, &quot;Yeah, it sucks.&quot; It was the SI and Sabbat books that finally broke me.<br /> <br /> W5 just has the same issue that I had with them where the massive sweeping changes were done by fiat rather than in-universe lore or logic.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to forgive a lot but as a lore junkie, I feel that ignoring the past is the biggest mistake you can make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T00:12:00-07:00","id":1523392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523373#post1523373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. the gist of my post was meant to be, &quot;There's no reason this had to be so shoddy in its handling of lore.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't just the lore, it is the mechanics as well. Like I already said, you can EASILY quit being a garou by just burning all your Rage and never howling at the moon. You cannot regain Rage as long as you have zero and don't howl at the moon. This is basically the same as if a vampire returned to life after losing all blood points, completely breaking the whole 'you can't ever go back' theme of WoD.<br /> <br /> The game not only does not offer any other creation rules but Caern creation for the ST, it actively refuses to offer any mechanics to its add-on PDFs. Sure these two NPCs have a custom totem, but giving it stats so YOU can use it? Naaah.<br /> <br /> Granted, unlike V5 that at least had a clear concept and setting planned, W5 went through three teams and the last run seems to have amounted to using what the second team left behind and what KM REALLY wanted to have.<br /> <br /> Plus the book spends far too long just going through all the flaws of the Nation, to the point where actual concrete setting info is minimal or missing. Or, as with the BSD loresheet, Fangs and Talons compared to Fenrir, it all ends up a disjointed shoddy mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T00:55:02-07:00","id":1523393,"title":"","content":"Some of the missed opportunities for this game that I wish they had dealt with:<br /> <br /> * <b>Pentex isn't really cartoony anymore</b>: There's actually people who really do for religious reasons believe we should pollute more to bring about the End of the World. You could have a Supply Side Jesus (The Patriarch?) avatar of the Wyrm telling them to do this and it would entirely be believable in this world. You also have high functioning psychopaths who do not CARE how much destruction they cause in the name of short term profit. Really, Pentex just happens to be the worst but other corporations aren't far behind.<br /> <br /> * <b>You could have added more tribes</b>: Rather than divorce all of the Garou from ethnicity you could have made them alliances of hundreds of smaller tribes. Have more discovered all the time along with the Fera. Perhaps the Garou have opened up the ancestral realm of many extinct Garou groups of absorbed ones in the last days of Gaia and flooded Earth with renewed ancestor spirits or maybe they were always there but hiding from the crazy Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you want to get rid of Kinfolk, have massive amounts of them turned and the Garou are no longer dying out-ish.<br /> <br /> * <b>Play up the Horror</b>: Being a Garou is something that was never really done with the personal horror angle. I think they should have put more rules about it and how to roleplay the struggle between your Beast of War and interactions with others. Garou don't have to be ticking time bombs but being unable to control their rage so they have to live among themselves was an angle always there but not one properly explored.<br /> <br /> * <b>If you're going to sweeping changes, justify them</b>: You can get away with a certain amount of, &quot;no, it was always this way.&quot; Renaming the Wendigo, Fianna, Metis, and so on is fine. However, a lot of these other changes could have been done in-universe and paid proper respect to the past lore. Albretch, Evan (who is suddenly no longer ridiculous--but could have been retconned as a &quot;stolen Native child&quot; to to pay into RL tragedies), and other characters have had 20 years to make upheavels in the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> * <b>Make Redemption a Thing for Fenris</b>: I feel that the Child of Gaia trying to win them back works here as for the first time there really is a substantive difference on how these things are being fought over and a Civil War. This should be a war of words as well as Claws.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T01:38:45-07:00","id":1523396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <b>Play up the Horror</b>: Being a Garou is something that was never really done with the personal horror angle. I think they should have put more rules about it and how to roleplay the struggle between your Beast of War and interactions with others. Garou don't have to be ticking time bombs but being unable to control their rage so they have to live among themselves was an angle always there but not one properly explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>So here's a funny thing; It technically IS a thing in W5 that you have to deal with your Rage more and that it makes having relationships hard. The more Rage dice you have the bigger the chance to tear stuff there is. You can't even control how much Rage you are using, you have to use all you have.<br /> <br /> It just isn't shown in the lore or example characters and your Touchstones actually LESSEN your Rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <b>If you're going to sweeping changes, justify them</b>: You can get away with a certain amount of, &quot;no, it was always this way.&quot; Renaming the Wendigo, Fianna, Metis, and so on is fine. However, a lot of these other changes could have been done in-universe and paid proper respect to the past lore. Albretch, Evan (who is suddenly no longer ridiculous--but could have been retconned as a &quot;stolen Native child&quot; to to pay into RL tragedies), and other characters have had 20 years to make upheavels in the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, the retcon is very recent. I feel it was done to silence the complaints of racism that WtA got on Twitter (lol.) It seems once W5 had its third version in the works, they let JA basically 'fix' the game to the state he always wanted it to be. Which meant rebooting everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <b>Make Redemption a Thing for Fenris</b>: I feel that the Child of Gaia trying to win them back works here as for the first time there really is a substantive difference on how these things are being fought over and a Civil War. This should be a war of words as well as Claws.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of Gaia are no longer the peacemakers of the Nation and more importantly, the Fenrir are fascists.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk, the insanity the Fenrir have fallen to, is basically a poorly disguised fascism meter. This means that anyone who reaches its peak becomes unredeemable since they became right wingers.<br /> <br /> The problem with these suggestions is, that by the third version, no one cared about the lore anymore. 95% of the changes made to W5 come not from the setting or its lore, but from the likes of the developers and the rush to have the book out. Just look how reluctantly lupus are included in the book, almost as if the only reason they stayed was an order from above that no one writing the third version liked.<br /> <br /> That is why you cannot redeem the Fenrir, they were meant to be a Take That against the racism in Europe. BSDs and Red Talons are worse, but they aren't there to serve as a strawman. The Fenrir are.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T02:20:39-07:00","id":1523399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523396#post1523396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with these suggestions is, that by the third version, no one cared about the lore anymore. 95% of the changes made to W5 come not from the setting or its lore, but from the likes of the developers and the rush to have the book out. Just look how reluctantly lupus are included in the book, almost as if the only reason they stayed was an order from above that no one writing the third version liked.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a bit in the recent V5 Players Guide which really emphasizes just how negative the WOD-team's attitude towards lore/worldbuilding has become. In the section that's supposed to give you advice on how to portray Backgrounds, there's a section on Loresheets as well and this is how Loresheets are described:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loresheets exist to highlight a certain aspect of the world for the interested player and Storyteller, \u200bwithout forcing every player to master the entire minutiae of the Vampire setting. A Loresheet foregrounds some group, historical event, or elder <b>as it relates specifically to the player</b>, encouraging them to take ownership of that aspect and reminding the Storyteller that vampiric arcana exists to serve the story at the table tonight, not as mandatory history lessons.\u200b </div> </div> </div>(What's in bold is in italics in the book)<br /> <br /> &quot;Forcing every player to master the entire minutiae&quot;, &quot;vampiric arcana&quot;, &quot;mandatory history-lessons&quot;... There's not a single moment here where lore/worldbuilding doesn't get a negative portrayal. And if you strictly look at lore/worldbuilding through that lens then of course you end up writing a lot of &quot;Who knows&quot; to explain stuff instead. Because what makes a setting intriguing and vibrant does require lore/worldbuilding. And we also saw that in how Justin Achilli described his development-decisions on Discord. Lore/worldbuilding is seen in a strictly negative light for the WOD-team. And they weren't able to ever resolve the contradiction of having a very distinct werewolf-game on their hands with the fifth edition of WtA while also being completely against any notion of lore/worldbuilding being an important part of a corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T04:59:03-07:00","id":1523402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523399#post1523399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Forcing every player to master the entire minutiae&quot;, &quot;vampiric arcana&quot;, &quot;mandatory history-lessons&quot;... There's not a single moment here where lore/worldbuilding doesn't get a negative portrayal. And if you strictly look at lore/worldbuilding through that lens then of course you end up writing a lot of &quot;Who knows&quot; to explain stuff instead. Because what makes a setting intriguing and vibrant does require lore/worldbuilding. And we also saw that in how Justin Achilli described his development-decisions on Discord. Lore/worldbuilding is seen in a strictly negative light for the WOD-team. And they weren't able to ever resolve the contradiction of having a very distinct werewolf-game on their hands with the fifth edition of WtA while also being completely against any notion of lore/worldbuilding being an important part of a corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think what the paragraph is describing has nothing to do with tabletop. Because you don't need to tell a ST that what they run is a unique experience.<br /> <br /> I think this is talking about LARPs and large online games and how in THOSE games a player would need to know a lot of lore just to play. Because in a large crowd, it is naturally important to keep the setting straight so everyone is on the same page.<br /> <br /> So loresheets are essentially a solution to a problem that does not exist in this medium.<br /> <br /> Also, given loresheets are dotted, it isn't exactly giving the players the freedom to explore this aspect of the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T06:05:55-07:00","id":1523405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523402#post1523402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, I think what the paragraph is describing has nothing to do with tabletop. Because you don't need to tell a ST that what they run is a unique experience.<br /> <br /> I think this is talking about LARPs and large online games and how in THOSE games a player would need to know a lot of lore just to play. Because in a large crowd, it is naturally important to keep the setting straight so everyone is on the same page.<br /> <br /> So loresheets are essentially a solution to a problem that does not exist in this medium.<br /> <br /> Also, given loresheets are dotted, it isn't exactly giving the players the freedom to explore this aspect of the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, no such distinction is made in the V5 Players Guide. And that reminds me of what James Sambrano talked about on the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrH7EZXzWmw\" target=\"_blank\">Bunch of Gamers podcast</a> where during the Hunters Entertainment version the writers were handed the directive to deemphasize the Umbra because they were worried about cross-play and Garou just going into the Umbra and popping out of it in order to assassinate Princes and then to quickly pop back into the Umbra again. But that was a LARP-problem, not a tabletop-one.<br /> <br /> And it wasn't just that snarky paragraph I quoted there. This was followed up with the decision that except for the Loresheets for the Hecata-Bloodlines, none of the other Loresheets (from the other supplements) were put into the V5 Players Guide. Even general ones like a werewolf-focused Loresheet called Lupine Expert (from Chicago by Night) weren't included. And this is in the context that the whole pitch of the V5 Players Guide was that it would supposedly gather all the new Disciplines, Predator-Types etc. from all the supplements in one place so that newcomers would only need the corebook and the Players Guide.<br /> <br /> And the emphasis on &quot;as it relates specifically to the player&quot; is also relevant with the whole &quot;Who knows&quot;-stuff in the W5 book. Using that logic from that paragraph caring about the lore is a problem for the specific person with that interest. You have somebody who plays a Children of Gaia character and wants to know more about the Tribe. Instead of pointing them to a Tribebook, the ST is supposed to say &quot;Sounds like a you-problem. How about you go figure it out?&quot;. And the reason I phrased it this crass is because, okay, you can pursue this idea of a less fixed setting where player-input/ideas are more important than having a setting-bible... but then you need to support this process like listing example-ideas or example-questions. Just saying &quot;Who knows?&quot;, shrug and think now the work is done is completely insufficient. W5's approach to a less fixed setting just doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T07:07:47-07:00","id":1523406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523405#post1523405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, no such distinction is made in the V5 Players Guide. And that reminds me of what James Sambrano talked about on the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrH7EZXzWmw\" target=\"_blank\">Bunch of Gamers podcast</a> where during the Hunters Entertainment version the writers were handed the directive to deemphasize the Umbra because they were worried about cross-play and Garou just going into the Umbra and popping out of it in order to assassinate Princes and then to quickly pop back into the Umbra again. But that was a LARP-problem, not a tabletop-one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two things about that that amuse me.<br /> <br /> One; If garou were using the umbra to kill princes those princes DESERVED it. Seriously, the amount of leash put on cross-play is immense. You cannot just randomly pop into umbra and kill a prince. STs of BOTH venues would have to approve that and there better be a GOOD reason for it.<br /> <br /> Second; Nothing is funnier than a &quot;these guys are too OP for my fave splat, make them more fair!&quot; The stakes couldn't be more different between VtM and WtA.<br /> <br /> How much DOES WoD5 support crossplay anyway?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T10:37:24-07:00","id":1523428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the missed opportunities for this game that I wish they had dealt with:<br /> <br /> * <b>Pentex isn't really cartoony anymore</b>: There's actually people who really do for religious reasons believe we should pollute more to bring about the End of the World. You could have a Supply Side Jesus (The Patriarch?) avatar of the Wyrm telling them to do this and it would entirely be believable in this world. You also have high functioning psychopaths who do not CARE how much destruction they cause in the name of short term profit. Really, Pentex just happens to be the worst but other corporations aren't far behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Revised's introduction of the general designation of Wyrm-Influenced Corporations (WICs), Pentex basically just became an older, more entrenched vision of what a WIC might become. Killing it wouldn't solve the problems; those are pretty much baked into the kind of capital accumulation that allows Pentex and other WICs to exist.<br /> <br /> Which VV5 <i>excused</i> as not being the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <b>You could have added more tribes</b>: Rather than divorce all of the Garou from ethnicity you could have made them alliances of hundreds of smaller tribes. Have more discovered all the time along with the Fera. Perhaps the Garou have opened up the ancestral realm of many extinct Garou groups of absorbed ones in the last days of Gaia and flooded Earth with renewed ancestor spirits or maybe they were always there but hiding from the crazy Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you want to get rid of Kinfolk, have massive amounts of them turned and the Garou are no longer dying out-ish. </div> </div> </div>Okay, but do you want these splats to be significant in any way? Because quantity tends to be the enemy of detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <b>Play up the Horror</b>: Being a Garou is something that was never really done with the personal horror angle. I think they should have put more rules about it and how to roleplay the struggle between your Beast of War and interactions with others. Garou don't have to be ticking time bombs but being unable to control their rage so they have to live among themselves was an angle always there but not one properly explored. </div> </div> </div>Oh no, it was attempted, and more than once. Back in the earliest design of the game, the game had werewolves chaining themselves up at night to avoid killing people. Then the designers realized that this was incredibly boring and also just repeating a lot of Vampire, so they changed it into what we got in 1e. Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies, introduced in 2e, might have been another attempt, but they're a fucking sledgehammer to the head compared with 1e's frenzies where you might just eat someone if you botched a Wits roll (now only for homids, because we have to do some kind of forced symmetry bullshit with the three breeds and equate them with the Triatic Wyrms, even for breeds that don't have the equivalent of Crinos-born like Corax).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we got a replacement in fully-summed up concept in 2e as well, in the form of Savage Horror, which is another way of saying &quot;this is the splatter game&quot;. There was an essay about it in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook detailing why they went with that and stuck with it, as well.<br /> <br /> tl;dr personal horror is Vampire's thing and no one else needs to have any part of it in their game, especially not if they're not likely to survive long enough to go through a protracted degeneration into an apathetic, blood-obligate micropredator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * <b>If you're going to sweeping changes, justify them</b>: You can get away with a certain amount of, &quot;no, it was always this way.&quot; Renaming the Wendigo, Fianna, Metis, and so on is fine. However, a lot of these other changes could have been done in-universe and paid proper respect to the past lore. Albretch, Evan (who is suddenly no longer ridiculous--but could have been retconned as a &quot;stolen Native child&quot; to to pay into RL tragedies), and other characters have had 20 years to make upheavels in the Garou Nation. </div> </div> </div>Revised actually just poof-retconned some things out of existence, like the Garou gene. Having the Garou work like the Nagah in terms of how they deal with where the next generation comes from could have been done similarly nowadays. (to wit, Nagah can produce Azhi Dahaka-born, but they're not guaranteed, and only one happens per mother per lifetime, and they're not disabled generally but very specifically more vulnerable to pollutants).<br /> <br /> Other details are probably in need of less evasive revision, but that had been the direction of Revised. Even the STV Ultimate Style Guide says as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T14:05:48-07:00","id":1523436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523406#post1523406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are two things about that that amuse me.<br /> <br /> One; If garou were using the umbra to kill princes those princes DESERVED it. Seriously, the amount of leash put on cross-play is immense. You cannot just randomly pop into umbra and kill a prince. STs of BOTH venues would have to approve that and there better be a GOOD reason for it.<br /> <br /> Second; Nothing is funnier than a &quot;these guys are too OP for my fave splat, make them more fair!&quot; The stakes couldn't be more different between VtM and WtA.<br /> <br /> How much DOES WoD5 support crossplay anyway?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The VtM-centric perspective you got from people like Kareem and Justin certainly didn't help. It was on their watch that they decided that not only was VtM &quot;Gothic Punk&quot;, but now <i>all </i>of the oWOD-splats would be considered &quot;Gothic Punk&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for crossplay... The irony is that WOD5E through all its trials and tribulations in development has just repeated the same mistakes the original WOD-editions did. You have some surface-level connections: The old WOD did it via metaplot, WOD5E does it via enforcing &quot;street-level-only&quot; and &quot;lore is bad&quot;. But system-wise the moment the first new corebook after V5 was released everything went wrong. The new in-house WOD-team mishandled the idea of cross-play immediately with H5. Instead of learning from CofD, WOD5E is just the old WOD all over again. The splats are just these tiny islands with their own idiosyncrasies in terms of mechanics that find no equivalent in other splats and weren't ever considered to be used in cross-play.<br /> <br /> Take H5... In contrast to V5 what has H5 got to do with the orginal version of Hunter the Reckoning? Absolutely nothing. That's the setting-side. With mechanics the new development-team looked at the systems of V5 and just abandoned them left and right: Convictions. Gone. Chronicle-Tenets (as in-game-mechanic). Gone. Humanity or any sort of morality-track. Gone. And even Hunger-Dice... In H5 the &quot;Hunger-&quot;rating is a group-based rating... Try making that work in cross-play... Also, both in H5 and W5 Touchstones aren't doing what they're supposed to do mechanically. And it's another throughline where just in this one instance somehow there's an insistence that &quot;Touchstones as people&quot; can't be changed as a mechanic.<br /> <br /> And W5 is just more of the same... Convictions still gone. No Humanity-equivalent. Sure, you could point to previous editions of WtA and say it wasn't handled like that but Forsaken managed to figure out a way to do it. And Hunter the Vigil managed to do it as well. Just because it's a game about mortal hunters doesn't mean you have to automatically abandon systems left and right.<br /> <br /> Also, why do PCs in W5 not have Ambition and Desire like in V5 and H5? It's not like these two ways of healing WP would break the game and both V5 and W5 had them. Of course, you could make Auspice and Tribe, for example, stand-ins in some way (which W5 didn't). Instead, Ambition and Desire are just gone in official W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T14:45:12-07:00","id":1523441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * <b>Pentex isn't really cartoony anymore</b>: There's actually people who really do for religious reasons believe we should pollute more to bring about the End of the World. You could have a Supply Side Jesus (The Patriarch?) avatar of the Wyrm telling them to do this and it would entirely be believable in this world. You also have high functioning psychopaths who do not CARE how much destruction they cause in the name of short term profit. Really, Pentex just happens to be the worst but other corporations aren't far behind.<br /> <br /> .\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>All those already existed when wta was first conceived. And that would still be cartoonish. Seriously, litt\u00e9ral evil Jesus appearing from the umbra to guide religious polluter would produce such a high rate of eyerolls from readers that we would have resolved the energy crisis. <br /> <br /> It would also be meaningless antagonists. Pentex was slightly believable because big inhumane corporation are a things and have great impact o' the world. How many &quot;let's pollute the world to bring the apocalypse&quot; religious nut jobs are there? And what power do they actually have? <br /> <br /> <br /> While people may like pentex as it is, ridiculous evil doesn't match well with a serious game. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> And pentex is and always was cartoonish. Even the worst corporation today is league behind even the meager pentex subsidiary in term of danger and evil. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523393#post1523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * <b>Play up the Horror</b>: Being a Garou is something that was never really done with the personal horror angle. I think they should have put more rules about it and how to roleplay the struggle between your Beast of War and interactions with others. Garou don't have to be ticking time bombs but being unable to control their rage so they have to live among themselves was an angle always there but not one properly explored.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, no. No more attempt to shoehorn personal horror outside of vtm. <br /> Everytime it's tried, it denaturate the game infected and ends up not working. <br /> <br /> The WOD isn't personal horror. VtM and WtO are. <br /> In fact, I would go as far as saying the WOD isn't horror either as a whole. Mage, changeling, or even mummy are not horror, despite the protest of writers and some of the fanbase. <br /> <br /> Writers should concentrate on what the games are, not to make them match their idea of the whole franchise as a whole homogeneous bunch<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T23:13:35-07:00","id":1523453,"title":"","content":"To play Devil's Advocate, WoD still doesn't offer you a traditional werewolf experience. Most non-WtA-fan Werewolf sites were harsh on Earthblood BECAUSE it didn't allow you to be more of a monster. There is a market for Personal Horror Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Buuuut, given Darker Days podcast interviewed one of the 1e devs and as Saur Ops said, they found your typical werewolf story too much like a vampire one (given how heavily popular culture draws from Romanian folklore where they could be the same creature, no wonder) the switch of gears made sense. Plus, I don't think there IS any other TTRPG focused on environmental and social corruption.<br /> <br /> And as much as W5 tries, it still wears the WtA label. It still has tribes and auspices and patrons. And you aren't given an option to play a Stolen Moon, either.<br /> <br /> So W5 is stuck between this Personal Horror mood and the Feral Horror of Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T23:35:49-07:00","id":1523454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523453#post1523453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Buuuut, given Darker Days podcast interviewed one of the 1e devs and as Saur Ops said, they found your typical werewolf story too much like a vampire one (given how heavily popular culture draws from Romanian folklore where they could be the same creature, no wonder) the switch of gears made sense. Plus, I don't think there IS any other TTRPG focused on environmental and social corruption.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>its probably worth noting my most scathing criticism of w5 is its just v5 again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T05:19:24-07:00","id":1523491,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf: The Apocalypse visual novel, WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE: HEART OF THE FOREST, was really heavy on personal horror and really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T09:45:20-07:00","id":1523500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523491#post1523491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Werewolf: The Apocalypse visual novel, WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE: HEART OF THE FOREST, was really heavy on personal horror and really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great for it, but if you want a general W:tA core book, you don't focus on personal horror. That's extremely niche for W:tA and, as noted, there was a good reason that they didn't base the mechanics around it. For more, again, read the Revised Storyteller's Handbook essay on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T10:14:05-07:00","id":1523502,"title":"","content":"To go with the &quot;nerf umbra so princes don't get umbra sniped&quot;, reading the start of the Second Inquisition book really sells the way anyone other than vampires are treated in WoD5. They don't just tell you the Inquisitors aren't playable, they outright tell you there is no redeeming qualities in the Inquisitors.<br /> <br /> Compared to the Inquisition book of old which starts explaining how thankless it is to hunt vampires and how the Inquisitors might be zealots, but they are defending humanity.<br /> <br /> I wanted to point this out, because the tone is very similar to W5's writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T13:49:04-07:00","id":1523510,"title":"","content":"Why is the game being designed on something you might do vtm vampires?<br /> <br /> <br /> plus considering you can just show up in the middle of the day....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T13:50:58-07:00","id":1523511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523510#post1523510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the game being designed on something you might do vtm vampires?<br /> <br /> <br /> plus considering you can just show up in the middle of the day....</div> </div> </div> </div>Because both Development Leads were Vampire Mains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T17:13:18-07:00","id":1523516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523502#post1523502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go with the &quot;nerf umbra so princes don't get umbra sniped&quot;, reading the start of the Second Inquisition book really sells the way anyone other than vampires are treated in WoD5. They don't just tell you the Inquisitors aren't playable, they outright tell you there is no redeeming qualities in the Inquisitors.<br /> <br /> Compared to the Inquisition book of old which starts explaining how thankless it is to hunt vampires and how the Inquisitors might be zealots, but they are defending humanity.<br /> <br /> I wanted to point this out, because the tone is very similar to W5's writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen lopsided writing like the new Second Inquisition book since Beast: the Primordial trying very hard to convince the reader that Heroes are evil despite, uh. Trying to protect people from literal monsters that feed on misery. Except now instead of one guy pushing that idea, it's the lead devs of the entire franchise.<br /> <br /> Between this, how H5 just plain doesn't work mechanically, and everything about W5, it's almost impressive how much the devs seem bitter that any game that isn't Vampire dares to exist in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T20:38:49-07:00","id":1523525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523510#post1523510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the game being designed on something you might do vtm vampires? Plus considering you can just show up in the middle of the day....</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the idea of game balance between the lines.<br /> <br /> Mages shouldn't be able to turn werewolves into butterflies with one attack either.<br /> <br /> But it's a stupid example to begin with. Yes, werewolves can show up in the Prince's chambers via a mirror but so is driving up to the guy and shooting him. There's ways around this. Hell, you can't attack the Prince from the Umbra easily because the dude's home is probably full of Banes from the staggering amount of murder and evil intent that is around them at all times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-04-2023, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T22:37:43-07:00","id":1523531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523525#post1523525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand the idea of game balance between the lines.<br /> <br /> Mages shouldn't be able to turn werewolves into butterflies with one attack either.<br /> <br /> But it's a stupid example to begin with. Yes, werewolves can show up in the Prince's chambers via a mirror but so is driving up to the guy and shooting him. There's ways around this. Hell, you can't attack the Prince from the Umbra easily because the dude's home is probably full of Banes from the staggering amount of murder and evil intent that is around them at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but a Prince's Haven is also going to have a stupidly-high Gauntlet score to overcome just to cross over in the first place. No one does this kind of thing in the TTRPG version of either game because it's insanely impractical and dangerous for most Garou of actual player-level range.<br /> <br /> However, apparently it's a thing that people do in LARPs. You know, a tiny subset of the playerbase that still apparently gets most of the attention from the devs. If it's really such a problem there, why not make special, separate rules for LARPs and not force the rest of the game to bend around it by taking away a massive part of WtA's setting for the sake of &quot;balancing&quot; something most players don't do in the first place?<br /> <br /> Oh, right. Because these are Vampire devs, and we can't let vampires have a disadvantage ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T23:03:37-07:00","id":1523534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523525#post1523525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand the idea of game balance between the lines.<br /> <br /> Mages shouldn't be able to turn werewolves into butterflies with one attack either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the balance between lines if the game has PCs from both lines. But in a single splat game, why shouldn't mages turn garou into butterflies? There are no garou players to complain about it.<br /> <br /> Instead of trying to balance the TT game from the outset, having alternative rules for crossover would be better. I don't mean NPC crossover but player crossover since that is clearly the reason for the Umbra thing to begin with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T04:35:04-07:00","id":1523537,"title":"","content":"H5 just continues to double down on that perspective from the Second Inquisition book mentioned previously with its fundamentally negative outlook on hunter-orgs. You get this from the Lexicon right at the start: &quot;Org: A formal organization that exists to hunt monsters as a means to an an end rather than for its own sake; orgs often support a status quo situation or preserve the power of elites (or themselves), and are generally larger and better resourced than individual cells\u200b&quot; The bit about hunter-orgs actually just reaffirming the status-quo is particularly interesting if you think about it. After all, if that cynical conception of hunter-orgs were true and hunter-orgs actually don't make a difference then that makes one aspect of WOD5E very peculiar: There's a thing called a Second Inquisition - so what about the first one? According to H5's conception there's no way it could've had an impact and yet obviously it did have an impact on vampire-society. So hunter-orgs can make a difference. And even in V5, you have the whole thing with Vienna. But according to H5 they are bad and ineffective and only local Hunter-cells of Hunters with Drive can be good but similar to how the young Garou-PCs in W5 aren't positioned to make changes beyond their street-level setting, the only-hunter-cells-are-good-idea of H5 similarly restricts what it allows mortal hunters to do.<br /> <br /> Also, in describing the hunter-org-types it also just doubles down on the fundamentally bad nature of hunter-org-hunters. Like this description for religious hunter-orgs: &quot;Religious orgs tend to have small but dedicated \u2014 even fanatical \u2014 memberships with rigid, fundamental outlooks. As with Governmental orgs, they attract support from those drawn to authoritarian figureheads and those who would inflict violence on others because an influential leader told them to do so; it\u2019s simply a religious authority as opposed to a secular one, and originates with a divine purpose instead of a temporal one\u2026 even if the results end up looking very similar.\u200b&quot; Rigid outlooks, drawn to authoritarian figureheads... Wait, where have I heard that before... Oh, right, the Cult of Fenris... I mean, if we're going by H5 and W5, the WOD5E-setting seems to be just chock full of lovers of authoritarianism. I can already picture someone making a pitch for M5: &quot;And of course, the big antagonist are the Technocracy who are very bad and...&quot; I interrupt &quot;Stop right there. Let me guess: They love authoritarianism.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's another striking similarity between H5 and W5: the vague history. Reckoning is even an actual concept in H5. But similarly to the vagueries in W5 with the Garou-Nation and Age of Apocalypse, Reckoning has the same whiff of &quot;Who knows&quot;. There's a sidebar called &quot;What is the Reckoning?&quot; and it says this: &quot;Ask a dozen Hunters, get a dozen answers. \u201cThe Reckoning\u201d has entered Hunter parlance as of late as a shorthand that conveys the same sort of awareness as many modern social-justice movements.\u200b [...] Ultimately, the Reckoning is the struggle against supernatural abuse and domination, and it is now.\u200b&quot; It's never explained how or why Hunters with Drive is a thing. This sidebar just makes it even weirder because this Reckoning-concept gets this nebulous time-window of &quot;as of late&quot; and &quot;it is now&quot;. It just happened. Like the Age of Apocalypse or the fall of the Garou-Nation. It just happened. Makes you wonder what the lore/worldbuilding for V5 would've been like if the same creative team that worked on W5 and H5 would've led development for V5...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T05:41:39-07:00","id":1523542,"title":"","content":"The vagueness of the timeline for H5 and W5 ironically makes me appreciate V5's metaplot changes, slightly. The Vienna Chantry's destruction. The Gehenna Wars in the Middle East. The rapid disappearance of Elders. The murder of others by Theo Bell. The Fall of London. Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> I still don't like all of these, and think they're fundamentally wasteful of material useful to Storytellers as adventure fodder. But at least they're <i>specific events</i>, that firmly establish when the old status quo gave way to the new. You can point to them and say, &quot;THIS is how we got where we are tonight&quot;. Characters in-universe can have their decisions informed by having experienced these plot points.<br /> <br /> Things like the Reckoning or the Apocalypse are made so vague, you have no real grounding for when it started, why, or what it means in practice. They are perfunctory terms, that the designers seem to resent having to even address as a setting element. &quot;Oh, the word in the title? Yeah, don't worry about that, it's whatever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T06:09:58-07:00","id":1523545,"title":"","content":"You know, I think the issue of setting arises from not understanding what keeps people in the WoD system. Because H5 and W5 treat it basically like a bit more robust DnD baseline. But for me, WoD is more like roleplaying in Star Wars or Lord of the Rings, in an established setting with established cultures.<br /> <br /> To put it crudely, W5 and H5 think players want creative writing, while they actually want to write fanfiction.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523542#post1523542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still don't like all of these, and think they're fundamentally wasteful of material useful to Storytellers as adventure fodder. But at least they're <i>specific events</i>, that firmly establish when the old status quo gave way to the new. You can point to them and say, &quot;THIS is how we got where we are tonight&quot;. Characters in-universe can have their decisions informed by having experienced these plot points.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHonestly, this is why the Second Inquisition book denying any chance to play the other side bothers me. Humanity has, after EONS, gotten an upper hand. Humanity finally can be a bit safer. And then the writing treats this as a purely bad thing.<br /> <br /> It is pretty much the same with how CoF are seen. Remove Hauglosk and Fascism and they are just doing what needs doing, they aren't even Wyrmy. Yet they are BAD because they do things RONG.<br /> <br /> Also, H5's hate for organized groups makes me really think of the phrase &quot;An army marches on its stomach.&quot; They are orgs because they can support a larger group and make use of what they hunt.<br /> <br /> Plus,idk, a small group of people seeing monsters and wanting them dead hasn't exactly been a positive thing in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 10-04-2023, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T16:38:07-07:00","id":1523582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523545#post1523545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I think the issue of setting arises from not understanding what keeps people in the WoD system. Because H5 and W5 treat it basically like a bit more robust DnD baseline. But for me, WoD is more like roleplaying in Star Wars or Lord of the Rings, in an established setting with established cultures.<br /> <br /> To put it crudely, W5 and H5 think players want creative writing, while they actually want to write fanfiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough newer and younger gamers, maybe the publisher's gamble was a good call or maybe a bad one. Only some time will tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T17:34:21-07:00","id":1523585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523525#post1523525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand the idea of game balance between the lines.<br /> <br /> Mages shouldn't be able to turn werewolves into butterflies with one attack either.<br /> <br /> But it's a stupid example to begin with. Yes, werewolves can show up in the Prince's chambers via a mirror but so is driving up to the guy and shooting him. There's ways around this. Hell, you can't attack the Prince from the Umbra easily because the dude's home is probably full of Banes from the staggering amount of murder and evil intent that is around them at all times.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be the wrong approach to enter the Prince's haven via a vanity mirror from the Umbra. The Garou should use Persuasion and other social Gifts to get a group of well-armed terrorists (in this case, a &quot;free militia&quot;) to do it, instead, and slip in during the confusion to enhance the devastation a bit. At all stages, get the Wyrm's minions to fight each other, even if they neither know nor care about the spiritual allegiances that they've cultivated. [/Shadow Lords]<br /> <br /> I mean, the prince probably has less to worry about from the Middle Umbra than the Dark Umbra, too. If you're a Silent Strider, you might know a ghost that can get a bus to have its &quot;brake lines fail&quot; so that it runs into an important building at full speed and thankfully with none of the quick on board. The Kindred suspect each other so much and have such a low opinion of werewolf actions that they probably wouldn't suspect a Garou of having engineered something to happen this way. There are literally so many more threatening options than popping in via the spirit world to enter the washroom and tell the Prince that you're watching them not-poop that this is just the most short-sighted BS imaginable... which means it might also be another lie to cover up some other opinion of the development staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T23:20:57-07:00","id":1523604,"title":"","content":"My idea is just to use your god tier lupus sense of smell, any relevant gifts and human tier intellect to locate his haven and show up at 1pm. His rent a cops arnt really going to be up to the challang and a safe room can only do so much.<br /> <br /> Historically it's been the mo for vampire hunting when I've played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-05-2023, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T23:25:47-07:00","id":1523605,"title":"","content":"In all honesty? I think the umbra attack happened once and the vampire playerbase freaked out. I've seen this happen in big games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T00:38:33-07:00","id":1523608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523605#post1523605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty? I think the umbra attack happened once and the vampire playerbase freaked out. I've seen this happen in big games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've been running/playing 30 years and....nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T00:54:13-07:00","id":1523610,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the lupus' god-tier sense of smell... I think it should be mentioned what W5 did with the Gift &quot;Heightened Senses&quot; from previous editions.<br /> <br /> Here's how it's described in W20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Gift sharpens the werewolf\u2019s senses to an incredible degree. She enjoys the olfactory and auditory acuity of a wolf whenever she is in Homid and Glabro forms, along with superior night vision. In Crinos, Hispo and Lupus, her senses become preternaturally potent, allowing sensory \u200bfeats that border on precognition. Sudden loud noises, bright lights or overwhelming scents can be disorienting, however. Wolf-spirits teach this Gift.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Seems straightforward enough, doesn't it? But here's how the new version called &quot;Sharpened Senses&quot; (one of the higher-tier Native Gifts) is described:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The werewolf heightens their senses to a level combining the most sensitive traits of wolf and human. In homid and glabro forms, they gain the senses of a wolf, whereas other senses while in crinos, hispo, or lupus sharpen to that of a human. A wolf-spirit grants this Gift.\u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sharpen to that of a human&quot;... Well, at least I guess you can now ace the eye test at the optometrist even in Lupus-form...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T01:03:24-07:00","id":1523611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523610#post1523610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the lupus' god-tier sense of smell... I think it should be mentioned what W5 did with the Gift &quot;Heightened Senses&quot; from previous editions.<br /> <br /> Here's how it's described in W20:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seems straightforward enough, doesn't it? But here's how the new version called &quot;Sharpened Senses&quot; (one of the higher-tier Native Gifts) is described:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Sharpen to that of a human&quot;... Well, at least I guess you can now ace the eye test at the optometrist even in Lupus-form...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Because no way there can be any hint that being a human is inferior in any kind of endeavour. Human is best master race yes yes, and our players are humans that now on average only play humans in fantasy games anyway. So go humanity go! Always and forever and unquestionable.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Accruing capital can be good also because it's a human thing that benefits humanity, animal species going extinct come second.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But also viking suprematists baaaad while Red Talons go grrrr.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T01:22:39-07:00","id":1523613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523610#post1523610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Seems straightforward enough, doesn't it? But here's how the new version called &quot;Sharpened Senses&quot; (one of the <b>higher-tier</b> Native Gifts) is described:<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Sharpen to that of a human&quot;... Well, at least I guess you can now ace the eye test at the optometrist even in Lupus-form...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait wait wait, a gift that has always been a cliath level is now HIGH tier one?<br /> <br /> And it doesn't do SHIT!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T01:26:17-07:00","id":1523614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523095#post1523095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Burning your Rage and quitting is more theory than practice: you acquire Rage by provocation, so losing the Wolf is granted to be temporary.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The rules say that, if you lose the wolf, howling at the moon or specific rites are the ONLY way to regain Rage(p.133 of W5.) You can be provoked all you want, but as long as that Rage count is zero you will not gain Rage.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it is good. I am saying that's what RAW says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T01:33:40-07:00","id":1523615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523613#post1523613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait wait wait, a gift that has always been a cliath level is now HIGH tier one?<br /> <br /> And it doesn't do SHIT!?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanic is &quot;Upon activating this Gift, the Difficulty of all Awareness tests made by the player are lowered by the character\u2019s Wisdom, to a minimum of 2. This Gift can be used in any form.\u200b&quot; And the requirement is a Total Renown of 4... You start with a Total Renown of 3 so it's at least not available to starting-characters.<br /> <br /> But in W5 there's also no accounting of the Lupus-form being superior in terms of sense of smell. Maybe you could say it's vaguely hinted at when it says &quot;Depending on the environment it can also gain various two-dice bonuses, such as to Survival or Stealth, depending on whether being a wolf would be beneficial in that specific situation.\u200b&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T04:00:44-07:00","id":1523617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523537#post1523537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">H5 just continues to double down on that perspective from the Second Inquisition book mentioned previously with its fundamentally negative outlook on hunter-orgs. You get this from the Lexicon right at the start: &quot;Org: A formal organization that exists to hunt monsters as a means to an an end rather than for its own sake; orgs often support a status quo situation or preserve the power of elites (or themselves), and are generally larger and better resourced than individual cells\u200b&quot; The bit about hunter-orgs actually just reaffirming the status-quo is particularly interesting if you think about it. After all, if that cynical conception of hunter-orgs were true and hunter-orgs actually don't make a difference then that makes one aspect of WOD5E very peculiar: There's a thing called a Second Inquisition - so what about the first one? According to H5's conception there's no way it could've had an impact and yet obviously it did have an impact on vampire-society. So hunter-orgs can make a difference. And even in V5, you have the whole thing with Vienna. But according to H5 they are bad and ineffective and only local Hunter-cells of Hunters with Drive can be good but similar to how the young Garou-PCs in W5 aren't positioned to make changes beyond their street-level setting, the only-hunter-cells-are-good-idea of H5 similarly restricts what it allows mortal hunters to do.<br /> <br /> Also, in describing the hunter-org-types it also just doubles down on the fundamentally bad nature of hunter-org-hunters. Like this description for religious hunter-orgs: &quot;Religious orgs tend to have small but dedicated \u2014 even fanatical \u2014 memberships with rigid, fundamental outlooks. As with Governmental orgs, they attract support from those drawn to authoritarian figureheads and those who would inflict violence on others because an influential leader told them to do so; it\u2019s simply a religious authority as opposed to a secular one, and originates with a divine purpose instead of a temporal one\u2026 even if the results end up looking very similar.\u200b&quot; Rigid outlooks, drawn to authoritarian figureheads... Wait, where have I heard that before... Oh, right, the Cult of Fenris... I mean, if we're going by H5 and W5, the WOD5E-setting seems to be just chock full of lovers of authoritarianism. I can already picture someone making a pitch for M5: &quot;And of course, the big antagonist are the Technocracy who are very bad and...&quot; I interrupt &quot;Stop right there. Let me guess: They love authoritarianism.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's another striking similarity between H5 and W5: the vague history. Reckoning is even an actual concept in H5. But similarly to the vagueries in W5 with the Garou-Nation and Age of Apocalypse, Reckoning has the same whiff of &quot;Who knows&quot;. There's a sidebar called &quot;What is the Reckoning?&quot; and it says this: &quot;Ask a dozen Hunters, get a dozen answers. \u201cThe Reckoning\u201d has entered Hunter parlance as of late as a shorthand that conveys the same sort of awareness as many modern social-justice movements.\u200b [...] Ultimately, the Reckoning is the struggle against supernatural abuse and domination, and it is now.\u200b&quot; It's never explained how or why Hunters with Drive is a thing. This sidebar just makes it even weirder because this Reckoning-concept gets this nebulous time-window of &quot;as of late&quot; and &quot;it is now&quot;. It just happened. Like the Age of Apocalypse or the fall of the Garou-Nation. It just happened. Makes you wonder what the lore/worldbuilding for V5 would've been like if the same creative team that worked on W5 and H5 would've led development for V5...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's a punk game. In what punk game is the federal government meant to be the defender of the weak and protector of the innocent?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've known people who say, &quot;Werewolf isn't Gothic Punk!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;Yeah, it really is.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, this is why the Second Inquisition book denying any chance to play the other side bothers me. Humanity has, after EONS, gotten an upper hand. Humanity finally can be a bit safer. And then the writing treats this as a purely bad thing.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I mean, humanity is behind Pentex.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is the people providing the ingredients but the supernatural isn't what makes the World of Darkness a hellhole. It's humans who gain supernatural powers misuse them the same way humans misuse capitalism, guns, and corruption in the real world. The Second Inquisition is a vile organization because it's committing inhuman atrocities on people because they're different, not because they have any interest in protecting humanity.<br /> <br /> Because, again, punk.<br /> <br /> It's great satire on the War on Drugs and War on Terror (which barely get mentioned despite obvious inspiration). &quot;Yes, there are bad people here but we'll spend 50 billion dollars trying to wipe out drugs rather than care for dying children. Because wars are sexy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-05-2023, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T04:30:46-07:00","id":1523619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523617#post1523617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it's a punk game. In what punk game is the federal government meant to be the defender of the weak and protector of the innocent?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've known people who say, &quot;Werewolf isn't Gothic Punk!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;Yeah, it really is.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To me, H5's obsession with hunter-orgs always had the whiff of &quot;missing the forest for the trees&quot;. Hunter is a game about mortal hunters versus supernatural monsters. The punk-aspect is that it casts humanity as the underdogs trying to fight against the power and influence that these supernatural monsters possess. Hunter isn't supposed to be &quot;hunter cells versus the federal government&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, the portrayal of <i>all </i>forms of hunter-orgs and anybody who works for them as bad is overly simplistic. Arcanum has skeletons in its closet but they're certainly not Pentex. But the way hunter-orgs are described in H5 it absolutely thinks hunter-orgs are Pentex-level evil-doers. They love authoritarianism, they're selfish and they don't care about humanity: That's what hunter-orgs in H5 are.<br /> <br /> As for WtA being gothic punk... it's certainly possible but W5's status as a gothic punk game is questionable at best. With its negative portrayal of Garou, W5 is a game telling its readers that direct action is bad, collective action is impossible and violence is never the solution. Certainly doesn't sound very punk to me...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T06:38:39-07:00","id":1523625,"title":"","content":"Someone know how are the Bone Gnawers in W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T06:50:01-07:00","id":1523626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523625#post1523625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone know how are the Bone Gnawers in W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are essentially the &quot;Nosferatu&quot; of the Garou now. It's all about information-gathering for them. There's still a bit about poverty/low social status but you get this vague paragraph about that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s a classic chicken-and-egg story. Were the Bone Gnawers always at the bottom, so they adapted to the tricks and trades of the bottom? Or were they so good at skullduggery and dirt-finding that they were pushed out of \u201cpolite society\u201d by colluding pipe-smokers and\u200b rhyme-saying furhead \u201cnobles\u201d? Who cares? Because when it comes down to it, who\u2019s got the goods? The rangy, shadow-slinking wolf who knows how to creep where creeping nets the most information, or some bespectacled ponytail with elbow patches on his tweed jacket?\u200b </div> </div> </div>Their Patron Spirit is still Rat and their Favor is one of the vaguer ones with &quot;A Bone Gnawer can add a die to a dice pool used to find something lost or overlooked.\u200b&quot;. The 'overlooked' bit is weird because if it's overlooked you wouldn't know it's there so how can you find something you don't know it's there. If it's overlooked by somebody else, does that mean the bonus only applies if somebody else has actually overlooked it before? Their Ban is similarly broad and vague: &quot;If a Bone Gnawer passes up a significant opportunity to give the disadvantaged a leg up, they regain only a single point of Willpower at the beginning of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b&quot; There again, &quot;give the disadvantaged a leg up&quot; and &quot;significant opportunity&quot;... certainly stuff the ST and the player should clear up beforehand what this exactly means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T07:17:49-07:00","id":1523629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523617#post1523617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, humanity is behind Pentex.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is the people providing the ingredients but the supernatural isn't what makes the World of Darkness a hellhole. It's humans who gain supernatural powers misuse them the same way humans misuse capitalism, guns, and corruption in the real world. The Second Inquisition is a vile organization because it's committing inhuman atrocities on people because they're different, not because they have any interest in protecting humanity.<br /> <br /> Because, again, punk.<br /> <br /> It's great satire on the War on Drugs and War on Terror (which barely get mentioned despite obvious inspiration). &quot;Yes, there are bad people here but we'll spend 50 billion dollars trying to wipe out drugs rather than care for dying children. Because wars are sexy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand the satire, I feel it suffers from its targets being mostly vampires. Vampires have human herds, they need to drink human blood to survive and even stealing bloodbags from hospitals is causing damage. They are the predators of humanity.<br /> <br /> And yes, I understand the whole 'taking out undesirables' part. But in order for the satire to work (in my opinion) you'd need the vampires to be neutral towards humanity. Not good or bad. But that is not what the vampires in WoD are. Even if the Second Inquisition doesn't care for humanity per se, they are taking out creatures that actively harm humanity.<br /> <br /> As for W5 and punk,yeah... it might work if W5 didn't basically say &quot;Direct action and fighting back with violence are bad. Groups can never lead to anything good UNLESS they are corporations. Corporations can work together!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, the CoF are bad BECAUSE they are taking direct action over sitting in their caerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T07:45:54-07:00","id":1523632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523626#post1523626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are essentially the &quot;Nosferatu&quot; of the Garou now. It's all about information-gathering for them. There's still a bit about poverty/low social status but you get this vague paragraph about that:<br /> <br /> <br /> Their Patron Spirit is still Rat and their Favor is one of the vaguer ones with &quot;A Bone Gnawer can add a die to a dice pool used to find something lost or overlooked.\u200b&quot;. The 'overlooked' bit is weird because if it's overlooked you wouldn't know it's there so how can you find something you don't know it's there. If it's overlooked by somebody else, does that mean the bonus only applies if somebody else has actually overlooked it before? Their Ban is similarly broad and vague: &quot;If a Bone Gnawer passes up a significant opportunity to give the disadvantaged a leg up, they regain only a single point of Willpower at the beginning of the next session, instead of their Composure or Resolve rating.\u200b&quot; There again, &quot;give the disadvantaged a leg up&quot; and &quot;significant opportunity&quot;... certainly stuff the ST and the player should clear up beforehand what this exactly means.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least at first glance they don't seem to have changed that much in terms of Lore, despite not even mentioning the Omega issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T07:55:40-07:00","id":1523634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523619#post1523619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, H5's obsession with hunter-orgs always had the whiff of &quot;missing the forest for the trees&quot;. Hunter is a game about mortal hunters versus supernatural monsters. The punk-aspect is that it casts humanity as the underdogs trying to fight against the power and influence that these supernatural monsters possess. Hunter isn't supposed to be &quot;hunter cells versus the federal government&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, the portrayal of <i>all </i>forms of hunter-orgs and anybody who works for them as bad is overly simplistic. Arcanum has skeletons in its closet but they're certainly not Pentex. But the way hunter-orgs are described in H5 it absolutely thinks hunter-orgs are Pentex-level evil-doers. They love authoritarianism, they're selfish and they don't care about humanity: That's what hunter-orgs in H5 are.<br /> <br /> As for WtA being gothic punk... it's certainly possible but W5's status as a gothic punk game is questionable at best. With its negative portrayal of Garou, W5 is a game telling its readers that direct action is bad, collective action is impossible and violence is never the solution. Certainly doesn't sound very punk to me...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, given the double-speak and twisted logic of &quot;people with Drive aren't authoritarian!!!&quot;, H5 comes off...well, it comes off like the kind of &quot;punk&quot; that other gothic punks dedicate a song to telling to fuck off.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, literally everyone outside our club is evil and all authority is corrupt that's why you need to dedicate your entire life to the cause and overthrow those weak effeminate moneyed interests...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Not All Corporations bit only cements it to me; &quot;money is bad, unless it supplies my interests-er, helps society.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T08:10:19-07:00","id":1523635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523617#post1523617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it's a punk game. In what punk game is the federal government meant to be the defender of the weak and protector of the innocent?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've known people who say, &quot;Werewolf isn't Gothic Punk!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;Yeah, it really is.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is, at a certain stage this attitude is liability not an asset.<br /> <br /> Plus it's a corporate mandated thing and/or the power fantasies of middle class boomer which is as far from punk as you can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T11:29:49-07:00","id":1523647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523634#post1523634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, given the double-speak and twisted logic of &quot;people with Drive aren't authoritarian!!!&quot;, H5 comes off...well, it comes off like the kind of &quot;punk&quot; that other gothic punks dedicate a song to telling to fuck off.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, literally everyone outside our club is evil and all authority is corrupt that's why you need to dedicate your entire life to the cause and overthrow those weak effeminate moneyed interests...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Not All Corporations bit only cements it to me; &quot;money is bad, unless it supplies my interests-er, helps society.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation with H5 only gets more twisted once you include Vigilante-hunter-orgs!<br /> <br /> The game has this binary: hunter-cells=good and hunter-orgs=bad. But what are Vigilante-hunter-orgs? They are hunter-cells who are focused <i>too much</i> on killing supernatural monsters. But this creates quite an interesting paradigm... So, all these hunter-orgs are selfish, love authoritarianism and don't care about humanity but hunter-cells are good. Yet conveniently the game acknowledges that hunter-cells can be bad - but they're classified as Vigilante-<i>hunter-orgs</i>. By that logic all hunter-cells are good and any hunter-cell that does something bad immediately gets classified as a Vigilante-<i>hunter-org</i>. There aren't any example of Vigilante-hunter-orgs in the H5 corebook because they are essentially just Hunters with Drive in hunter-cells who &quot;play H5 wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly what's also interesting is the critique of hunter-orgs is that they don't care about humanity, have their own selfish goals, treat the hunt of supernatural monsters as a means to an end and they love authoritarianism (let's not forget that...). But what is the sin of the Vigilante-hunter-org? It's that it cares <i>too much</i> about hunting supernatural monsters. This is interesting because where does this put the <i>good</i> kind of a hunter-cell? Is there any horizon beyond being a sort of neighborhood-watch for supernatural trouble? And considering what is declared to be fundamentally bad in the H5 corebook, there really isn't. It's street-level-only - and don't leave your local environment.<br /> <br /> And W5 carries over similar sentiments as it wants the <i>good </i>kind of Garou to just settle down in a caern and just stay there. On one side you have the Garou-Nation as a symbol of failure and defeat and on the other, you have the Cult of Fenris as a symbol of how anger and adventurism are fundamentally bad. You sit in your caern and you stay there. And occasionally you solve local street-level-only problems.<br /> <br /> I mentioned adventurism because that's the thing about WtA... What Garou aspire to be is heroes and those don't just stay in a local environment. Quests, adventures, missions... all sorts of heroic endeavors to go beyond the local setting. But W5 isn't a fan of that perspective. In a way, the Garou of W5 might as well team up with the H5-hunter-cells since they're just two types of neighborhood-watch. The world sucks but they can get self-righteous about what happens in their block...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T11:57:09-07:00","id":1523649,"title":"","content":"On top of everything else here, I think all this shows the massive problems with trying to force Hunter and Werewolf to fit that &quot;rage against authority within your group&quot; mentality that V5 has, or even just the &quot;your own group are your main antagonists&quot; of Vampire in general.<br /> <br /> Vampires have to deal with hunters sometimes, but most of the conflict has always come from other vampires. Vampires of a rival sect, competing for resources, politicking for power, that kind of thing. Also having to cope with how your character is a predator now, and how fast they fall into being a monster. It's a game with a very particular structure to it that isn't really found anywhere else in WoD. V5 turning into &quot;Camarilla Bad, don't even think about playing Sabbat, Anarchs only&quot; is overly simplistic and limiting but it at least has some kind of basis in how Vampire is usually played.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Hunter are games where the threat is mostly external. Werewolves have the Wyrm and Hunters have monsters that threaten humanity. Their brand of punk is about raging against other societal issues (the destruction of the planet and against those with powers above normal people that seek to prey on the downtrodden) instead of just the general &quot;Man&quot;. So when you give lip service to the original points but then just go on about how the <i>real</i> bad guy is organization within these groups, things just get... really, really unfortunate. Not only because it makes these games really confusing and boring by saying the only good thing the PCs can do is sit in one place and hope problems come to them, but also because even if they're flawed, the organizations here are a lot closer to activist groups than the government, so it (accidentally? That &quot;Not All Corporations&quot; sidebar makes me wonder) gives off the impression that organizing for an actual cause is bad. Not just bad, but organizing for a cause basically makes you a Nazi.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This isn't even getting into how both H5 and W5 treat &quot;caring about your cause&quot; as a fast-track to authoritarianism and fascism...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 10-05-2023, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T13:27:55-07:00","id":1523657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523647#post1523647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The situation with H5 only gets more twisted once you include Vigilante-hunter-orgs!<br /> <br /> The game has this binary: hunter-cells=good and hunter-orgs=bad. But what are Vigilante-hunter-orgs? They are hunter-cells who are focused <i>too much</i> on killing supernatural monsters. But this creates quite an interesting paradigm... So, all these hunter-orgs are selfish, love authoritarianism and don't care about humanity but hunter-cells are good. Yet conveniently the game acknowledges that hunter-cells can be bad - but they're classified as Vigilante-<i>hunter-orgs</i>. By that logic all hunter-cells are good and any hunter-cell that does something bad immediately gets classified as a Vigilante-<i>hunter-org</i>. There aren't any example of Vigilante-hunter-orgs in the H5 corebook because they are essentially just Hunters with Drive in hunter-cells who &quot;play H5 wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly what's also interesting is the critique of hunter-orgs is that they don't care about humanity, have their own selfish goals, treat the hunt of supernatural monsters as a means to an end and they love authoritarianism (let's not forget that...). But what is the sin of the Vigilante-hunter-org? It's that it cares <i>too much</i> about hunting supernatural monsters. This is interesting because where does this put the <i>good</i> kind of a hunter-cell? Is there any horizon beyond being a sort of neighborhood-watch for supernatural trouble? And considering what is declared to be fundamentally bad in the H5 corebook, there really isn't. It's street-level-only - and don't leave your local environment.<br /> <br /> And W5 carries over similar sentiments as it wants the <i>good </i>kind of Garou to just settle down in a caern and just stay there. On one side you have the Garou-Nation as a symbol of failure and defeat and on the other, you have the Cult of Fenris as a symbol of how anger and adventurism are fundamentally bad. You sit in your caern and you stay there. And occasionally you solve local street-level-only problems.<br /> <br /> I mentioned adventurism because that's the thing about WtA... What Garou aspire to be is heroes and those don't just stay in a local environment. Quests, adventures, missions... all sorts of heroic endeavors to go beyond the local setting. But W5 isn't a fan of that perspective. In a way, the Garou of W5 might as well team up with the H5-hunter-cells since they're just two types of neighborhood-watch. The world sucks but they can get self-righteous about what happens in their block...</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have mentioned this before, but WoD5 gives me strong &quot;Neo-liberalism&quot; vibes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, everything sucks. No, you aren't allowed to do anything about it on a systemic scale. You aren't allowed to do Direct Action, and you aren't allowed to build coalitions either. Only individualistic solutions to problems are permitted. You have to lift yourself up by your own bootstraps, and take personal responsibility. Going outside the proper channels - which we admit don't work - is Bad. Caring too much is Bad. Responding to systemic violence with counter-violence is Bad. <b>Stay in your lane</b>. The world is going to burn, and nothing can be done about it that disrupts the systems in place or involves curtailing Capitalism.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T13:50:46-07:00","id":1523658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523657#post1523657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have mentioned this before, but WoD5 gives me strong &quot;Neo-liberalism&quot; vibes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, everything sucks. No, you aren't allowed to do anything about it on a systemic scale. You aren't allowed to do Direct Action, and you aren't allowed to build coalitions either. Only individualistic solutions to problems are permitted. You have to lift yourself up by your own bootstraps, and take personal responsibility. Going outside the proper channels - which we admit don't work - is Bad. Caring too much is Bad. Responding to systemic violence with counter-violence is Bad. <b>Stay in your lane</b>. The world is going to burn, and nothing can be done about it that disrupts the systems in place or involves curtailing Capitalism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HqjhHVUzl8o\" data-code=\"HqjhHVUzl8o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HqjhHVUzl8o/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T19:59:36-07:00","id":1523676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523657#post1523657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have mentioned this before, but WoD5 gives me strong &quot;Neo-liberalism&quot; vibes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, everything sucks. No, you aren't allowed to do anything about it on a systemic scale. You aren't allowed to do Direct Action, and you aren't allowed to build coalitions either. Only individualistic solutions to problems are permitted. You have to lift yourself up by your own bootstraps, and take personal responsibility. Going outside the proper channels - which we admit don't work - is Bad. Caring too much is Bad. Responding to systemic violence with counter-violence is Bad. <b>Stay in your lane</b>. The world is going to burn, and nothing can be done about it that disrupts the systems in place or involves curtailing Capitalism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this popular in the USA lately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T20:34:27-07:00","id":1523679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523676#post1523676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this popular in the USA lately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but it was for a long while, especially in the 90s.<br /> <br /> Today, it's mostly associated with doomer subculture, ie the kind of people who are personally offended by the idea the world might get better or even not end, because then they'd have to care about things or especially find pleasure in life beyond dunking on people they dislike, and that's hard. It's why South Park's appeal has soured for younger generations (along with...other things, but that's a key one).<br /> <br /> EDIT: An important sidenote is that doomerism is more associated with political fringes these days, especially the alt-right - ironically the same kind of people the Cult of Fenris thinks it's a parody of. Not to say doomerism isn't an apolitical trait, but generally, it's one only found in accelerationists, as it's easier to sell &quot;make the world worse in the belief that only ending it can bring about utopia&quot; to people who already think it's doomed without their active efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-05-2023, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T23:59:35-07:00","id":1523681,"title":"","content":"I feel the, &quot;You can't make systemic change because it is a HORROR game and about your personal struggles is authoritarian&quot; is a helluva take.<br /> <br /> That would mean film noir is authoritarian.<br /> <br /> But forget it, Jake, it's Fifth Edition.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically, I feel like this dangerously comes close to arguing that non-idealistic storytelling is somehow morally relevant rather than artistically. The idea that you have to be able to make a difference and good to be able to triumph over evil in order to not be supporting authoritarian ideals. Which is nonsense. I could easily make the same argument that idealistic storytelling where good triumphs over evil is inherently fascist because it lies to people that the system can in any way allow a non-corrupt non-tyrannical victory without being torn down first. Which is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with depicting the World of Darkness as a place where there's a corrupt authority in the Garou Nation and systemic evils that the player characters can't necessarily beat. That's basically always been the depiction of the Garou Nation leadership (Silver Fangs are insane/corrupt, the Shadow Lords are, well, Evil) and they're up against Pentex which has always been shown to be so ubiquitous that it was undefeatable unless you totally destroyed Western civilization.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has never been non-Punk. It was always about fighting the incarnation of Western pollution, capitalism, and authority. The big difference as mentioned is that Vampire: The Masquerade allowed you the opportunity to JOIN the forces of corruption and greed while Werewolf never allowed you to be a Pentex executive. Which gives a very different feel toward Werewolf. Werewolf has always been a bit more binary in its morality with Werewolves guilty of things like past genocides and incompetent leadership but no one argues its not better than the alternative.<br /> <br /> There's no, &quot;The Anarchs are children and the Camarilla are the adults in the room&quot; or &quot;The Technocracy is right while the Traditions are Luddite terrorists.&quot; Which actually does seriously impact the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> Which are VERY common views in their gamelines. As mentioned I'm a V:TM guy then a M:TA guy but W:TA is still on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-06-2023, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T00:54:05-07:00","id":1523683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523681#post1523681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with depicting the World of Darkness as a place where there's a corrupt authority in the Garou Nation and systemic evils that the player characters can't necessarily beat. That's basically always been the depiction of the Garou Nation leadership (Silver Fangs are insane/corrupt, the Shadow Lords are, well, Evil) and they're up against Pentex which has always been shown to be so ubiquitous that it was undefeatable unless you totally destroyed Western civilization.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has never been non-Punk. It was always about fighting the incarnation of Western pollution, capitalism, and authority. The big difference as mentioned is that Vampire: The Masquerade allowed you the opportunity to JOIN the forces of corruption and greed while Werewolf never allowed you to be a Pentex executive. Which gives a very different feel toward Werewolf. Werewolf has always been a bit more binary in its morality with Werewolves guilty of things like past genocides and incompetent leadership but no one argues its not better than the alternative.<br /> <br /> There's no, &quot;The Anarchs are children and the Camarilla are the adults in the room&quot; or &quot;The Technocracy is right while the Traditions are Luddite terrorists.&quot; Which actually does seriously impact the themes of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is glamouring for a game where the evil is beat, it is more that the book should still encourage the PCs to fight back.<br /> <br /> WtA isn't about philosophical differences between its factions like Vampire and Mage are. Even if it is binary, it is still a binary between flawed people trying to do good and forces of pollution, corruption,racism,etc. That is why you can't play BSDs or Pentex workers, because that is just not the tone of the game. And BSDs are automatic Black Dog in the worst way.<br /> <br /> W5 takes that setup and then tells the PCs to not try. Not that there are more shades of gray between groups, just that fighting back is bad and makes you into a fascist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T00:59:56-07:00","id":1523684,"title":"","content":"\u200b <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523681#post1523681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the, &quot;You can't make systemic change because it is a HORROR game and about your personal struggles is authoritarian&quot; is a helluva take.<br /> <br /> That would mean film noir is authoritarian.<br /> <br /> But forget it, Jake, it's Fifth Edition.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Basically, I feel like this dangerously comes close to arguing that non-idealistic storytelling is somehow morally relevant rather than artistically. The idea that you have to be able to make a difference and good to be able to triumph over evil in order to not be supporting authoritarian ideals. Which is nonsense. I could easily make the same argument that idealistic storytelling where good triumphs over evil is inherently fascist because it lies to people that the system can in any way allow a non-corrupt non-tyrannical victory without being torn down first. Which is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with depicting the World of Darkness as a place where there's a corrupt authority in the Garou Nation and systemic evils that the player characters can't necessarily beat. That's basically always been the depiction of the Garou Nation leadership (Silver Fangs are insane/corrupt, the Shadow Lords are, well, Evil) and they're up against Pentex which has always been shown to be so ubiquitous that it was undefeatable unless you totally destroyed Western civilization.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has never been non-Punk. It was always about fighting the incarnation of Western pollution, capitalism, and authority. The big difference as mentioned is that Vampire: The Masquerade allowed you the opportunity to JOIN the forces of corruption and greed while Werewolf never allowed you to be a Pentex executive. Which gives a very different feel toward Werewolf. Werewolf has always been a bit more binary in its morality with Werewolves guilty of things like past genocides and incompetent leadership but no one argues its not better than the alternative.<br /> <br /> There's no, &quot;The Anarchs are children and the Camarilla are the adults in the room&quot; or &quot;The Technocracy is right while the Traditions are Luddite terrorists.&quot; Which actually does seriously impact the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> Which are VERY common views in their gamelines. As mentioned I'm a V:TM guy then a M:TA guy but W:TA is still on the list.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but I think you've missed the point here. It's not that people want WoD to become Good Guys vs. Bad Guys, or never ever explore corruption within these groups, or that addressing this corruption is somehow authoritarianism\u200b. It's that Hunter and Werewolf had the aspects that made them &quot;punk&quot; in their own unique ways removed to try to make them more like Vampire, and in the process, they were just left as empty husks that do nothing but tell the player they're worthless and they will never accomplish anything, while actively removing any structure or tools they could have used to actually play the game. It's one thing to be nihilistic or have seemingly impossible odds, but it's another for a supposedly &quot;punk&quot; game to actively tell you that trying to fight the power is useless and stupid. Which W5 does. A lot.<br /> <br /> I'm speaking admittedly a WtA main, but I've played my share of every WoD line, including a lot of VtM. I've read W5 front to back by this point, and tried to play H5 (had to stop because the mechanics just plain don't work, but that's a story for another day), and for the former especially, there is no more Nation to fight against. It's been gone for a while. The Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords are now just some guys, barely different from any of the other tribes and don't hold any real authority. So who are the Garou supposed to rage against. The Wyrm? Well, no, W5 keeps telling us that the Wyrm isn't all that bad and maybe the Garou are overblowing this whole thing. Corporations? No, the book won't shut up about how the Garou can't actually do anything meaningful to stop them and probably shouldn't even try because hey corporations aren't that bad either. Fighting for Gaia? Nope. Gaia's either unfixably terminally ill or already dead, and you can't go into the Umbra. And if you try to fight anyway? Well, we call that Hauglosk and it'll make your character unplayable <i>very</i> quickly.<br /> <br /> So what's even left to this game? Why even bother playing it? Like you said, Werewolf has no option to join the bad guys. What's &quot;punk&quot; about being told to sit in one place and guard your singular block until the world explodes? There's nihilism, and then there's being given no point in playing the game at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T02:02:52-07:00","id":1523687,"title":"","content":"Honestly between The Maggot Symphony, The Red Talon Archetypes and that Wedding Bullshit I'm seeing BSDs getting squeezed out of their conceptual space big time. All three released adventures focus solely on the Cult of Fenris as the main enemy of the Garou......kind of like a certain Dev always wanted his notzee expys to be....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T02:16:39-07:00","id":1523688,"title":"","content":"Also, the whole bit about &quot;divorcing Tribes from their cultural identity&quot; isn't really adhered to with the Get of Fenris/Cult of Fenris. In The Deepest Of Wounds adventure it's now stated that the CoF's Patron-Spirit is Fenris, the Apocalypse Beast (rather than just Wolf). And the main-bad-guy CoF Ahroun called Black Lung has the Gift Luna's Armor except apparently the Fenrir-version is called... Viking Pelt (very subtle...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T03:55:17-07:00","id":1523692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523688#post1523688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the whole bit about &quot;divorcing Tribes from their cultural identity&quot; isn't really adhered to with the Get of Fenris/Cult of Fenris. In The Deepest Of Wounds adventure it's now stated that the CoF's Patron-Spirit is Fenris, the Apocalypse Beast (rather than just Wolf). And the main-bad-guy CoF Ahroun called Black Lung has the Gift Luna's Armor except apparently the Fenrir-version is called... Viking Pelt (very subtle...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they aren't, what matters is that they give the players the laziest version of the nazi they can. There isn't any discussion on how not all Nordic people or symbols are bad, just assumes its all bad.<br /> <br /> Oh and, since we are here, the sole Finnish NPC?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>P.21 of Deepest Wounds</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draug had no qualms leveraging \u201cdeplorable\u201d, hateful and prejudiced aspects of human society like the white nationalist movement and neo-Nazism. His ideas were unwelcome by everyone except Black Lung, which is why the two stuck together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a out and out neo-nazi. I don't mean we don't have them here, but it SURE looks bad when the one North European NPC is the nazi.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T04:24:11-07:00","id":1523694,"title":"","content":"The scenario also starts out with a strange setup:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Split<br /> Five or so years ago, a nearby caern, a Garou spiritual nexus, died. The dead caern was controlled by the Cult of Fenris. Despite feverish work by the caern\u2019s Fenrir defenders, as well as aid from the players\u2019 caern, the caern\u2019s spirit energies dried up.\u200b<br /> As a result of the dying of their caern, the local Cult of Fenris succumbed to Hauglosk.<br /> The Fenrir protectors of the dead caern put out a call to all nearby Garou packs to join them on a great reaving against the enemies of Gaia. They called for all loyal Garou to join them and go on the attack.<br /> Most of the nearby Garou refused the call to join the reaving. Three members from the sept of the players\u2019 characters volunteered to join the reaving; two Cult of Fenris including Claude \u201cBlack Lung\u201d Moreau and Eli \u201cDraug\u201d Markkanen; and a Red Talon known as Butterfly Eater.\u200b </div> </div> </div>What's weird:<ul><li>So until five years ago this Sept were happy neighbors with a Cult of Fenris caern...? That's certainly not how the W5 corebook portrays them.</li> <li>The dying of the caern is what made them succumb to Hauglosk...? But they're Cult of Fenris! Their whole deal is that they already succumbed to Hauglosk.</li> <li>Then these Cult of Fenris announced that they would leave to find and fight the forces of the Wyrm and according to this most Garou were like &quot;Nah, we're good.&quot;. This game really wants to emphasize that good Garou just manage and hunker down in a caern, doesn't it?</li> <li>A Red Talon joined them which would make the CoF more of a multi-Tribal-affair - which is not how it's portrayed in the corebook. And with that take on the Cult, you certainly could've managed to come up with a good remnant of the old Get of Fenris.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:09:20-07:00","id":1523697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523687#post1523687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly between The Maggot Symphony, The Red Talon Archetypes and that Wedding Bullshit I'm seeing BSDs getting squeezed out of their conceptual space big time. All three released adventures focus solely on the Cult of Fenris as the main enemy of the Garou......kind of like a certain Dev always wanted his notzee expys to be....</div> </div> </div> </div>Maggot Symphony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:13:33-07:00","id":1523698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523697#post1523697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maggot Symphony?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the adventure Deepest of Wounds one of the Garou in the Sept is kidnapped by the Cult of Fenris and they try to convert him which is described like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Three Slices is held in the center of the room. He is battered, beaten, and exhausted. Three Slices wears the tattered remnants of his clothes, barely able to cover him any longer. He is in homid form, and rests on his hands and knees with his head low. His eyes are closed. He breathes slowly and deliberately with the hint of a wheeze at the end of every breath.<br /> <br /> Six silver spikes encrusted with scabrous blood are driven into his back. His wrists are ankles are bound with thick rope (enough to make escape attempts impossible \u2014 even in crinos). The ropes lead to nearby metal rings that are secured to the concrete floor.<br /> <br /> Surrounding Three Slices are a plethora of TVs and computer screens. Each of the screens is on and is regularly flashing between various images and short video clips. Each image is something disturbing or horrific \u2014 especially for the Garou. Many of the images show the after-effects of massive environmental degradation like dried lakes, shriveled forests, and waterways choked with plastic. Other images are just colors that fade into one another \u2013vibrant greens, reds, or blues that are overtaken and overwhelmed by veins of black or white. There are also images of text with words like, \u201cSubmit,\u201d \u201cAnger,\u201d and \u201cDead.\u201d<br /> <br /> The disturbing images are accompanied with a cacophony of sounds and pre-recorded spoken words. Hundreds of small and large speakers surround Three Slices. Words like those on the screens are repeated, as are longer phrases that explicitly call out the Garou as \u201cfailures.\u201d Electronic voices from many different languages speak short phrases praising and venerating Fenris.<br /> <br /> A character who watches and listens to the Symphony for a bit can make a Composure + Occult at Difficulty 3 roll to determine the Cult of Fenris connection to the multimedia assault.\u200b </div> </div> </div>And the audio-file used during this &quot;conversion&quot; is called Maggot Symphony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:20:03-07:00","id":1523699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523698#post1523698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the adventure Deepest of Wounds one of the Garou in the Sept is kidnapped by the Cult of Fenris and they try to convert him which is described like this:</div> </div> </div> </div>Soo, why not BSDs? Like, seriously, this is BSD stuff.<br /> <br /> Heck, this doesn't even fit CoF MO as their whole thing is that other garou are weak. Why try to convert someone at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:29:48-07:00","id":1523700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523699#post1523699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soo, why not BSDs? Like, seriously, this is BSD stuff.<br /> <br /> Heck, this doesn't even fit CoF MO as their whole thing is that other garou are weak. Why try to convert someone at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and especially the moment it was decided to call it the &quot;Maggot Symphony&quot;, somebody should've realized that this sounds very Wyrm-ish.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole torture-scene/Maggot-Symphony revolves around calling Garou &quot;failures&quot; and showing images of environmental destruction which is... just stuff the W5 corebook thinks is objectively true. Age of Apocalypse, the fall of the Garou-Nation: The W5 corebook is completely in agreement with what this Maggot Symphony is saying. It's just that unlike the &quot;bad&quot; Cult of Fenris who want to go out there and fight the Wyrm, the &quot;respectable&quot; response is instead supposed to be to just get a caern and never move very far away from it.<br /> <br /> And while Justin Achilli may be gone, Karim Muammar is still the Brand Editor of the WOD and we know at least one thing about his opinion on W5: That the Cult of Fenris should be the new main-antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:35:40-07:00","id":1523701,"title":"","content":"As many of you know I like and defended many w5 stuff but<br /> <br /> - the depiction of fenrir in the new edition is almost the same of the first and second ed fenrir. Nothing really changed except the whole Nordic thing being more philosophical and their totem is just now &quot;Wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> 1 - the depiction of them in the new chronicle despite being raw and violent (which I like, uncompromising and extreme bastards , us vs the world ) makes them on a bsd level which is nonsense (torture, conversion, ecc)<br /> 2 - the Cult hates weaklings and think about non zealots grou as weaklings. Why the hell they convert them through weaver stuff ? ( they also believe the wyrm could be everywhere and I refuse to accept that a veteran like Black Lung would ever accept something like &quot;symphony of maggots&quot; cmon)<br /> 3 -maybe the writer wanted to leave an ambiguous sense of wyrm taint or the suspect about. Still, this totally destroy the new fenrir concept because:<br /> 4 - portraying them as wyrm tainted means totally ignore the tragedy behind them because..<br /> 5 - after all in the same chronicle, it is said there is a tragedy behind the fact they leave the nation and became antagonistc, in this case, in fact, they suffer a great loss after a huge battle and no tribe, no tribe answer their call for help.<br /> 6 - what they represent should be a warning about the strong authoritarian danger the garou culture may produce, the black spiral dancers represents the danger of falling to the wyrm.<br /> 7 - what should be scary is the thing that sometimes, as mentioned in the core, fenrir and other tribes can find themselves facing the same enemy. Which means the fenrir work as non wyrm tainted antagonist. Again, we already have the black spiral. The fenrir represent the danger within, and they should be scary exactly because they are extreme but not tainted.<br /> <br /> My two cent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-06-2023, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:36:55-07:00","id":1523702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523700#post1523700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and especially the moment it was decided to call it the &quot;Maggot Symphony&quot;, somebody should've realized that this sounds very Wyrm-ish.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole torture-scene/Maggot-Symphony revolves around calling Garou &quot;failures&quot; and showing images of environmental destruction which is... just stuff the W5 corebook thinks is objectively true. Age of Apocalypse, the fall of the Garou-Nation: The W5 corebook is completely in agreement with what this Maggot Symphony is saying. It's just that unlike the &quot;bad&quot; Cult of Fenris who want to go out there and fight the Wyrm, the &quot;respectable&quot; response is instead supposed to be to just get a caern and never move very far away from it.<br /> <br /> And while Justin Achilli may be gone, Karim Muammar is still the Brand Editor of the WOD and we know at least one thing about his opinion on W5: That the Cult of Fenris should be the new main-antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and Muammar clearly thinks Ultimate Despair from Danganronpa is an entirely realistic depiction of a terrorist cult.<br /> <br /> It has to be, otherwise why would Fenrir be tattooed on a member? Convergent Evolution? What's that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T06:37:45-07:00","id":1523703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523700#post1523700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and especially the moment it was decided to call it the &quot;Maggot Symphony&quot;, somebody should've realized that this sounds very Wyrm-ish.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, would it hurt to make bad guy factions at least distinct? BSDs convert, CoF takes in those worthy,etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:10:22-07:00","id":1523704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523703#post1523703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If nothing else, would it hurt to make bad guy factions at least distinct? BSDs convert, CoF takes in those worthy,etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the kidnapping/conversion-part of Deepest Of Wounds feels a bit forced. I get the part where the CoF-members return trying to recruit new members and scrounge for some more resources in order to go back to running around and fight the Wyrm wherever they can find it. But at the end of the day, the CoF still think of themselves as Gaia's warriors so this brainwashing-stuff really doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> And the weirdest part: There is another NPC who is willing to join them! (I'm pretty sure the CoF-NPCs could've convinced Fancy (who is also yet another Red Talon) to join them.) So much trouble could've been avoided if they hadn't done that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:17:37-07:00","id":1523705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523629#post1523629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As for W5 and punk,yeah... it might work if W5 didn't basically say &quot;Direct action and fighting back with violence are bad. Groups can never lead to anything good UNLESS they are corporations. Corporations can work together!&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, the CoF are bad BECAUSE they are taking direct action over sitting in their caerns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is absolutely not the case, and I can easily point to several instances of the corebook saying that the whole concept of the game is to take direct action against those who are destroying the world.<br /> <br /> What the corebook says, it's that Garous can become jaded and cynical, fractious and bitter over details and interpretations, or get lost in their fight and ignore what happens around them.<br /> <br /> Which, I would say as a socialdemocrat who is now voting the radical left out of desperation, are exactly the risk activist groups run into, every day, every time.<br /> <br /> By the way, of course that small blurb about corporations is not entusiasticallty endorsing corporations, it's just saying that like other forms of human cooperation it's not like every business is a tool of the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:20:27-07:00","id":1523706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523694#post1523694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]A Red Talon joined them which would make the CoF more of a multi-Tribal-affair - which is not how it's portrayed in the corebook. And with that take on the Cult, you certainly could've managed to come up with a good remnant of the old Get of Fenris.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>The origin story of the Cult mentions that they challenged the Tribes and took a piece of the Nation with them. Also, there is the former Fenris loresheet to represent those who have not joined the Cult (although, as one the levels is called &quot;Bootlicker&quot;, it surely doesn't do much to present the fallen Tribe in a favourable light).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:26:14-07:00","id":1523707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523706#post1523706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The origin story of the Cult mentions that they challenged the Tribes and took a piece of the Nation with them. Also, there is the former Fenris loresheet to represent those who have not joined the Cult (although, as one the levels is called &quot;Bootlicker&quot;, it surely doesn't do much to present the fallen Tribe in a favourable light).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Loresheet is about former Fenrir joining other Tribes. There was no reason to make the whole Tribe unplayable. And the adventure presents an obvious solution for this: The bad Fenrir venerate Fenris, the Apocalypse-beast (hence the name, &quot;Cult of Fenris&quot;) and you give the good ones a new name and their Patron-Spirit is Wolf. Easy peasy.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris is not multi-Tribal in the W5 corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:38:48-07:00","id":1523708,"title":"","content":"I guess if Fenrir is the evil Apocalpse-Beast (could it be that Fenris was really just a mask worn by the Beast of War?) then it makes me rethink the whole Odin-vampire thing since that would place Odin in a more heroic light, at least in his opposition to Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T07:45:23-07:00","id":1523709,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you do the same thing like with Galestalkers and Ghost Council but it's the Get of Fenris. You rename them, you give them a slightly different culture completely unconnected to any human ethnicity and culture. They're a good Tribe of absolute warriors who hate weakness with Wolf as their Patron Spirit. And then you just say that in the Age of Apocalypse when the Cult of Fenris forms most of their Tribe joins them. But the remnant is still a playable option.<br /> <br /> Also, by making the Cult of Fenris less about one particular Tribe and more about this one big movement of Garou from all sorts of Tribes, it becomes more believable how it destabilized the Garou-Nation and led to its fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T08:02:25-07:00","id":1523711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523698#post1523698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the adventure Deepest of Wounds one of the Garou in the Sept is kidnapped by the Cult of Fenris and they try to convert him which is described like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the audio-file used during this &quot;conversion&quot; is called Maggot Symphony.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really seems like a BSD thing. Which makes me question why the switch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T08:08:05-07:00","id":1523712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523679#post1523679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, but it was for a long while, especially in the 90s.<br /> <br /> Today, it's mostly associated with doomer subculture, ie the kind of people who are personally offended by the idea the world might get better or even not end, because then they'd have to care about things or especially find pleasure in life beyond dunking on people they dislike, and that's hard. It's why South Park's appeal has soured for younger generations (along with...other things, but that's a key one).<br /> <br /> EDIT: An important sidenote is that doomerism is more associated with political fringes these days, especially the alt-right - ironically the same kind of people the Cult of Fenris thinks it's a parody of. Not to say doomerism isn't an apolitical trait, but generally, it's one only found in accelerationists, as it's easier to sell &quot;make the world worse in the belief that only ending it can bring about utopia&quot; to people who already think it's doomed without their active efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagined it because I've been getting a lot of this kind of thing lately, every now and then ok, but it's too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T08:11:26-07:00","id":1523714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523711#post1523711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really seems like a BSD thing. Which makes me question why the switch?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we know, KM wanted CoF to be the worst. It makes no sense otherwise as even the adventure notes that their ways are simple and direct. Torture is NOt simple OR direct, especially that Danganronpa torture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T08:19:01-07:00","id":1523715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523705#post1523705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is absolutely not the case, and I can easily point to several instances of the corebook saying that the whole concept of the game is to take direct action against those who are destroying the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can say whatever it wants, but if the rules endorse something else, it is, at best, mistaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the corebook says, it's that Garous can become jaded and cynical, fractious and bitter over details and interpretations, or get lost in their fight and ignore what happens around them.<br /> <br /> Which, I would say as a socialdemocrat who is now voting the radical left out of desperation, are exactly the risk activist groups run into, every day, every time. </div> </div> </div>This makes sense for human activist groups, which Garou are most assuredly not. Though, this is more in legacy; VV5 stripped out anything that couldn't be mechanically reflected by something similar to a bit of mechanics from V5, so the Garou of this edition do come across as scattered members of an activist community instead of being an ancient culture of wolf shapeshifters that have been fighting corruption since before humans had fully gotten the hand of cave painting. While the modern world certainly has a lot of shakeups, it shouldn't outright have erased that culture, in a major case of Does This Remind You Of Anything with regard to Indigenous cultures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, of course that small blurb about corporations is not entusiasticallty endorsing corporations, it's just saying that like other forms of human cooperation it's not like every business is a tool of the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>Any given corporation could become a WIC because modern corporations aren't doing anything good as their MO, they're plutocracies sucking up wealth for uncaring investors so that they can cash dividend checks on time. That environment is a feast for the bits of the Wyrm poking through their prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T10:13:38-07:00","id":1523722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523712#post1523712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagined it because I've been getting a lot of this kind of thing lately, every now and then ok, but it's too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also something that's very good for clickbait and a convenient way out of caring - and yeah, also is associated with accelerationism, which is not known for the politeness, quiet, and general lack of verbiage of its practitioners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T11:11:05-07:00","id":1523726,"title":"","content":"Okay, I want to REALLY get into why I find the CoF torturing someone for conversion and using THAT method so lazy and contrary to the whole point of the tribe.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir are a tribe that let in very few garou, no matter if they had high breeding or not. To become a Fenrir was to deal with gruelling tests and endless insults. What mattered was not your physical state but your willpower. Those who said 'fuck you I'll win' to every challenge and tired again after being kicked down got rited.<br /> <br /> Torture is about breaking one's will. It is about making someone more pliable. The very opposite of what the Fenrir want.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers use torture because they live by the 'meat to the grinder' mentality. That and their whole Rite of Passage RELIES on breaking the target's will.<br /> <br /> Plus, let's remember that the CoF are under Hauglosk and multiple times it is said they seek to simplify things to emulate Fenris. Yet Black Lung (whose name I think is meant to be Black Dragon and not the disease) is said to be calm in his actions and calculating. Which is not how someone under Hauglosk should be. Nevermind torturing for converts.<br /> <br /> This all reads like the module was originally using BSDs and then later it was switched to CoF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T12:52:23-07:00","id":1523730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523709#post1523709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you do the same thing like with Galestalkers and Ghost Council but it's the Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>The HE team attempted to do this, and was repeatedly shot down by Muammar. It was clear that his vision of cultural de-emphasis (not removal during our tenure) was focused on the Tribes that represented marginalized culture: The colonized Tribes, the black and brown Tribes, the feminist Tribes. But he absolutely insisted that the Fenrir could not be isolated from a culture of white supremacy. It was mandatory that this be a major part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Here is his response to one of the writers, who while I won't name, is a Jewish woman, which I think matters in context with how he is speaking to her, when she tried to write a non-fascist version of the Fenrir who were focused on glory and becoming legends and dying for Gaia. This is essentially &quot;Vanir's Wrath&quot; as they appeared in Heart of the Forest, which was based on the HE draft of the book.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"428\" height=\"184\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28127-j-f-sambrano","name":"j.f. sambrano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28127_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T13:27:02-07:00","id":1523732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>j.f. sambrano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523730#post1523730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is his response to one of the writers, who while I won't name, is a Jewish woman, which I think matters in context with how he is speaking to her, when she tried to write a non-fascist version of the Fenrir who were focused on glory and becoming legends and dying for Gaia. This is essentially &quot;Vanir's Wrath&quot; as they appeared in Heart of the Forest, which was based on the HE draft of the book.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"428\" height=\"184\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;If the writers are unwilling to tackle <u><b>their </b></u>unsavory history&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Saying that to a Jewish woman, huh.<br /> <br /> Other than that, as a Nordic person of the Finnish persuasion, I find how Muammar is handling the Fenrir really curious and insulting.<br /> <br /> For one, I don't know how much you know about this JF, but Sweden is currently dealing with a LOT of issues with its immigrant population and the racism in their system. This has been a thing for a while. I feel that Muammar's goal for the Fenrir reflects how Sweden is currently doing.<br /> <br /> The last sentence is scary, though. There have been noble Nordic warriors in history, vikings were VERY open minded and traded with everyone,etc. It isn't neo-fascism to treat Nordic cultures with respect, while admitting their faults. The way Muammar writes hints that there is zero good to be found in 'Noble Nordic Warriors.'<br /> <br /> It is especially awful as a Nordic person to see the culture around me (Finland is kind of an odd duck) being used as proof of villany.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T13:36:57-07:00","id":1523733,"title":"","content":"How is it that he was that focused on Garou tribes as exemplars of associated human cultures? Was the vast gulf between Ancient Greece and the Black Furies absolutely lost on him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T14:18:16-07:00","id":1523736,"title":"","content":"If one wanted to avoid comparisons to Neo-Nazis with the Get of Fenris, this could have been accomplished ably by establishing a schism within the Tribe. Have the Swords of Heimdal not only survive the purge of the early 00s, but have a resurgence in the decades since that parallels the Real Life resurgence of Fascism. Slowly radicalizing Fenrir youths, until they felt they had enough clout to attempt a power play within the Tribe. When this failed - non-Fascist Fenrir and other Garou correctly seeing them as the monsters they were and acting against them - the Swords of Heimdal broke off from the Garou nation. Trying to prosecute their crusade against &quot;Impurity&quot; on their own, or perhaps recruiting similarly radicalized members of other Tribes. (Like, for example, the most hateful and extreme parts of the Red Talons, who felt even their own Tribe weren't doing enough to exterminate humanity.)<br /> <br /> This could serve duel purpose. First, it gives a new Bad Guy Werewolves faction for Garou PCs to struggle against. Second, it creates a clean division between morally upstanding &quot;Viking Werewolves&quot; and the &quot;Viking Cosplayers&quot; that are the Fascists. It's also a good way to soften the edges of one or more Tribes, as the most extreme and anti-social Garou within the Gaian camp go off to form a coalition of evil, bereft of moderating influences. So while, say, the Red Talons probably won't like humans still, they may not be genocidal in outlook. You may even say that the Red Talons who left took the strongest anti-Homid sentiments with them, allowing the Tribe that remained to be more accepting (or at least tolerant) of non-Lupus within their ranks.<br /> <br /> (I'm also of the idea that, in order to bulk out their numbers, the Fascist Garou coalition may attempt to swell their ranks with Stolen Moons somehow. Creating half-werewolves. These, naturally, are held in contempt by the coalition's Garou members, as Fascists love both having contempt for weakness and making coalitions on convenience, even with groups they hate. They intend to exterminate the Stolen Moons the moment they feel they no longer need them. This also more or less applies to every constituent group within the coalition's Garou population, because Fascists love hating other Fascists. There's no such thing as being &quot;too Pure&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, all this may be too nuanced an arrangement for project leads who cannot be asked to do their due diligence in portraying Indigenous groups respectfully, and would rather just erase them from the game.<br /> <br /> Also, having Fenrir who are gung-ho for action and taking the fight to the Wyrm would mean establishing that as a viable option. Which seems a bit too &quot;Direct Action&quot;-y or &quot;not accepting the Apocalypse as a foregone conclusion&quot;-y for Paradox's liking. I have a feeling the decision to villainize the Get of Fenris has as much to do with wanting to villainize playstyles that aren't Cairn-protecting Street Level games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T17:42:11-07:00","id":1523746,"title":"","content":"To bring up HEART OF THE FORREST again, they have the Fenrir hated and loathed by the local Garou and your protagonist turns out to be of the Get of Fenris bloodline. However, you're descended from a bunch of POLISH Get of Fenris who obviously did not fight for the Nazis but against them.<br /> <br /> I feel like the biggest issue I have with the Get of Fenris is that it seems like it really is Flanderizing the Clan.<br /> <br /> I mostly remember them from RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA versus the Nazi element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-06-2023, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T18:46:04-07:00","id":1523748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523746#post1523746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To bring up HEART OF THE FORREST again, they have the Fenrir hated and loathed by the local Garou and your protagonist turns out to be of the Get of Fenris bloodline. However, you're descended from a bunch of POLISH Get of Fenris who obviously did not fight for the Nazis but against them.<br /> <br /> I feel like the biggest issue I have with the Get of Fenris is that it seems like it really is Flanderizing the Clan.<br /> <br /> I mostly remember them from RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA versus the Nazi element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Get around the world were probably converging on Germany and German colonial holdings during the 30s and 40s to kill as many Nazis as they could. German Get had a head start in this competition, but a higher difficulty, because the Swords had some nasty occult backup in the form of the Verbena Iron Circle, Technocracy, Asatru, and some plausibly deniable BSDs, along with decidedly non-Naturae spirits summoned with their patchwork (and wholly fabricated, of course) &quot;Vril Magic of Atlantis&quot;.<br /> <br /> Afterward, the Get hunted Nazis, especially those among the Swords that had evaded justice. It was a matter of honor, at that point.<br /> <br /> That's the way of things - human countries are big at that point, and they're even bigger today. I wouldn't assume that all, or even most, Garou of a given country are going along with its policies unless said policies are highly unusual ones for humans to take and prioritize the well-being of animals, habitat, and natural features far above those of humans. Their involvement with human society is mostly a ruse, with a few nuggets of genuine affection for a small number of humans that they've found are worth it. About the only reason why any Garou might have observed the draft in the USA is because they believed that they were going to fight a great evil, and that Uncle Sam was going to give them a lift where they needed to go, as quickly as possible. A lot might have just Moon Bridged in and avoided having to deal with any chains of command that weren't entirely Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T19:24:40-07:00","id":1523750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523733#post1523733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it that he was that focused on Garou tribes as exemplars of associated human cultures? Was the vast gulf between Ancient Greece and the Black Furies absolutely lost on him?</div> </div> </div> </div>It strikes me that he simply wanted to get rid of the Get of Fenris for his own reasons. All of the other Tribes were intentionally pulled away from their human ancestry in W5, with the single exception of the Get, who doubled down on it during the design phase. Any Get of Fenris who weren't from Germany and Scandinavia (and there were a lot) are treated as if they didn't and never existed. In the end it's just weird how he wants Nordic peoples from Sweden, Iceland, Finland, Norway, and Denmark to be presented as villainous monsters in W5.<br /> <br /> All I can think is that stems from some sort of personal grudge because I can't see any other explanation for odd statements like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T19:54:33-07:00","id":1523751,"title":"","content":"Wow. So much positive representation and fixing Wta's remaining representation flaws had to die so KM could tell us that all Nordic people are bigots. And that rewrite would have been much more accurate to real Norse mythology than insisting that it's inherently tied to fascism. The only reason neo-nazis latched onto it was because it's perceived as &quot;&quot;&quot;the most white&quot;&quot;&quot;, not because the mythology itself is inherently bigoted.<br /> <br /> This whole situation is just so immensely tasteless. And it keeps getting worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T20:53:03-07:00","id":1523753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>j.f. sambrano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523730#post1523730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The HE team attempted to do this, and was repeatedly shot down by Muammar. It was clear that his vision of cultural de-emphasis (not removal during our tenure) was focused on the Tribes that represented marginalized culture: The colonized Tribes, the black and brown Tribes, the feminist Tribes. But he absolutely insisted that the Fenrir could not be isolated from a culture of white supremacy. It was mandatory that this be a major part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Here is his response to one of the writers, who while I won't name, is a Jewish woman, which I think matters in context with how he is speaking to her, when she tried to write a non-fascist version of the Fenrir who were focused on glory and becoming legends and dying for Gaia. This is essentially &quot;Vanir's Wrath&quot; as they appeared in Heart of the Forest, which was based on the HE draft of the book.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"428\" height=\"184\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>When Justin Achilli talked about the Fenrir as antagonists he talked about the developers not being able to come up with distinct verbs - which was odd. Equally odd was him mentioning that this way they would still be included rather than getting cut. I always wondered why that was the binary: Since the developers supposedly can't come up with verbs they either would be antagonists or get cut. But I guess, now it's clear that Karim Muammar was just still singing the same tune after development switched to the in-house-team. The Fenrir either had to be antagonists or get cut: Those would be the only acceptable options for him.<br /> <br /> Karim Muammar bringing all that baggage of his firmly held beliefs on what W5 should be like into the version the in-house WOD-team worked on couldn't have been helpful... No wonder that the whole deal of divorcing Tribes from their human cultural identity utterly failed with the Fenrir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T23:36:21-07:00","id":1523757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523750#post1523750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All I can think is that stems from some sort of personal grudge because I can't see any other explanation for odd statements like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the guy or his situation, but his bio says he lives in Stockholm (the capital), Sweden and with the name Karim Muammar... yeah, it is very likely he has run into the neo-nazi group Soldiers of Odin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T00:53:03-07:00","id":1523758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523757#post1523757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know the guy or his situation, but his bio says he lives in Stockholm (the capital), Sweden and with the name Karim Muammar... yeah, it is very likely he has run into the neo-nazi group Soldiers of Odin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, that seems about right. The Get have just felt so unfairly treated and don't fit into the new W5 design philosophy at all. Everything about the Get in W5 feels completely different from everything we've seen from other Tribes. But if it's more of a personal issue then it makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> I guess retconning them out of existence in the new edition wasn't enough. They had to be turned into the new big villains of the gameline because some people who live in the same geographic area the Tribe us tied to are racist assholes.<br /> <br /> It's a real shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T00:56:20-07:00","id":1523759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>j.f. sambrano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523730#post1523730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The HE team attempted to do this, and was repeatedly shot down by Muammar. It was clear that his vision of cultural de-emphasis (not removal during our tenure) was focused on the Tribes that represented marginalized culture: The colonized Tribes, the black and brown Tribes, the feminist Tribes. But he absolutely insisted that the Fenrir could not be isolated from a culture of white supremacy. It was mandatory that this be a major part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Here is his response to one of the writers, who while I won't name, is a Jewish woman, which I think matters in context with how he is speaking to her, when she tried to write a non-fascist version of the Fenrir who were focused on glory and becoming legends and dying for Gaia. This is essentially &quot;Vanir's Wrath&quot; as they appeared in Heart of the Forest, which was based on the HE draft of the book.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"428\" height=\"184\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/9kMvJ0O.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for swinging by and posting here! I've always been a big fan of W5, and while I was leery of a new edition there were some things I was excited about. For what it's worth, from what I've seen and heard I think you're vision would have been more or less exactly what I was hoping to see.<br /> <br /> I'm just really sorry that it didn't work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T02:54:45-07:00","id":1523761,"title":"","content":"Renegade have announced what the first supplement of W5 will be. It's called &quot;Scent Of Decay&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rotting from the inside.</b><br /> <br /> Milton has become a company town, and that company is Pentex. Between the rent-a-cops, the wasp fomori and the malicious spirits life there gets harder every day. Can a single pack of Garou scrape off the rot and turn Milton into territory they actually want to hold?<br /> <br /> Scent of Decay presents guidance for character creation and three pre-written stories set in the same small town and scenes which can be included in any Werewolf chronicle:<ul><li>The Break Room: A corporate fulfillment center seeks productivity at a terrible human cost</li> <li>Shadows on the Prison Walls: A trickster spirit tries to use the Garou for their own ends</li> <li>A Pound of Flesh: A rival pack and their patron spirit challenge Milton\u2019s Garou</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Features<ul><li>Three pre-written stories that can be run separately or linked together</li> <li>Guidance for character creation and session zero, useful for running these stories or any others</li> <li>Plug-and-play scenes showing Garou relationships with humans and their world, suitable to drop into any story</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>The three scenarios are all using the small town Milton as a backdrop. So still street-level-only like always...</li> <li>Pound For Flesh once again having Garou with custom Pack-Patron-Spirits while I guess PCs are still stuck with the corebook-rules of only being able to choose Tribal Patron Spirits for their Pack-Patron-Spirit...</li> <li>Don't really feel like advice for character-creation and session zero is what W5 needs</li> </ul><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T04:06:22-07:00","id":1523763,"title":"","content":"Well at least it's not yet another CoF focused thing....well, maybe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T06:05:13-07:00","id":1523769,"title":"","content":"On one hand, at least this feels slightly more like an actual werewolf plot than all the CoF stuff does. On the other, though, I find it weird and disappointing that it feels like the main priority of taking down Milton is just to get more turf instead of striking at the Wyrm or Pentex. Especially since, yet again, they have to force in more inter-Garou conflict where I assume you're going to have to fight the rival pack to see who gets the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T06:20:11-07:00","id":1523770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523769#post1523769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, at least this feels slightly more like an actual werewolf plot than all the CoF stuff does. On the other, though, I find it weird and disappointing that it feels like the main priority of taking down Milton is just to get more turf instead of striking at the Wyrm or Pentex. Especially since, yet again, they have to force in more inter-Garou conflict where I assume you're going to have to fight the rival pack to see who gets the land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres a touch of Forsaken about it...yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T06:48:40-07:00","id":1523772,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the scenarios we got so far follow of course the street-level-only model but it's also striking how 