wishing to do about the same to anyone pulling for him? Does this also mean that the All High is Vampire Elder No Longer Appearing In Canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T14:47:40-07:00","id":1523783,"title":"","content":"I just want point out that the Umbra is not off limits at all. There a entire chapter dedicated to the Umbra, It describes what the Umbra is like, in detail. there's rules for entering the Umbra. There's rules for interacting with the Umbra and it's inhabitants.<br /> you can have spiritual allies beyond your tribal Patron,my player's pack has two.<br /> \u200bthe Umbra is part of w5. A huge part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 10-07-2023, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T14:50:40-07:00","id":1523784,"title":"","content":"I also should point out that you can are NOT locked in small street level stories where &quot;you don't do anything&quot; or where &quot;you can't move away from your caern&quot;<br /> If you want your player characters to be part of a huge organisation made of dozens,maybe even hundred of werewolves working together toward a single goal. You can do just that and the game's rules support that<br /> This is not a defeatist game<br /> This is not a game that says &quot;you can't solve the problems&quot;<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bthe idea that w5 tells the reader societal and environmental and any other issues are unsolvable is false.<br /> the book clearly gives you tools to solve them and tells its possible to do so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 10-07-2023, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:15:28-07:00","id":1523787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523783#post1523783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want point out that the Umbra is not off limits at all. There a entire chapter dedicated to the Umbra, It describes what the Umbra is like, in detail. there's rules for entering the Umbra. There's rules for interacting with the Umbra and it's inhabitants.<br /> you can have spiritual allies beyond your tribal Patron,my player's pack has two.<br /> \u200bthe Umbra is part of w5. A huge part</div> </div> </div> </div>How long can you stay in the Umbra before it kills you? Cos my W5 books rules mean your dead in less than half a day.<br /> <br /> My W5 book has only the Tribe Patrons as available Pack Patrons.<br /> <br /> My W5 book indicates that the majority of spirits distrust, blame or hate the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:18:14-07:00","id":1523788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523784#post1523784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also should point out that you can are NOT locked in small street level stories where &quot;you don't do anything&quot; or where &quot;you can't move away from your caern&quot;<br /> If you want your player characters to be part of a huge organisation made of dozens,maybe even hundred of werewolves working together toward a single goal. You can do just that and the game's rules support that<br /> This is not a defeatist game<br /> This is not a game that says &quot;you can't solve the problems&quot;<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bthe idea that w5 tells the reader societal and environmental and any other issues are unsolvable is false.<br /> the book clearly gives you tools to solve them and tells its possible to do so</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah....nah.<br /> <br /> Literally not in the book that I'm reading right now.<br /> <br /> Hell at times the book literally tells you that Garou don't have the tools and thats why they have always failed.<br /> <br /> The only possible tools shown to somewhat mitigate...not solve...things on a smaller scale are human tools.<br /> <br /> Your ST is doing a lot of work off their own back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-07-2023, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:20:30-07:00","id":1523789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523787#post1523787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How long can you stay in the Umbra before it kills you? Cos my W5 books rules mean your dead in less than half a day.<br /> <br /> My W5 book has only the Tribe Patrons as available Pack Patrons.<br /> <br /> My W5 book indicates that the majority of spirits distrust, blame or hate the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>On on your second point They're called &quot;spiritual allies&quot; not pack patrons.<br /> on your first and third point, the Umbra is still present but it's not the Garou's playground. It's not a place for them to rest and regroup and relax. it's a place of mystery and wonder. And great danger but also of great potential.<br /> Like I said,the Umbra is part of the game. But it's not an place that makes the Garou's lives automatically easier in this edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:23:27-07:00","id":1523790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523788#post1523788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah....nah.<br /> <br /> Literally not in the book that I'm reading right now.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200byou and I are different people,and that means we take different interpretations from the same stuff of course,but what I saw in my copy was almost hopeful ,in an angry way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:24:14-07:00","id":1523791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523783#post1523783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want point out that the Umbra is not off limits at all. There a entire chapter dedicated to the Umbra, It describes what the Umbra is like, in detail. there's rules for entering the Umbra. There's rules for interacting with the Umbra and it's inhabitants.<br /> you can have spiritual allies beyond your tribal Patron,my player's pack has two.<br /> \u200bthe Umbra is part of w5. A huge part</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but what's the point if you start taking Aggravated damage if you're there for any length of time and you lose your character if you stay there for longer than a few hours, when older editions would let you stay pretty much indefinitely with little consequence? That's the problem with all of W5. The text says one thing, but the mechanics railroad you into one particular style of play. This is not Forsaken. There was no reason to add the Umbral damage unless they didn't actually want you to play in the Umbra and only added it out of obligation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523783#post1523783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also should point out that you can are NOT locked in small street level stories where &quot;you don't do anything&quot; or where &quot;you can't move away from your caern&quot;<br /> If you want your player characters to be part of a huge organisation made of dozens,maybe even hundred of werewolves working together toward a single goal. You can do just that and the game's rules support that<br /> This is not a defeatist game<br /> This is not a game that says &quot;you can't solve the problems&quot;<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bthe idea that w5 tells the reader societal and environmental and any other issues are unsolvable is false.<br /> the book clearly gives you tools to solve them and tells its possible to do so\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"center\">\u200b</div> <br /> Again, the book <i>says</i> this at several points, but the rules and general tone of the text disagree. Over and over we're told that the Nation did nothing but constantly fail, that the Garou are too incompetent to even remember things that happened a few years ago, how just existing as a Garou makes you bad at affecting change, that they might have even spent the last few thousand years blowing the whole Wyrm thing out of proportion. The only group that actually <i>cares</i> about fighting the Wyrm in any real way are violent fascists and all the example characters in the tribes are just fucking around doing nothing. Mechanically, Rage rolls are more volatile than they've ever been. A critical fail <i>or success</i> can make you spontaneously murder your packmates. The rules explicitly say that large groups of Garou feed each other's Rage so gathering in anything larger than a few packs is dangerous and irresponsible. Rituals aren't even allowed to have more than a very small amount of Garou or else they all get so worked up they, you guessed it, murder each other.<br /> <br /> The game can <i>say</i> whatever it wants, but unless it actually backs that up, it's just paying lip service to the original game while undermining it at every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:37:13-07:00","id":1523792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523791#post1523791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but what's the point if you start taking Aggravated damage if you're there for any length of time and you lose your character if you stay there for longer than a few hours, when older editions would let you stay pretty much indefinitely with little consequence? That's the problem with all of W5. The text says one thing, but the mechanics railroad you into one particular style of play. This is not Forsaken. There was no reason to add the Umbral damage unless they didn't actually want you to play in the Umbra and only added it out of obligation.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">\u200b</div><br /> Again, the book <i>says</i> this at several points, but the rules and general tone of the text disagree. Over and over we're told that the Nation did nothing but constantly fail, that the Garou are too incompetent to even remember things that happened a few years ago, how just existing as a Garou makes you bad at affecting change, that they might have even spent the last few thousand years blowing the whole Wyrm thing out of proportion. The only group that actually <i>cares</i> about fighting the Wyrm in any real way are violent fascists and all the example characters in the tribes are just fucking around doing nothing. Mechanically, Rage rolls are more volatile than they've ever been. A critical fail <i>or success</i> can make you spontaneously murder your packmates. The rules explicitly say that large groups of Garou feed each other's Rage so gathering in anything larger than a few packs is dangerous and irresponsible. Rituals aren't even allowed to have more than a very small amount of Garou or else they all get so worked up they, you guessed it, murder each other.<br /> <br /> The game can <i>say</i> whatever it wants, but unless it actually backs that up, it's just paying lip service to the original game while undermining it at every turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>So,you're gonna laugh at me... I just reread the Rage rules and I was SO certain you and there others were making shit up . When you guys were telling the truth I have to eat crow.<br /> I was wrong.<br /> I while i sill like the edition,I wasn't defending it so vehemently because I like it I was defending because I thought you guys were making shit up wholesale,that you attacks on wod5 were fake,lies,bullshit.<br /> Now that I've checked for myself you guys weren't lying. I gotta admit your arguments.<br /> I'm sorry for not believing y'all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:56:49-07:00","id":1523793,"title":"","content":"Give your ST a hug, Nic. Sounds like they are running a great chronicle for you mob. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:59:01-07:00","id":1523794,"title":"","content":"Thanks,I will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T16:38:22-07:00","id":1523796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523792#post1523792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So,you're gonna laugh at me... I just reread the Rage rules and I was SO certain you and there others were making shit up . When you guys were telling the truth I have to eat crow.<br /> I was wrong.<br /> I while i sill like the edition,I wasn't defending it so vehemently because I like it I was defending because I thought you guys were making shit up wholesale,that you attacks on wod5 were fake,lies,bullshit.<br /> Now that I've checked for myself you guys weren't lying. I gotta admit your arguments.<br /> I'm sorry for not believing y'all</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries there. I really do wish we were making this all up, but alas.<br /> <br /> If you're having a good time with the game, that's great. It's just a bit of a sore point for older players how much was taken away from it and how much newcomers to the game are missing out on stuff that W5 decided not to put in/changed for whatever reason. I'm fine with new editions changing things, but a lot of these really were for the worse all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 10-07-2023, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T23:13:16-07:00","id":1523861,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> 1) W5 has definitely more settings content in the book than the one you can find in the three basic books of D&amp;D. Did they remove the Litany/Umbra/Spirit/Rite/Auspicies/Forms?<br /> <br /> 2) There is only one W5 book, you can not compare it to the whole D&amp;D books lineup, it is not fair nor sensible. Please note the D&amp;D 5ed settings book is few and usually criticized by some of the fans because they assume that the player already knows something about the settings due to a decades-long legacy. For example, you may search for some reviews of Sword Coast Adventurer's Guide which was particularly infamous for this.<br /> <br /> 3) I think that both justifications for the Silent Strider's wandering are plot hooks, you like the tightest one which makes all Silent Strider cursed and introduces the vampire's elements, I like the loose one which allows for multiple interpretations of the wandering and for exploring different idea in different games. Could you please elucidate to me why the vampiric curse is the only explanation for the Silent Strider's wandering that is compatible with the Rage, the existence of the Garou Nation, and the Impergium?<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, maybe is a cultural or linguistic thing, but I am quite confused by your posts. From the content and the context, it is quite clear that you are expressing your personal opinion and your tastes, yet the way you are expressing it makes it look to me like you are proclaiming some undeniable truth.<br /> <br /> 4) Each tribe could be defined by a small set of attributes, a sentence of a list of 3 to 5 words. Once the core is fixed you can explore different implementations of the core idea. Removing the vampire curse from the Silent Strider does not change them into the Black Fouries or the Star Gazer because the curse by itself is not the core point of the tribe.<br /> <br /> Do you think that any chronicle with a Silent Strider PC or NPC must involve their vampiric curse in an explicit way? Not its generic consequence (the wandering and the lack of contact with the ancestors) but the explicit fact that a powerful vampire cursed the whole tribe, making it relevant that the curse comes from an Egyptian vampire with godlike power and not from other supernatural sources.<br /> <br /> 5) I came out with those questions in less than 20 min, I'm not a long-term player of WtA nor a super expert in world-building. I'm sure that 80% of the W5 readers without prejudice toward the game could come up with a sensible story to fill the gap in the book in less than 3 hours.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28015-ermenegildo","name":"Ermenegildo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T00:09:30-07:00","id":1523864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> 1) W5 has definitely more settings content in the book than the one you can find in the three basic books of D&amp;D. Did they remove the Litany/Umbra/Spirit/Rite/Auspicies/Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, it would have been better if they DIDN'T have auspices/forms/litany set up. Because the way W5 is written and how it goes into how is V5, having a more free'er range of werewolves to pick from would have been better.<br /> <br /> As well, the issue isn't that those things aren't there but the WAY they are there. The Litany is the sacred law of the garou... but the only descriptors are negative and do not explain each tenet properly. In older books, each tenet was gone over how it is intended and how it is actually used.<br /> <br /> Granted, I think as someone new to WtA, you have an easier time filling the holes because you don't know what is missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T00:32:41-07:00","id":1523866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference is that Knightingales posts are considered statements backed up by mechanics and material directly from the book, thoroughly examined and quoted where necessary and your post does not argue against any of that but rather just says ' Nuh-uh' and expects that to carry equal weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T05:20:01-07:00","id":1523872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> 1) W5 has definitely more settings content in the book than the one you can find in the three basic books of D&amp;D. Did they remove the Litany/Umbra/Spirit/Rite/Auspicies/Forms?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>These are barebones compared to every single edition of werewolf. <br /> <br /> The reasons for the litany tenets are gone, the realms and inhabitants of the umbra are gone, and so on<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) There is only one W5 book, you can not compare it to the whole D&amp;D books lineup, it is not fair nor sensible. Please note the D&amp;D 5ed settings book is few and usually criticized by some of the fans because they assume that the player already knows something about the settings due to a decades-long legacy. For example, you may search for some reviews of Sword Coast Adventurer's Guide which was particularly infamous for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> That's incorrect, these books are criticized by comparison with their equivalents in previous editions. <br /> New editions exist only in comparison to the history of an ip, they aren't in a vacuum. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;there's only one book&quot; is not an excuse for a 5th edition of a game.<br /> The core book of werewolf for each of the four previous editions contained all the things missing in W5. There was no need to having even heard of werewolf to open w20 core book and learn all these things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I think that both justifications for the Silent Strider's wandering are plot hooks, you like the tightest one which makes all Silent Strider cursed and introduces the vampire's elements, I like the loose one which allows for multiple interpretations of the wandering and for exploring different idea in different games. Could you please elucidate to me why the vampiric curse is the only explanation for the Silent Strider's wandering that is compatible with the Rage, the existence of the Garou Nation, and the Impergium?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Well, there's 13 tribes that both have rage, lived in the garou nation and originated from the imperium. <br /> Yet only one is cursed to wander, so these elements are not enough to explain it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, maybe is a cultural or linguistic thing, but I am quite confused by your posts. From the content and the context, it is quite clear that you are expressing your personal opinion and your tastes, yet the way you are expressing it makes it look to me like you are proclaiming some undeniable truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Knightindale describes things backed up by the books, it's hardly opinions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4) Each tribe could be defined by a small set of attributes, a sentence of a list of 3 to 5 words. Once the core is fixed you can explore different implementations of the core idea. Removing the vampire curse from the Silent Strider does not change them into the Black Fouries or the Star Gazer because the curse by itself is not the core point of the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> You confuse &quot;you can quickly explain something with a few words&quot; with &quot;that thing's core is purely defined. By these few words&quot;.<br /> <br /> The silent strider are defined by their ancient conflict with set, as much as uktena and wendigo by the conflict with European garous, stargazer by the action of klaytal and so on. <br /> <br /> Without the Greek origins, there's no black furies, and the stargazer are not simply mystics obsessed with enigma, they are defined by their longstanding in Himalayan cultures. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that any chronicle with a Silent Strider PC or NPC must involve their vampiric curse in an explicit way? Not its generic consequence (the wandering and the lack of contact with the ancestors) but the explicit fact that a powerful vampire cursed the whole tribe, making it relevant that the curse comes from an Egyptian vampire with godlike power and not from other supernatural sources.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The WOD is not d&amp;d or even chronicle of darkness, such elements are not mysterious with a few options offered to the dm as a toolbox. The WOD is a setting with many set events. Such as the origin of the striders' curses<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) I came out with those questions in less than 20 min, I'm not a long-term player of WtA nor a super expert in world-building. I'm sure that 80% of the W5 readers without prejudice toward the game could come up with a sensible story to fill the gap in the book in less than 3 hours.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's no prejudice in judging an edition based on the previous It\u00e9ration of a game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T12:16:06-07:00","id":1523882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ermenegildo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523861#post1523861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a><br /> <br /> 1) W5 has definitely more settings content in the book than the one you can find in the three basic books of D&amp;D. Did they remove the Litany/Umbra/Spirit/Rite/Auspicies/Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... One might wonder, though: What exactly is \u201csetting content\u201d? Is it the mere info-dump of what has happened when in the past of the setting? Of course not, it\u2019s a game after all! It\u2019s all about what you can do with it as a player or Storyteller.<br /> <br /> So, in that sense, I have to say: You\u2019re quite wrong. D&amp;D 5E has more setting-content than W5. Excessively so even. And yes, I\u2019m just talking about the three main-books. After all, the quantity of options of all those classes ranging from level 1 to level 20, the variety of monsters offered that present challenges to the aforementioned variety of adventurer-PCs of various levels and a system supporting tactical fights and map-based dungeon-delving.<br /> <br /> W5 is rather lackluster in terms of setting content in comparison<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) There is only one W5 book, you can not compare it to the whole D&amp;D books lineup, it is not fair nor sensible. Please note the D&amp;D 5ed settings book is few and usually criticized by some of the fans because they assume that the player already knows something about the settings due to a decades-long legacy. For example, you may search for some reviews of Sword Coast Adventurer's Guide which was particularly infamous for this. </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t compare it to the whole D&amp;D 5E lineup\u2026? I was already constricting myself to only talk about WotC-content and even that already frustrates your imagination\u2026?! There\u2019s third-party-content as well, mind you, of course and what even is the point of your complaint here? Where\u2019s the unfairness? And W5 is getting more books\u2026 The first one just has been announced and Renegade has already released additional supplementary material. So \u201conly one W5 book\u201d is a temporary thing and already untrue at this point anyway. And since W5 is about to be a line of multiple books, of course I will mention it within the context of D&amp;D 5E\u2019s multiple books. After all, the whole comparison to D&amp;D started with you. You were the one who invited us to delve into this comparison. You were the one responsible for choosing this to be the two game-lines that are getting compared. No reason to shy away from it now when the comparison is helpful in elucidating W5\u2019s flaws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) I think that both justifications for the Silent Strider's wandering are plot hooks, you like the tightest one which makes all Silent Strider cursed and introduces the vampire's elements, I like the loose one which allows for multiple interpretations of the wandering and for exploring different idea in different games. Could you please elucidate to me why the vampiric curse is the only explanation for the Silent Strider's wandering that is compatible with the Rage, the existence of the Garou Nation, and the Impergium? </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the old version of the vampiric curse wasn\u2019t just about wandering. It also cut off the Silent Striders from their Homeland in the Umbra and also cut their connection to their ancestor-spirits. And while the Silent Striders acclimated to the curse by being nomadic and fulfilling roles like messengers and diplomats, that loss of their homeland is mark of shame for the Tribe. And that then colors how other Garou treat them and how, for example, Silent Striders treat vampires wherever they encounter them.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s conflict here, drama and complication. That\u2019s intriguing. What this delivers is a hook. Something that inspires curiosity and interest. And your mention of the \u201conly explanation\u201d only invites the obvious notion: At least, you got <i>an </i>explanation in the past. While the past explanation may introduce constraints, the \u201cno explanation\u201d-approach to making Silent Striders being forced to wander only shows off a lack of effort and/or imagination by the W5-writers. If the writers want to pay so little attention to a concept like the Silent Striders having to wander, they should have just not mentioned it to begin with. Just turning it into mandatory homework for STs is not an improvement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, maybe is a cultural or linguistic thing, but I am quite confused by your posts. From the content and the context, it is quite clear that you are expressing your personal opinion and your tastes, yet the way you are expressing it makes it look to me like you are proclaiming some undeniable truth. </div> </div> </div>Well, I\u2019m not running for President, if that\u2019s what you\u2019re worried about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Each tribe could be defined by a small set of attributes, a sentence of a list of 3 to 5 words. Once the core is fixed you can explore different implementations of the core idea. Removing the vampire curse from the Silent Strider does not change them into the Black Fouries or the Star Gazer because the curse by itself is not the core point of the tribe.<br /> <br /> Do you think that any chronicle with a Silent Strider PC or NPC must involve their vampiric curse in an explicit way? Not its generic consequence (the wandering and the lack of contact with the ancestors) but the explicit fact that a powerful vampire cursed the whole tribe, making it relevant that the curse comes from an Egyptian vampire with godlike power and not from other supernatural sources. </div> </div> </div>See, you ask the most important question right there: \u201cRemoving the vampire curse from the Silent Strider does not change them into the Black Fouries or the Star Gazer because the curse by itself is not the core point of the tribe.\u201d Good point\u2026 So why mention the wander-bit at all then\u2026? See, that\u2019s the thing you\u2019re overlooking: Why mention it at all\u2026? W5 is supposed to be a \u201cre-imagination\u201d, so\u2026 where\u2019s the re-imagination then\u2026? Forcing Silent Striders to wander but only this time around you don\u2019t explain it at all is the complete opposite of that. The W5-writers just copy-pasted a bit from previous editions and cut out the explanation. That\u2019s it. Zero imagination and effort happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) I came out with those questions in less than 20 min, I'm not a long-term player of WtA nor a super expert in world-building. I'm sure that 80% of the W5 readers without prejudice toward the game could come up with a sensible story to fill the gap in the book in less than 3 hours. </div> </div> </div>Oh, and so you think the game-developers\u2019 time is too previous to offer aid in that process? I guess we need to give PbtA-game-developers a call and tell them that putting those questions on the Playbook-sheets is a waste of time. I wonder why PbtA-games have kept doing that despite you insisting it\u2019s a waste of time\u2026<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T12:51:05-07:00","id":1524764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1523617#post1523617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it's a punk game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the discussion went one, but I just want to say that to me the game was already stopping being punk with the Beckoning and the &quot;accruing capital isn't necessarily a bad thing&quot; is the nail on the coffin.<br /> <br /> Beckoning: &quot;Having an invincible metaphor ot The Man isn't fun or interesting, let's remove it so players can go anarch in easier mode and they can freely go punking now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Accruing capital: I can stand by this theory partially in the real world, but the WtA shouldn't. But I forgot the tendency of today's gaming, my bad: &quot;Muh character can't have different ideas than real meself because it's bad, I won't to go punking but also stay true to my everyday self.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T00:40:44-07:00","id":1524794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1524764#post1524764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know the discussion went one, but I just want to say that to me the game was already stopping being punk with the Beckoning and the &quot;accruing capital isn't necessarily a bad thing&quot; is the nail on the coffin.<br /> <br /> Beckoning: &quot;Having an invincible metaphor ot The Man isn't fun or interesting, let's remove it so players can go anarch in easier mode and they can freely go punking now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Accruing capital: I can stand by this theory partially in the real world, but the WtA shouldn't. But I forgot the tendency of today's gaming, my bad: &quot;Muh character can't have different ideas than real meself because it's bad, I won't to go punking but also stay true to my everyday self.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs were never supposed to be unable to win but some Editions seemed to forget they existed.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, the Glass Walkers always believed this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:31:30-07:00","id":1524815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1524794#post1524794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be fair, the Glass Walkers always believed this.</div> </div> </div> </div>So did the Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords and the Fianna.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T14:01:59-07:00","id":1524833,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about the accumulation of capital? Because the Glass Walkers and Silver Fangs are quite torn about that. Some Fangs are from families that followed the trend of corporate acquisition, and some Glass Walkers are in a Camp that snorts it like nose candy, but the entirety of the tribe is still set rather against it, either from being very set in ways of the legendary past, or because they tend to take another tack with how they think technology should progress, and that happens to be &quot;not under corporate control&quot; more often than not. Given that Glass Walkers were so often presented as the premier hackers, it's a wonder they didn't end up punkier.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords are acquisitive as hell, meanwhile, but they apply the &quot;what's mine is mine, what's yours is mine, too,&quot; mindset to pretty much everything that isn't specifically fought for, and they ultimately crave whatever influence they can get. As for the Fianna... I lost track of them a long time ago. I think it was when the first tribebook made a Cheers reference.<br /> <br /> Specifically, that Cheers was an example of Fianna sept. My head hurts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T18:15:39-07:00","id":1524855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1524833#post1524833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the Fianna... I lost track of them a long time ago. I think it was when the first tribebook made a Cheers reference.<br /> <br /> Specifically, that Cheers was an example of Fianna sept. My head hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is little point in going back to the 1st ed Tribebooks for anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T12:06:29-07:00","id":1524877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1524855#post1524855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is little point in going back to the 1st ed Tribebooks for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, I didn't get the Revised version for budget reasons back in the day, and didn't feel much like revisiting it, but maybe during the next DTRPG sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T13:56:38-07:00","id":1524883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1519425-w5-release-thoughts?p=1524877#post1524877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case, I didn't get the Revised version for budget reasons back in the day, and didn't feel much like revisiting it, but maybe during the next DTRPG sale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! You are in for a treat then! I would like to single out Glass Walkers, Silent Striders and Get as really special, but all are really nice - except for CoG which may actually be worse than the original.<br /> <br /> All the tribes are reexamined historically, geographically and contextually and built into a more vibrant whole.<br /> <br /> Even the Native tribes are pretty solid in how they were approached, especially Younger Brother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","